window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS=(window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"title":"Chapter 1","paragraphs":["Continental Integration Gallery","Sometimes in life, you find yourself in a situation you never could have anticipated.","Most of the time, you can overcome such situations by thinking on your feet or drawing upon past experience.","But what happens when something occurs that goes far beyond anything like that?","What are you supposed to do then?","What else? You search for a solution by any means necessary.","\"Fuck. What the hell is this?\"","A harsh curse escaped my mouth at the sight before me.","Then again, anyone who saw the situation I was in would probably react the same way.","There was a forest in front of me.","A forest behind me.","A forest to my left and right.","Nothing but forest in every direction.","The trees were so enormous that they even blocked out the sun.","Where was this place, and why was I here?","I could not make sense of the situation at all.","[Welcome to the Continental Integration Gallery.]","\"Ah, shit! You scared me.\"","Just as my mind was going blank, a strange message appeared before my eyes.","It floated in midair like a hologram.","My surprise lasted only a moment before the message transformed into something else.","[Day 114 of Praying for a Full Recovery.][1]","[IThinkImGoingInsaneIThinkImGoingInsaneIThinkImGoingInsaneIThinkImGoingInsane][12]","[Whatever You Do, Don’t Click the Post Below!!!][52]","[This Is the One for Today!][105]","[Is this... the Continental Gallery...?][8]","[I Started Dating My Childhood Friend! AMA!!][10]","[Is there no one willing to engage in a profound discussion with this lady? It is a grave matter.][2]","It had transformed into the most horrifying embodiment of chaos imaginable.","Had I drunk too much last night?","I was seeing things the moment I woke up.","Yet no matter how many times I rubbed my eyes, the window floating in the air remained.","It was enough to drive me insane.","\"Am I... dreaming right now?\"","I had absolutely no idea what was going on.","Half mesmerized, I moved my finger.","Could I actually open these?","It looked remarkably similar to the online galleries I had often seen on the internet.","Among the collection of chaotic posts, I selected the one with the highest number of comments.","[This post does not exist or has been deleted.]","\"...?\"","It left me with an even greater mystery than the chaos itself.","Had I known this would happen, I would have clicked it sooner.","Still, thanks to that, I began to understand the situation I was in.","I folded my arms and started browsing through the gallery.","I had never been a particularly devoted gallery user, but I had looked through them a few times when I needed information.","Even though this one appeared like a hologram, it was extremely simple to use.","Whether I gestured with my hand or merely moved my eyes, it responded exactly as I intended.","Title: Day 114 of Praying for a Full Recovery","Starlight Princess","Day 114 of praying for a full recovery.","└ Hang in there.","I selected the post with the fewest comments, but it contained only a short message and an equally short reply.","That alone was not enough to judge anything.","Before that, however, I needed to determine whether my current location was safe.","’I have no idea what’s going on, but I should be careful.’","There was no telling what might emerge from the forest.","I would be in serious trouble if something like a bear suddenly appeared.","Fortunately, a little light filtered through the trees here and there, so I could at least see what was ahead.","I started walking.","\"Hmm?\"","Then I noticed a peculiar plant.","The densely packed trees concealed it from view, but they could not hide its faint glow.","I also needed somewhere to conceal myself.","Moving cautiously, I slipped between the trees and settled into place.","’That looks strange.’","At first glance, it seemed like an ordinary plant, but its petals were shaped exactly like crescent moons.","Even without any light falling upon it, it shimmered like a crescent moon in the night sky.","It was an incredibly beautiful flower.","’Beautiful things usually contain poison.’","So I did not touch it.","Things like that were exactly what you were never supposed to mess with in an unfamiliar forest.","If you do not know what it is, do not eat it.","Especially mushrooms.","You would be better off eating bugs or insects instead.","I sincerely hoped things would not deteriorate to that point, but given my current circumstances, I had to consider the possibility.","’Are there any rules?’","I raised my head and opened the gallery.","Apparently, merely thinking about it was enough to bring it up.","When I checked the post at the very top, I found a notice prominently displayed.","Title: Notice","Don’tAbandonTheHero (Head Admin)","Posts that cause discomfort or disgust to others are prohibited!Obscene photographs and videos are prohibited!Posts that create tension between nations are prohibited!Excessive socializing and hostility toward newcomers are prohibited!Violating any of the above rules will result in a ban!Let us preserve peace within the gallery!Heroes are not harmful! Please do not abandon them!","(Most important!)","└ Forget everything else. What’s with the last rule? LMAO","└ What’s the hero doing right now? Sleeping?","└ For real, I heard people saying the hero is useless now that the world is at peace.","└ Rumor has it the Empire sent an execution squad after them, lol.","└ Damn, that’s pitiful. LMAO","The orange-colored name probably meant that person was some kind of administrator.","I remembered hearing something like that before.","The notice was fairly straightforward.","It did not seem like there would be any reason to ban someone as long as they did not cross the line.","The gallery was also extremely easy and convenient to use.","Users could take and upload photographs and videos, and they could even trade with one another.","However, direct trades between users, rather than auctions, were limited to those with registered usernames.","Apparently, it was meant to prevent illegal transactions.","More importantly, because personal relationships between users posed a risk, private conversations during trades were limited to three minutes.","’Users can trade with each other?’","Of everything I had discovered, that was the best news.","I did not even know where I was right now.","Money and everything else could go to hell.","What mattered was obtaining supplies necessary for survival.","Even finding food would be difficult.","I also needed a weapon to protect myself, tools for making fire, and countless other things.","However, trades tended to be one-sided.","That was especially true when one side was desperate.","After thinking it over again and again, I created a registered username.","Before worrying about trading, I first needed to determine where I was.","Title: Woke Up in a Forest. Where Am I?","Wild Grylls","(A photo of a forest densely packed with trees.)","I drank last night and woke up here. ;;","Does anyone know where this is?","For now, I uploaded a post to the gallery.","At the very least, I already understood that this was another world.","The problem was figuring out where in that world I had landed.","I did not even have the luxury of wondering why I had been brought here.","I needed to survive first.","Only then could I take my time thinking about everything else.","There was no point in anything if I died.","But thanks to the post, I realized one thing.","I had just done something incredibly stupid.","Obviously, if I posted nothing but a random picture of a forest, it would be difficult for anyone to identify which forest it was.","Still, the fact that they had bothered to comment at all meant they were at least somewhat helpful bastards.","So I made another post.","Title: What’s the Most Famous Forest on the Continent?","Wild Grylls","└ ? What is this guy even trying to do?","└ This is like posting a picture of someone’s leg and asking us to guess who it belongs to, lol.","└ Want me to upload a picture of my leg? Try guessing who I am.","└ You’re a woman.","└ Correct.","└ Actually, I’m a man, lol.","└ You bastard.","Hmm.","Nothing but completely useless comments.","Assholes.","└ Let’sGrowTrees: Obviously, it’s Alfheim!","└ Get lost, knife-ears.","└ Let’sGrowTrees: Knife-ears? We merely stated the truth!","└ Says the knife-ear bastards who destroyed their own forest and started invading other people’s territory.","└ Let’sGrowTrees: The Mother of Nature has spoken. Every forest is Alfheim!","└ PassingDwarf: Because of those bastards, all the firewood disappeared. Fuck.","└ Knife-ears really stick their noses into everything. Nothing but trouble.","└ Didn’t they invade the underground a hundred years ago because they wanted to grow the World Tree’s roots? Lol.","└ These days, those bastards are worse than demons, lmao.","Guys.","Could you please leave some normal comments?","I had hoped the registered user called \"Let’sGrowTrees\" would be useful, but apparently not.","Every forest was Alfheim.","Alfheim was elven territory.","Therefore, every forest belonged to the elves.","They were spreading that absurd logic around.","’What is this, imperialism?’","Weren’t elves supposed to be a race that loved nature?","The fact that other races existed was shocking enough, but their mentality was even more surprising.","One thing was certain.","Nothing good would come from getting involved with that race.","I asked another question.","└ Wild Grylls: Is there any forest the elves hate?","└ PassingDwarf: Yeah, there is. It’s called the Forest of Four Seasons. Famous for being a goddamn nightmare.","└ Wild Grylls: What kind of place is it?","└ PassingDwarf: Is your head an anvil? Did someone hit it with a hammer?","What the hell?","This bastard started insulting me out of nowhere.","My head did hurt as though someone had smashed it with a hammer, probably because I had drunk so much last night.","But I had not actually been hit.","└ Wild Grylls: Yeah, I told you I woke up in a forest. ;; My head hurts too, so maybe you’re right.","└ PassingDwarf: ;;","└ Boo! Trash!","└ Still, the OP is kind of pitiful. What the hell did you do?","└ Wild Grylls: All I did was drink. Though I did drink quite a lot.","└ PassingDwarf: Fuck, then it’s your own fault. ;; What kind of idiot can’t even find his way home?","└ An alcoholic getting scolded by a dwarf, damn.","Was that really the issue?","I had woken up in another world.","What was I supposed to do about that?","Fortunately, PassingDwarf went on to explain the Forest of Four Seasons in detail.","Apparently, it was the most dangerous forest on the continent.","Just as its name suggested, it contained spring, summer, autumn, and winter.","At first, I had no idea what that meant.","But it did not take long for me to understand why it was called the Forest of Four Seasons.","’Each region has its own season? What kind of bullshit is that...?’","And that was not all.","The forest was rich in mana, so all kinds of dangerous monsters lurked within it.","Worse still, anyone who entered completely lost their sense of direction and could never find their way out.","Because of that, criminals were often thrown into the Forest of Four Seasons.","Not a single person had ever emerged alive.","└ PassingDwarf: On the bright side, it has plenty of elixirs and medicinal herbs.","└ Wild Grylls: But I don’t know which plants are medicinal.","└ PassingDwarf: Then I guess you die, lol. Eat a mushroom and drop dead.","└ Wild Grylls: You bastard.","\"Haah...\"","A frustrated sigh escaped me.","I sincerely hoped this was not the Forest of Four Seasons.","If it really was...","I had no idea what I would do.","Still, he said there were many medicinal herbs, so perhaps I could survive by using them somehow.","Thinking about returning home could wait until after I escaped the forest.","There was nothing I could accomplish by staying rooted here.","’In that case...’","I glanced between my legs.","More precisely, at the ground beneath them.","The plant with the distinctive crescent-shaped petals.","Could this be a medicinal herb as well?","Since I knew nothing about this world, asking the gallery seemed like a reasonable idea.","Online galleries had been useful whenever I posted questions before.","A Continental Integration Gallery ought to be even more useful.","Title: Anyone Know What Herb This Is?","Wild Grylls","(A picture of the crescent-shaped plant.)","I don’t know what kind of herb this is. Anyone recognize it?","Less than three seconds after I uploaded the post—","└ Heavenly Demon: Would you be willing to trade it with this lady? It is an urgent matter.","Someone with the registered username Heavenly Demon immediately left a comment.","Wasn’t \"Heavenly Demon\" the sort of title that only appeared in martial arts novels?","I immediately checked the user’s post history.","I had no intention of trading with some lunatic.","[Heavenly Demon]","[Posts: 2,548] [Comments: 3,817]","[Is there no one willing to engage in a profound discussion with this lady? It is a grave matter.] — 10 minutes ago","[My body grows heavier by the moment.] — 30 minutes ago","[The heavens are the heavens, and the earth is the earth. To think I failed to comprehend such a simple truth.] — 1 hour ago","It was filled with ordinary shitposts.","Hardly any of the posts had many comments, either.","’What is this? Some role-playing freak?’","Her manner of speech was unbearably lofty, yet she spent her time browsing a gallery.","The two things did not seem to fit together.","Still, I should at least hear her out.","First, I checked the comments.","└ How much money do you need? Just name your price.","└ Sword Master: Is that thing valuable?","└ Starlight Princess: That herb is useless to me... I need something containing the energy of the sun...","└ PassingDwarf: Good sir, would you perhaps be interested in a sword personally crafted by a dwarf?","Oh my.","What was going on?","After I briefly checked Heavenly Demon’s posts, an enormous number of comments had appeared.","Even PassingDwarf, who had been so abrasive until moments ago, had suddenly become polite.","Was this herb really that valuable?","└ Heavenly Demon: Silence!! This lady claimed it first, yet you are all consumed by greed!!","└ Yeah, that means nothing~","└ Claimed it first, my ass, lol. The OP will choose whoever they like.","└ Move aside, old hag~","└ Fuck, is that really a New Moon Spirit Herb? Why is one of those there?","└ GiveItToMeGiveItToMeGiveItToMeGiveItToMeGiveItToMeGiveItToMeGiveItToMeGiveItToMe","Heavenly Demon, who had left the first comment, was eventually buried beneath the flood.","Even when she repeatedly tried to make her presence known, it was useless.","Since users could trade with one another, I occasionally saw astronomical amounts being offered.","Of course, I had no idea how valuable this world’s currency was.","Still, one thing was obvious.","’I should choose the person who looks the most desperate.’","And among them, one user continued stubbornly asserting her presence.","As anyone could have guessed, it was Heavenly Demon.","She must have truly been in a hurry, because she was posting comments at an astonishing speed.","Watching her made me feel a little sorry for her.","’Judging from her posts, maybe she really is sick.’","Starlight Princess also seemed ill, but she had already made it clear that the herb was useless to her.","After thinking it over again and again, I decided to choose Heavenly Demon.","Countless trade requests had already arrived, but I ignored them all and selected her.","Having something taken away from you even after you claimed it first was a filthy, despair-inducing feeling.","I knew that all too well.","Apparently, the administrators possessed more authority than I had expected.","Or perhaps they were simply that wary of illegal transactions and excessive socializing.","I was doing neither, so I sent the request without hesitation.","What I needed right now were survival supplies.","’What will she give me?’","I waited with anticipation.","[Heavenly Demon has accepted your request.]"]},{"title":"Chapter 2","paragraphs":["Fortuitous Encounter (1)","If someone asked who the strongest person on the continent was, who would come to mind?","It was one of those debates that frequently broke out not only in the Continental Integration Gallery, but also in everyday life.","Some would name Ash, the Sword Master of the Empire.","Others would point to Kadir, the Archmage of the Kingdom.","Some would choose the princess of the demon race, while others would name the vanished Hero.","Everyone had a different answer depending on their nationality, birthplace, background, and personal connections.","Even so, the fact that those people were extraordinarily powerful remained unchanged.","Title: Who Is the Strongest Person on the Continent?","Ash of the Messiah EmpireKadir of the Iris KingdomKeirin of MephistoThe Missing Hero","└ Heavenly Demon: Strange. Why is this lady not included in the poll?","└ Who are you?","└ Heavenly Demon: This lady is the rightful successor and ruler of the Divine Cult—the Heavenly Demon.","└ Yeah, but who the hell is that? LMAO.","However, rumors originating from the gallery were never particularly trustworthy.","In other words, they were unofficial.","More than anything, the very idea of the Heavenly Demon browsing an online gallery was ridiculous.","Why would someone powerful enough to bring every master of the Central Plains to their knees and unite the martial world spend her time on a gallery?","And she invested a considerable amount of time into it, too.","Hardly a day passed without the Heavenly Demon uploading some meaningless shitpost.","Most people were unaware of it, but a monster lived in \"Jung,\" the nation known for its mysticism.","Jung was far more isolationist than other countries, so very little information about it was available.","However, not even its isolationist policies could block access to the gallery.","└ If she really is the Heavenly Demon, then she’s not wrong. She’s absurdly strong.","└ How strong?","└ She’d probably crush every one of them in a one-on-one fight, lol. Every master in the Central Plains got wrecked by the Heavenly Demon.","└ Then why hasn’t anyone heard about her? I think I’ve seen similar stories on the gallery before.","└ Why don’t you try investing in stocks based entirely on rumors too?","└ Ah.","└ Heavenly Demon, who do you think is the strongest person on the continent?","└ Heavenly Demon: Naturally, it is this lady.","└ LMAO. Why even ask her? Of course she’d say herself.","└ Heavenly Demon: Then allow this lady to ask in return. What realm have those people reached? Have they attained the Transformation Realm?","└ Sword Master: I’m a Sword Master.","└ Allfather: I’m a Tenth-Circle mage.","└ PrincessPickMe: I’m a Ninth-Circle mage!","└ Heavenly Demon: What are those things? This lady is unfamiliar with the language of the Western Lands.","└ Look at this ancient hag, lmao.","As a result, the gallery users treated Heavenly Demon as either a role-playing freak or an out-of-touch old-timer.","In truth, users from the Central Plains were generally unfamiliar with the languages and slang of other countries.","Everything on the gallery was automatically translated.","However, proper nouns and slang could not always be translated into the corresponding terms of another country.","It was a consequence of Jung’s isolationism.","Ironically, that was also why so many people from there used the gallery.","└ Heavenly Demon: When this lady entered the martial world, she was also granted the title of the Greatest Beauty Under Heaven.","└ If you’re really the Heavenly Demon, do something about the emperor. Apparently, using the gallery is punishable by death.","└ Heavenly Demon: To think he would dare obstruct this lady’s hobby. He clearly does not fear the heavens.","After that post, rumors spread that the emperor of Jung had been assassinated.","Gallery usage also suddenly became legal and unrestricted.","Thanks to that, everyone reached the point where they began wondering whether Heavenly Demon might actually be the real Heavenly Demon.","Title: Heavenly Demon, Read This","If you’re really the Heavenly Demon, prove it by showing your face. Then we’ll believe you.","└ Heavenly Demon: You dare demand that this lady reveal her august countenance? How insolent.","└ Are you ugly or something? An old hag? LMAO.","As time passed, Heavenly Demon became increasingly famous.","Not as the actual Heavenly Demon, but as an old role-player who had become completely consumed by her character.","Someone even commented that if the real Heavenly Demon ever saw her posts, she would tear out the impersonator’s organs and personally have her ripped apart by horses.","It was understandable.","Almost everything Heavenly Demon posted was complete nonsense.","The prevailing opinion was that no one could write that many posts unless they had a truly absurd amount of free time.","\"Strange. Why does no one believe this lady?\"","Meanwhile, the real Heavenly Demon stared at the gallery with a puzzled expression.","Skin as white as milk.","Full lips.","A breathtakingly beautiful face and voluptuous curves that could not be concealed even by her black martial robes.","She was Yu So-Wol, the sole being who reigned as the one true \"Demon\" beneath the heavens.","She was also the user called Heavenly Demon, who diligently browsed the gallery every day.","\"This lady has proven everything already. Tsk, tsk.\"","Yu So-Wol clicked her tongue.","Despite that, there was not a trace of irritation on her face.","If anything, she looked amused.","After all, the gallery was the Heavenly Demon’s only hobby.","One might wonder why a grand figure like the Heavenly Demon would waste her time browsing a gallery.","But in the end, she was human too.","Even after defeating every master in the Central Plains and claiming the title of Greatest Under Heaven, she still could not escape boredom.","She had become so overwhelmingly powerful that no one even dared challenge her anymore.","So, under the pretense of entering secluded cultivation, she shut herself away in the mountains.","Title: Upvote If You Think the Heavenly Demon Is Weak as Shit LMAO","└ LMAO.","└ Upvoted, lmao.","└ Agreed, hahaha.","\"Hehe. These bastards deserve to be chewed to pieces. To think they dare mock this lady.\"","This was exactly what she liked.","People who hid behind anonymity and spouted whatever nonsense came to mind.","Back in the Divine Cult, most followers could not even bring themselves to meet her eyes.","Naturally so.","Yu So-Wol was the sole supreme ruler beneath the heavens.","They were too busy worshipping her.","But the gallery was different.","Using anonymity as a shield, people hurled insults at her so outrageous that they could never have spoken them aloud.","Sometimes, they even made sexually suggestive remarks.","Yu So-Wol generously ignored those.","They were strangers whose faces she did not even know.","’Truthfully, this lady would like to fight the masters of the Western Lands...’","Still, there was one thing that bothered her.","Whenever people discussed the strongest person on the continent, she was always excluded.","The other nations had interacted extensively, so the names of their strongest warriors had become widely known.","The Central Plains were different.","Because of their isolationist policies, they remained frogs trapped at the bottom of a well.","She had considered visiting the Western Lands herself, but strangely enough, her followers had desperately opposed it.","\"You cannot.\"","\"Why not?\"","\"If Heaven personally leaves, countless problems will arise.\"","\"How so?\"","\"If you remain absent for too long, the believers will fall into confusion. Wicked martial artists may also use the opportunity to attack. More importantly...\"","\"More importantly?\"","\"Shouldn’t those arrogant barbarians come here themselves? It would make no sense for the Supreme One to personally visit them.\"","\"Hmm. That is true.\"","Thus, the Heavenly Demon was persuaded by her trusted strategist, the \"Demon Brain.\"","However, the Demon Brain’s actual reasoning was entirely different.","Things would become a complete disaster the moment she fought one of the masters from another country.","The Central Plains had not even been fully stabilized yet.","What would happen if they dragged foreign barbarians into the mess as well?","The Heavenly Demon Divine Cult, which they had struggled so hard to establish, might collapse.","It was a perfectly realistic judgment.","└ Is that bastard insane? LMAO.","└ SmartDemon: If that happened, my head would explode.","Title: I’m Going Insane Because of the Woman I Serve","SmartDemon","That woman has nothing but martial arts in her head, and she’s trying to cause trouble again. Thank god I barely managed to stop her. Otherwise, I would’ve run away immediately.","└ Hang in there, man. What do you do for a living?","└ SmartDemon: In the language of the Western Lands... a secretary? A steward? Just think of it as something like that.","└ Sounds rough working for a boss like that.","└ SmartDemon: Haah... Fuck, I want to quit so badly.","└ Why don’t you?","└ SmartDemon: It’s a lifetime position, lol. I started serving her under her parents.","A suspiciously meaningful post appeared on the gallery shortly afterward, but the Heavenly Demon ignored it.","Things like that happened all the time.","Afterward, she remained inside the Divine Cult, briefly emerged because of the emperor, and then returned to her ordinary days.","Being Yu So-Wol the \"human,\" who traded vicious insults with others, was far more entertaining than being Yu So-Wol the \"Heavenly Demon,\" whom everyone revered.","Then, one day, she attained a sudden enlightenment and entered secluded cultivation.","However, she soon encountered a completely unexpected obstacle.","\"Cough!\"","Splatter!","When Yu So-Wol coughed, a large mouthful of pitch-black blood spilled out.","It was a considerable amount.","She wiped the blood from her lips and stared ahead with a complicated expression.","\"To think this lady would suffer qi deviation...\"","That was right.","While deeply immersed in cultivation, she had fallen into qi deviation.","└ But if he’s a secretary, does he actually crawl under the desk?","Since her condition was practically terminal, she emptied her mind and wrote a post on the gallery.","Title: Is There No One Willing to Engage in a Profound Discussion with This Lady? It Is a Grave Matter.","Heavenly Demon","The title says everything.","└ Heavenly Demon Death Beam!!","└ Taaaang!","One might ask how the sole supreme ruler beneath the heavens could possibly suffer qi deviation.","However, this was a kind of trial.","It was like an insect shedding its skin, where success meant survival and failure meant death.","To begin with, anyone could suffer qi deviation.","Being the Heavenly Demon did not make her an exception.","’My internal energy... is becoming far too powerful.’","The Heavenly Demon was strong.","The problem was that she was far too strong.","Yu So-Wol looked down at her hand.","Cracks spread across it like a spiderweb, making it seem as though it might shatter at any moment.","Her body could no longer withstand the power contained within it and was collapsing under its own strength.","There were only two ways to overcome this.","Either she had to bring the energy inside her under control, or neutralize it with a powerful elixir.","However, despite repeatedly attempting the former, her internal energy only continued to grow stronger without diminishing in the slightest.","’The heavens are the heavens, and the earth is the earth...’","Even so, she continued browsing the gallery until the bitter end.","In truth, she had already half given up.","As long as her internal energy continued growing stronger, it was only a matter of time before her frail shell failed to endure it and burst apart.","\"Hehe.\"","Yu So-Wol laughed.","Her expression was filled with pity, as though she were looking at some pathetic idiot.","To think the only thing she could rely on at a time like this was the gallery.","Her self-mockery soon turned into self-loathing.","That only caused her qi deviation to worsen, but she had already reached a state of resignation.","’Is this how it ends...?’","She might as well browse the gallery one last time.","She had no desire to die alone in silence.","Yu So-Wol had initially been furious, but it did not take long for anxiety to replace her anger.","The competition had become far too fierce.","She had already sent a trade request long ago.","However, Wild Grylls had not accepted it.","’How disgraceful.’","Yu So-Wol let out a bitter laugh.","She had behaved disgracefully until the very end.","Still, it was unbearably frustrating.","She had wanted to die in battle, not perish in such a miserable fashion.","The energy within her grew increasingly uncontrollable, while the life remaining to her dwindled by the moment.","Just as Yu So-Wol was about to lament her fate and close her eyes—","The moment her request was accepted, a rectangular window appeared in front of her.","It was an empty chat box.","[Wild Grylls: Hey, hey. You’re Heavenly Demon, right?]","A brief greeting filled the empty space.","It sounded frivolous, yet it was surprisingly polite.","Yu So-Wol cleared her throat without realizing it and sent a reply.","[Heavenly Demon: Indeed. This lady is the one and only Heaven of the Heavenly Demon Divine Cult—the Heavenly Demon. Do you truly intend to trade with this lady?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. You left the first comment, didn’t you? First come, first served.]","[Heavenly Demon: Thank you. It is rare to find someone who understands proper manners.]","[Wild Grylls has sent you a trade request. Would you like to accept?]","A hand of salvation had descended from the heavens.","Yu So-Wol’s eyes gradually widened.","Why?","Why had he chosen her out of so many people?","Her thoughts were lengthy, but her actions were swift.","She hurriedly accepted the request.","Fortunately, Wild Grylls did not appear to be ill-mannered.","The Heavenly Demon sighed inwardly in relief.","The gallery was much like a cesspit.","Countless people hid behind anonymity and revealed their desires without restraint.","Yet within that cesspit, she had discovered such courtesy.","It felt like finding a single rose blooming amid filth.","[Heavenly Demon: Is there anything you desire? This lady will obtain anything within her power.]","Her options were currently limited because she needed to remain in secluded cultivation.","However, once she returned to the Heavenly Demon Divine Cult, she intended to grant him anything he wished.","Even the Heavenly Demon did not forget debts of gratitude or grudges.","If he desired it, she was even willing to pass down a secret martial arts manual.","[Wild Grylls: For now, I need a tool for making fire and a compass. A weapon to protect myself and some simple food. That should be enough.]","The Heavenly Demon was puzzled.","That was all he wanted?","What was the New Moon Spirit Herb?","It was one of the greatest medicinal herbs in existence, something people would gladly pay a fortune to obtain.","It was possible.","The Heavenly Demon turned her head toward the corner of the cave.","There lay a secret manual containing the insights she had gained, a large pile of fasting pills, and even her cherished sword.","She could satisfy two of his conditions.","She did not possess a tool for making fire, but there was another method.","[Heavenly Demon: What realm have you reached? Have you entered the Transformation Realm?]","[Wild Grylls: I’m just an ordinary person...]","\"Damn.\"","In that case, she could not teach him how to use the Samadhi True Flame.","Yu So-Wol hurriedly moved on to the next matter.","[Heavenly Demon: Is that truly all you require? As you surely know, the New Moon Spirit Herb is an exceedingly precious medicinal herb.]","[Wild Grylls: Even so, can it be worth more than my life? I only need what I actually need.]","[Heavenly Demon: Hmm... Very well. Given this lady’s current circumstances, there are some things that will be difficult to obtain immediately. However, they can be acquired with time.]","[Wild Grylls: I’m in a difficult situation too, so I’m in a hurry. Can you provide them or not?]","[Heavenly Demon: Regrettably, this lady can only satisfy two of your requests at present. A weapon and food.]","[Wild Grylls: Hmm...]","[Heavenly Demon: However, once this lady descends from the Divine Cult, the other two items shall also be delivered.]","Yu So-Wol grew increasingly anxious.","As her internal energy continued to intensify, cold sweat began pouring down her body.","Furthermore, trades were limited to three minutes.","Once those three minutes passed, the two users would be unable to trade again for an entire day.","[Wild Grylls: Okay, got it.]","[Heavenly Demon: Truly?]","[Wild Grylls: You said you’d give them to me, so I’ll trust you. If you don’t, then I’ll stop trusting you afterward.]","\"Ah...\"","What an exceptionally courteous young man.","Yu So-Wol was deeply moved.","He was both a fortuitous encounter and a benefactor who had appeared at her most desperate moment.","She had never experienced anything like this, not when she first entered the martial world nor when she unified the Central Plains.","It felt as though everything in the world had grown brighter.","Even though she sat inside a dark cave, her conversation with Wild Grylls shone as brightly as the sun.","’Ah. This is no time for that.’","Yu So-Wol hurriedly gathered her sword and fasting pills.","If she successfully entered the next realm, she would no longer need either of them.","As someone who had used the gallery for a long time, she already knew how trading worked.","All she had to do was hold or touch the object she wished to send.","[Wild Grylls has registered an item for trade.]","[Heavenly Demon has registered items for trade.]","[Would you like to complete the trade?]","She accepted immediately.","The other side must have accepted just as quickly, because the message changed at once.","[The trade has been completed.]","[Wild Grylls: Mine arrived. Did yours?]","Yu So-Wol did not see the message.","She was too busy hurriedly stuffing the New Moon Spirit Herb into her mouth.","She felt truly apologetic toward Wild Grylls, but her life was in danger.","The moment she consumed the herb, she entered meditative circulation.","As expected, the instant she absorbed the herb’s energy, her internal energy—which had burned like an active volcano—gradually began to stabilize.","Even Yu So-Wol herself was surprised.","At this rate, she would be able to break through her shell and ascend to the next realm.","Relief washed over her, but she did not lose focus.","She had no desire to waste this hard-earned opportunity through carelessness.","’Just a little more... Just a little more.’","Wooooong—","Yu So-Wol’s body slowly rose into the air as she continued circulating her energy.","Her beautiful ebony hair floated around her as though drifting underwater, while a faint light seeped from her body.","Crack!","Like a bird breaking free from its egg, Yu So-Wol underwent a similar transformation.","Her body had already experienced Bone and Marrow Cleansing once, yet it was undergoing the process again.","The cracked layers of her skin fell away as new flesh emerged beneath them.","Her bones and body shifted into a form more suitable for the power she now possessed.","A realm liberated from all demonic limitations—","The Realm of Transcending Demonhood.","In the Central Plains, it was known as the Profound Realm.","Yu So-Wol’s closed eyes slowly opened.","They were not the eyes of someone who had just stared death in the face.","Her black pupils were as calm as a still lake and as gentle as a spring breeze.","The Heavenly Demon, Yu So-Wol, had broken free of her shell once more and taken the world into her eyes anew.","\"Phew...\"","Yu So-Wol released a long breath.","It was a sigh filled with countless complicated emotions.","She then looked down at her hand.","Smooth, pale skin had grown over it.","It was the very image of a delicate jade hand.","She was satisfied.","A smile naturally appeared on her lips.","She had no idea how she could possibly repay this grace.","’Ah. Damn. I never thanked him.’","Yu So-Wol hurriedly accessed the gallery.","Too much time had passed, and her conversation with Wild Grylls had already ended.","All she could do now was write a public post.","Even after reaching the Realm of Transcending Demonhood, Yu So-Wol the human had not disappeared.","Quite the opposite.","Meeting a benefactor in her moment of crisis had only strengthened her human side.","She wanted to repay this kindness by any means possible.","But how could she repay such grace?","She had never been indebted to anyone in her entire life.","She had accumulated more grudges than she could count, but this was the first time anyone had ever shown her such kindness.","Her heart pounded, and a smile unconsciously formed on her lips.","Even she did not notice her own reaction.","Title: Wild Grylls, Read This","Heavenly Demon","Thanks to you, this lady has received a debt of gratitude that will take a lifetime to repay.","This lady shall obtain anything you desire, so name whatever you wish.","If you desire it, this lady can personally grant you a secret martial arts manual.","Ah, and lest there be any misunderstanding, the items you requested will be delivered without fail.","\"...Why are you not answering?\"","Yu So-Wol voiced her disappointment.","Only a few minutes had passed, but to her they felt unbearably long.","’Could it be because I failed to thank him immediately?’","Yu So-Wol’s concern deepened.","***","The Heavenly Demon had even addressed him as \"young master.\"","It was a form of address bordering on the highest possible level of respect.","Several comments appeared afterward, but none came from the person she wanted.","Yu So-Wol waited endlessly for her benefactor to respond.","Yet even after several minutes passed, Wild Grylls left no comment.","Meanwhile, Wild Grylls was—","\"Woof! Woof! Grrrr! Woof!\"","\"Whoa! Fuck!\"","—being chased by a beast.","Contrary to the Heavenly Demon’s assumptions, he was in absolutely no position to access the gallery."]},{"title":"Chapter 3","paragraphs":["Fortuitous Encounter (2)","What was the most dangerous thing in the wilderness?","The three great poisons—poisonous plants, venomous insects, and venomous snakes?","Correct.","Or perhaps mushrooms, the ultimate gamble?","Also correct.","Maybe starvation or dehydration?","That was correct too.","Beyond the protective boundaries of civilization, everything in the wilderness was dangerous.","Even the ground beneath your feet could not be trusted.","And when judged individually, humans were incredibly weak creatures.","Without tools, a person probably could not even defeat a large dog.","\"Woof! Woof! Woof!\"","\"Woof! Woof!\"","A pack of massive dogs was barking viciously in front of me.","The problem was that they were not merely large dogs.","They were almost as big as cattle.","As expected of a fantasy world, even the stray dogs had absurdly high specs.","’At least they can’t come any closer because of their size...’","Taking their enormous bodies into account, I had deliberately entered a densely wooded area.","The place where I had found the herb had also been decent, but it was open on all sides.","The trees there were thinner too.","So I had fled in a hurry.","I had not forgotten the sword and bundle of food I received from the Heavenly Demon.","Now, I was holding my ground with my back against a gigantic rock wall.","The wild dogs did not seem willing to force their way between the trees.","They merely watched me from outside.","In other words, they were intelligent.","They knew I currently had the advantage.","’What should I do?’","Was my only option to remain here?","I sincerely hoped those damn dogs would give up and leave.","However, one should always prepare for the worst.","I immediately accessed the gallery.","Since they had not attacked yet, I planned to ask for help.","Title: Urgent—How Do I Deal With These Damn Dogs?","Wild Grylls","(A picture of enormous dogs glaring between the trees.)","What am I supposed to do with these bastards? Anyone have a method?","└ Aren’t those Mad Dogs? Why are they so huge?","└ Even a Sword Expert would have trouble fighting those things.","└ Farewell. I’ll pray for your soul.","└ The moment one bites you, you’ll probably die of rabies, lmao.","└ Wild Grylls: Stop answering my question with more questions, you bastards.","These people were completely useless.","I frowned.","As time passed, these Mad Dogs would continue looking for an opportunity.","I had to come up with something.","└ Heavenly Demon: No! You must not die! Please survive long enough for this lady to repay her debt!","└ Why does she sound so desperate? LMAO.","└ Anyone would think they were lovers, lol.","The Heavenly Demon’s not-quite-encouragement was somewhat comforting.","It did not provide any practical help, though.","Still, the growing number of comments meant more people were seeing the post.","Hopefully, at least one useful person would appear.","I did not know what a Sword Expert was, but I could tell that these creatures were monsters by my standards.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Ah! I’ve encountered those monsters many times! Their noses are their weak point. If you stab one in the nose with a sword, it should lose consciousness for several seconds!","└ How does the head admin know that?","└ Aren’t those monsters difficult to encounter?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Because I’m the Hero! I know how to deal with every monster and demonic beast!","Fortunately, the passing head administrator kindly explained their weakness.","Just as I was about to feel encouraged—","└ Sword Master: But to actually do what the head admin suggested, wouldn’t you need to be at least a high-level Sword Expert? As far as I know, anyway.","└ The most useless theory in the world: \"As far as I know,\" lmao.","└ What happens if he fails?","└ Sword Master: They’ll enter a berserk state, smash through the trees, and then he’ll die.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: That’s why you have to cut off their heads or stab their hearts before that happens! I can do it!","Holy shit.","The head admin was apparently a monster wearing human skin.","And how did Sword Master know all this?","└ Wild Grylls: Fuck, is there no method for an ordinary person? All I have is the sword the Heavenly Demon gave me.","└ Ordinary people never encounter those things. ;; OP, are you really in the Forest of Four Seasons? Are you perhaps a criminal?","└ No, that can’t be it. They gouge out criminals’ eyes before throwing them into the Forest of Four Seasons so they can’t use the gallery.","└ That’s insanely brutal. ;;","└ Doesn’t gallery access stop working inside the Forest of Four Seasons?","└ It’s \"doesn’t,\" not \"don’t.\"","└ Yeah, I heard the mana there gets tangled and blocks access.","└ Just hit them in the head. No matter how big they are, dogs are still dogs.","A great deal of useless nonsense appeared, but the conclusion was simple.","Hit them in the head.","Truly valuable information.","It was about as insightful as saying, \"Humans die if they do not drink water.\"","└ Heavenly Demon: This lady’s sword is a masterpiece among masterpieces. Severing the heads of those wild dogs should be effortless. Trust this lady.","└ Sword Master: How good is it? Better than Durandal or Excalibur?","└ Heavenly Demon: What are those? In any case, this lady’s sword was forged from Ten-Thousand-Year Cold Iron.","└ Ten-thousand-year cold iron, lmaoooo.","└ Does Ten-Thousand-Year Cold Iron grow on trees or something? LMAO.","Thus spoke the Heavenly Demon:","Her sword was a masterpiece among masterpieces.","After reading her words, I looked down at the weapon.","It certainly did not look ordinary.","I could tell that it had been meticulously maintained.","I also had the advantage of the terrain.","I should be able to fight them.","’It’s do or die.’","I looked at the largest dog standing in the center.","There were three of them in total, and the one in the middle was by far the biggest.","It was probably the leader.","Without hesitation, I charged toward it.","\"Woof! Woof!\"","The two dogs guarding either side of the leader immediately began squeezing through the gaps between the trees.","\"It was a trap, you bastards!\"","I had only pretended to target the leader.","Instead, I turned toward one of its subordinates.","The one on the left came first.","More than half its body had already emerged between the trees.","I swung the sword down vertically toward its head.","I knew absolutely nothing about swordsmanship, so rather than cutting, I simply struck downward with all my strength.","Swish—","\"Hmm?\"","Something was strange.","I had definitely swung the sword, yet the blade seemed to pass straight through the dog’s head.","For a moment, I wondered whether I had struck an illusion.","But the result appeared soon afterward.","Split!","The dog’s head suddenly split vertically down the middle.","Thud!","It collapsed with its tongue hanging out.","Even its tongue had been divided cleanly in half.","I stared down at the dog in bewilderment.","I had felt almost no resistance in my hands.","At most, it had felt like cutting tofu with a knife.","The sheer unreality of it left me dazed.","\"Grrrwoof!\"","Ah.","Right.","There was still another one.","The instant I heard the sound behind me, I swung the sword reflexively.","It had come from so close that my body moved before I could think.","Splatter!","Fortunately, the dog never managed to pounce on me.","Instead, its head and torso separated and fell to the ground.","Just like before, I barely felt the blade cut through anything.","I stared blankly between the two corpses.","Whatever else might be true, I had realized one thing.","The Heavenly Demon was a god.","And this sword was invincible.","\"Grrrr...!\"","\"Ah. You were still here.\"","Only the leader remained.","It glared at me warily, every muscle in its body tense.","A taut silence stretched between us through the thick trees.","Which of us would retreat first?","Naturally, it was the leader.","It glanced back and forth at the corpses of its subordinates, then slowly began to back away.","It must have realized that as long as I had the sword, it was the one at a disadvantage.","Smart bastard.","\"Phew!\"","The danger had finally passed.","I let out a long breath filled with all the tension that had built up inside me.","What would have happened if I had not received the Heavenly Demon’s sword?","Or if I had never happened to discover that herb in the first place?","I still did not have a compass, so wandering around recklessly was difficult.","I would have to wait until the Heavenly Demon sent one.","’Ah. Before that, I should thank her.’","Without delay, I wrote a post on the gallery.","Title: The Heavenly Demon Is a God","Wild Grylls","(A picture of the dead dogs on the ground and my hand gripping the sword tightly.)","And this sword is invincible.","└ Holy shit, he actually killed those things?","└ That sword really is insanely good, lmao.","└ Sword Master: Those were extremely clean cuts. Even with an excellent sword, achieving that would be difficult.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: You’re alive! What a relief! It seems there will be nothing to mourn today!","└ Heavenly Demon: Are you injured anywhere?","└ Wild Grylls: I’m fine, thanks to you. Thank you for the excellent sword.","└ Heavenly Demon: That is a relief. This lady feared that something terrible had happened to you.","└ Heavenly Demon: This lady is proficient with every weapon. If one had to be chosen, however, it would be the sword.","Come to think of it, Sword Master also seemed rather old-fashioned.","Unlike most users, they used proper punctuation and spacing.","I generally did not care about such things, but when the other person showed me courtesy, I tended to respond in kind.","At least halfway.","Concern practically dripped from the Heavenly Demon’s comments.","How could such a warmhearted person possibly be the Heavenly Demon?","It made no sense.","Her manner of speaking also reminded me of my late grandmother, which made her feel even more familiar.","Leaning against the rock wall, I began browsing the gallery while resting.","└ Sword Master: If you have nothing else to do, would you be interested in learning swordsmanship? You seem to have talent.","└ Heavenly Demon: Silence! This lady shall personally bestow a secret manual upon him! How dare you interfere!","└ Sword Master: Come on, don’t be so strict. Do you use a sword as well, Heavenly Demon?","└ Wild Grylls: I need survival supplies more than swordsmanship right now...","└ Sword Master: That is true. I’ll give it some thought and return later.","└ Heavenly Demon: This lady shall descend the mountain at once. The items you requested will be delivered without fail.","That was enough gallery browsing for now.","I rose to my feet.","If I remained here too long, other beasts might be drawn by the smell of blood.","It had not exactly been a fierce battle, but the tension had drained a considerable amount of my strength.","It would be better to keep moving.","’I need somewhere to hide until the compass arrives...’","Rrrrrrrumble!","Without warning, the ground began to shake.","I blinked, then hurriedly sprang upright.","A natural disaster immediately after a beast attack?","What kind of absurd cosmic persecution was this?","But something was strange.","The moment I pulled my back away from the wall, the vibrations seemed to weaken.","Before I could identify the source of that unnatural sensation, the wall behind me began to change.","Grrrrrrind!","\"...Oh, dear God.\"","The wall was rising.","Literally.","The entire wall was lifting into the air.","A gigantic slab of rock tore itself from the ground like an uprooted tree.","It did not take me long to realize that the \"rock wall\" I had been leaning against was actually a leg.","I stared as what had appeared to be an ordinary rocky hill transformed into a two-legged giant.","Then I accessed the gallery.","└ Holy shit, isn’t that a Stone Guardian?","└ Why the fuck is a Guardian there? LMAO.","└ Isn’t that thing difficult even for a Sword Master to kill?","└ Dude, what are you doing? Run!","Everyone was screaming at me to flee.","I immediately turned and ran.","But I did not forget the bundle of food on the ground.","It was a gift from the Heavenly Demon.","I could never abandon it.","Title: What the Hell Is This Thing?","Wild Grylls","(A picture of an enormous stone giant towering above the forest.)","└ You get fifty thousand gold if you kill that thing, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: FUcKyOUiDoNtNeEdIt","└ He’s still browsing the gallery while running. ;;","└ Someone translate that.","└ Doesn’t it say, \"Fuck you, I don’t need it\"?","└ Seems right, lmao.","└ This lunatic, hahaha.","I barely managed to escape.","To catch my breath, I leaned against a tree.","I could still hear heavy thuds in the distance, but they were gradually fading.","It was not coming after me.","’This is driving me insane.’","The moment I overcame one crisis, another appeared.","What kind of ridiculous forest was this?","’This can’t actually be the Forest of Four Seasons, can it?’","I desperately hoped not.","After all, they had said the gallery could not be accessed from inside the Forest of Four Seasons.","I took several ragged breaths, then opened the gallery again.","The notifications had been ringing nonstop even while I ran, so I could not help checking.","└ Sword Master: Defeating that creature is simple. Cut off one of its legs and it will lose its balance. Then drive your sword into the core in its chest.","└ Why are you explaining it like a recipe for instant noodles? LMAO.","└ \"See? Easy, isn’t it?\"","[You Can Do It Too! Advanced Swordsmanship Lecture 15] — 2 hours ago","[You Can Do It Too! Advanced Swordsmanship Lecture 14] — 1 day ago","[You Can Do It Too! Advanced Swordsmanship Lecture 13] — 2 days ago","Sword Master was also surprisingly far from normal.","What exactly did this person do?","Just as I had with the Heavenly Demon, I searched through Sword Master’s posting history.","\"...\"","Oh, fuck.","They were obsessed with swords.","Every single post was a swordsmanship lecture.","They were insane in an entirely different way.","They had fewer posts than the Heavenly Demon, but unlike her endless stream of shitposts, every one of these was filled with effort and detail.","An unnecessarily diligent lunatic.","There was no better way to describe Sword Master.","Among all those posts, one stood out above the rest.","Title: Looking for a Life Partner","Sword Master","Requirement: Must be stronger than a Sword Master.","└ How hard do you hit?","└ Sword Master: Not telling.","There was not a single normal person in this gallery."]},{"title":"Chapter 4","paragraphs":["Crisis (1)","Why was the Messiah Empire called an \"empire\"?","There were several reasons, but the answer was simple.","It possessed the largest territory, the greatest wealth, and overwhelming military power.","Of those, military strength was inevitably influenced by the power of exceptional individuals.","And the Empire possessed a Sword Master.","What was a Sword Master?","A monster who stood at the pinnacle of swordsmanship and was regarded not merely as a tactical weapon, but as a strategic one.","Sword Masters were famous for splitting the earth with one strike and cleaving mountains with the next.","The existence of a Sword Master was precisely why other nations could not recklessly defy the Empire.","Title: Are Sword Masters Supposed to Be Rare?","I thought they were everywhere in the old days.","└ Yeah, they were back then.","└ Why aren’t they now?","└ Ash is gatekeeping the title. She says anyone weaker than her has no right to call themselves a Sword Master, lmao.","└ Fuck, is she the level cap? LMAO.","└ Hahahaha.","└ The Sword Saints of the past would only qualify as modern Sword Masters.","└ Are there no Sword Masters among races other than humans?","└ There are. They just all got wrecked by Ash.","└ Is she even human? LMAO.","At the age of fifteen, Ash made a declaration.","And everyone accepted it.","Anyone who desired both her beauty and her hand in marriage had only to defeat her.","After she became an adult, of course.","Three years passed.","She reached adulthood and waited with anticipation, but no man capable of defeating her appeared.","Five years passed.","She was approaching the ideal age for marriage and began growing anxious, but she patiently continued to wait.","Ten years passed.","Her family began begging her to marry someone.","That was when she first sensed that something had gone terribly wrong.","In truth, the rank of Sword Master was not exclusive to the Empire.","It was simply that the Empire’s Sword Master was the strongest.","Overwhelmingly so.","Ash Menethil, the Sword Master of the Empire, was renowned as the greatest swordswoman of the age.","She was famous not only for her strength, but also for her snow-white hair, blue eyes, and exceptional beauty.","Her looks had blossomed brilliantly from an early age, stealing the hearts of countless men.","Naturally, marriage proposals poured in even while she was still young.","\"I will marry a man stronger than me!\"","Title: ???: \"I’ll Marry a Man Stronger Than Me\"","Fifteen years had passed since then.","No man had managed to defeat her.","└ She’s become a total auntie now, lmao. Wait, someone’s knocking at my door.","└ Only a cold, lifeless comment remains.","└ What happens if you call Ash an auntie to her face?","└ Not sure, but apparently some brat heard her age and teased her by calling her one, lol.","└ Couldn’t an elf or demon take her?","└ There’s no one clearly stronger than Ash, lol.","└ Humans are surprisingly powerful, anyway. Their average is low as hell, but their peak is absurdly high.","└ Just how strong is she?","Fifteen years passed.","Her abilities continued to rise, yet still no man appeared who could defeat her.","She had undergone Bone and Marrow Cleansing and retained the beauty of a woman in her twenties, but her actual age was now in her thirties.","She had long since passed the usual age for marriage, so very few men dared approach her.","Of course, some men were captivated by her beauty and proposed anyway.","The problem was that every last one of them was weaker than Ash.","She did not want to abandon her final shred of pride and the conviction she had upheld for so long.","So she endured.","And endured.","Men also found women stronger than themselves intimidating, so they understood her position.","\"This can’t continue.\"","She could not simply wait forever.","Ash decided to personally train disciples.","She would raise promising candidates herself.","Surely, at least one of them would succeed.","Not a single one did.","They all lost to Ash and married other women.","People in this world generally married young, so they all ran off before reaching her level.","\"I’ll share all my knowledge with the gallery.\"","Feeling a growing sense of crisis, Ash began carefully uploading her swordsmanship expertise to the gallery.","She hoped to create a virtuous cycle.","It actually worked.","The general level of martial ability across the continent steadily rose.","At this rate, a man stronger than Ash would surely emerge from one kingdom or another.","Would that not cause international problems?","Her path to marriage was completely blocked.","International relations could go fuck themselves.","Yet even then, no man appeared who could defeat her.","Instead, mass-produced Sword Masters simply began appearing everywhere.","To make matters worse, Ash’s strength continued increasing even when she did nothing but breathe.","\"Why? Why is there no one? Why the hell?!\"","Ash could not understand it.","Why was there such a complete lack of talent?","She had tried everything imaginable, yet no man capable of defeating her emerged.","After examining the problem, she finally realized something far too late.","\"I get stronger just by breathing? Are you kidding me?!\"","That was right.","The woman praised as a heavenly genius was also a natural disaster in another sense.","Mana accumulated inside her simply through breathing, and she possessed the talent to channel it into her sword effortlessly.","Her obsession with marriage had distracted her, but had she trained consistently, she would have reached the rank of Grand Sword Master at a remarkably young age.","Yet Ash was already always included whenever people debated the strongest person on the continent.","She had no need to become any stronger.","\"Fuck my life.\"","Everything suddenly felt meaningless.","A crushing wave of emptiness washed over her.","In the end, Ash abandoned every one of her official positions and withdrew from public life.","The Emperor personally begged her to remain, but she rejected every request.","She did permit the Empire to continue using her name whenever necessary.","Still, a symbolic figurehead had value precisely because people could see her.","The fact that the Empire itself trembled at the mere possibility of losing Ash demonstrated once again just how great her presence was.","And so, after a total of twenty years had passed, the reclusive Ash was—","\"Hehehe.\"","—lying on her bed and eating a banana.","She giggled foolishly.","Her snow-white hair had been tied into a messy bun, and she wore the simple, comfortable clothes of a complete shut-in.","The round glasses on her face completed the image of an unemployed recluse.","These days, she spent her time diligently lurking on the gallery and enjoying her peaceful, if questionable, life.","Smack!","\"Ow!\"","\"You little brat! I told you to go outside!\"","A powerful slap landed on the back of Ash, who had been endlessly browsing the gallery.","Her body was as hard as forged iron, yet the blow stung strangely badly.","\"Look at your younger sister! She’s thirty and pregnant again! She’s about to have her fifth child—her fifth! You were even the captain of the Imperial Guard, so why aren’t you married?!\"","\"Ah, Mom...\"","Naturally, it hurt because the blow was filled with a mother’s love.","Ash rubbed her stinging back and looked at her mother.","Though her face was marked by many wrinkles, her features closely resembled Ash’s.","She must have been stunning in her youth.","Ash was already in her thirties, but her mother had given birth to her at nineteen.","For this era, that was perfectly normal.","\"What am I supposed to do when there isn’t a man I like...?\"","\"Lower your standards! Where in the world are you going to find a man stronger than you?!\"","\"...\"","Ash had no answer to her mother’s criticism.","It was, in fact, mostly correct.","Even among all races, Ash was exceptionally powerful.","She was stronger than elves and demons alike.","Of course, there was probably some man somewhere in the world who was stronger than her.","She simply had not found him.","\"My goodness, this mother’s heart is going to burst. What good is being a Sword Master or whatever if you’re still unmarried at thirty-five? I’m already in my mid-fifties, so please listen to me!\"","\"Well... my younger sister married well, didn’t she? Mom, we’re nobles now. Nobles.\"","Ash’s family had originally been commoners.","They rose in status when Ash became the greatest swordswoman on the continent.","The title she received was none other than countess.","Considering that marquises generally governed the borderlands, it was among the highest honors the Emperor could grant.","Her younger sister was also beautiful and had married well.","The fact that she already had five children made it obvious that she and her husband were very affectionate.","Unlike her older sister, she had found her perfect match.","Ash was jealous.","\"What good does that do when my eldest daughter is in this state? At least go outside and exercise!\"","\"I get stronger just by breathing...\"","\"Do you seriously expect me to believe that nonsense? Get out!\"","\"Yes, ma’am!\"","No matter how old a child became, they remained a child in their parent’s eyes.","At her mother’s shout, Ash hurriedly climbed out of bed.","She picked up a practice sword and headed toward the estate’s exit.","Then, after pretending she was going outside, she turned around.","Training was annoying.","Because she became stronger merely by breathing, she felt no need to do it.","’I should upload another post.’","She returned to her bed and accessed the gallery.","Her role there was simple.","Title: You Can Do It Too! Advanced Swordsmanship Lecture 15","Sword Master","Today’s advanced lesson is about parrying. What is parrying, you ask—","Uploading swordsmanship knowledge to the gallery had become part of her daily routine.","Originally, she had posted these lessons to raise the continent’s overall level of swordsmanship.","Now, it felt more like a job.","She had not always been so deeply immersed in the gallery.","In the past, she had merely lurked from time to time.","But after belatedly discovering the truth about her constitution and falling into despair over the feeling that the world itself had deceived her, she became completely addicted to it.","└ What do you think about quick-draw swordsmanship?","└ Sword Master: You should learn the fundamentals instead of wasting your time practicing that nonsense.","└ But it looks cool.","└ Sword Master: Do it after you become a Sword Master.","└ But Sword Masters are strong no matter what they do, lmao.","There were occasionally some complete idiots, but Ash always responded politely.","Why did she bother maintaining such decorum in a gallery where everyone openly displayed their desires?","’This is the only way to keep people from suspecting me.’","It was because of Ash’s usual personality.","She was rather rough and outspoken by nature.","That had allowed her to get along well with nobles despite being born a commoner, but none of that mattered here.","More importantly, she had been using the gallery for far too long.","Her activity was nothing compared to the truly hardcore gallery addicts, but she had still been around for years.","She was someone who had consistently used the gallery for a very long time.","She had even drawn suspicion when she first began uploading swordsmanship knowledge.","’I’d rather kill myself than die of embarrassment.’","There was always a chance someone might discover her identity, so she deliberately adopted a calm and refined manner of speech.","For the same reason, she never uploaded photographs or videos when posting swordsmanship lessons.","Fortunately, as a genius among geniuses, she seemed to possess considerable talent for writing as well.","Her explanations were so excellent that the lack of visual material caused no problems.","\"Ah. I want to get married.\"","Ash muttered while scratching her firm abdominal muscles.","Even though she had long since passed the usual age of marriage, she had not given up.","She was still willing to accept a challenger.","The Empire simply rejected them on her behalf because she was living in seclusion.","Since the gallery served as her main window into the outside world, she remained completely unaware of that fact.","\"Could this one be strong?\"","When browsing the gallery, she occasionally encountered people who showed promise or boasted about their strength.","She had wanted to meet some of them personally, but their lack of ability was usually exposed before long.","└ Fuck, how are you supposed to dodge that? Are you joking?","└ Sword Master: Why would you be unable to dodge it? Flexibility is essential. To think you do not even understand that. You were nothing but a loudmouthed insect.","└ Damn, she went straight for the throat, lmao.","It usually went something like that.","Most of them had theories that were complete garbage.","Others simply lacked knowledge.","Still, not everyone was an idiot.","There was one famous user who had caught Ash’s attention.","’Just how strong is this Heavenly Demon?’","Heavenly Demon constantly produced posts that were no better than excrement.","The users treated her like any other eccentric gallery addict.","Ash had initially done the same.","However, some of Heavenly Demon’s occasional remarks were deeply connected to martial arts.","Others scoffed at them, but Ash did not.","In fact, she hated Heavenly Demon several times more than everyone else did.","’That bastard made me even stronger...’","A genius recognized another genius.","Heavenly Demon’s posts had influenced Ash considerably.","It was almost like having enlightenment forcibly injected into her.","Every time Ash read one of Heavenly Demon’s posts, the mana within her visibly increased.","It did not happen only once or twice.","At first, she dismissed it as a coincidence.","But after experiencing it several times, she realized the truth.","That Heavenly Demon bastard was carelessly scattering her own enlightenment everywhere.","The amusing part was that most users failed to recognize its true value.","’Judging by the way she talks, she’s definitely a woman...’","Had Heavenly Demon been a man, Ash would have found him by any means necessary.","Someone capable of reaching such profound insights had to possess extraordinary strength.","However, Heavenly Demon constantly referred to herself as \"this lady,\" and everything about her speech suggested she was female.","An elderly woman, at that.","One thing was certain.","She was older than Ash.","’...Not that I’m in any position to say that.’","Ash also freely distributed her swordsmanship knowledge through the gallery.","Swordsmanship was traditionally highly secretive.","Yet because she spread techniques that anyone could learn, everyone’s abilities began rising.","The nation that benefited most was the Iris Kingdom, the Empire’s eternal rival.","Originally, the Iris Kingdom was a country where mages were stronger than knights.","Thanks to Ash’s trolling, however, its knights had now caught up to the continental average.","\"Bring me this user called Sword Master at once!\"","\"Your Majesty, it is impossible to identify the personal information of gallery users.\"","\"Y-You... You...! Urgh! Ugh!\"","\"Y-Your Majesty!\"","Naturally, the Emperor of the Empire had erupted in fury.","But there was no way to capture an anonymous gallery user.","It was one of the reasons Ash had resigned as captain of the Imperial Guard.","How could she continue serving while enduring that level of awkwardness?","If the Empire encountered a problem, the Emperor had to come and find her personally.","From Ash’s perspective, this allowed her to enjoy a comfortable life.","Title: The Heavenly Demon Is a God","Wild Grylls","(A picture of dead dogs lying on the ground and a hand tightly gripping a sword.)","And this sword is invincible.","\"Hmm?\"","Ash was diligently browsing the gallery while avoiding her mother’s eyes when a registered user caught her attention.","It was the person who claimed to have suddenly awakened in a forest.","At first, she had assumed it was another ordinary shitpost.","Then he found some herb called the New Moon Spirit Herb, and the entire gallery erupted into chaos.","That was when she began taking a slight interest in him.","She wondered what kind of person he was.","’Is the New Moon Spirit Herb really that valuable?’","For the record, Ash knew nothing about it.","Her body had no need for medicinal elixirs.","Later, he encountered Mad Dogs as large as cattle.","She had wondered how things would end, only for him to kill two of them.","’Those cuts... are incredibly clean.’","Ash looked surprised.","Interest glimmered in her blue eyes behind her round glasses.","Even from the photograph, the severed surfaces were extraordinarily smooth.","No matter how good the weapon was, most people could not even cut tofu in a perfectly straight line.","There had been no wavering in his strike.","He claimed to be an ordinary person, which only made him more intriguing.","More importantly—","└ Sword Master: If you have nothing else to do, would you be interested in learning swordsmanship? You seem to possess talent.","└ Heavenly Demon: Silence! This lady shall personally pass down a secret manual to him! How dare you interfere!","Heavenly Demon was interested in him.","That Heavenly Demon, who was usually too busy posting garbage!","She fussed over him as though warning everyone not to touch something she had already claimed.","She failed to realize that her behavior only drew more attention.","’Would you look at that?’","Ash flashed a broad, healthy smile.","That reaction made her want to tease Heavenly Demon even more.","Heavenly Demon was famous for doing whatever she pleased without caring about anyone else.","And now she was reacting like this?","Ash wanted to provoke her even more.","It would also be useful to learn more about Wild Grylls.","Ash waited for him to upload another post.","Title: Found a Cave. Should I Go Inside?","Wild Grylls","(A picture showing the entrance of a dark cave.)","It’s getting dark, so I need somewhere to rest. Should I go in? What if there’s a bear?","└ You’d better pray it’s only a bear. It could be a dungeon, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: What comes out of a dungeon?","└ No idea, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: You bastard.","└ It’s basically a real-life loot box, lmao.","Ash had initially thought he was pretending, but it seemed he was genuinely surviving in the wilderness.","Adventurers who wandered the world occasionally posted on the gallery.","But none of them did so completely unequipped like Wild Grylls.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Since there are no torches, it probably isn’t a dungeon! Still, you should throw a rock inside just in case!","└ Wild Grylls: What if a monster comes out?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Then you fight it!","└ Wild Grylls: The head admin says anything she wants because she’s strong. ;; Fine, I’ll try it.","Five minutes passed.","Title: This Cave Belongs to Me Now","Wild Grylls","(A picture of the surprisingly comfortable cave interior and a thumbs-up.)","I can do whatever I want with it.","└ Was there nothing inside?","└ Wild Grylls: Nope. It’s a little damp, though.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Be careful! The owner may return later!","└ Wild Grylls: I’m tired, so I’m going to sleep for now.","Ash was not quite sure what to make of him.","If Wild Grylls needed something, she could give it to him then.","Afterward, he appeared to have genuinely fallen asleep, because he stopped posting.","Ash continued browsing the gallery.","Even though it was nighttime where Wild Grylls was, it was still daytime in the Empire.","She had plenty of energy left.","Eventually, the sun began to set, and evening arrived.","It seemed he had managed to secure a cave where he could stay for at least one day.","Ash chuckled.","There was something strangely entertaining about it.","After spending every day watching idiots upload meaningless posts, this felt refreshingly different.","Still, none of it would matter if he died.","Later, she should tell him to read the survival-related posts she had uploaded.","’What sorts of things would he need to survive?’","[Someone Help Me. Urgent.]","\"Hmm?\"","A new post from Wild Grylls appeared.","Even the title looked ominous.","Ash immediately opened the post at the top of the page.","What could possibly have happened?","\"Eek?\"","She could not help crying out in shock.","Title: Someone Help Me. Urgent.","(A picture of a right arm riddled with holes and bleeding heavily.)","(A picture of the Mad Dog leader from earlier lying dead with its head severed.)","Fuck, this bastard was inside the cave. I’m losing too much blood. Can anyone help?","Wild Grylls’s right arm had been mangled.","Severely.","It was not merely punctured.","The wounds were so deep that bone was visible.","At this point, excessive blood loss was a more immediate concern than infection.","└ Put a gore warning on this.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m about to fucking die, and that’s what you care about?","└ Not my problem, lol.","└ But isn’t this actually dangerous?","An emergency had occurred."]},{"title":"Chapter 5","paragraphs":["Crisis (2)","Contrary to the notice posted by the head administrator, the gallery had a few unspoken rules.","No matter how difficult someone’s circumstances were or how pitiful their story sounded, never help them carelessly.","Even if someone was injured, never rush to help them.","The reason these rules came into existence was very simple.","Title: F king Scammer Bastard**","(Photo of a sickly young girl lying in bed)","You all know this picture, right? It’s that registered user who said his daughter had an incurable disease and begged everyone to help him.","Turns out this bastard was abusing his own daughter and deliberately starving her. ;;","Then he claimed he had no money and begged for donations, so I supported him, only to get scammed.","└ That’s roughly what happened. Hang in there.","└ Wild Grylls) Thanks for the f**king exposition, asshole.","└ Why are you making such a big deal out of this?","└ Even a potion would have trouble healing wounds that bad, wouldn’t it? There’s also a risk of infection.","└ Wild Grylls) Then what should I do?","└ Cut it off.","└ That’s f**king extreme. Lmao.","\"F**k.\"","I understood their reasoning, but it was still a shitty rule. I spat out a curse.","You could say I had let my guard down. I had been so exhausted that I closed my eyes for just a moment, and this was what happened.","Fortunately, it had bitten my arm instead of my throat. I had used that opportunity to cut the beast’s head off with my sword.","’Should I just cut it off?’","I stared at my mangled right arm. It was riddled with puncture wounds and had also been badly torn apart.","That son of a bitch had bitten down on my arm and violently shaken its head. I had barely stopped it from ripping my arm off completely.","’I need to stop the bleeding.’","I looked around the cave. Since it had been used by wild dogs, there wasn’t much inside.","There were only bones that presumably belonged to other animals. I should have seen this coming after finding those.","’Should I sell the sword for now?’","I felt truly sorry toward the Heavenly Demon, but I was in a situation where I might have to sell the sword and use the money to obtain medicine.","My life was in immediate danger. The gallery didn’t seem willing to help me, either.","Identifying myself? Who would believe me if I said I came from another world? They would just treat me like a lunatic.","For now, making a trade was my best option. Suppressing the burning pain in my arm, I searched through the comments.","’Let’s find a registered user first. Who should I choose...?’","[SwordMaster has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","It happened while I was hesitating and dripping with cold sweat. A trade request suddenly appeared.","It came from the registered user who constantly gave bizarre advice and was also an industrious madman.","For a moment, I wondered why this person was helping me. Then another wave of pain surged through my right arm, and I hurriedly accepted.","[SwordMaster: You’re the person who injured their arm, right?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes.]","[SwordMaster: I’ll give you a potion. Apply it to the wound and you should be fine.]","[SwordMaster has registered an item for trade.]","[SwordMaster: You don’t have to give me anything in return, so hurry up and take it.]","A wingless angel was right here!","After a brief moment of emotion, I immediately completed the trade.","I closed the gallery and looked at the ground. Whenever a trade was completed, the item would usually appear on the floor.","’...What is this?’","I blinked.","Inside a small cylindrical glass bottle was a liquid that glowed golden.","At least it definitely wasn’t anything strange. It didn’t sparkle like starlight, for one thing.","Before I could even wonder what it was, I picked up the bottle.","With one arm ruined, even removing the cap was an ordeal.","Splash—","\"Aaaaaaargh...!\"","Even though I had taken a deep breath before pouring it on, it stung like hell. Tears instantly welled up in my eyes.","You might say that a grown man shouldn’t scream over something like this, but fuck, it hurt so badly I thought I was going to die.","It was roughly five times more painful than applying cauterizing medicine to a mouth ulcer. The injured area was much larger, too.","\"Ughhh... Oh, ooh?!\"","Still, its effectiveness was equal to or perhaps even greater than that medicine.","In other words, it healed quickly. The puncture wounds riddling my arm closed in an instant.","I hadn’t been able to completely wash away the blood, but I could clean it later.","\"Whoa...\"","I moved my restored right arm around in every direction. It had healed perfectly.","Not only had it recovered, but it even felt sturdier than before. I could only describe it as a miracle.","After a brief moment of amazement, I immediately connected to the gallery again.","Title: Is SwordMaster a God?","(Photo of an unharmed right arm)","(Photo of a glass bottle containing golden liquid)","Is SwordMaster a god? Is SwordMaster a god? Is SwordMaster a god? Is SwordMaster a god?","I would like to express my gratitude to Lord SwordMaster for granting me a new arm. By the way, what is this yellow liquid?","└ Oh? Your arm is completely healed? Lmao.","└ I was about to give you something too. Too bad.","└ Bullshit. Lmao.","└ What the hell did he give you to completely heal an arm that had been torn apart?","I stared at the golden liquid remaining in the bottle. About one-third of it was left. I had saved it just in case.","└ SwordMaster) It’s nothing special. I just received it as a gift from my boss, I guess? I have plenty at home.","└ Wild Grylls) So what’s it called?","└ SwordMaster) An elixir. Oh, and since there’s still a risk of infection, you should drink the rest.","└ Wild Grylls) Yes, sir!","Following SwordMaster’s advice, I drank everything that remained.","It had a strangely familiar taste, with a fizzy sensation like carbonation.","You know that orange-flavored medicine you used to drink whenever you got sick as a child? It tasted similar to that.","└ An elixir? You gave him an elixir?","└ Come on, don’t bullshit us. Why would you give him that?","└ An elixir really was the only solution, though.","└ Just how rich is this guy? He received that as a gift from his boss?","Good point. I was curious about that too.","The gallery’s reaction was strange. Everyone was losing their minds over it.","Puzzled, I posted another question.","└ Wild Grylls) I’m kind of an idiot, so is an elixir expensive?","└ Of course it’s expensive. ;;","└ Even the lowest-grade elixir costs about as much as one month of living expenses for an ordinary family.","└ Wild Grylls) I don’t know how much that is.","└ He really was an idiot.","└ Lmaoooo.","└ Wild Grylls) Excuse me, but is there anything I can do for you?","└ SwordMaster) Become strong and marry me.","└ Wild Grylls) Wha...?","└ Lmaoooo, look how flustered he is.","└ This bastard proposes to everyone who shows even the slightest potential. Lmao.","Ah, right.","SwordMaster wasn’t exactly a normal person either.","I suddenly felt strangely deflated.","At least I understood that elixirs were expensive. They weren’t all absurdly costly simply because they were called elixirs, though. Apparently, their value depended on the ingredients.","The better the ingredients were, the more intense the golden glow became, but I didn’t really understand any of that.","There was only one thing I knew for certain.","I owed SwordMaster my life.","He wanted to repay the favor somehow.","’I should be the one receiving help right now, not repaying anyone...’","Still, I should at least leave a comment. The least I could do was express my gratitude.","└ SwordMaster) I was kidding. Just read my posts from the beginning. They’ll help you.","└ I don’t know about anything else, but this guy’s posts are genuinely useful. Read them no matter what.","└ Seriously, they’re top-tier.","└ The Empire’s in tears. Lmao.","\"Are they really that good?\"","Since I still didn’t understand how this world worked, it didn’t really sink in.","Even so, I owed him a debt of gratitude, so it was only right to do as he asked. It would be rude not to.","Besides, the only weapon I had was a sword. If I wanted to make proper use of it, reading his posts was probably a good idea.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) Ah...! It looks like everything got resolved while I was asleep! That’s a relief!","└ The sucker has arrived!","└ Oh, the sucker’s here.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) I’ll delete the post with your injury in a minute! It was way too gruesome!","Just as things had finally settled down, the head admin appeared. Everyone immediately started teasing them, calling them a sucker.","Wondering why they kept calling the admin that, I tilted my head. Another user quickly explained.","└ Grylls, whatever you do, don’t take advantage of the head admin.","└ Wild Grylls) Why? What happened?","└ They can’t say no whenever someone asks for help. They’ll agree to anything like a complete pushover.","└ Didn’t they once give away their entire fortune because of that?","└ Though, to be fair, their entire fortune was only ten gold. Lmao.","\"So they really are a pushover.\"","They were genuinely too kind. Now I understood.","Of course, that didn’t mean I was going to ask the head admin for anything.","Even if I did, I’d make it a fair trade. I had a conscience too.","’If I find any medicinal herbs later, I’ll give them to SwordMaster.’","For now, it was time to clean up.","I dragged away the dog’s corpse, which was still bleeding warmly.","The smell of blood might attract other beasts, so I also needed to block the cave entrance.","’I’ll stay here until the Heavenly Demon comes back with the rest.’","After carrying the corpse a fair distance away, I gathered nearby rocks and sealed the entrance.","Once I finished cleaning up, I opened my bundle of provisions.","It was the same food I’d eaten before going to sleep.","\"No matter how I look at it, this thing looks exactly like a rice ball.\"","The size certainly matched one.","The taste didn’t.","I shoved the rice-ball-sized lump into my mouth and forced myself to chew while making the ugliest face imaginable.","Did the Heavenly Demon really consider this food?","The sharp aroma of medicinal herbs pierced my nose.","And the taste?","Absolutely awful.","Bitter beyond belief.","There wasn’t even the slightest hint of sweetness.","\"Well... at least it’s food.\"","I’d have to ask the Heavenly Demon later.","Just what the hell had he made this out of for it to taste this terrible?","Strangely enough, it didn’t make my throat feel dry.","It was simply unbelievably disgusting.","After finishing the entire thing, I leaned back against the cave wall.","Way too much had happened today.","\"At least now I know this isn’t a dream.\"","What had I possibly done to wake up in a place like this?","And what was this gallery, anyway?","The sudden wave of reality almost made me cry, but I held it back.","First, I needed to figure out what kind of world this was.","Which meant I had to log back into the gallery.","Right now, the gallery was the only thing I could rely on.","[A Ridiculously Hot Demi-Human Big Sister Photo] [Image]","\"...\"","That was the very first post waiting for me.","I froze.","Then, out of pure reflex, I looked around to make sure nobody was nearby.","Even though I already knew I was alone.","\"Hmm... it’s the top post, so...\"","After successfully convincing myself with some shameless mental gymnastics, I clicked on it.","\"GYAAAAAH!!!\"","I suffered severe internal damage.","***","Title: You Crazy Bastards","Wild Grylls","Where the hell did you freaks even get a picture like that? Are you all insane?!","└ Welcome. Lmaoooo.","└ Ah, another victim today.","└ So? Isn’t our dwarf big sister gorgeous? Give us your review.","└ Wild Grylls) Shut the hell up.","└ Isn’t this the registered user who posted earlier saying his arm was ruined?","└ His arm’s already healed and he’s back to work. Lmao.","└ Naturally. A man can’t skip his daily routine. Lmao.","└ Men truly live tragic lives.","As expected...","This gallery really was a gathering place for lunatics.","***","\"Looks like he’s fine after all.\"","Ash smiled as she watched Wild Grylls completely lose his mind after opening the post.","The elixir she had given him was one of the many gifts bestowed upon her by the Emperor.","She couldn’t even remember when she’d received it.","Besides, she had enough elixirs to practically trip over them.","If she ever ran out, she could simply ask the Emperor for more.","\"I wonder how the Heavenly Demon will react?\"","More than anything else, she was curious about his reaction.","The injury photo Wild Grylls had uploaded had already been deleted by the head admin.","From the Heavenly Demon’s perspective, the whole situation would be incredibly confusing.","’What on earth happened for Grylls to suddenly start praising me?’","That was probably what he’d be wondering.","\"An ordinary person? Don’t make me laugh.\"","Ash snorted.","Wild Grylls was far too skilled in a fight to be called ordinary.","If he had really been just a normal civilian, Mad Dog would have killed him without him putting up even the slightest resistance.","Instead, he had sacrificed one arm to launch a counterattack.","He had potential.","\"And he’s entertaining.\"","The more support she gave him, the more noticeably he grew.","That said, he wasn’t the type to simply accept handouts over and over again.","He always tried to repay what he’d received somehow.","It was... admirable.","Smiling with her trademark broad grin, Ash focused on the gallery once more.","Maybe Wild Grylls needed something.","Or perhaps he had another question.","Watching him had become a new source of amusement.","[Guys, I’m Screwed.] [0]","\"There it is!\"","What was he asking this time?","Ash immediately clicked on the post.","She had no idea what kind of disaster had happened now, but checking came first.","***","Title: Guys, I’m Screwed","Wild Grylls","I need to take a dump, but I don’t have any toilet paper.","I’m screwed.","└ Can’t you just use leaves?","└ Wild Grylls) I’m worried I’ll get a rash from poisonous plants. ;;","└ Then wipe with the monster you just killed. Skin it with your sword.","└ Wild Grylls) Oh! G-good idea.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) No! If you wipe yourself with Mad Dog hide, bacteria could infect you!","└ How does the mod even know that?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) U-Um...?","└ Wild Grylls) Then what the hell am I supposed to do?","Wild Grylls had encountered an entirely different kind of life-threatening crisis.","Just as he was about to sacrifice his pants...","\"He’s just as much of an idiot.\"","Ash couldn’t help letting out a laugh.","\"Should I wipe with my pants? It’s not like there’s anyone else here anyway. Dear God... please.\"","But for Wild Grylls, who had been dropped into the wilderness with nothing, this was a genuinely serious problem.","He couldn’t exactly relieve himself inside the cave.","Even if he did, cleaning it up afterward would be a nightmare.","Right now, collective wisdom was his only hope.","The situation was so urgent that he couldn’t even think straight.","└ PassingDwarf) I’ve got a pair of ripped underwear. Want it?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah, yeah! Hurry up and send it!","└ PassingDwarf) Just so you know, I’m a guy.","└ Wild Grylls) I don’t care! It’s an emergency, damn it!","└ This guy’s the real deal. Lmao.","└ PassingDwarf) You actually sound serious, so I just sent you some toilet paper instead.","└ Wild Grylls) Oh, thank God! Thank you so much!","└ Lmaoooo. What kind of religion is that?","└ Wild Grylls) Anyone who helps someone in an emergency is basically a god.","└ That’s the dumbest thing I’ve heard... but you’re not wrong.","Thanks to PassingDwarf’s toilet paper, the crisis was finally resolved.","It had been a ridiculous commotion, but the gallery users all came to realize one thing after witnessing Wild Grylls’ desperate situation.","└ Grylls really has absolutely nothing, huh? His life’s insanely chaotic.","└ At least he’s not like those scammer bastards.","└ Poor guy. Lmao.","At the very least...","Everyone now knew he wasn’t a scammer."]},{"title":"Chapter 6","paragraphs":["The Forest of Four Seasons (1)","Human Park Jong-hyeok.","He had overcome the greatest crisis of his life.","Thanks to PassingDwarf, I had managed to survive the emergency, but the problem still wasn’t completely resolved.","I had no idea what effect those Cocoa Puffs had on me, but my stomach kept hurting.","And it was definitely the kind of stomachache that meant I needed to take a dump.","’There’s no way the Heavenly Demon gave me something spoiled.’","It might have tasted bitter, but there had been no sour or rotten smell, so it definitely hadn’t gone bad.","My body probably just couldn’t handle it.","Besides, feces were nothing more than bodily waste, so it didn’t mean there was anything seriously wrong with me.","The real problem would be if nothing came out at all.","That would mean I hadn’t eaten anything.","It wasn’t diarrhea either, so there was no immediate danger of dehydration.","For now, I could dismiss it as a minor incident.","’I guess I should wait until the Heavenly Demon gives me the other supplies.’","I stored the toilet paper I had received from PassingDwarf in a corner.","Even the toilet paper was different from what I knew.","Its texture was somewhat rough, and it wasn’t very absorbent, so cleaning myself had been difficult.","Still, having some was far better than having none.","Toilet paper could be used for all kinds of things.","’More importantly, where the hell am I?’","I didn’t mean the forest.","I meant this world.","There was no internet, yet somehow the gallery existed.","It even floated in front of me like a status window, so I had countless questions.","After wondering what I should investigate first, I decided to begin with the structure of this world.","There seemed to be many different races, so it would be best to learn about them in advance.","’The races are roughly divided into humans, elves, dark elves, beastfolk, demons, and dwarves.’","There were four human nations, one nation where the races were evenly mixed, and one nation belonging to each of the remaining races.","There were also regions that weren’t recognized as proper nations.","Most of those were inhabited by humans.","I wondered why humans were the most numerous, but I could learn that gradually.","For now, obtaining basic common knowledge was more urgent than learning every detail.","That way, people wouldn’t treat me like a lunatic when I finally went outside.","***","Title: Listen Up, Knife-Ears","Fucking stop cutting down trees and planting new ones wherever you want. You’re only making things harder for the rest of us.","└ LetUsGrowTrees) Why? If there are more trees in the world, wouldn’t that mean more resources for everyone?","└ You bastards dig up all our trees and then plant your own.","└ Then you claim those trees belong to you and insist the land is yours too—","└ Average knife-ear behavior. Lmao.","└ LetUsGrowTrees) We don’t plant them indiscriminately. We only plant them on suitable land! It’s even depicted in the World Tree’s watermelon diagram.","└ Won’t someone kill this knife-ear bastard? Is persuasion impossible?","└ Nope. The Elf Queen is insane too, so there’s no reasoning with her.","└ Isn’t this going to cause an actual war eventually?","└ The Elf Queen may be insane, but she still has enough sense to know exactly how far she can push things. Lmao.","What surprised me was how elves were treated.","The elves I knew were a proud race that loved nature.","But judging by how the gallery viewed them...","They had practically been branded as the most hated race in the world.","***","Title: Typical Knife-Ears","In the past, they kept bragging about being superior until the other races beat the shit out of them.","After losing, they tried scheming behind everyone’s backs and got beaten again.","Now they secretly plant trees on other people’s land, get caught, and get beaten again.","Do these bastards have no ability to learn?","└ Watch your mouth. We once fought against the entire world.","└ And you lost to the humans, didn’t you? Want to lose again?","└ LetUsGrowTrees) We have no intention of fighting. We are a race that loves peace.","└ Bullshit. Then why do you throw tantrums over territory?","└ LetUsGrowTrees) Because those lands originally belonged to us elves. Isn’t it only natural that we reclaim them?","└ Hahaha. Lmao.","└ From their perspective, that actually makes sense. They’re a long-lived race.","└ For humans, it would probably be the equivalent of something that happened ten years ago.","└ The young ones these days... keep causing trouble... I am truly sorry...","└ Goodness, elder. You must be having a hard time.","└ I heard the Grand Council suffers because of the Elf Queen. Lmaoooo.","└ Shouldn’t it normally be the other way around?","└ The Queen is just that much of a lunatic. ;;","└ Ordinary madness is meaningless before true madness.","Hmm...","I decided to move on.","Even after leaving the forest, I should avoid getting involved with elves whenever possible.","The registered user named LetUsGrowTrees appeared frequently in posts related to elves.","Judging by how many people recognized them, they seemed to be a famous user like the Heavenly Demon or SwordMaster.","However, because they had accumulated so much dislike, they rarely received a positive response.","’That should be enough for now. Should I check the swordsmanship posts?’","Since survival was my priority, I should only spend a little time studying common knowledge.","However, I couldn’t wander around recklessly before obtaining a compass either.","I opened the post written by SwordMaster.","It was the introductory section on basic swordsmanship.","***","Title: You Can Do It Too! Basic Swordsmanship Lecture 1","SwordMaster","Before getting to the main point, anyone who still doesn’t know how to fight properly should carry a shield along with their sword.","I recommend learning how to fight first before devoting yourself to swordsmanship.","You think a shield looks uncool?","Keep acting recklessly and you might end up dying a stupid death.","Right now, you’re a pathetic weakling who doesn’t know anything, so shut up and carry a shield.","Also, anyone who cannot use mana should first learn a mana cultivation method.","***","One good thing about the gallery was that I could use it to tell the time.","Since new posts constantly appeared, it was easy to estimate how much time had passed.","There were simply far too many of them.","Even while posts came flooding in like a tidal wave, it was strange that my own posts never seemed to get buried.","Everything was fine, except for one problem.","How the hell was I supposed to learn a mana cultivation method?","I blinked.","I already knew that mana existed in this world and that people could become stronger through it.","But that was all.","I had no idea where I could obtain a mana cultivation method.","’Even the popular posts are filled with nothing but weird garbage...’","I scratched my head.","The gallery was useful, but it was far too disorganized.","Other than popular posts, the auction house, and the marketplace, nothing was properly categorized.","It seemed I would have to find someone like SwordMaster and ask directly.","Searching through the gallery myself was far too inefficient.","’There are about thirty minutes left before I can trade with the Heavenly Demon again.’","***","Title: Does Anyone Know How Mana Cultivation Works?","Wild Grylls","’Maybe it’s because I’m a registered user?’","That thought occurred to me after posting the question.","Anonymous users vastly outnumbered registered users.","Registered users were an insignificant minority.","Then again, anonymity was important in a gallery.","By using a fixed username, they had already abandoned half of that anonymity.","If their true identity were ever exposed, they would instantly create enough embarrassing history to last a lifetime.","While I was distracted by those thoughts, an alert sounded.","Someone had left a comment.","I checked it immediately.","It was the Heavenly Demon.","└ Heavenly Demon) A mana cultivation method would be the same as an internal energy cultivation technique in the Central Plains, would it not?","└ Yeah, that’s right.","└ Heavenly Demon) In that case, this lady shall teach you.","└ How good is the mana cultivation method you know?","└ Heavenly Demon) It is a cultivation technique capable of shattering the heavens and making the earth tremble.","└ Lmaoooo. Look how grandiose that sounds.","└ This reeks of a scam. Lmao.","I wasn’t so sure.","At the very least, I didn’t think she was lying.","The reason was the sword.","Before coming here, the only sword I had ever held was a bamboo sword during kendo practice.","Even so, I could tell that the sword given to me by the Heavenly Demon was terrifyingly powerful.","There was a high chance that the Heavenly Demon was also a superhuman worthy of possessing such a weapon.","Ironically, that was precisely why I hesitated to learn from her.","└ Wild Grylls) I feel like I’m receiving too much from you already, so it’s okay.","└ Heavenly Demon) You are this lady’s benefactor and a fortuitous encounter. Please allow this lady to repay the favor.","└ Wild Grylls) I only need a compass and something to start a fire...","└ Heavenly Demon) That will not be nearly enough.","Now I felt even more guilty.","I had only found that Moonlight Spirit Herb or whatever it was by coincidence.","I hadn’t even known whether the Heavenly Demon had truly been in danger.","One coincidence had simply piled on top of another, so I couldn’t help hesitating.","’...No. What am I thinking in my current situation?’","I should accept her kindness as far as my conscience allowed.","Still, I shouldn’t take advantage of her generosity.","I had a conscience, and I planned to repay her however I could.","I typed an affirmative response.","└ Wild Grylls) All right. But please write it in a private post. It might attract unnecessary attention otherwise.","└ Heavenly Demon) Very well. First, assume the lotus position.","The lotus position?","I tilted my head.","I vaguely recognized it as a term that might appear in a martial arts novel.","That was the extent of my knowledge.","└ Wild Grylls) What’s the lotus position?","└ Heavenly Demon) ?","└ Lmaoooo. She’s flustered.","└ Isn’t this the first time we’ve ever seen that old fossil get confused? Lmao.","In the end, we decided that I would learn the mana cultivation method later.","Even the Heavenly Demon seemed too bewildered to continue.","I asked in the comments whether the lotus position was absolutely necessary for mana cultivation.","Most of the replies only made fun of me.","After a moment of confusion, I searched for it in the gallery.","Apparently, the posture was common enough that there were even photographs demonstrating it.","I opened a random post and tried to imitate the position.","I was supposed to place my feet on top of my thighs.","\"Aaaaaagh!\"","A girlish scream burst from my mouth.","I hurriedly tried to untangle my legs, but only twisted them further and nearly burst into tears.","It felt as though every joint in my legs was being wrenched out of place.","Collapsed on the ground, I trembled violently.","Was the lotus position truly mandatory?","I would have to ask the Heavenly Demon.","└ It’s just the standard procedure.","└ Wild Grylls) Standard procedure?","└ You do it even if you don’t know why. Lmao.","└ Wild Grylls) ;;","└ Wild Grylls) Heavenly Demon, do I really have to sit in the lotus position? It hurts like hell. ;;","└ Heavenly Demon) Why would it hurt? This lady cannot understand.","└ It does hurt when you try it for the first time. Lmao.","└ Work on your flexibility, dude. Lmao.","Either way, it seemed I would have to practice the lotus position gradually.","Improving my flexibility in my current situation would be difficult.","Instead, I continued reading SwordMaster’s post.","Rather than wielding only a sword, I should use a shield as well.","The explanation was convincing, and it was well suited to my current circumstances, so I accepted the advice without much resistance.","’The problem is where I’m supposed to find a shield.’","Cutting down a tree and making one myself wasn’t necessarily a bad choice.","The sword was exceptionally sharp, after all.","However, with no immediate source of water, using my energy to cut down a tree would be inefficient.","’Oh, right. I should ask the Heavenly Demon whether she can give me water too. Asking for a shield would be shameless.’","At times like this, I wished the gallery had private one-on-one messages.","Apparently, the feature had once existed, but I didn’t know why it had been removed.","It was probably because users had formed cliques.","For now, I placed several of the bitter pellets on my palm.","I wanted to identify their purpose first.","└ So she really was an old fossil. Lmao.","It seemed I should speak to her more respectfully.","At the very least, she appeared to be older than me.","The Heavenly Demon herself didn’t seem particularly bothered, but there was no harm in earning her goodwill.","***","Title: Heavenly Demon, What Are These Things You Gave Me Earlier?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of several pellets resting on a palm)","Putting aside how terrible they taste, I hope this isn’t rude, but they haven’t gone bad, right?","└ Heavenly Demon) They are fasting pills. They are somewhat bitter, but they have not spoiled.","└ Wild Grylls) They’re way more than somewhat bitter.","└ Heavenly Demon) Hmm. They suited this lady’s palate.","└ Grandma taste buds. ;;","└ Excuse me, but how old are you?","└ Heavenly Demon) I do not know. Age is unimportant anyway, is it not?","└ Old people always answer like that.","└ Wild Grylls) How many of these should I eat each day?","└ Heavenly Demon) As far as this lady knows, one is normally consumed per meal.","\"Eh?\"","I had eaten an entire handful at once.","There wouldn’t be any side effects, would there?","└ Wild Grylls) I ate a lot of them... There aren’t any side effects, right?","└ Heavenly Demon) This lady shall ask and return.","└ Your dick is going to explode now. Lmao.","└ Boom. Lmao.","└ Wild Grylls) Don’t say things like that, even as a joke.","I was genuinely afraid it might happen.","My body had already begun to feel strangely energized.","You might think having more strength was a good thing, but the problem was that it was excessive.","My body felt hot enough for me to notice.","If I became sick in this situation, it would be disastrous.","I desperately prayed that nothing would happen.","After some time passed, the Heavenly Demon returned.","└ Heavenly Demon) I asked one of my close aides. There are no side effects. On the contrary, they are beneficial to the body. In particular, they are said to remove accumulated impurities.","└ Wild Grylls) Impurities?","└ Heavenly Demon) In ordinary people such as yourself, they are usually expelled as feces.","└ Wild Grylls) What about the sudden surge of strength?","└ Heavenly Demon) They possess effects similar to a medicinal elixir, so that is only natural.","What a relief.","So there was no chance of my Big Johnson exploding.","I breathed a sigh of relief and rubbed my chest. Apparently, the heat spreading through my body was also a sign that I was absorbing the energy.","The fasting pills were a type of emergency ration, but they were extremely suitable for my current situation.","’She said one was the minimum, so I’ll have to eat more if I want enough nutrients.’","Either way, I had no choice but to keep eating these horribly bitter pellets.","I wasn’t in any condition to hunt right now.","Even if I successfully hunted something, meat alone wouldn’t provide every nutrient I needed.","└ You expect us to believe those tiny pellets have effects comparable to an elixir? What a joke. Lmao.","└ Heavenly Demon) They were specially made for this lady’s training, so that is only natural.","└ Then make one for me too.","└ Heavenly Demon) This lady shall make you a strangely shaped fasting pill. 凸","Considering the sword and the quality of the food she ate, the Heavenly Demon was clearly someone of high status.","Then why was someone like her using the gallery?","Well, regardless of the reason, she had helped me enormously.","Without her, I would probably have died already.","While browsing the gallery, a good idea suddenly occurred to me, so I posted another question.","***","Title: How Much Is a Mad Dog Corpse Worth?","Wild Grylls","Could I buy at least one crappy shield with it?","└ You could probably get a used shield.","└ Wild Grylls) A new one would be too much, right?","└ Yeah. Mad Dog hide isn’t particularly valuable.","└ Wild Grylls) Roughly how much is it worth? I want to trade it for something.","└ Just put it up at the auction house.","└ Wild Grylls) I don’t need money. It’s annoying to carry around.","└ Ah, right. You’re a newbie. You don’t need to carry it. Items can be stored directly inside the gallery.","Still, considering the gallery had saved one person’s life and allowed them to form a valuable connection, the flaws were understandable.","Besides, because of the terrifying transaction fees, plenty of users preferred direct trades over the auction house.","Stored inside the gallery?","After reading the reply, I investigated the system in more detail.","Apparently, users could deposit physical currency directly into the gallery, and it would be categorized according to each nation’s currency.","Exchange rates were applied automatically.","The greatest drawback, however, was the transaction fee.","The fees were far more brutal than those of an ordinary auction house, so the system wasn’t entirely convenient.","Nevertheless, its overwhelming advantage was that it completely ignored normal distribution and transportation.","That was why so many people used it.","’Wait. Then I could’ve just listed the Moonlight Spirit Herb in the auction house?’","This was why information was important.","└ Wild Grylls) Then where do all the transaction fees go? To the head admin?","└ Yeah. The auction house and everything else are managed by the head admin. But for some reason, the head admin is always broke.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) The fees are donated to the underprivileged or used to improve the gallery!","The head admin, who had remained silent until then, suddenly appeared.","Their answer practically radiated kindness.","└ Head admin... I’m underprivileged too... Could you give me ten thousand gold...?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) Ah...! I don’t have any money right now...!","└ Don’t fucking give it to him.","└ This is exactly why we need a deputy admin. Why won’t the mod appoint one?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) It’s better if I handle all the difficult work myself! Deputy admins don’t get paid!","Just how many times had the head admin been stabbed in the back for even the anonymous users to stop them?","Most replies to the anonymous user pretending to be poor warned the head admin not to give them anything, even as a joke.","It was clear that public opinion toward the head admin was extremely positive.","More importantly, how was a head admin chosen in the first place?","’I can figure that out later.’","For now, I needed to put the Mad Dog corpse up for auction.","I left the cave.","I had dumped the corpse a considerable distance away.","Since I had memorized the route, there shouldn’t have been any problems.","\"Chomp. Chomp. Munch, munch.\"","\"...\"","\"Crunch! Crack!\"","Correction.","There was a problem.","Something was enjoying the Mad Dog corpse as though it were filming a gourmet eating show.","A bear.","No, an owl.","Its face clearly belonged to an owl, but its body was larger than a bear’s.","I hurriedly took a picture and uploaded it.","***","Title: What the Hell Is This Thing?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of something happily devouring the Mad Dog corpse)","I came back to retrieve the Mad Dog’s corpse, but this fat bastard is eating it.","Does anyone know what this thing is?","└ Fuck, that’s an owlbear.","└ Forget that it’s an owlbear. Why is it so huge?","└ Fucking hell. That house is walking around. Lmaoooo.","└ One hit from those claws and you’re dead.","So that was an owlbear.","The moment I learned what it was, I slowly began backing away.","Was this what people meant by doing all the work only for someone else to reap the reward?","At least I had survived, so I supposed I should be grateful.","’Fuck. I need to get out of here quickly.’","Wild dogs were one thing.","A bear was something else entirely.","And its size was absurd.","I slowly retreated until I had put enough distance between us, then sprinted back toward the cave.","What would have happened if I had arrived a little earlier?","Just imagining it made my blood run cold.","’What should I do? Should I defend myself from inside the cave?’","Unknown dangers lurked outside, but remaining inside the cave was also frightening because of the owlbear.","I had barely escaped the greatest crisis of my life, only for another one to appear.","The only thing I could rely on was the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","[The Heavenly Demon has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","While I was trembling with anxiety, the Heavenly Demon sent me a trade request.","Considering the time, it made sense.","I hurriedly accepted her proposal.","At the same time, the familiar empty trade window appeared.","[The Heavenly Demon has registered items for trade.]","[Heavenly Demon: These are the compass and ignition stone you requested. The ignition stone can be recharged using internal energy.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. But I don’t know how to use internal energy. Do you have anything else?]","[Heavenly Demon: Hmm? If you cannot use internal energy, how are you accessing the gallery? The matter of the lotus position was strange as well.]","Judging by what she said, one apparently needed to know how to use internal energy—or mana—to access the gallery.","I couldn’t explain it properly either.","The moment I opened my eyes in this world, all kinds of bizarre phenomena had simply started happening.","Explaining every detail would be difficult, so I answered as briefly as possible.","[Wild Grylls: It’s difficult to explain my circumstances in detail. I’m also short on time.]","[Heavenly Demon: Hmm. Very well. In any case, pressing the button on the ignition stone will produce a flame, so you should still be able to use it. Do you require anything else?]","[Wild Grylls: I’m sorry to ask, but could you give me a little water as well...?]","[Heavenly Demon: If it is your request, then gladly.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh! Thank you!]","I thanked the Heavenly Demon and accepted the trade items.","The relief supplies appeared on the ground.","There was a compass, an ignition stone, and a large water bottle.","Every item had a distinctly Eastern design.","I examined the ignition stone first.","\"The button is... here.\"","Whoosh!","When I pressed it, a small flame appeared along its edge.","This was more than enough.","Next came the compass.","With a compass, escaping the forest would become much easier.","The reason people became lost in forests was because they couldn’t maintain a sense of direction.","With this one item, everything would be—","\"Huh?\"","Before I could finish the thought, confusion escaped my mouth.","My eyes widened.","A compass needle should normally settle in one fixed direction.","This one didn’t.","It spun around and around without stopping.","Had the Heavenly Demon given me a broken compass?","Slightly flustered, I posted on the gallery.","***","Title: Heavenly Demon, I Think the Compass Is Broken","Wild Grylls","(Video of a compass needle spinning helplessly after losing all sense of direction)","The needle keeps spinning around. Why is it doing this...?","I think you gave me a broken one.","└ Heavenly Demon) Hmm? That should not be possible. It was functioning properly when this lady sent it.","Why had a perfectly functional compass suddenly started behaving like this?","This only made my situation more difficult.","└ Maybe something went wrong during the trade?","└ No, that probably isn’t it. Trading works more like teleportation.","└ Compasses don’t normally break without warning.","└ It’s spinning pretty well.","└ Just like your life?","└ Lmao.","The other users were equally confused.","Why would a compass that had been working perfectly suddenly behave like that?","Of course, it was possible that an unlikely coincidence had caused it to break immediately after the trade.","I needed another one to confirm it.","└ Wild Grylls) Can someone lend me a compass? I’ll return it as soon as the trade cooldown ends.","└ StarlightPrincess) I’ll give you one.","└ SpeargirlPrincess) I’ll give you one too!","└ PraiseTheSun) Me too.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) I’d like to give you one as well, but I’m sad to say I don’t have any.","Perhaps they sensed that something unusual was happening.","Several registered users who rarely commented appeared all at once.","It seemed I had captured their interest in only a short time.","The Moonlight Spirit Herb had probably played a large role in that.","Thanks to them, I obtained compasses of all kinds.","They were surprisingly varied.","***","Title: Fuck, They’re All Doing the Same Thing","Wild Grylls","(Video of several compass needles spinning in circles)","They’ve all completely lost their sense of direction like a bunch of outsiders.","Why the hell is this happening?","└ Heavenly Demon) How strange.","└ SwordMaster) That is strange.","└ SpeargirlPrincess) That’s strange.","└ PassingDwarf) What’s wrong with those things? Did you pour alcohol on the compasses?","└ Wild Grylls) Fuck off.","└ There is exactly one situation where something like this can happen.","└ What is it?","└ When you enter the Forest of Four Seasons. I heard both magnetism and mana are distorted there, so compasses don’t work.","└ Bullshit. If that were true, he wouldn’t be able to access the gallery either.","└ Still, the Forest of Four Seasons is the only explanation, isn’t it?","└ There’s no way every compass suddenly broke.","└ Where the hell is the original poster? Lmaoooo.","└ Got drunk and wandered into the Forest of Four Seasons. Lmaoooo.","Every compass behaved exactly the same way.","They all spun endlessly.","While everyone was trying to understand what was happening, several users began exchanging theories in the comments.","None of them sounded entirely certain.","There were two main possibilities.","The compasses were malfunctioning because I was inside the Forest of Four Seasons.","Or that was impossible, because entering the Forest of Four Seasons should have made it impossible to access the gallery.","Either way, my feelings could be summarized in a single thought.","’...I think I might be completely fucked.’","The situation was taking a very strange turn."]},{"title":"Chapter 7","paragraphs":["The Forest of Four Seasons (2)","Title: Who’s the Highest-Ranking God in This World?","Wild Grylls","└ Why do you ask?","└ Wild Grylls) So I can curse them out.","└ He just openly declared his intent to commit blasphemy. Lmao.","└ So that’s why you were dropped into the Forest of Four Seasons. Lmaoooo.","└ You’re being punished. Lmao.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) Blasphemy is bad!","It felt as though the hope I had barely managed to cling to was collapsing before my eyes.","I folded my arms and stared down at the ground.","The compasses I had received from the registered users were lined up there.","Every single needle spun around and around as if they were broken.","└ At least he’s not a scammer. He’s just a little mentally unstable.","There was no way all of them had broken at once.","The problem was most likely the place I was currently in.","’Am I really inside the Forest of Four Seasons?’","I raised my head and checked the gallery.","Word must have spread because nearly every post was about me.","Many users claimed this phenomenon would be impossible anywhere other than the Forest of Four Seasons.","However, just as many argued that I shouldn’t be able to access the gallery if I were truly there.","***","Title: What If Wild Grylls Faked Everything?","Did this bastard deliberately break all the compasses?","└ It’s \"deliberately,\" not \"on purposefully.\"","└ If he faked it, every one of his posts has been way too intense.","└ First there was a Mad Dog, then a Guardian, and then an owlbear.","└ Look at that lineup. Lmaoooo.","└ Even the owlbear was fucking enormous. There’s no way this was staged.","└ The Moonlight Spirit Herb seems real too. Look at the post the Heavenly Demon made.","I wished it were fake too.","A sigh escaped me in frustration.","Just like the compass needles spinning in circles, my thoughts felt as though they were doing the same.","In other words, I felt like I was going insane.","I had no idea what the hell I was supposed to do now.","’Still, there’s some hope left.’","It hadn’t been confirmed that this was the Forest of Four Seasons.","The world was vast, and there were probably many regions that had yet to be fully explored.","This could be one of those places.","Everyone described the Forest of Four Seasons as an utterly inhospitable realm beyond human limits.","As someone who had always lived under the protection of civilization, I needed to escape somehow.","Doing something was better than sitting still and doing nothing.","***","Title: Can Someone Tell Me the Characteristics of the Forest of Four Seasons?","Wild Grylls","└ Why do you want to know?","└ Wild Grylls) I want to check whether I’m really there.","└ It has spring, summer, autumn, and winter weather all at once.","└ More precisely, it contains every kind of climate. I heard there’s even a desert.","└ Wild Grylls) Why the fuck is there a desert inside a forest? You said it was a forest.","└ We don’t know either.","└ For reference, the Forest of Four Seasons is about the size of a small country.","└ Wild Grylls) That information is fucking useless.","└ I said it was just for reference. Lmao.","What kind of ridiculous forest was this?","For now, confirming my location came first.","Going outside was dangerous, but with the compasses useless, staying still wouldn’t accomplish anything.","It would be best to use the cave as a base and gradually expand the range of my exploration.","’I’ll need paper and a pen too.’","I intended to draw a rough map.","Even if the compass was useless, having a map would still be better than having nothing.","I could get lost halfway through and fail to find my way back.","I needed to prepare for the worst.","’I’ll do everything I can.’","I had heard that the most important thing in a survival situation was the will to live.","There were probably more cases where people gave in to despair, did nothing, and truly ended up with nothing.","Danger was everywhere, but I would have to accept some risk.","I turned and looked toward a corner of the cave.","’There probably isn’t anywhere safer than this cave right now...’","Since there was a good chance I would have to remain in this forest for several days, finding water took priority over escaping.","A person could survive for three weeks without food, but without water, they would die in three days.","Even though I could receive help through the gallery, I intended to handle whatever I could by myself.","’There might come a time when no one can help me during a real emergency.’","I had realized that after being bitten by the Mad Dog.","That time, I had safely overcome the crisis thanks to SwordMaster’s kindness.","There was no guarantee something similar wouldn’t happen again.","In fact, it was highly likely.","If I couldn’t receive help during a life-or-death moment, I would die.","’That means I need to become friendly with the registered users...’","I had no idea what any of them actually did.","I reviewed the few registered users I had formed some connection with.","The Heavenly Demon was clearly someone important.","SwordMaster was rich and a master swordsman.","PassingDwarf was a dwarf.","That was all I knew for now.","I had no idea who the registered users who gave me compasses were.","’StarlightPrincess seems like a sick person.’","I meant physically sick, not mentally.","That wasn’t what I was implying.","Since people prayed for her recovery every day, she was probably suffering from some illness.","Perhaps she had a chronic disease.","As for the others...","I couldn’t tell from their posts.","Everything was too chaotic to reach any firm conclusions.","***","Here’s My Asshole","└ Lmaoooo. Did Speargirl lose again today?","└ SpeargirlPrincess) Those motherless bitches conceded two goals in stoppage time. Haha.","└ No wonder all the lunatics started appearing.","***","Title: Asshole Reveal","SpeargirlPrincess","(Photo of an emblem bearing a deer pattern)","Or maybe not.","I made an uncomfortable expression at the outrageously explicit title.","This SpeargirlPrincess person was definitely obsessed with sports.","Among all her posts, most were related to sports.","[I want to cry. Why am I a Speargirl fan?]","[These fucking bastards. They conceded in the dumbest way possible.]","[As expected of Evers!! I knew I could trust you!]","[This is seriously fucking awful. You call that a team?]","[LiverMidTable! LiverMidTable! LiverMidTable!]","A very familiar scent drifted through this unfamiliar gallery.","Most sports had a tendency to cause mental illness.","It was a taste I knew well.","I had once been deeply addicted to both soccer and baseball, only to develop stress-induced hair loss.","After that, I attained enlightenment and recovered.","’To become friendly with this person...’","That would probably be difficult for now.","It might have been possible on Earth, but here, I didn’t even know what kinds of sports existed.","For now, I stopped investigating the personalities of the registered users.","I needed to explore the surroundings before sunset.","Holding the Heavenly Demon’s sword, I placed several fasting pills into my mouth.","The moment I bit down, bitterness spread across my tongue.","I quickly took a sip of water to wash away the taste.","I had no idea how long I would have to keep eating these things.","’All right. I’m ready.’","Before leaving the cave, I posted one more message.","I also remembered to put a handful of fasting pills into my trouser pocket, just in case.","***","Title: Preparations Complete","Wild Grylls","(Photo showing the cave entrance)","I’m going to explore and check whether this is really the Forest of Four Seasons.","└ Isn’t that too dangerous?","└ You ran into an owlbear earlier. ;;","└ The compasses are acting strangely, so exploring is probably the right choice.","└ Heavenly Demon) Be careful.","└ SwordMaster) Good luck.","└ PassingDwarf) You should’ve waited a little longer. I was going to give you a used shield.","└ Wild Grylls) Later. I’m planning to run immediately if anything dangerous happens anyway.","└ The next day, Grylls never posted again.","└ T_T","└ Wild Grylls) Fuck off.","Everyone seemed to be cheering me on.","Of course, most of those encouraging me were registered users.","The others were closer to saying, \"Why should I care?\"","A few comments went far beyond the line, but they were deleted shortly afterward.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) Severe insults and abuse directed at someone working hard to survive will result in a ban!","└ Wild Grylls) Thank you. ;;","I wasn’t sure whether this counted as working hard to live.","I had only ended up here by accident.","In any case, I had now uploaded what could potentially be my final post.","Taking a deep breath, I stepped outside the cave.","The familiar scenery greeted me.","It was a warm forest.","’At least the weather being warm is one good thing among all this misfortune.’","If it had been cold, the difficulty would have increased even further.","I looked around and began walking.","I headed in the opposite direction from where the owlbear had been eating the Mad Dog’s corpse.","To avoid getting lost, I used the sword to leave marks along the way.","’Focus on the sounds.’","The chirping of insects.","The rustling of bushes in the wind.","The distant roars of animals.","I concentrated on my hearing so I wouldn’t miss a single sound.","My heart pounded from tension.","This was an environment where a single moment of carelessness could decide whether I lived or died.","The sword was the only thing I could trust.","Rustle—","An ominous sound reached my ears, which had become hypersensitive from tension.","It came from directly above me.","I immediately snapped my head upward.","There was no time to raise it slowly.","\"HSSSSSSS!\"","A gigantic snake lunged at me with its jaws stretched wide open.","Its long, sharply protruding venomous fangs looked terrifying.","I didn’t even have time to scream.","I hurriedly twisted my face aside.","The snake’s jaws barely grazed past me.","Without wasting another moment, I swung the sword down at the snake’s body.","Thud!","\"What...?\"","Something completely unexpected happened.","This was the Heavenly Demon’s sword—the same sword that had cleanly sliced the Mad Dog in half.","Yet the blade only sank halfway into the snake before becoming lodged.","Its scales were far tougher than I had imagined.","\"HSSSSSS!\"","The venomous snake thrashed wildly in pain.","At the same time, it opened its enormous jaws and lunged at me.","It was as large as an anaconda.","If it managed to bite me even once, I was finished.","I hurriedly tried to move my right hand, only to freeze.","Squeeze!","\"Ghk?!\"","The snake had already wrapped its body around my right arm.","When the hell had it done that?","I was startled only for a moment.","Just before it could bite me, I grabbed it by the neck.","Snake scales were normally smooth and unpleasant to touch, but this one was different.","It felt like gripping a solid sheet of iron.","Squeeeeeze!","\"Agh!\"","The pressure around my right arm intensified.","But my left hand wasn’t free either.","The moment I released the snake’s neck, it would obviously bite me.","Maintaining this position was my best option.","’What should I—ah!’","Something entered my field of vision amid the chaos.","The section of the snake’s body that had been cut halfway through.","It was between the part wrapped around my right arm and the snake’s head.","I immediately slammed both arms downward as if I were swinging a jump rope.","The half-severed section dropped beneath my feet.","Now it was time to use my strength.","Stomp!","\"Huaaaaaagh!\"","\"HSSSSSSS!\"","I planted my foot on the middle of its body and pulled as though I intended to tear the half-severed section apart completely.","The snake writhed in agony, shaking its head from side to side.","Venom sprayed dangerously from its fangs.","My right arm wasn’t faring any better.","The snake tightened its grip even further, as if determined to crush the bones completely.","It had become a game of chicken to see which of us would die first.","Then I encountered an unexpected obstacle.","’Fuck! Why are these scales so damn tough?!’","This was a snake that even the Heavenly Demon’s sword had failed to cut cleanly.","Of course it was tough.","Did that mean I intended to give up?","Absolutely not.","If I wanted to survive, I had to rip this bastard in half and kill it.","Riiip! Tear!","The result of our struggle gradually began to show.","Its body started splitting apart.","The cut made by the sword slowly widened.","I pulled with every ounce of strength I had.","Since I was using both my hands and my foot, I could exert far more force.","Riiip! Riiiiiip!","At last, the long and brutal struggle came to an end.","The snake’s body tore in half.","I felt the strength rapidly drain from the severed body now that it had lost the commands from its head.","I immediately shook my right arm free.","The section wrapped around my arm fell away, and I drove the sword downward at once.","Stab!","The Heavenly Demon’s sword pierced directly through the snake’s head.","Even with a blade embedded in its skull, the snake continued to writhe.","Breathing heavily, I collapsed onto the ground.","Just in case, I didn’t pull the sword out.","I had heard somewhere that snakes were bizarre animals capable of continuing to move even after only their heads remained.","Even now, despite the sword piercing through its skull and being driven deep into the ground, it continued twitching.","What a tenacious creature.","Throb! Throb!","\"Ow...\"","I looked down at my aching right arm.","The snake’s coils had left clear marks.","There was also heavy bruising beneath the skin.","Considering my bones had nearly been crushed, it was a relatively minor injury.","’What the hell are those scales made of for them to be this tough?’","Even the Heavenly Demon’s sword had barely penetrated them.","I uploaded pictures to the gallery.","I planned to rest for about thirty seconds before continuing onward.","I had lost far too much strength.","***","Title: Even the Snakes Are Fucking Huge Here","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the snake’s head)","(Photo of the snake’s body separated from its head)","I seriously thought I was going to die.","I freaked out when the sword didn’t cut through it in one strike. ;;","└ Whoa, that’s fucking disgusting. Is it venomous?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah. It tried to kill me with its fangs at first, then wrapped itself around my right arm. I thought my bones were going to break.","└ You cut the Mad Dog in half, but couldn’t cut through some snake in one swing? How did you kill it?","└ Wild Grylls) I tore apart the section the sword had already cut. It was fucking tough, though.","└ Holy shit.","└ Doesn’t that look like a Steel-Scaled Serpent?","└ If it really is one, isn’t it insanely expensive?","└ Yeah. Both the venom and the scales should be valuable.","So this thing was called a Steel-Scaled Serpent.","It certainly lived up to its name.","I watched the comments descend into chaos again, then simply closed the gallery.","There was no point paying attention to them right now.","The snake was too large to drag back to the cave.","It would be better to list it directly in the auction house.","’I should learn from what happened with the Mad Dog.’","Without hesitation, I opened the auction house.","All kinds of items were listed there.","Occasionally, I saw strange things like an elf’s underwear or socks that hadn’t been washed for several days.","The world truly was vast, and there was no shortage of idiots and perverts.","I let out a hollow laugh.","Unlike direct trades, anyone could list items in the auction house.","That was probably why things like this appeared.","’The fee is... What the hell? Forty percent?’","So this was what people meant when they said the fees were murderous.","Even so, the auction house remained popular because of its advantage of completely bypassing transportation and distribution.","I placed my hand on the body rather than the head and registered it in the auction house.","The listing name was \"Snake I Just Killed,\" and the minimum bid was five gold.","I had been struggling with how to dispose of the corpse anyway, so I would benefit as long as someone bought it.","’At least the listing fee isn’t very high.’","The gallery had given me a small amount of money when I first created my registered account.","Thanks to that, I didn’t have to worry about being unable to afford the listing fee.","That was fortunate.","[Note: Fees may vary depending on the item’s weight.]","I didn’t care.","I completed the listing and stood up.","The snake’s body disappeared after being registered in the auction house.","Only the head remained.","The head was still moving, so I couldn’t list it.","The safest option was probably to cover it with dirt.","’This is difficult right from the start.’","Why did my life have to be so miserable?","Rubbing my still-throbbing arm, I continued onward.","I prayed that nothing else would happen.","Trickle, trickle—","Before long, I heard a sound that instantly sharpened my senses.","Running water.","Water was one of the most important resources for survival.","I hurried toward the sound.","I might be able to secure drinking water.","And if I followed the stream downstream, it might lead me out of the forest.","That was what I thought.","\"...What the hell is this?\"","At least, I would have thought so if there hadn’t been a desert on the other side of the stream.","I was more dumbfounded than alarmed.","No matter how many times I rubbed my eyes and looked again, it was unmistakably a desert.","A vast expanse of reddish sand stretched out before me.","I was clearly standing inside a forest.","So why was there a desert on the other side of a stream?","It felt as though every law of common sense was collapsing at once.","I stood there blankly for a while before opening the gallery.","***","Title: Guys, Let Me Show You Something Amazing","Wild Grylls","(Photo showing the stream and the forest)","Here we have a forest and a river!","(Photo showing a vast desert beyond the stream)","And beyond the river, we have a desert!","Think it’s fake?","(Video alternating between the forest, stream, and desert)","Wow, fuck!","Where do you think I am?","Aren’t. You. Just. Dying. To. Know?","└ Wow. That. Is. So. Amazing.","└ ??? You really were inside the Forest of Four Seasons?","└ Then how are you using the gallery?","└ Lmaoooo. This is seriously spectacular.","└ So it was real. Lmaoooo.","└ Heavenly Demon) What a beautiful place.","└ Wild Grylls) Ma’am?","└ The Heavenly Demon clearly has no idea what this place is. Lmaoooo.","└ Why does she sound like such an old person? Lmao.","└ PassingDwarf) Are you experiencing hallucinations?","└ Wild Grylls) I sobered up a long time ago. ;;","└ PassingDwarf) Drink again. Then you’ll sober up from this.","└ Fighting poison with poison. Lmao.","Not a single one of the comments was helpful.","I sighed in frustration.","\"Hah...\"","My current feelings could be summarized in a single word.","\"Fuck.\""]},{"title":"Chapter 8","paragraphs":["The Forest of Four Seasons (3)","The Continental Integrated Gallery could be accessed anytime and anywhere as long as certain conditions were met.","The first condition was that the mana in the atmosphere had to be stable.","If the atmospheric mana was unstable, accessing the gallery became difficult.","The second condition was that the user had to be capable of controlling mana at will.","This was connected to the next requirement.","The final condition was knowing the access formula.","The calculations were so simple that even a child could perform them.","Therefore, if the mana was unstable, the user couldn’t control mana, and they didn’t even know the access method, using the gallery should have been impossible.","***","Title: What If All of This Is Actually a Dream?","Wild Grylls","What if I’m actually dreaming?","Maybe the gallery and all of you are nothing more than parts of my dream.","I need to wake up soon. Lmao.","└ He’s finally lost his mind. Lmaoooo.","└ Hang in there, dude.","└ StarlightPrincess) Stay strong.","└ Damn, things must be bad if even that person is telling him to stay strong.","└ Bro, you should start over from day one of survival. Lmao.","└ SpeargirlPrincess) Are you really inside the Forest of Four Seasons? I still can’t believe it.","└ You have to believe it. There’s nowhere else like that except the Forest of Four Seasons.","└ SpeargirlPrincess) But he’s been using the gallery nonstop.","└ That’s what we’re wondering too. Lmao.","└ The common sense of this world is collapsing in real time.","└ All-Father) May I use you as research material?","└ Wild Grylls) What are you planning to do with it?","└ All-Father) I intend to write a paper.","└ Wild Grylls) Do whatever you want.","└ He’s given up. Lmaoooo.","Wild Grylls.","Every compass had malfunctioned, and now he had even provided undeniable proof that he was inside the Forest of Four Seasons.","Most of the evidence was impossible to dispute.","And yet, someone who ignored every condition required to access the gallery had appeared.","At first, everyone had assumed he was merely another ordinary registered user.","But as time passed, he gradually began attracting the gallery’s attention.","He had suddenly discovered a Moonlight Spirit Herb.","He had fought and defeated a Mad Dog.","He had even been bitten by another Mad Dog while sleeping—","***","Title: Isn’t There Something Strange About the Snake Grylls Uploaded?","Isn’t that thing actually a Steel-Scaled Serpent?","Aside from the fact that it’s fucking enormous, it looks exactly like one.","└ What’s a Steel-Scaled Serpent?","└ Exactly what the name says. It’s a snake with scales as hard as steel. Even a Sword Expert would barely be able to kill one.","└ Is it expensive?","└ If processed properly, it’s extremely useful. Think of it as fabric with the durability of iron.","└ Why is that Steel-Scaled Serpent so huge? It’s as big as an anaconda. ;;","└ How large are they normally?","└ About the size of an ordinary snake. That’s why they’re usually relatively easy to kill, but I don’t know about that monster.","└ How much would it be worth?","└ The minimum price would probably be around one hundred gold.","The snake Wild Grylls had listed in the auction house caused another major stir.","Unlike direct trading, the auction house was open to a much wider range of users.","Direct trades were restricted to registered users, but anyone could register items or place bids in the auction house.","One might ask whether that meant drugs and other dangerous goods could also be sold.","Fortunately, such trades rarely occurred, if only because of the murderous fees.","Even if someone attempted it, the head admin immediately issued a permanent ban and stopped the problem before it could spread.","└ Whoa, it passed five hundred gold.","└ What happens if it’s a scam?","└ Grylls listed it for only five gold and left, so he isn’t responsible for the bidding war.","└ Besides, who takes responsibility for something bought through an auction house? Lmao.","└ Considering the fees, he listed it absurdly cheaply.","Even while Wild Grylls was drowning in despair, the excitement surrounding the auction didn’t fade.","Since it used a bidding system rather than an instant-purchase option, it was only natural that countless users would flock to it.","The structure also encouraged fierce competition once the fees were taken into consideration.","└ Damn! It passed one thousand gold!","└ A sucker has appeared. Lmao.","└ Even that price is cheap, though. Assuming it’s genuine.","└ But is it really genuine?","└ If it turns out to be fake, people will probably go insane trying to hunt Grylls down. Lmao.","└ But Grylls is in the Forest of Four Seasons. Can anyone even catch him?","└ Good point. Lmaoooo.","└ Pleasure without responsibility. Lmao.","└ Doesn’t he have neither responsibility nor pleasure?","└ True. Lmaoooo.","└ Wild Grylls) Huh? What the hell? Why did it become so expensive? ;;","└ The man himself has appeared!","└ Grylls, is that really a Steel-Scaled Serpent?","└ Wild Grylls) How would I know? I listed it immediately because I was worried something else would eat it later.","└ Don’t tell me it was delivered straight from the wild.","└ Wild Grylls) It was still twitching until right before I put it in the auction house. Lmao.","└ Kyaaaaaaagh!","└ Gyaaaaaaagh!","From Wild Grylls’ perspective, he had only listed the snake because he wanted to dispose of it quickly.","The reaction left him bewildered.","More importantly, he couldn’t care less whether it was a Steel-Scaled Serpent or anything else.","How could he pay attention to the auction house when he didn’t even know how he was going to survive?","He felt like crying.","***","Title: Upvote If Grylls Makes You Want to Kill Yourself","I’ll start. Lmaoooo.","└ Wild Grylls) Upvoted. Lmaoooo.","└ Why is the original poster joining in? Lmaoooo.","└ I didn’t think he’d actually appear.","└ Grylls must be completely broken. Lmao.","Of course his mind was breaking.","Every hope he had of escaping had vanished.","Getting lost in an ordinary forest was already life-threatening.","This was the Forest of Four Seasons, a place described as a hellscape beyond human limits.","Compasses didn’t work, and even space itself was distorted.","His chances of survival were already extremely low.","***","Title: Where Is Grylls Originally From?","Now that I think about it, I’m curious.","What the hell did he do to end up inside the Forest of Four Seasons?","└ Wild Grylls) I’m originally from Earth. I drank alcohol, woke up, and found myself here.","└ Where is Earth? I’ve never heard of it.","└ Wild Grylls) Another world.","└ ...?","└ You didn’t enter the forest because you developed a mental illness, did you?","└ Another world. Lmaoooo.","└ Does that world have a gallery too?","└ Wild Grylls) It does. The galleries are more specialized, though.","└ Oh! Are you interested in becoming a deputy admin?","└ Wild Grylls) What’s a deputy admin? Do they do the same work as the head admin?","└ Yeah, except they have less authority and don’t get paid. Lmao.","└ Wild Grylls) Fuck no.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) I can handle all the difficult work by myself!","Perhaps his mind had truly snapped, because Wild Grylls answered every question with complete sincerity.","He began with the claim that he came from another world, then proceeded to talk about that world.","Of course, the gallery users didn’t seem to believe him.","They simply treated him like a lunatic.","└ SwordMaster) So that was your character concept. Understood.","└ Wild Grylls) It’s not a character concept. ;;","└ SwordMaster) Who would believe that a single bomb could destroy an entire city?","└ Wild Grylls) I find it harder to believe that a person can destroy a mountain.","└ Heavenly Demon) This lady is capable of doing so.","└ SpeargirlPrincess) I can do it too!","└ All-Father) I am also capable of it.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) I could do it if I really exerted myself!","└ Wild Grylls) Is everyone here a monster or something? ;;","└ PassingDwarf) What you said sounds interesting. Do you know how to make one?","└ Wild Grylls) How the hell would I know that?","└ PassingDwarf) Then what can you do?","└ Wild Grylls) Eat, shit, and laze around?","└ PassingDwarf) Then just die and become fertilizer.","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah... I guess I should...","└ PassingDwarf) Ah, fuck. Sorry. Don’t actually die. I’ll send you some alcohol later.","└ Look how he panicked when Grylls sounded like he might really kill himself. Lmaoooo.","Or they assumed it was simply an elaborate character act.","From their perspective, that was only natural.","The fact that Wild Grylls had fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons and the claim that he came from another world were separate matters.","It wasn’t especially important either.","The most important issue at the moment was the Steel-Scaled Serpent listed in the auction house.","└ How did you kill that? You said you were an ordinary person.","└ Wild Grylls) The sword couldn’t cut through it, so I just tore it apart.","└ And you call that an ordinary person?","└ He’s saying he tore through a steel plate with his bare hands. Lmaoooo.","└ Wild Grylls) No, it wasn’t that extreme. The sword had already cut partway through it, so I targeted that section. It was huge, but I could still grip its neck with one hand.","└ And then you ripped it apart in that state?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah.","└ Fuck, that still doesn’t make sense.","└ Are all ordinary people in your world like that?","No matter how anyone looked at it, his answer didn’t sound like something an ordinary person could do.","Still, it wasn’t entirely impossible.","People often displayed several times their normal strength when their lives were in danger.","The gallery users could accept it as something along those lines and move on.","└ The bidding stopped at eleven hundred gold. Looks like it’ll be sold soon.","└ How much time is left?","└ Ten minutes.","└ Grylls set the duration to six hours because he wanted to sell it quickly.","└ Wild Grylls) Huh? You could set the auction duration?","└ He didn’t know. Lmaoooo.","└ He must have been in a real hurry. Lmao.","└ Still, selling it quickly is better for Grylls.","└ Otherwise, something might eat it again like last time. Lmaoooo.","***","Title: Fuck, Fuck, Fuck. I Shouldn’t Have Bought This","(Video of a headless snake body violently twitching)","First of all, it really is a Steel-Scaled Serpent.","Did this thing seriously come straight from the source? Fuck.","└ Ugh... You should add a gore warning.","└ The twitching is kind of cute. Lmao.","└ ?","└ Sir?","└ Since it doesn’t have a head, it probably wasn’t delivered completely fresh. Lmaoooo.","└ It was just extremely fresh. Lmao.","└ If it had still been alive, the auction house wouldn’t have accepted it. Lmao.","The Steel-Scaled Serpent that had caused such an uproar was eventually sold for approximately eleven hundred gold.","It was an extraordinarily high price.","Even after accounting for the auction house’s murderous fees, Wild Grylls had earned a large amount of money in an instant.","The item had also been confirmed as genuine.","At the same time, the gallery’s trust in Wild Grylls increased.","He seemed to have something slightly wrong with his head, but he was honest.","That became the general opinion of him.","***","Title: Are There Any Survival Experts Here?","Wild Grylls","Title: Are There Any Survival Experts Here?","Wild Grylls","If there are, please give me some tips.","I want to live.","└ There used to be a lot of them, but there aren’t any these days.","└ Wild Grylls) Why?","└ They all died. Lmao.","└ Wild Grylls) ;;","└ Several famous users entered the Forest of Four Seasons and then disappeared, right?","└ Yeah.","└ Grylls started inside it from the very beginning. Lmaoooo.","└ Hardcore mode from the start.","└ Wild Grylls) None of you bastards are helpful.","While Wild Grylls lamented through tear-filled eyes, another commotion was unfolding elsewhere.","It was the home of the being who had once shaken the entire Central Plains—the Heavenly Demon—and a paradise for those rejected by society.","The Demonic Cult.","Even the imperial family of the Central Plains watched it closely.","\"Heavenly One! You absolutely must not enter the Forest of Four Seasons!\"","\"This lady intends to rescue her benefactor. Why do you stand in her way? Do you truly wish to die?\"","The Heavenly Demon, Yu So-wol, threatened the man before her with an icy expression.","Her gaze alone carried enough force to make it seem as though she could tear a person apart.","That pressure was no mere illusion.","It affected the man before her considerably, making his insides feel not only overturned but tightly twisted.","He felt as though he might lose consciousness at any moment, yet he forced himself to endure and spoke.","\"That is not my intention. It is simply that the Forest of Four Seasons is a forbidden realm from which even the Heavenly One would struggle to escape.\"","\"Demonic Brain. You know well what realm this lady has reached.\"","\"Of course. You have transcended the principles of martial arts and earned the qualification to ascend.\"","He had noticed it the moment he faced her.","The Heavenly Demon, Yu So-wol, had entered a realm beyond all conventional standards.","Previously, she had been like the sun suspended high in the sky.","Now, she seemed to have become the sky itself.","Even before this breakthrough, Yu So-wol had stormed the imperial palace alone and taken the Emperor’s head.","Now that she had reached an even greater realm, no one could stop her.","\"However, the Forest of Four Seasons mentioned by the Heavenly One is nature itself, something that surpasses even the heavens. Every force of nature has converged there, transforming the entire region into a forbidden realm.\"","\"Explain it simply.\"","\"It would be easiest to think of the entire region as being filled with formations. Even if one breaks a formation, nature’s powerful regenerative force restores it almost immediately, and it returns in a different form.\"","Once someone entered the Forest of Four Seasons, they could never leave.","The Demonic Brain had just explained why.","The entire region was a barrier.","Even if one formation was destroyed, another formation with a different pattern appeared.","The forest itself was a living barrier.","No matter how many times it was broken through, it regenerated.","Therefore, no matter how powerful Yu So-wol had become, she would likely be unable to conquer the Forest of Four Seasons.","\"Can even your mind find no solution?\"","\"Regrettably, the reality is that this foolish mind of mine cannot comprehend something even the heavens themselves cannot read.\"","\"Hmm.\"","Yu So-wol withdrew her pressure and stopped threatening him.","If the Demonic Brain, the Demonic Cult’s greatest strategist, spoke so firmly, there truly was no current solution.","Forcing the issue would produce nothing.","Nor could she kill a trusted adviser over it.","It would be better to work the Demonic Brain to the bone until he found a way to conquer the Forest of Four Seasons.","\"Very well. Investigate the Forest of Four Seasons. This lady’s benefactor is trapped there.\"","\"I shall obey. Then what will the Heavenly One do from this point onward?\"","\"This lady requires time to organize her enlightenment, and she shall also help her benefactor survive. By any chance...\"","Yu So-wol almost asked whether the Demonic Brain used the gallery, but stopped herself.","She remembered all the thoughtless garbage posts she had written.","The Heavenly Demon, Yu So-wol, felt not even the slightest shame.","The human Yu So-wol, however, did.","She was embarrassed.","Of course, her garbage posts were closer to diary entries than anything else.","She had also included various realizations she had attained.","Even so, she couldn’t ask.","After hesitating, Yu So-wol changed the subject.","\"If anything may aid his survival, provide advice at any time.\"","\"For now, I believe it would be best to advise him not to abandon hope. The will to live is the most important thing in survival.\"","\"This lady shall remember it. Is there anything else?\"","\"No.\"","\"Then leave.\"","At the order dismissing him, the Demonic Brain bowed and withdrew.","Once he left, Yu So-wol was alone in the room.","She was about to naturally access the gallery when a sudden question occurred to her.","’Come to think of it, he did not ask who this lady’s benefactor was.’","She hadn’t intended to tell him, but the Demonic Brain hadn’t asked either.","That struck her as strange.","The question only occupied her mind for a moment before Yu So-wol accessed the gallery.","Thinking did not suit her.","She could simply leave all matters requiring thought to the Demonic Brain.","She had lived that way until now, and there had never been a problem.","\"I almost died. She’s a genuine calamity. A walking disaster.\"","Meanwhile, the Demonic Brain muttered something close to a lament.","His internal organs had been shaken so badly that a small amount of blood leaked from his mouth.","He roughly wiped the blood away and swallowed some medicine.","Only then did he feel slightly better.","’There is no longer anyone capable of stopping the Heavenly Demon.’","The Heavenly Demon had become far stronger than before.","She had already possessed monstrous power, and now she had attained another enlightenment on top of it.","At the very least, no one in the Central Plains could stop her.","That meant the Demonic Cult could finally achieve the long-awaited ambition of its dreams.","’Not yet. There is still too much to organize.’","The Demonic Cult was a paradise for the abandoned.","Put another way, it also suffered from a great deal of internal discord.","Only after firmly establishing discipline within could it exert influence outside.","For that reason, they would continue waiting quietly for now.","’We must also keep a close watch on the Western Nations.’","If the Central Plains were the only concern, things would be simple.","However, the Western Nations also required caution.","The moment the Demonic Cult acted openly, the Central Plains would be thrown into turmoil, and outside forces would naturally take an interest.","Since ancient times, whenever civil war broke out, external powers had inevitably become involved.","Some madmen even invited them in merely to preserve their own authority.","Surprisingly, such things happened often.","’The problem is how to persuade that monster...’","The Demonic Brain looked around and confirmed that no one was nearby.","Then he stared into empty space.","A familiar-looking window appeared before him.","It was the same gallery Yu So-wol used.","’When she said benefactor, she must have meant Wild Grylls.’","In truth, the Demonic Brain knew Yu So-wol used the gallery.","He even knew that her registered username was Heavenly Demon.","His own gallery history was longer than hers.","It would have been stranger if he hadn’t noticed.","Then why had he remained silent?","└ Heavenly Demon) If matters become impossible, this lady shall go and rescue you herself.","└ Wild Grylls) Really? Aren’t you an extremely busy person?","└ Heavenly Demon) This lady asked an aide, and he said it would be best to give you hope.","└ Wild Grylls) Ma’am? ;;","└ Heavenly Demon) Is there a problem?","└ We’ve decided to call that giving someone false hope.","└ The Heavenly Demon is surprisingly stupid. Lmaoooo.","└ Does she just have no understanding of how the world works?","└ It’s not exactly that. Her thought process is simply different from an ordinary person’s.","\"...\"","Because it was enough for him alone to know this embarrassing truth.","The Demonic Brain sighed before he could laugh.","The Heavenly Demon, revered by countless people, was a gallery addict?","Even a beggar asking for alms would throw away his bowl in disbelief.","At first, he hadn’t believed it either.","Yu So-wol had risen to the highest position through sheer martial power alone.","It was impossible to imagine someone like that wasting time in an online gallery.","However, the Demonic Brain was one of the Heavenly Demon’s closest aides.","He was also exceptionally intelligent, so it hadn’t taken him long to figure it out.","The decisive incident had been the Emperor’s assassination.","She had suddenly gone to the imperial palace, beheaded the Emperor, and returned.","How could he possibly fail to connect the events?","The imperial family had concealed the truth by presenting it as an ordinary power struggle, but the Demonic Brain knew what had really happened.","’What in the world was she thinking when she wrote all these posts...?’","An even greater problem was the content of the Heavenly Demon’s posts.","She carelessly scattered the realizations she had attained without thinking.","Fortunately, her peculiar old-fashioned style caused users to mock her as an old fossil instead of taking her seriously.","However, if those same words had been written in a secret martial arts manual instead of the gallery, the entire Central Plains would have been overturned.","It was similar to how something approaching true literature occasionally appeared among ordinary gallery posts.","’This is something I must carry to my grave.’","Separate from Yu So-wol’s gallery use, the Demonic Brain was also an outstanding gallery addict.","Judging by his posts, more than half of them were devoted to insulting her.","If she ever discovered his identity, his head would fly.","Did that mean he would quit the gallery?","***","Title: I’ve Been Wondering About Something","SmartDemon","There are people in this world who seem stupid and intelligent at the same time.","My superior is like that.","I can’t tell whether she has no thoughts or simply refuses to think.","Maybe she’s intelligent but just doesn’t use her brain.","└ There are quite a few people like that. Lmao.","└ A lot of people simply have strange standards.","└ The important thing is their personality. Does she pay well?","└ SmartDemon) The boss isn’t greedy for money, so she pays well. Lmao.","└ What’s your boss like? A man or a woman?","└ SmartDemon) A woman.","└ Is she pretty?","└ SmartDemon) She is pretty, but she’s a little stupid, so she’s not my type. ;;","└ What is your type?","└ SmartDemon) A beautiful and intelligent woman.","└ You were from the Central Plains, right? What about the Zhuge Clan?","└ SmartDemon) Who are they? Are their women beautiful?","└ Tell us your qualifications first. Lmao.","└ SmartDemon) Is being from the Demonic Cult acceptable?","└ Of course not, you crazy bastard. Lmaoooo.","└ SmartDemon) Damn. Lmao.","Of course not.","A dog was more likely to stop eating its own filth.","The Demonic Brain chuckled.","After using his mind so intensely every day, emptying it always felt refreshing.","Of course, he didn’t completely stop thinking whenever he used the gallery.","There had recently been one registered user causing considerable commotion.","’For now, I should keep a close watch on Wild Grylls...’","He had no intention of helping directly.","Yu So-wol might not think often, but she wasn’t oblivious.","He intended to pretend ignorance as much as possible while merely observing Wild Grylls’ actions.","Yu So-wol was already watching him anyway.","Despite all the talk about the Forest of Four Seasons, the Demonic Brain remained unconvinced.","He would revise his assessment of Wild Grylls only after more definitive evidence appeared.","***","Title: Please Send Me Home","Wild Grylls","I miss my mom.","He was somewhat pitiful.","Should he help?","└ Is your mother doing well at home?","└ Wild Grylls) I’m an orphan.","└ ...","└ Wild Grylls) But I think I’ll be seeing her soon. I should give her a hug when I get there. Lmaoooo.","└ Ah.","└ Aah...","└ Aaaaaah...","└ Wild Grylls) Why is everyone reacting like that?","└ Stay strong, dude...","He truly was pitiful."]},{"title":"Chapter 9","paragraphs":["The Forest of Four Seasons (4)","I have no thoughts.","Because there is literally nothing on my mind.","Ever since I returned to the cave, I’ve just been sitting there, completely spacing out.","I still can’t believe the reality I’m in right now. I wish this were all just a dream.","But no matter how much time passes, nothing changes. This damned place is the Forest of Four Seasons, and this is where I woke up.","There was no way my mental state wouldn’t fall apart.","So I spent the entire day writing depressing, self-pitying posts on the gallery.","Title: The Five Stages of Death (Live Updates)","[Bullshit. I’m looking around a bit more.]","Denial","[Why me? The hell did I do to deserve this?]","Anger","[I’ll be your slave for life. Someone please come pick me up.]","Bargaining","[Please send me home. I want to eat the leftover kimchi stew from yesterday.]","Depression","Those are the actual titles of Grylls’ posts in real time lol.","Only Acceptance is left now.","ᄂ True lololol","L StarlightPrincess) You’re such a terrible person.","_ Science, lol.","L What’s kimchi stew?","_ Dunno.","_ StarlightPrincess) That’s unfortunate.","ᄂ It’s not like he’s terminally ill.","L StarlightPrincess) Then what is it?","_ More like he’s living on borrowed time?","About the same as me, honestly.","One kind user had even made a timeline of my mental breakdown.","Seeing it actually made me chuckle.","To be honest, I was already thinking it was about time to move on to the acceptance stage.","Sitting around sulking wasn’t going to help.","I still had no idea why I had to suffer here of all places, but I couldn’t keep escaping from reality forever.","\"...It’s not like there’s absolutely no way out... right? Right...?\"","The gallery had explained it.","The entire Forest of Four Seasons was surrounded by barriers.","Break through one, and another appears.","Even the barriers you’ve already broken eventually regenerate in a different pattern.","The same applies not only to the ground, but also underground and in the sky.","Once you enter...","You never get out.","First, I need to figure out how big this forest actually is.","If I ended up settling here, I’d better get familiar with my surroundings first.","The cave was right nearby, but getting lost within sight of it would be beyond pathetic.","The problem was...","Apparently that happened pretty often.","I’d need to be careful.","Let’s head to the river first. I need to check whether the water’s safe to drink.","I hadn’t been in the right state of mind to check yesterday.","Back then, I was too busy wanting to cry.","The water itself was probably drinkable.","What I really wanted to know was...","What lived in it.","This forest was crawling with monsters the size of anacondas and bears as big as houses.","Who said the riverbank was any safer?","Even man-eating fish wouldn’t surprise me.","I could literally die while taking a drink.","If it’s safe to drink, I can make the cave my base.","It had already been two days.","Other than the Mad Dog who originally lived there, nothing else had shown up.","Well...","There had been that owlbear.","But let’s pretend that didn’t count.","I got away fast enough.","Besides, the cave was easy to defend.","I’d probably be staying there for the foreseeable future.","Maybe I should just survive on Wall-Fasting Pills?","That was something I’d need to think about.","I stood up.","For now, checking the river came first.","I’d worry about everything else after I got back.","Or maybe I’d just make a poll on the gallery.","Only users with permanent nicknames would be allowed to vote, of course.","There were way too many people whose attitude was,","\"Not my problem, so why should I care?\"","Not collective wisdom...","Collective stupidity.","Whooooosh—","\"Whoa... what’s this?\"","The moment I arrived at the stream I’d noticed yesterday, I couldn’t help but stare.","Was there some dangerous beast?","No.","Man-eating fish?","No.","It was something else entirely.","The scenery beyond the stream.","Yesterday, it had been a desert.","***","Title: Guys, check this out.","Wild Grylls","(Photo of snow-covered mountains beyond the stream.)","Yesterday it was a desert.","Today it’s snowy mountains.","Wonder what it’ll be tomorrow lol.","L Definitely the Forest of Four Seasons! Confirmed!","L Wait... what the heck is that...?","L ...What are you even supposed to say in a situation like this?","ᄂ StarlightPrincess) Just cheer him on.","_ SwordMaster) Excuse me, but... you’re not a criminal, are you?","L Wild Grylls) Does stealing money from my mom’s wallet as a kid count?","L SwordMaster) Didn’t you say you were an orphan?","L Wild Grylls) She was around back then.","ᄂ SwordMaster) ;_; Sorry...","L Wild Grylls) I’m used to it lol.","_ SwordMaster) I stole from my parents’ wallet too haha...","L Wild Grylls) Then why aren’t you coming already?","L SwordMaster) Busy with work.","L Wild Grylls) Doing what?","L SwordMaster) House security. Haha.","L So... unemployed? lol","ᄂ Seriously, what’s gonna happen to Grylls?","_ At this point, I have no idea lol.","ᄂ He’ll have to survive on his own.","L Shouldn’t we give him disaster relief funds? lol","ᄂ Heavenly Demon) The mountains are beautiful.","_ CheongguPrincess) They really are. Almost as pretty as my face lol.","L Heavenly Demon)?","L ?","L ?","L ?","_ CheongguPrincess) What? If you’ve got a problem, come fight me.","ᄂ Heavenly Demon) Where do you live?","Even getting challenged to a duel had become normal.","I let out a dry laugh.","Yesterday, everything beyond the stream had been a desert.","Today...","It was an enormous mountain range blanketed in pure white snow.","For a second I wondered if I’d somehow come to the wrong place.","But that made no sense.","A desert right next to snowy mountains?","The boundary was perfectly clear.","The environment hadn’t gradually changed.","Everything beyond the stream was simply...","Different.","Is someone messing with me?","I sighed and walked over to the stream.","Judging by all the minnows swimming around, the water quality looked excellent.","At least there was one piece of good news.","Later, I’d bring the water bottle the Heavenly Demon had given me.","Still...","Better check things first.","I started by testing the depth.","Splash.","The moment I stuck my hand in...","Confusion hit me before the coolness did.","For a second I thought my eyes were playing tricks on me.","But the farther I pushed my arm in...","The deeper it kept going.","I couldn’t touch the bottom.","The water was so unbelievably clear that it looked much shallower than it actually was.","This should be enough.","It wasn’t bottomless.","You could probably cross it if you really wanted to.","Of course...","There was absolutely no reason to cross into the snowy mountains.","Unless I was trying to kill myself.","\"Ribbit.\"","\"Hm?\"","I’d just pulled my arm out of the water when I heard an odd sound.","It had come from nearby.","I turned toward it.","\"Ribbit.\"","\"...A frog?\"","A frog.","A golden frog.","It sat atop a rock in the middle of the stream.","Whatever else it was...","Its entire body glittered with a metallic golden sheen.","And somehow that only made it seem more dangerous.","Animals with colors that vivid usually had one thing in common.","Poison.","I’d better stay away.","Poison was the last thing I wanted to deal with.","Even if it wasn’t poisonous...","The thing was about the size of a small dog.","It was seriously unsettling.","\"RRAAAAK!\"","\"Huh? Wait—\"","Just as I turned to leave...","The golden frog suddenly stood upright on its long hind legs.","Then it leaned its head all the way back.","It made a disgusting noise, almost like a person gathering phlegm in their throat.","A moment later, it snapped its head forward.","\" Ptooey! \"","Piiing!","A sticky golden glob shot out of its mouth like a bullet.","Straight at my face.","I barely managed to dodge.","The viscous golden projectile grazed past me.","A split second later...","It struck the tree behind me.","Sssssssss!","\"Holy shit.\"","The tree...","Melted.","So it wasn’t poison.","It was acid.","But I didn’t have time to admire it.","The frog had already leaned its head back again to reload.","Getting away took priority.","I bolted before it could spit again.","\" Ptooey! \"","\"Whoa!\"","Another near miss.","If I hadn’t ducked, it would’ve nailed me in the back of the head.","Fortunately...","The frog didn’t chase me.","It seemed to consider the stream its territory.","\"Huff... huff...\"","I ran for my life all the way back to the cave before finally catching my breath.","What kind of suffering was this?","I’d finally found clean water...","Only to get bullied by a damn frog.","Unbelievable.","The stream’s too deep to approach safely...","If only I had a bow.","Not that I’d know how to use one anyway.","That frog definitely hadn’t been there yesterday.","Maybe...","Did it only attack because I’d put my hand in the water?","Now I wasn’t even sure whether I could drink safely.","Worst-case scenario...","The frog might spit into the river itself.","***","Title: Guys, I found a golden frog.","Wild Grylls","No picture.","I was too busy running for my life.","This bastard spits acid.","Anyone know what it is?","L A frog that spits acid? What kind of frog is that? lol","L Sure, it’s the Forest of Four Seasons, but that’s a bit much lol.","L No picture means it’s 99% fake lol.","ᄂ AllFather) Did you happen to find it in a river?","L Wild Grylls) Do you know what it is?","L AllFather) Yes. Its official name is the Golden Poison Frog. It’s an extremely rare species found only in exceptionally clean water. Its poison is so potent that many people have died trying to capture one. Please be careful.","L Wild Grylls) Wait... it wasn’t acid? It was poison??","L AllFather) The poison is simply that powerful.","Amid all the usual pointless comments...","One user with a permanent nickname replied.","AllFather.","He was one of those users who only appeared occasionally to leave a comment before disappearing again.","He barely made any posts himself.","When he did, they were almost always about magic or alchemy.","Most of them were filled with technical jargon, so I usually ignored them.","He gave off serious professor vibes.","He also tended to speak politely, so I did the same.","L Wild Grylls) Yeah. I found it in the river. It spat at me the moment I put my hand in the water.","L AllFather) Approximately how large was it?","L Wild Grylls) About the size of a dog.","L AllFather) It must have grown larger because it’s in the Forest of Four Seasons. They’re normally only about the size of a finger joint.","This place really did have every bizarre creature imaginable.","A frog whose venom was so potent it looked like acid.","And with the entire river serving as its fortress...","It was practically the equivalent of an archer firing from atop a castle wall.","More than anything... I just want to be able to drink water safely.","If I showed up there too often...","That thing might start waiting for me on purpose.","That would be a serious problem.","Even while I was thinking it over, notifications kept pouring in.","Lately, every post I made seemed to attract a flood of comments.","L AllFather) If you manage to capture the Golden Poison Frog, I’ll pay you 20,000 gold. I’d like to study it.","L Isn’t that just a roundabout way of telling him to go die?","L If you catch it, I’ll give you 50,000 gold lol.","L Wild Grylls) I kind of have to catch it... Otherwise I can’t get any water. Any other advice?","ᄂ AllFather) I’m afraid not. It’s such a rare species that very little is known about it. The only confirmed fact is that it’s primarily active in the morning. You may also need an antidote.","ᄂ Then just go drink water in the evening lol.","L Wild Grylls) Evenings are more dangerous ;;","ᄂ What comes out at night?","L Wild Grylls) It’s dangerous because I don’t know what might come out.","There was no obvious way to deal with it.","In the end, I had no choice but to solve the problem myself.","This was the first obstacle standing between me and a secure source of drinking water.","To overcome it, I would need to prepare thoroughly.","Before that, I should return the compasses.","I planned to return all of them to their original owners except the one the Heavenly Demon had given me.","First, I made a public post so everyone would see it.","Five minutes later, I began sending trade requests.","The first person I contacted was the user named StarlightPrincess .","Maybe it was because she practically lived on the gallery all day, but she accepted the request almost immediately.","[Wild Grylls: Hello. I sent you a trade request because I wanted to return your compass.]","[StarlightPrincess: Oh. Okay! You really don’t have to return it, though...]","[Wild Grylls: The one the Heavenly Demon gave me is enough. Carrying the rest around would be difficult.]","[StarlightPrincess: I understand. Let’s both do our best.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. I hope you recover soon.]","It seemed she really was sick.","She had a kind personality too.","Next was PraiseTheSun , the user I suspected was a dark elf.","[Wild Grylls: Hello. I sent you a trade request to return your compass.]","[PraiseTheSun: Keep it.]","[Wild Grylls: I still have a conscience. I should return it.]","[PraiseTheSun: I don’t take pocket change like that.]","[Wild Grylls: ;;;]","That was so casual it almost made me feel embarrassed.","Still, since they had helped me, I ought to repay the favor.","When I said I would compensate them later if I found something valuable, I received an unexpected reply.","[PraiseTheSun: I like you. Need anything else? Looks like you could use a shield.]","[Wild Grylls: I do need one, but I’ll buy it properly. I sold something called a Steel-Scale Snake.]","[PraiseTheSun: I don’t take pocket change.]","[Wild Grylls: Wait ;; You’re a dark elf, right?]","[PraiseTheSun: Yeah.]","[Wild Grylls: Are all dark elves rich?]","The dark elves I knew were a race opposed to ordinary elves.","They shared the same roots, but their dispositions were completely different.","Unlike peace-loving elves, they did not hesitate to use dirty tactics.","Even so, they did not cross certain lines.","Their beliefs were closer to the idea that one had to cultivate strength in order to preserve peace.","Perhaps because of that, though, they tended to lack social skills.","Of course, that was merely what I knew.","I could not apply my own assumptions to this world.","Even the elves here were far removed from peace.","They were practically defined by imperialism.","[PraiseTheSun: There are a lot of rich ones, I guess? Cetan produces tons of gold and resources. Isn’t that common knowledge?]","[Wild Grylls: I’m from another world, so I don’t really know.]","[PraiseTheSun: That wasn’t just a character gimmick?]","[Wild Grylls: It’s real...]","Whether they believed me or not did not matter.","I was trapped in a forest where I could not meet anyone anyway.","My place of origin was meaningless.","PraiseTheSun seemed to understand that and casually moved on.","[PraiseTheSun: Anyway, dark elves are a kinder and more easygoing race than those insane, old-fashioned elves. Got it?]","[Wild Grylls: That sounds very emphatic. Was it different in the past?]","[PraiseTheSun: It used to be the opposite. But after we settled in the desert and became rich, everyone grew more generous. We used to have awful tempers because we were constantly discriminated against.]","[Wild Grylls: That’s realistic.]","[PraiseTheSun: Still, don’t underestimate us. Surviving in the desert made us damn good at fighting.]","[Wild Grylls: I wasn’t planning to. Is there anything in particular I should be careful about?]","[PraiseTheSun: Call us darkies and you’re dead. No, I’ll curse you to death.]","[PraiseTheSun has registered a trade item.]","[PraiseTheSun: I’ll give you this, so send me anything that’s good for the body. I don’t have much time, so hurry up and take it.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. I won’t forget this favor.]","[PraiseTheSun: Sure. Stay safe.]","Were they in roughly the same social position as Black people back on Earth?","Usually cheerful, but terrifying the instant someone touched a sore spot.","Here, it was racial discrimination in the literal sense of discrimination between species, so I needed to be careful.","I should learn about these things gradually.","Even though the gallery was anonymous, openly making discriminatory remarks did not suit my personality.","Besides, I was in a situation where I needed to build goodwill.","If all I did was make people dislike me, I would only be hurting myself.","Was everyone on the gallery kind?","Or were users with permanent nicknames simply nicer?","I disconnected from PraiseTheSun.","The moment the connection ended, I checked the item they had sent me.","\"...?\"","I could not help but stare in confusion.","The item glittered brilliantly.","It was shaped roughly like a shield, but its entire surface was covered in gold.","A literal golden shield.","Just how obscenely rich did someone have to be to casually give away something like this?","...I wonder if it performs well.","I turned the gleaming golden shield over in my hands before equipping it.","It was lighter than expected and comfortable to carry, though I should probably test how durable it was.","I had no intention of testing it with the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","I had a feeling that would only damage the shield.","\"Next is CheongguPrincess, I guess?\"","What a peculiar username.","Judging by the name alone, she seemed to be a woman.","However, ninety percent of the people who lived on the gallery were abnormal.","What kind of person would it be this time?","[CheongguPrincess: Then cheer for our Chae-U. That’ll be enough.]","[Wild Grylls: I don’t know much about this world. What kind of team is Chae-U?]","I knew this world had things resembling sports.","However, I did not know the details.","It was an entirely different world populated by a wide variety of races.","It was bound to be completely different from what I knew.","[Wild Grylls: Hello. I sent you a trade request to return your compass.]","[CheongguPrincess: Hellooo. Just keep it.]","Her reply was similar to PraiseTheSun’s.","She said she did not need the compass back.","For a moment, I wondered whether the gallery was filled with nothing but kind people.","But after thinking about it, perhaps it was only natural.","These were the people who had willingly given me compasses the moment I made my post.","That was all the more reason to strengthen my relationships with them.","[CheongguPrincess: Oh my gosh! You don’t know Chaemes United, the most famous and prestigious club in all of Mephisto?! You’ve wasted half your life!]","[Wild Grylls: The half I have left is hanging by a thread.]","[CheongguPrincess: Ah! Sorry! You were living on borrowed time, weren’t you!]","She was not wrong, but hearing her say it so bluntly was depressing.","How had my life ended up like this?","Just as CheongguPrincess’s bluntness began to dampen my mood—","[Wild Grylls: I have a conscience, so I should return it. I just don’t have anything I can give you right now.]","[CheongguPrincess has registered trade items.]","[CheongguPrincess: I’ll give you these, and from now on, you’re a Chae-U fan.]","[Wild Grylls: What did you send me?]","[CheongguPrincess: Jerseys of the most famous players, Neves and Vannir! The material is excellent, so wear them around. I’ll send two home jerseys and two away jerseys.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh. Okay...]","[Wild Grylls: What exactly is that?]","[CheongguPrincess: There’s a cheap imitation called Chaemes City, so ignore them! They’re funded by Cetan’s filthy gold money. They have no tradition. None at all.]","I felt slightly bewildered.","Still, I happened to need clothes, so this was fortunate.","I planned to buy soap with money, so that was not a problem.","But I needed something else to wear while my clothes were drying.","For now, I could still endure it.","As more time passed, however, my need for extra clothing would only increase.","[CheongguPrincess: Chaemes United is a club with a proud two-hundred-year history. I guarantee you’ll be completely obsessed with them soon, Mr. Grylls.]","[Wild Grylls: First, I need to check whether it’s even a sport I know. It might be different from what I’m familiar with. Either way, thank you very much for the clothes.]","[CheongguPrincess: Don’t mention it. But there’s one thing I need to ask of you.]","Why did this stranger give off such a familiar feeling?","A dry laugh escaped me.","CheongguPrincess ended the conversation after saying she would upload a highlight reel later and that I should watch it to calm my mind and body.","Once the conversation ended, I checked the clothes she had sent me.","They were jerseys with large names printed across them.","I have no idea what language this is.","Unfortunately, I could not read the names.","Hadn’t they said the gallery had an automatic translation feature?","The emblem on the chest, however, looked rather impressive.","Just as she had claimed, it gave off a distinct sense of history and tradition.","It was not only the design.","The white and blue colors were blended tastefully, making the jerseys look quite beautiful.","They were not ideal colors for the wilderness, but what I needed most was clothing, so it did not matter.","The material is good too.","It was also highly elastic.","They would probably prove useful in many ways.","I smiled briefly, then immediately opened the gallery to check the latest posts.","CheongguPrincess had said she would upload something soon.","I intended to leave a comment thanking her when she did.","[Chaemes United Special Highlights Collection]","The instant I saw the post, I clicked it without hesitation.","\"Huh?\"","My eyes widened as I watched the video she had uploaded.","\"This is soccer.\"","Why did soccer exist here?","Then do they have baseball too?","Every so often, a lunatic would appear on the gallery.","Could that be why?"]},{"title":"Chapter 10","paragraphs":["The Forest of Four Seasons (5)","There were many different races in the world, but whenever people were asked which race was the most specialized in combat , they all gave the same answer.","The demons.","Even the demons themselves acknowledged it.","Horns growing from their heads, blue-toned skin, and inverted eyes that sharply distinguished them from other races.","Mana they could naturally wield thanks to their innate physiques.","Magic of overwhelmingly greater power than that of other races.","All of these traits combined had earned them the name \"the devil race,\" and true to that name, they were fiercely devoted to their desires.","***","Title: I’ll Teach You Continental History","In the past, demons caused all the trouble.","Now it’s the elves.","History lesson over!","L Looking at history, demons were absolute thugs.","L There’s a reason a Hero appears in every era lol.","L If nobody keeps these bastards in check, the world is screwed lol.","L What kind of lives do demons even live?","Because they were so faithful to their desires, they had been infamous for their cruelty in the distant past.","Their tyranny had been so severe that a Hero appeared in every generation to kill or restrain the Demon King .","The Demon King was the ruler of Mephisto, the nation of demons, while the Hero was an elite warrior personally cultivated by humanity.","A noble character.","Outstanding talent.","Devout faith.","And overwhelming divine power granted in proportion to those qualities.","Because of these circumstances, the past had been filled with repeated clashes between the Demon King and the Hero, resulting in no small number of casualties.","But perhaps the demons eventually grew tired of that long conflict.","Or maybe they simply got bored.","L It’s not like they actually came to their senses. There was once a guy who killed a player for scoring an own goal lol.","L Holy crap, that’s insane lolol.","L Is that why they stopped calling it a \"suicide goal\" and changed it to \"own goal\"?","_ That’s why player protection is extremely strict in Mephisto.","***","Title: When Did the Demons Finally Come to Their Senses?","They suddenly got quiet at some point.","L They calmed down when they got bored of fighting and invented that weird ball game.","L Hey, don’t call it weird! Say that to a demon and they’ll tear you limb from limb.","L Those bastards are surprisingly serious about ball games lol.","The demons desperately craved a form of combat that did not involve fists.","They wanted something as exciting and tense as battle.","They had grown tired of simply punching and kicking each other.","So they put their battles against the Heroes aside and conducted study after study.","Eventually, they created an entire culture.","Ball games such as soccer, baseball, basketball, rugby, and American football.","In other words—","Sports.","At first, even the demons themselves thought it was ridiculous.","Why play with balls when they could simply fight?","There were already gladiators who fought each other, so why choose ball games of all things?","However, as time passed and society and law developed, violence gradually became taboo.","More importantly, there were far too few forms of entertainment.","When people gained peace of mind, they naturally sought amusement.","Because of that social trend, along with the limitations of an era lacking proper entertainment, the demons inevitably began to take sports seriously.","Thus, the demons—who were passionately devoted to every source of dopamine except drugs and gambling—became completely obsessed with mere \"ball games.\"","***","Title: Here’s How Serious These Bastards Are","You can mock demons for being weak in a fight and they’ll just laugh it off.","Why?","Because they know they’re stronger.","They’re naturally powerful enough to rival elves.","But ball games?","Call them weak at those and they’ll charge at you like they genuinely intend to kill you.","Especially soccer. Their pride was shattered when humans won the championship lol.","ᄂ How do you know that?","L I teased my demon friend while we were playing futsal and he broke my arm.","With demons potentially invading at any moment while blasting magic everywhere, there was no reason for other races to accept their culture.","Ironically, however, the first race to adopt demon culture was humanity.","One might ask why humans, who had suffered the greatest losses during the long wars against demons, would do such a thing.","The answer was simple.","Humans had short lifespans.","That meant their generations changed far faster than those of other races.","The generations that remembered the demons’ past atrocities gradually disappeared.","Eventually, only generations who remembered them as idiots obsessed with ball games remained.","As interaction with the demons slowly increased and humans began adopting their culture, humanity came up with a clever strategy.","ᄂ He brought it on himself lololol.","_ Did he at least pay your medical bills?","ᄂ Yeah, he did. But he warned me not to say that to any other demons. Apparently, I might actually die.","L Just how serious are they about this? lololol.","Naturally, sports had originally been a culture enjoyed only by demons.","The other races had shown no interest.","***","Title: An Unavoidable Trap from the Demons’ Perspective","Human: If we have a problem, let’s settle it through ball games. You’re already insanely strong anyway.","Demon: Fair enough lol.","Human: But you know how pathetic it would look if you started causing trouble just because you lost, right?","Demon: Why would we lose? lol.","And ten years later, the humans completely crushed them.","Human: We won, you losers lol.","Demon: Screw this. It’s war.","Human: Wow, you’re starting a war because you lost a ball game? Have you got no pride?","Demon: Ah, damn it... This pisses me off, but I can’t argue with that.","L Lololol, there’s literally nothing they can do.","_ Does diplomacy really work like that?","L It’s summarized, but that’s genuinely what happened lol.","The demons were a race whose pride rivaled that of the elves.","They had a history of tormenting neighboring nations using their natural strength, but that had been during a more barbaric age.","After spreading the culture of sports across the world, their reputation gradually improved.","Their pride, however, remained unchanged.","Humans cunningly took advantage of that pride, provoking it little by little to gain benefits.","The demons had effectively trapped themselves in a contradiction, so they had no choice but to grit their teeth and focus on diplomacy.","L That’s a fact.","L It only worked because their strength was roughly equal lol.","L But what were the elves doing?","ᄂ Those bastards just stood back with their arms folded until it was all over lol.","L That’s because Mephisto is close to the human kingdoms.","L Elves are useless as always.","ᄂ And now those same damn elves are causing trouble, right?","L What the hell did we humans ever do wrong?","L Our ancestors founded the country in the wrong place lol.","L We’re surrounded by nonhuman nations on all sides lolol","***","Title: One Important Fact","Without the Hero, the demons would still have started a war.","Of course, most of this was spoken half-jokingly.","Sports remained sports.","Its popularity, however, rose to the heavens because it allowed different races to overcome their natural differences and compete fairly.","Mana could not be used.","Victory depended solely on physical ability and skill.","Most importantly, sports embodied the chivalric spirit appropriate to the age.","Sportsmanship.","That romantic ideal captivated people as well.","***","Title: What Are Dwarves Even Good At?","They’re too short for soccer and basketball.","They don’t have the physique for rugby or American football.","Even baseball is difficult because their strike zone is weird.","What can they even do?","_ PassingDwarf) We make the balls, asshole.","ᄂ Do you earn a lot?","L PassingDwarf) We make a shitload whenever there’s a major tournament.","_ Did dwarves make the balls in ancient times too?","L I heard they used human heads as balls back then.","L What the hell ;;","***","Title: Something Interesting About Beastfolk","The race that loves both the quietest sport, baseball, and the roughest sport, American football, the most.","Why?","L SuspiciouslyFurry) What are you talking about? In baseball, they smash people’s heads with bats.","L That’s a gang fight, you idiot lololol.","L Bench-clearing brawls lololol.","L Beastfolk are built tough, so they’re fine even after that lol.","Dwarves were disadvantaged by their stature and could not participate in many sports directly, but they still gained plenty of related opportunities.","Balls, uniforms, and all kinds of equipment.","Given the technological level of the age, every form of precision craftsmanship was entrusted to dwarves.","As industrialization and commercialization rapidly progressed and various tournaments began to be held, Mephisto transformed into a nation of culture.","Sports could make people feel joy, anger, sorrow, and pleasure simply by watching.","At the same time, they were a drug capable of driving people insane.","Popular sports differed from nation to nation and race to race, but the fact that Mephisto had invented them never changed.","For that reason, sports were deeply woven into everyday life in Mephisto.","A form of entertainment enjoyed by everyone, regardless of age, sex, or social status.","\"No! How could he miss that?! Are you kidding me?!\"","The same applied even to Mephisto’s highest-ranking figures.","A woman with the blue skin and inverted eyes unique to demons, yet possessing exceptional beauty.","Her glossy hair was as black as midnight, while the curled horns growing from her head gave her a strangely captivating charm.","And finally, she had a figure capable of setting countless men’s hearts ablaze.","There was not a single flaw to be found.","\"Wow. Even I could’ve scored that.\"","She was Keirin Rondel Archive , princess of Mephisto and heir to the title of Demon King.","She cursed as she watched the soccer match being displayed through a magical broadcasting orb.","After the creation of sports, Mephisto had invented various forms of magic to properly industrialize them.","The broadcasting magic Keirin was currently watching was one such invention.","Its coverage extended across an enormous area.","\"That piece of garbage cost one hundred billion yura? Are the people running Chae-U blind?\"","Keirin clicked her tongue and furrowed her elegant brow.","Her expression was filled with displeasure.","As the princess of Mephisto, she was revered by countless people.","Thanks to her innate strength and background, she faced almost no political pressure.","If something displeased her, she could apply pressure whenever she wished.","But doing so in sports would cause a massive scandal.","I know there’s nothing I can do, but it’s still frustrating.","A noble could own a club.","However, the moment they used political influence, they would be expelled immediately.","It was not formally written into law, but it was an unspoken rule.","Sports were a culture enjoyed not only by nobles, but by everyone.","Unless it involved something unavoidable, like war, not even the highest-ranking members of society could completely control it.","They could exert some influence through policy, but interference beyond that was impossible.","[The match is over! Chaemes United suffer a two-to-one defeat at home!]","[It’ll be a festival in Moss Village tonight. They’ve taken another step closer to their long-awaited promotion to the Challengers League!]","[Meanwhile, Chaemes United are now barely holding on to their position in the table. How will Manager Horen respond to—]","\"Damn it.\"","Click.","Keirin irritably shut off the broadcasting magic.","They had thrown away a match they had practically won because someone got sent off.","She covered her face with both hands for a long moment before slowly lowering them.","Then, with a blank expression, she accessed the gallery.","[Chae-U are mid-table trash! Chae-U are mid-table trash! Chae-U are mid-table trash!]","[The Cheonggu bastards are trembling~ The Cheonggu bastards are trembling so hard~ The Cheonggu bastards are trembling~]","[???: Better start sucking up now, huh?]","[Cheonggu fans eliminated lololol.]","The moment the match ended, lunatics flooded the gallery.","It happened every time.","Keirin let out a hollow laugh and made a post.","***","Title: Revealing My Asshole","CheongguPrincess","(Picture of an emblem bearing a deer symbol.)","This is my asshole.","L Lololol, did Cheonggu lose today?","L CheongguPrincess) Those motherless bitches conceded two goals in stoppage time lol.","L No wonder the lunatics came crawling out.","After making the post, Keirin rose from her seat.","Her head felt far too hot.","She needed to cool down.","Before that, I should clean the room.","She looked around.","Chaemes United jerseys, replica trophies, and countless other pieces of Chae-U merchandise filled the space.","It was exactly the kind of room someone utterly obsessed with soccer would decorate.","And that was precisely what she was.","Snap!","Keirin snapped her fingers.","Every item disappeared, leaving behind a completely barren room.","This place had originally been designed as a training hall.","It was a private training facility constructed solely for Keirin.","She looked around the empty hall several times before lowering her gaze.","Instead of a dignified dress, she was wearing an almost painfully ordinary jersey.","The name printed on it belonged to a former legend of Chae-U.","Snap!","Another snap of her fingers transformed the jersey into a beautiful black dress.","All of it had been done through magic.","Normally, a mage would need to chant an incantation.","Keirin had no such need.","She could manifest magic with a simple gesture.","After carefully checking that nothing was out of place, she walked toward the exit.","A door protected by numerous security spells and locking mechanisms stood there.","Clunk!","Keirin disengaged every lock and stepped outside.","A middle-aged butler was waiting with several knights.","\"You’ve worked hard, Princess. Have you finished your training?\"","\"Yes. You have worked hard as well.\"","\"Not at all. It is my duty to serve you, Princess.\"","The butler bowed deeply as he answered.","Keirin walked past him and gently patted his shoulder.","It was her way of acknowledging his efforts.","Emotion immediately appeared on the butler’s face.","A warmth that could not be found in the current Demon King.","That warmth drew people toward her.","She had every reason to become arrogant as the next heir to the title of Demon King.","Keirin’s personal strength also ranked among the five greatest on the entire continent.","Despite that, she was neither arrogant nor unkind.","Her heart was gentle as well.","One might wonder whether such a small gesture really mattered.","However, it was necessary to remember that these people were demons.","Besides, Keirin only spoke stiffly. She was kind and considerate not only toward the butler, but toward everyone.","Her Highness seems to be in a poor mood today. Did she fail to gain anything from her training?","The butler thought as he followed behind Keirin.","After serving her for many years, he had learned to read her emotions to some extent.","Today, she was in a terrible mood.","An exceptionally terrible one.","At times like this, the wisest course of action was to remain silent.","She might be kinder than most demons, but Keirin was still a demon.","If someone irritated her, magic would come flying.","Even emotional-control training, which she only does once or twice a week, must be difficult.","Demons were a warlike race, rivaling even beastfolk in that regard.","They enjoyed the act of competing to determine victory and defeat.","In the past, that nature had manifested as violence and caused tremendous damage to those around them.","But things were different now.","As violence became taboo, controlling one’s emotions grew increasingly important.","This was especially true for those of high status, since a single impulsive outburst could ruin everything.","For that reason, emotional-control training was extremely important.","And because of that, it was also difficult and painful.","Damn it. Seriously. How the hell do you concede two goals in stoppage time?","Keirin had indeed been practicing emotional control.","Her method, however, differed from the usual one.","As an ardent Chaemes United supporter, simply watching a match sent her emotions surging up and down without warning.","In the past, she had struggled to control herself and smashed the training hall whenever she got the chance.","That was no longer the case.","Now she had reached the point where she could simply think, Sigh. You useless bastards. Of course you’d do that, and move on.","Whatever else might be said, her mental fortitude was slowly reaching a level comparable to that of a Saintess.","\"Why am I a Chae-U fan?\"","After returning to her bedroom, Keirin lay on the bed and thought back on the past.","Why had she become a fan of soccer, and Chaemes United in particular?","Originally, she had lived a life far removed from soccer.","No matter how widely the culture had spread across the world, she was still a member of the upper class.","Soccer, in particular, had spread upward from the lower classes, so the aristocracy had harbored a fair amount of hostility toward it.","However, not even the upper class could ignore the wealth generated by culture.","Culture itself was also impossible to suppress.","The moment someone tried to stop it, it only spread further.","Without it, things probably would have been even harder.","Keirin had been educated to believe that soccer was something watched only by ignorant commoners.","Yet many clubs were owned by nobles.","Only royalty and a handful of particularly old-fashioned aristocrats truly disliked it.","Even they viewed sports in a generally favorable light.","It was soccer alone that drew their hostility.","Because of that, Keirin had once looked down on soccer as well.","Then, little by little, she became obsessed with it.","The cause was none other than the gallery .","Everything changed when she happened to gain access to it.","Knowledge she had never encountered while being raised like a flower in a greenhouse.","And the strange, addictive quality found only in soccer.","For Keirin, who had been born a demon, it was no different from trying a new kind of drug.","Naturally, she began supporting Chaemes United, the club representing her home region.","She even created the gallery username CheongguPrincess .","Damn it. It’s frustrating that I can’t even attend matches in person.","Keirin did not express that frustration in reality.","There were political reasons.","One might wonder how something as trivial as soccer could become a political issue.","Strictly speaking, it was closer to a generational conflict.","Demons might not live as long as elves, but their lifespans were still considerable.","As a result, generational turnover was slow.","Many members of the older generation who remembered the demons’ brutal past were still alive.","That older generation firmly controlled the existing power structure, creating a politically delicate situation.","One generation regarded glory stained with violence as a form of honor.","The other had embraced a new form of entertainment called sports.","As the two generations clashed, nobles naturally had no choice but to pay attention.","Since soccer was the most popular sport of all, it inevitably became entangled in politics.","Why did I do that... I only did it because I hated seeing Chae-City grow...","On the surface, Keirin was regarded as someone belonging to the generation distant from soccer.","That was because of one of her policies.","She had imposed certain restrictions on Cetan’s gold money.","Part of the reason was that those damned dark elves were notorious for swallowing famous clubs with their obscene spending.","But the biggest reason was the Noisy Neighbor .","Chaemaster City had once been a third-division club.","Then it received an injection of gold money and rose into a powerhouse almost overnight.","It had even won the biggest tournament in the world last year.","Meanwhile, Chae-U continued to struggle.","Keirin’s pride had been thoroughly crushed.","Naturally, it made her blood boil.","That was why she had spoken up just once.","***","Title: Poll—Who Do Chae-U Fans Hate the Most?","The Medes FamilyPrincess Keirin","L I know why people hate the Medes Family, but why Princess Keirin?","L She made the acquisition process much stricter. Otherwise, Chae-U could’ve enjoyed that sweet gold money too.","***","Title: Basically, It Went Like This","Medes Family: We’re selling Chae-U~ Huge bargain sale!","Cetan: Oh! We’ll buy it! Here’s the money!","Keirin: Hell no! Not happening! Policy enacted immediately!","Medes Family: Oh no. The policy means we’ll have to raise the price lol.","Cetan: Fuck this, we’re not buying.","ᄂ Lololol, now I understand perfectly.","L But doesn’t Keirin’s position make sense too?","L Opinion is split about fifty-fifty. Still, to Cheonggu fans, she’s an enemy they want to tear apart lol.","L Doesn’t Keirin hate soccer too?","_ There’s no official statement, but she probably does.","For Keirin, it was enough to make her explode in frustration.","Her love for soccer went beyond even her love for Chae-U.","If she were ever allowed to cut loose, she would attend matches every week.","She might even become a hooligan and cause trouble now and then.","Since she could not do that, she secretly bought jerseys and merchandise to soothe herself.","Of course, watching the matches only made her angry again, but that was beside the point.","Just wait until I become Demon King. I’ll attend matches openly while wearing the jersey.","With soccer at its core, sports had become an area not even the Demon King could recklessly interfere with.","The moment the ruler touched it, they would effectively be declaring hostility toward the people.","That was both the terrifying power of culture and one of its side effects.","Was that not why demons and other races alike had become completely absorbed in it?","Countless forms of magic had been invented merely to develop that single culture.","Broadcasting magic was one example.","Amusingly enough, Mephisto was moving closer and closer not toward victory through conquest, but toward victory through culture.","None of that matters. I just wish they’d stop making such terrible signings.","Keirin sighed inwardly and made a gloomy face.","She no longer looked like the ever-dignified princess of the demons.","She looked like nothing more than a troubled Chae-U supporter.","The gallery was the best place to soothe feelings like these.","There was still plenty of time before the next match anyway.","Wild Grylls... Why did this human end up in the Forest of Four Seasons?","Normally, she spent the days before a match writing about Chae-U or posting nonsense.","Recently, however, that had changed.","Among the endless posts and countless kinds of people, Wild Grylls’ posts stood out.","He was the person who claimed to have fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons.","At first, she had not believed him.","She could not have believed him.","But as time passed, she found herself paying more and more attention.","The biggest reason was that his posts received overwhelmingly more recommendations than others.","He says he came from another world? What a joke.","Whether it was a character gimmick or the ramblings of a lunatic, it was still interesting enough to hold her attention.","She had nothing else to do in her free time anyway.","There were still several days until the next soccer match.","So, partly to pass the time and partly to help him, she had sent him a compass.","Then—","[CheongguPrincess: Then cheer for our Chae-U. That’ll be enough.]","[Wild Grylls: I don’t know much about this world. What kind of team is Chae-U?]","\"What?!\"","Keirin was horrified.","How could anyone not know the famous Chae-U?","Someone living in a remote countryside village might be excused.","But Grylls was a gallery user.","Ninety percent of gallery users were abnormal, but among them, sports fans were unquestionably the most conspicuously abnormal.","Sports fans were not merely insane.","Their minds had rotted beyond repair.","Some had even rotted so completely that they attained enlightenment and became Buddhas.","\"He doesn’t know Chae-U? Then I’ll have to teach him.\"","Keirin began preaching the greatness of Chae-U and even gifted him several jerseys.","Grylls accepted them, albeit somewhat reluctantly.","Keirin did not stop there.","Deciding that she should upload a special highlight reel, she posted a collection of Chae-U highlights on the gallery.","The gallery had a storage function and allowed users to upload videos from outside sources.","That was also why sports highlights could be posted at regular intervals.","Not long after she uploaded the Chae-U special","***","Title: Starting Today, I Am a Chaemes United Fan","(Photo of a thumbs-up directed toward the jerseys laid on the floor.)","Thank you, CheongguPrincess.","Thanks to you, I don’t have to worry as much about clothes anymore.","L Ahhh. The whole world is Chae-U.","ᄂ Of all teams, it had to be Chae-U lololol.","L He’s alone anyway, so does it really matter?","L Better than walking around naked.","L From this day forward, this is the Chaemes United Gallery.","L KingLeor) Why would you give him that garbage? It must smell awful.","Satisfying.","Extremely satisfying.","Keirin smiled proudly as she read Grylls’ post.","As of today, Chae-U had gained one more supporter.","He might be trapped in the Forest of Four Seasons, but a fan was still a fan.","More than anything else, that pleased her.","Now she could support him as much as she wanted.","If a fan dies, Chae-U will be sad too. I need to support him properly so he doesn’t die.","If a Chae-U fan became sad, then Chae-U would be sad as well.","And that might even affect their performance.","It was a one-track line of reasoning, but people were like that.","Once they became deeply obsessed with something, their thoughts naturally grew simpler.","Just as Keirin was about to close the gallery in satisfaction, a comment appeared that immediately irritated her.","Her elegant brow furrowed.","She knew this permanent-name user.","He was a supporter of Leor, Chae-U’s greatest rival.","He was also the user Keirin hated most.","Mocking Chae-U by calling them \"Cheonggu\" whenever he had the chance was only the beginning.","He also had a talent for scraping at her nerves in countless other ways.","L CheongguPrincess) You’re here again? You really must have nothing better to do.","_ KingLeor) As if you’re any better lol. So, did we win or not?","\"You bastard.\"","Keirin swore.","Chae-U had recently lost three-nil to Leor.","The score could only be described as completely one-sided.","That was precisely why the user could mock her.","Those bastards used to be mocked as mid-table trash...!","Ten years earlier, Leor had been a fallen royal house.","But after changing managers, it regained its former prestige.","Meanwhile, Chae-U continued its endless decline.","Changing managers had made no difference.","L CheongguPrincess) Hehe. Once our owner changes, we’ll beat you too.","_ KingLeor) Nope. Keirin is still there~","L Lololol, look at him scraping her nerves.","L After the Medes Family, it’s Keirin lol.","L This rivalry is intense lololol.","_ But isn’t Leor more famous worldwide?","L What the fuck did you just say?","ᄂ I only stated a fact lol.","How could someone be so skilled at getting under her skin?","Keirin clenched her fist.","Unable to control her emotions for a moment, mana began seeping out around her.","She barely managed to suppress it.","Nothing good would come from getting angry now.","She struggled to calm herself.","A sudden fandom war erupted.","\"Hmm... I should probably just keep my damn mouth shut.\"","Grylls silently watched from the sidelines.","It was an exceptionally wise decision."]},{"title":"Chapter 11","paragraphs":["Golden Poison Frog (1)","There was a slang expression: \"the comments got gutted.\"","Put another way, it meant the whole thing had turned into a complete mess.","I had only made the post to express my gratitude, but a few people barged in, and the comment section descended into chaos almost instantly.","It started with CheongguPrincess, followed by KingLeor suddenly crashing in, along with countless anonymous users.","Everyone hurled insults and made jokes about each other’s parents.","The notification chime rang without pause.","Doesn’t the head moderator usually step in when this happens?","As far as I knew, the head moderator intervened when things became too heated.","There had been a similar rule in the pinned notice.","Even if sports fans were the ones arguing, once it devolved into personal attacks, the discussion could no longer be considered sports-related.","L DontAbandonTheHero) Stop it! If you keep spamming, I’ll ban you!","_ CheongguPrincess) That bastard started it first!","_ KingLeor) She’s the one talking nonsense.","L DontAbandonTheHero) Even so, don’t fight under someone else’s post! I’ll open an arena thread, so fight there!","_ CheongguPrincess) Okaaay.","_ KingLeor) Okay lol.","The moment I thought that, the head moderator appeared.","They ordered everyone to stop fighting under my post and take it to the arena instead.","Everyone obediently disappeared.","At last, I was freed from notification hell.","Not long afterward, a new post from the head moderator appeared on the gallery.","[Arena: Which Team Has More Tradition?]","I refreshed the page once, and comments immediately began pouring in.","Nothing good would come from going in there.","I had heard that posts encouraging conflict between nations were bannable, but this seemed to be allowed because it was about sports.","Of course, the head moderator would probably intervene personally if things became too heated.","They seemed fairly competent at their job.","I should focus on my own work.","Now that I had returned all the compasses, I began devising a way to deal with the Golden Poison Frog.","First of all, the river where it lived was a natural fortress in itself.","The water was so clear that it was difficult to judge the depth, and the current was fairly strong as well.","If I entered it, I would probably die from a single spit attack.","That meant a ranged weapon was essential.","A bow would be difficult... A crossbow is probably my best option.","I did not know how to use a bow.","A crossbow, at least, should be relatively easier to handle.","I currently had around 650 gold in my gallery balance.","It was the money I had earned from selling the Steel-Scale Snake.","I had no idea whether that would be enough to buy a crossbow, let alone the specific type I wanted.","For now, I decided to make a post.","***","Title: Crossbow Question","Wild Grylls","I’m planning to catch a frog.","Is there a harpoon-type crossbow?","Something where the bolt stays connected to the crossbow so I can reel the target in after hitting it.","ᄂ SwordMaster) Why do you need a crossbow?","_ Wild Grylls) I need it to catch the frog. The river’s too deep to approach carelessly.","_ SwordMaster) Can’t you just fire sword energy at it?","_ Wild Grylls) ;;;","L SwordMaster) Or you could just walk on the water.","_ Wild Grylls) Sir?","_ PassingDwarf) The kind you described can be made by modifying one.","L Wild Grylls) About how much would that cost?","_ PassingDwarf) Since it’s dwarven-made, around 500 gold. That okay?","Was this guy joking with me?","I was so dumbfounded that a dry laugh escaped me.","Then again, considering the level of swordsmanship knowledge SwordMaster had posted, he might actually have been serious.","Only after I repeatedly emphasized that I was an ordinary person did the conversation finally settle down.","ᄂ Heavenly Demon) Why not master all the internal cultivation methods this Lady has taught you before attempting to catch it?","L Wild Grylls) I still need water to survive, ma’am.","L Heavenly Demon) This Lady can provide you with more than enough water.","L Wild Grylls) Then I won’t be able to ask for your help when I truly need it.","\"What the hell...\"","Why was it so expensive?","Was it studded with diamonds or something?","The price far exceeded my expectations.","I had been told that around 300 gold was enough to cover a commoner’s living expenses for a month.","This went well beyond that.","Maybe it was because it was dwarven-made, just like in fantasy novels.","I had no idea whether that logic applied in this world too.","As I had said before, I intended to ask for help only when I truly needed it.","It was like keeping a special opportunity in reserve.","Until then, I needed to be self-sufficient.","Otherwise, I would have to earn money and buy what I needed from the auction house.","Besides, a crossbow could prove useful in many different situations.","L Wild Grylls) Why is it so damn expensive? Is it plated in gold or something?","L It’s dwarven-made. Of course it’s expensive lol.","_ Isn’t that actually on the cheap side because it’s only a crossbow?","L Crossbow prices vary wildly depending on the maker.","L Crossbows are probably second only to swords in that regard.","_ PassingDwarf) Don’t forget the modification fee. This is genuinely cheap. I’m only offering it like this because I feel bad.","L Wild Grylls) What do you feel bad about?","_ PassingDwarf) For telling you to go become fertilizer. I didn’t know your situation was that serious.","L Wild Grylls) Hmm. How much does a normal crossbow cost?","L PassingDwarf) I don’t know much about human-made ones.","ᄂ Probably around thirty gold.","L A normal bow is around ten gold.","L Wild Grylls) What kind of insane premium is that?","_ PassingDwarf) If you don’t like it, don’t buy it.","L Wild Grylls) Hey now. I never said I wasn’t buying it.","L Lololol, look at that immediate change in attitude.","Either way, this was an opportunity.","PassingDwarf might be the only person capable of providing the exact type of crossbow I wanted.","It was expensive, but if dwarven goods were known for their reliability, then the price might be worth paying.","Even if it turned out to be a scam, I could simply refuse to buy from him again.","If things went badly, I could ask someone else for a crossbow.","L Don’t tell me everything else is also written in the World Tree Watermelon Manual lol.","L Wild Grylls) I’m only using a crossbow because this is urgent. I don’t know how to use a bow.","L LetsGrowTrees) I see. In that case, why not practice archery and learn about the greatness of elves at the same time?","L What greatness? lol.","ᄂ There are plenty of people better at archery than those damn elves lol.","ᄂ Here we go again. The elves are getting active ;;","L LetsGrowTrees) But generally speaking, the bow is the symbol of elves. Let me ask you in return: when you think of archery, which race comes to mind?","ᄂ Damn, that sounds annoying, but she’s right, so I can’t argue.","_ Those damn elves really are good with bows lol.","_ What good does that do? They don’t have a proper frontline, so they get wiped out anyway lol.","Despite being steeped in imperialism, elves apparently still being associated with bows was common knowledge.","At least that part matched what I knew.","I left a comment under the increasingly noisy post.","L LetsGrowTrees) A bow is still superior to a crossbow. This is also proven in the World Tree Watermelon Manual.","L What the hell is with this elf?","ᄂ She’s making that World Tree Watermelon Manual joke again.","L Historically speaking, she’s not wrong...","ᄂ Wild Grylls) My country was really good at archery too.","ᄂ LetsGrowTrees) Were your ancestors perhaps elves?","L Wild Grylls) No, no ;;","L Lololol, look at her. Not a single prejudice in sight.","ᄂ I can’t tell whether that’s good or bad lololol.","L Wild Grylls) Also, the world I lived in only had humans.","L LetsGrowTrees) A world with nothing but humans? That’s impossible!","_ He said he came from another world. Try to be understanding.","L Let it slide. He’s pitiful.","L It’s just a gimmick lol.","While I waited, it seemed PassingDwarf had finished modifying the crossbow.","I immediately sent him a trade request.","A crossbow made by a dwarf.","I wondered how good it would be.","I sincerely hoped it would justify the price.","They still refused to believe that I truly came from another world.","It did not matter much.","Whether they believed me or not, all I had to do was survive here.","ᄂ But was your country really that good at archery?","L Wild Grylls) Yeah. Extremely good. Not me personally, though.","L Was there a reason? Some kind of racial trait?","L Wild Grylls) Because there were a lot of countries above and below us that we wanted to shoot at lol.","L Lolololololol.","L Is this bastard insane? lololololol.","_ PassingDwarf) Hey. I finished the modifications. Send the trade request.","[PassingDwarf has registered trade items.]","[PassingDwarf: I included the harpoon bolt you asked for, plus several other bolts. Just know that the harpoon bolt’s range is really damn short.]","[Wild Grylls: How short?]","[PassingDwarf: Its maximum effective range is around fifty meters.]","Around fifty meters.","At those words, I thought about the stream where the Golden Poison Frog lived.","It was narrow enough to be called a stream rather than a river.","Its depth was the real problem.","Still, considering the range of the frog’s spit, fifty meters was cutting it close.","Ideally, I should hide and launch a surprise attack.","What’s this?","There was a brown bottle sealed with a cork.","The cork told me what it was.","Alcohol.","I remembered PassingDwarf saying before that he would give me a drink, so I should not kill myself.","I had not expected him to actually send it.","For all his rough talk, he had a surprisingly soft heart.","I’ll save this for later.","I planned to use the alcohol as something similar to an anesthetic or painkiller.","Being drunk could dull pain to some extent.","I carefully placed the bottle against the wall so it would not break, then inspected the crossbow.","It had a mostly black frame.","Perhaps because it had been made by a dwarf, even the design looked impressive.","The bolt is connected to it.","The harpoon-shaped bolt was linked to the crossbow by a thin rope.","I had a rough understanding of how it was supposed to work.","I should test it first.","A crossbow was difficult to make, but as far as I knew, using one was not particularly complicated.","I placed my foot into the stirrup-like part at the front of the crossbow.","I had heard that was how it was supposed to be used.","[Wild Grylls: All right lol. I’ve added the money too.]","[PassingDwarf: I included a pair of gloves too, just in case.]","[Wild Grylls: How much are those? I’ll pay extra.]","[PassingDwarf: Stop trying to get ripped off and just take them ;;]","He had already given me toilet paper for free, so I felt bad accepting anything else.","Somehow, I had ended up receiving gloves as well.","Considering that touching the frog carelessly could cause serious trouble, they were quite an appropriate gift.","If I found any valuable medicinal herbs later, I should give them to him.","Or perhaps leather would be better.","Since he was a blacksmith, leather would probably be more useful than herbs.","Let’s see. He sent it in a box.","Once the trade was complete, a box appeared.","I opened the lid of the neatly shaped container.","The first things I saw were the crossbow and the gloves.","Behind them was a bottle.","It was so unexpected that I stared at it in confusion.","I set the crossbow on the ground, secured it with my foot, and pulled the string to cock it—","Clunk.","\"Hm?\"","...Or at least, that was what was supposed to happen.","Why wasn’t it working?","I was slightly flustered.","I pulled on the string, but it would not move.","Instead, my entire body jerked with the effort.","At first, I thought it might have caught on something.","But when I pulled harder, the string slowly began to rise.","\"Grrrrraaaagh!\"","Only after shouting with effort did I barely manage to cock it.","I panted heavily, unable to hide my disbelief.","What kind of crossbow was this that even loading it required so much strength?","Was this normal?","There were superhumans in this world who could shatter mountains with their bare bodies, so it was not impossible.","I sighed and loaded a bolt.","I would start with the harpoon bolt.","I needed to conserve the others, so I planned to practice with the reusable harpoon first.","...It even has a stock, so aiming should be easy.","It was also fairly light for its size.","That made it easy to aim.","I stepped outside the cave and pointed it at a tree some distance away.","If I fired it at the hard stone wall of the cave, the harpoon might break.","A tree was a better target.","Hold my breath...","Thwang!","The moment I pulled the trigger, the sound of air being torn apart reached my ears.","The draw weight was so powerful that the gust stirred my hair.","Thud!","The harpoon flew across the distance and struck the center of a straight tree.","No—","It did not merely lodge itself in the trunk.","It pierced straight through it.","The power was terrifying.","That Golden Poison Frog would not stand a chance against this.","It probably would not even realize what had hit it.","Now I understand why it was so expensive.","I clicked my tongue in amazement at the power, which far exceeded my expectations, then retrieved the harpoon.","Because it was attached to the rope, recovering it was not difficult.","Still, I need to practice.","Part of me wanted to hunt the Golden Poison Frog immediately.","But there was a saying that the more urgent something was, the more carefully one should proceed.","Since reloading took an absurd amount of time, I would only have one chance.","I needed to kill the frog with that single shot.","If I failed, I would have no choice but to turn around and run for my life.","The moment its poison hit me, I was as good as dead.","I had to prepare thoroughly if I wanted to drink as much water as I pleased from now on.","It definitely had nothing to do with being blinded by AllFather’s offer of twenty thousand gold.","Even if only because I feel filthy, I’m definitely taking a bath.","After going two days without washing, I felt unbearably grimy.","It was fortunate that the weather was only moderately warm.","If it had been humid and sweltering, it would have been unbearable.","I continued practicing until sunset.","I even became slightly more accustomed to pulling the string back.","As the sky began to darken, I returned to the cave.","With the money I have left...","After buying the crossbow, I had roughly one hundred gold remaining.","I planned to buy as much as I could with it.","The most urgent items were snake and insect repellents.","I had been lucky so far, but I could easily be bitten by a venomous snake or insect while sleeping.","I also needed antidotes and various medicines.","An antidote was especially essential because of the frog.","The auction house has almost everything, but... it’s all so expensive.","The ridiculous fees were holding me back.","Being able to ignore normal distribution channels was certainly convenient, but the prices were still outrageous.","That did not mean I could simply refuse to buy anything.","Gritting my teeth, I purchased one bottle of antidote.","There was always a chance of being scammed, so I carefully read through the reviews beforehand.","For the repellent... I’ll buy this one.","By the time I finished purchasing everything, I had only twenty gold left.","I did not feel particularly regretful.","Not when these items might extend my life.","I sprayed the repellent around the cave entrance and near the place where I slept.","I had no idea whether it would truly work, but I could only hope.","I had read those reviews carefully too.","Crunch. Crunch.","\"Ugh. This tastes like shit.\"","I did not forget to eat several Wall-Fasting Pills for dinner.","The intensely bitter taste of medicinal herbs spread through my mouth.","I would have to survive on these for a while, so I had no choice but to endure it.","At least I had something to eat.","\"Ughhh...\"","After eating the pills, I tried to sit in the lotus position.","It was not time to sleep yet.","The moment I crossed my legs, pain shot through me as if my joints were being twisted apart.","Even so, I stubbornly endured it.","Was this the posture people used for mana cultivation and internal cultivation techniques?","The Heavenly Demon had offered to teach me, so all I needed to do for now was practice sitting properly.","Will I get used to it after about a week?","Flexibility did not improve overnight.","I would need to keep practicing for several days.","Still, I had nothing else to do before going to sleep, so I had plenty of time.","If I were at home, I would probably be playing games nonstop.","I’m glad I at least have the gallery.","I browsed the gallery while practicing the lotus position.","In truth, the gallery played an enormous role in keeping me sane.","Humans were creatures that struggled to endure loneliness.","There was a reason they were called social animals.","Was it Robinson Crusoe ?","I remembered reading a story about a man stranded on a deserted island who treated a ball like a person.","That was how essential communication was to humans.","For now, the gallery was filling that need.","I should get some sleep soon.","Time passed quickly while I explored the gallery.","I finally uncrossed my legs.","Because I had been reading posts while sitting in the lotus position, I had almost forgotten the pain.","Of course, the instant I became conscious of it again, an overwhelming wave of agony struck me.","Enduring the feeling that my joints were being torn apart, I prepared my sleeping area.","The daytime was warm, but the temperature dropped at night, so a fire was essential.","Crackle! Crackle!","I used the ignition stone the Heavenly Demon had given me and some wood from outside to start a fire.","The cave felt slightly warmer.","On the first day, I had been so exhausted that I had not even noticed the cold.","Besides, I had nearly died after being bitten by the Mad Dog.","I added several pieces of firewood, then made a post on the gallery.","***","Title: End of Survival Day 1","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a single line scratched onto the wall.)","(Photo of a blazing campfire.)","That marks the end of Survival Day 1.","Time to sleep.","_ Heavenly Demon) You have endured much. Rest well.","L SwordMaster) Sleep well.","L So today counts as Day 1?","ᄂ Seems like it. If the updates suddenly stop...","L Ugh ;; That would feel awful.","_ StarlightPrincess) Let’s both keep trying. I’ll be waiting for Day 2.","_ Living on borrowed time versus terminally ill.","L My heart is swelling with emotion.","_ Thank you for supporting Wild Grylls until now.","L StarlightPrincess) You people are truly awful.","Right.","What the hell did I expect from those idiots?","Just to be clear, I meant the anonymous users, not the permanent-name users.","Most of the permanent-name users encouraged me.","The anonymous ones, though...","No explanation was necessary.","Still, it’s better than nothing.","I chuckled and closed the gallery.","Then I lay down on the hard stone floor.","If I caught the Golden Poison Frog tomorrow, should I buy a blanket first?","A pillow might be nice too.","Perhaps because I had gone through another exhausting day, those thoughts did not last long.","Drowsiness began to overtake me.","As my eyes slowly closed and the chirping of insects gradually faded—","I want to go home.","With that desperate wish in my heart, my consciousness completely disappeared."]},{"title":"Chapter 12","paragraphs":["Golden Poison Frog (2)","Normally, falling asleep in the wilderness without any protection was extremely dangerous.","Just yesterday, I had nearly died after being attacked by the Mad Dog in my sleep.","But once someone stayed awake all night, their physical condition inevitably deteriorated.","If sleep was unavoidable, the best option was to prepare as many defenses as possible.","That was why I had spent so much money on snake and insect repellent.","I had roughly blocked the cave entrance with branches and rocks, and I had left the sword right beside me just in case.","Thanks to that, I managed to spend the night safely.","***","Title: A Strong and Powerful Morning!","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the cave with faint light shining inside.)","If you ask me who I am, I am Wild Grylls!","L You survived lol.","L Last time, you got bitten by the Mad Dog.","ᄂ So this is Day 2 now?","L Wild Grylls) Yeah. But one side of my face is stiff. I’m screwed.","L That happens when you sleep on a cold floor lolol.","ᄂ Hang in there lololol.","L Wild Grylls) My whole body aches too. This is bad ;;","Maybe it was because I had slept on the hard stone floor.","Or perhaps it was because I had no pillow.","Either way, my entire body ached.","As if that were not enough, one side of my mouth had gone numb and crooked.","The dawn must have been cold enough for dew to form.","I hurriedly rekindled the firewood, which had almost completely burned out and retained only a little warmth.","Right now, warmth was essential.","It was fortunate that I had used the clothes CheongguPrincess gave me as a blanket.","Otherwise, things could have been dangerous.","Even so, isn’t it way too cold? Did it rain during the night?","The day I was bitten by the Mad Dog had not been this chilly.","After warming myself somewhat, I stepped outside the cave.","The moment I did, I realized it had indeed rained before dawn.","Does the temperature really drop this much just because it rained?","Fog had also settled over the forest, making it difficult to see.","Shivering, I went back inside the cave.","It was so cold that I even put on one of the jerseys CheongguPrincess had given me.","It was surprisingly warm.","For now, I planned to remain inside until the fog cleared.","After that, I would hunt the Golden Poison Frog.","The time is... six in the morning. I woke up way too early.","The sun set early in the forest, so naturally I had no choice but to sleep early as well.","Fortunately, the gallery prevented me from completely losing track of time.","I should eat a few Wall-Fasting Pills for breakfast and wait until the weather cleared.","Until then, I should practice sitting in the lotus position.","My body ached, but that was probably because it had stiffened during the night.","Some light stretching should make it better.","After stretching, I groaned and forced myself into the lotus position.","Strangely enough, it was much easier than yesterday.","Yesterday, it had felt as though my joints were being twisted apart.","Now, it merely hurt a little.","That’s good for me, but...","That was not all.","Despite the aches, my body felt full of energy.","Could it be because of the Wall-Fasting Pills the Heavenly Demon had given me?","She had said they were made from a variety of medicinal herbs, so it seemed likely.","Grrrrrgle!","Ah.","That aside, my stomach had been hurting often.","The worst part was the diarrhea, which made cleaning up an enormous problem.","Fortunately, I had the toilet paper PassingDwarf had given me.","Without it, I would have suffered through several crises already.","I cleaned everything up thoroughly so the smell would not spread.","I would need to build some kind of toilet later.","I should start preparing.","I had gathered most of what I needed to hunt the Golden Poison Frog.","The most important item was the crossbow.","Then there was the Heavenly Demon’s sword and the golden shield PraiseTheSun had given me.","Could I carry all of that?","Yes.","I had separated fibrous strands from trees and woven them into something resembling rope.","It’s only temporary, but it’s sturdy enough.","It was not perfect, but that was fine.","I would strap the shield to my back and hang the sword at my waist.","The crossbow was too large, so I would carry it in my hands.","With that, all preparations were complete.","I had even purchased an antidote, so I was ready for an emergency.","I need to remember to block with the shield.","Before leaving, I made a post on the gallery.","This hunt could become my final one, so I wanted to leave a record.","***","Title: Heading Out!","Wild Grylls","(Photo of me holding the crossbow.)","Twenty thousand gold.","I’m coming for you.","ᄂ Oh. He’s finally going lololol.","L What if we don’t hear from him afterward?","ᄂ Then he died, obviously lol.","L Aww, he died TT","L StarlightPrincess) Please try to encourage him, everyone.","L Heavenly Demon) If you find yourself in danger, initiate a trade with this Lady immediately.","L He probably won’t even have time to trade lololol.","ᄂ One hit and he’s finished~","L Do you seriously think AllFather will pay him twenty thousand gold? lol.","...","That last comment was surprisingly sharp.","Even if I caught the Golden Poison Frog, would AllFather really give me twenty thousand gold?","It would not matter much even if he did not.","I had to kill the Golden Poison Frog if I wanted access to clean water.","Receiving twenty thousand gold would be nice.","If he took the frog and disappeared without paying, I would simply cut ties with him afterward.","Or I could just dump the corpse on him.","Since it was poisonous, handling it would probably be as difficult as preparing pufferfish.","One mistake could kill me.","Rather than taking that risk, I would prefer roasting insects and eating those instead.","If I disposed of the corpse carelessly, I also had no idea what effect it might have on me or the water.","So giving it to AllFather would solve the disposal problem as well.","It would benefit both of us.","Safety comes first right now.","After checking the comments, I cautiously stepped out of the cave.","The time when the forest was still damp with morning dew had passed, and the sun was now somewhat higher in the sky.","Other beasts might appear, so I had no choice but to move carefully, one step at a time.","If I have enough time, I should build a fence too.","Simply blocking the cave entrance was not enough to make it safe.","If an owlbear smashed through everything, it would be over.","I needed to use the cave’s narrow passage to fight anything that entered.","If I only noticed danger after hearing the cave entrance being destroyed, it would already be too late.","So the best option was to gradually build a fence using nearby trees.","It would take a while, but that was fine.","Then I’ll need an axe and a dagger in addition to the sword.","Since I planned to use the cave as a permanent settlement, I needed all kinds of tools.","Fortunately, the gallery made purchasing things easy.","As long as I had money.","If I killed the Golden Poison Frog and received twenty thousand gold, I intended to buy everything I needed.","As for food... I should hunt for it myself whenever possible.","Because of the ridiculous fees, buying food from the auction house was a luxury.","It was also difficult to trust what was being sold.","It might have been different if they had things like fried chicken or pizza, but this world had nothing like that.","One might suggest buying ingredients instead, but very few people sold them.","Because of the auction house’s brutal fees, almost nobody bothered listing basic foodstuffs.","Even when they did, the expiration dates were extremely questionable.","But I absolutely need to buy salt.","No matter how expensive it was, salt was essential.","It was something humans needed to survive.","Hadn’t someone once said that one measure of salt was worth one measure of gold?","That was how important it was.","On Earth, most food was already seasoned, so it was easy to overlook.","That was not the case in this world.","Judging from the general level of civilization, it seemed to be somewhere between the medieval and early modern periods.","Salt would be extremely valuable.","Rooooar—","While thinking about everything I needed for settlement, I eventually arrived at the stream.","Perhaps because of the rain before dawn, or for some other reason, the current seemed stronger than it had been yesterday.","Even so, the water remained so clear that it was almost transparent, and the riverbed was plainly visible.","How am I supposed to lure out that frog?","Now that I had arrived, I realized I had no idea how to draw it out.","I could not simply wait forever.","Should I put my arm into the water like yesterday?","If I did that, bringing the crossbow would have been pointless.","I needed to attack before it noticed me.","Since it was poisonous, I had to be even more careful.","Splash!","While I was still thinking, I heard something burst out of the stream.","I turned toward the sound.","Something golden, about the size of a dog, was soaring high through the air with a fish as large as a salmon clamped in its mouth.","A moment later, the frog—its entire body covered in gleaming gold—landed on a rock in the middle of the stream.","The fish’s tail was still flapping outside its mouth, so it seemed to have just finished hunting.","Lucky me.","Just as AllFather had said, it was active in the morning.","I hid in the bushes and quietly aimed the crossbow.","I would only get one chance.","If I missed, there was no telling when another opportunity would come.","Keeping my nerves under control, I slowly lined up the shot.","The distance was greater than what I had practiced yesterday.","Still, this was a crossbow personally modified by a dwarf.","As long as I aimed properly, I should be able to hit it.","Besides, the frog was almost the size of a dog.","There was little risk of missing.","\"Ribbit.\"","\"...\"","The moment it finished its meal, I held my breath.","Fwing!","Then I pulled the trigger.","The harpoon-shaped bolt shot forward with tremendous force, dragging the attached rope behind it.","There was a slight wobble, but the harpoon flew straight toward the frog.","Thud! Splash!","The bolt struck the frog’s body.","The impact knocked it into the stream.","\"Yes...! Huh?\"","My celebration lasted only a moment.","I barely managed to keep hold of the crossbow as it nearly tore itself from my hands.","I could not tell whether the frog was still alive despite being impaled or whether the current was simply dragging it around, but its violent struggling nearly made me lose the weapon.","And so began an unexpected fishing session.","Instead of holding the crossbow, I grabbed the rope connected to the harpoon and pulled.","It was fortunate that I was wearing gloves.","Otherwise, the rope would have cut deeply into my bare hands.","\"Grrrrraaaagh!\"","Gritting my teeth, I hauled on the rope.","Fortunately, it did not take long before the frog was dragged out of the stream.","Once I confirmed that it was on dry land, I clasped my hands together.","They did not merely ache.","They burned.","Ugh. At least there aren’t any wounds.","When I removed the gloves, I found deep marks across my palms but no actual cuts.","I repeatedly massaged my hands.","Then I carefully pulled the rope closer and examined the frog pierced by the harpoon.","Its long tongue and the fish it had just swallowed were both hanging out of its mouth.","It was completely motionless.","It was definitely dead.","\"Hehehe.\"","This dog-sized bastard was worth twenty thousand gold.","Twenty thousand gold was equivalent to approximately two hundred million won.","No matter how absurd the auction-house fees were, there would still be more than enough I could do with that much money.","Still, I needed to handle it carefully.","I was wearing gloves, but there was no such thing as being too cautious.","\"Ribbit.\"","\"Hm?\"","What?","Was this thing still alive?","I tilted my head at the sound.","But even after checking again, the frog remained dead with its tongue hanging out.","Besides, the sound had not come from it in the first place.","If it wasn’t this one...","With a sinking feeling, I turned my head toward the stream.","\"Ribbit, ribbit, ribbit.\"","\"Ribbit. Ribbit.\"","\"Ribbit.\"","And then I saw them clearly.","Several Golden Poison Frogs were sitting on the rocks.","The one I had caught had been the size of a small dog.","These were only about the size of large toads.","The problem was their numbers.","There were so many that they might have been an entire family.","...First, I should take a picture.","Even as I slowly backed away, I took a photograph.","It was not because I was a gallery addict.","I was simply curious how AllFather would react when he saw it.","Would he pay twenty thousand gold for each of them?","Or would he offer less?","More importantly, how was I supposed to get water from now on?","I already felt filthy from being unable to bathe.","\"Hrrraaaak!\"","\"Kraaak!\"","The Golden Poison Frogs all tilted their heads backward at once.","It was the signal that they were about to fire poison.","One frog would have been manageable.","If several fired simultaneously, there would be nowhere to dodge.","I hurriedly pulled the golden shield from my back.","\"Ptoo!\"","\"Ptooh!\"","\"Puh!\"","Golden blobs of poison shot toward me at high speed.","I rapidly retreated while blocking them with the shield.","Perhaps because it was ordinary poison rather than acid, the shield did not melt.","Or maybe the shield itself was simply that good.","I should send PraiseTheSun a message of thanks later.","For now, getting back to the cave came first.","This is such bullshit.","After barely making it back to the cave, I let out a long sigh.","Every obstacle only led to another.","Still, the hunt had not been entirely fruitless.","I had caught what seemed to be the leader of the Golden Poison Frogs.","I would have to comfort myself with the twenty thousand gold.","The drinking-water problem would need to be solved gradually.","***","Title: What a Weak Little Bastard lol","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the Golden Poison Frog impaled on the harpoon.)","Frog bastard eliminated lol.","L Damn, look at the size of that thing lolol.","_ Is that really a frog? lololol.","ᄂ What’s it holding in its mouth?","ᄂ Isn’t that a fish?","_ Wild Grylls) Yeah. I caught it while it was eating the fish.","_ You attacked it while it was eating? lololol.","L That’s seriously underhanded lololol.","L Even dogs aren’t bothered while they’re eating lol.","L Wild Grylls) It’s not a dog, though lol.","_ Heavenly Demon) Were you injured anywhere?","L Wild Grylls) No. I’m fine. The hunt itself was unexpectedly easy.","_ Heavenly Demon) That is a relief. This Lady prepared an antidote in case it was needed, so tell me if you require it.","L Wild Grylls) I’m okay. I already have one antidote, and there’s something else I need to think about.","_ AllFather) Oh! You caught it. May I initiate the trade immediately?","L Wild Grylls) Before that, I’m going to make one more post. I think you’ll really like it.","_ AllFather) Something I would like? How intriguing.","He was going to love it.","I had taken the photograph in advance precisely for this reason.","The gallery had a photo-album function, allowing users to upload any picture whenever they wished.","I posted the photograph of the Golden Poison Frog family gathered peacefully together.","****","Title: AllFather, Look at This","Wild Grylls","(Photo of several Golden Poison Frogs gathered together.)","Do these things normally live in groups?","There were a lot of them.","ᄂ AllFather) Ooooooh...! Forgive my vulgarity, but I find myself becoming aroused below.","L Is this guy really a professor? That was unbelievably vulgar lololol.","As expected, there was not a single normal person on the gallery."]},{"title":"Chapter 13","paragraphs":["Golden Poison Frog (3)","It took me only a moment to realize that even Allfather was borderline abnormal. Then I turned my attention to the drinking-water problem.","It wasn’t as though I had any resistance to poison, and the golden poison frog’s venom was especially deadly.","How deadly did it have to be to make a tree sizzle and melt? If it hit me, I would be finished instantly.","I had bought an antidote just in case, but I had no idea whether it would actually work.","So I planned to make a separate request of Allfather—something more valuable than money.","[Wild Grylls: Hello. You’re Allfather, correct?]","[Allfather: Yes, I am. Thank you for initiating the trade.]","The moment I sent Allfather a trade request, he replied. His manner of speaking was far more refined than that of the others.","Judging by how he had immediately identified the golden poison frog and by the posts he normally wrote in the Gallery, he seemed to be some kind of academic, perhaps a professor.","An extremely wealthy academic, at that. He had been willing to burn twenty thousand gold on a single frog, so I couldn’t even begin to guess what he did for a living.","Then again, I barely knew who anyone here really was.","[Wild Grylls: You need the frog, right? I’ll register it immediately.]","[Allfather: Thank you. As promised, I will register twenty thousand gold. However, are you aware that trades exceeding ten thousand gold transmit your location to the moderators?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. I know.]","Trades worth more than ten thousand gold automatically transmitted the participants’ locations to the moderators because there were too many ways such transactions could be abused.","They could be used to launder illegally acquired profits or purchase war supplies in bulk.","Gold charged into the Gallery could not be converted back into cash, but there were still plenty of opportunities for misuse.","Of course, since I was in the Forest of Four Seasons, it hardly mattered. In fact, having my location transmitted might not be entirely bad.","[Wild Grylls: Before that, may I ask one more favor? If you agree, I’ll lower the price from twenty thousand gold to fifteen thousand.]","[Allfather: Hmm? What kind of favor?]","[Wild Grylls: I need an antidote suitable for the golden poison frog’s venom. As you saw in my earlier post, I’m having trouble securing water.]","There might have been another river nearby. However, that stream was the closest source of water.","As long as the golden poison frog remained there, I could neither wash myself nor obtain drinking water.","Searching for another river would also be extremely difficult, since I might get lost.","[Allfather: I believe I understand your situation. I accept your request. As it happens, I was interested in researching that aspect as well.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. We can consider the remaining five thousand gold payment for the antidote. Would having more specimens make your research easier?]","[Allfather: Naturally. However, golden poison frogs are extremely rare, so please take care not to drive them to extinction.]","I wasn’t so sure about that.","No matter how precious the golden poison frog was, could it possibly be more valuable than my life?","If the antidote worked, that would be a different story. But if it didn’t, I might have to wipe out every golden poison frog in the area.","I had recently learned just how important a stable water supply was. Not being able to wash was driving me insane.","Whenever a transaction exceeded ten thousand gold, the user’s location was immediately sent to the head moderator.","The rule was supposedly meant to prevent abuse, but the head moderator could also abuse it.","I didn’t know the exact conditions or method by which a head moderator was selected, but there must have been previous head moderators as well.","I suddenly became curious about the Gallery’s history, but that wasn’t something I needed to worry about right now.","[Allfather: If you discover any rare plants or animals in the future, or anything you have never seen before, please make a post about it. I will answer to the best of my knowledge.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. I’ll see you next time.]","[Allfather: It is rare to find someone as polite as you in the Gallery, Mr. Grylls. How remarkable. Please stay safe.]","And with that, my trade with Allfather came to an end.","As soon as the transaction was completed, I checked the money deposited into my Gallery account.","A small fee had been deducted because of the size of the transaction, but nearly fifteen thousand gold had still been credited to my account.","I could use it to purchase various supplies from the auction house. I had already considered what I needed.","’Before that, I should ask the head moderator where my location shows up.’","Title: Head Mod, Can You See My Location?","Wild Grylls","I just traded with Allfather. Can you see where I am?","_DontAbandontheHero: Yes! It says you’re in the Forest of Four Seasons! Right in the middle of it, too!","└ Wild Grylls: Ah, f—","└ LMAOOOOO","└ LMAOOOOO","└ Abandon all hope kekekekeke","_ Officially confirmed by the head mod: Forest of Four Seasons, LOL.","I shouldn’t have asked.","I suppressed the despair surging through me.","The Gallery was supposed to be inaccessible from the Forest of Four Seasons, yet I was an exception. It had even clearly revealed my location.","Who the hell was playing this kind of prank on me?","I couldn’t understand it at all.","└ Wild Grylls: You’re seriously not lying?","_DontAbandontheHero: Yes! I swear on my holy sword that it’s true!","_ Grylls, let’s just give up already...","└ You’re going to have to live there.","Those bastards.","Was escaping not even considered an option?","Now that even the head moderator had confirmed it, all I could do was let out a bitter sigh. Even the last shred of hope had vanished.","Escaping would be difficult anyway. The landscape changed constantly even just beyond the stream, severely limiting the area in which I could move.","’Fine. I’ll survive here. But I’m definitely going to escape.’","Even if it took years, I wanted to see civilization again someday.","I immediately wrote another post in the Gallery.","This time, it wasn’t to complain about my situation. I wanted to ask what supplies I would need from now on.","Title: Survival Experts, Help","Wild Grylls","Looks like I’ll have to live in the forest from now on, so I’m planning to buy some supplies.","So far, I’ve thought of an axe, dagger, shovel, hammer, emergency rations, water, soap, medicine, and stuff like that. Is there anything else I need?","└ Use unscented soap if possible. The smell might attract bears.","_ If you know how to set traps, make some around your shelter. No idea whether they’ll work in the Forest of Four Seasons, though.","└ You should definitely gather charcoal. You can use it to filter water or even brush your teeth.","└ That’s useful, but the warmth might attract snakes.","_ Never eat mushrooms unless it’s an emergency.","They weren’t being sarcastic. They sincerely taught me useful survival tips one by one.","I hadn’t known about the charcoal in particular.","As for snakes, I could probably deal with them using repellent. That was why I had spent so much money buying it.","└ Nobody knows what’s in the Forest of Four Seasons, so everything will probably be dangerous.","└ You’ll likely have to learn most things through personal experience.","└ Yeah, that’s probably right.","└ When would anyone ever have a reason to enter the Forest of Four Seasons? Kek.","But those were ultimately only the most basic principles of ordinary wilderness survival.","I was the first person to actually live in the Forest of Four Seasons.","There was already a frog the size of a dog wandering around. The truth was that no one knew what else might be out there.","’Still, I should buy whatever I can.’","One by one, I purchased the items recommended by the adventurers.","It would be best to use this cave as my base.","Finally, I bought a large sheet of paper, a quill, and a bottle of ink.","Since the compass didn’t work, I planned to create a map using nothing but my own sense of direction.","’I should mainly mark the places where the terrain changes constantly.’","There was a good chance places other than the stream changed in the same way. Knowing which areas did so would make it easier to move around.","It would also be wise to mark the zones where dangerous beasts appeared. More precisely, their territories.","Perhaps the reason no other beasts had approached this place until now was because it had originally been the mad dog’s territory.","But that protection would not last forever. The owlbear had already devoured the mad dog’s corpse with great enthusiasm.","There was no guarantee that the owlbear would not come here next. I needed to prepare for that possibility.","\"Hmm...\"","I crossed my arms as I looked at the various supplies I had purchased.","What should I do first?","People said that when you were truly busy, you had so many things to do that you couldn’t even decide where to begin. That described my situation perfectly.","Should I build a fence and secure the area first, or explore the surroundings a little more?","The former would take far too long, while the latter would leave me vulnerable in the future.","’I don’t even know how long building a fence will take.’","This was the kind of situation where I should ask for advice.","I wrote another post in the Gallery.","If it looked like the work would take too long, I would explore the area instead.","Title: I’m Planning to Build a Fence Around My Home. Any Advice?","Wild Grylls","I want to build a fence to prevent intruders from getting in. Any advice?","_Passing Dwarf: Do you even know how to build a fence?","└ Wild Grylls: You just hammer it together, right?","└ Passing Dwarf: ;;;","└ \"Just hammer it together,\" LMAO.","_ That phrasing is killing me, kekekeke.","└ Passing Dwarf: Anyway, what you’re imagining is probably closer to a defensive wall than a fence. You said there’s an owlbear nearby, right?","└ Wild Grylls: Y-Yeah.","└ Passing Dwarf: In that case, you’d be better off setting traps near the entrance. Give yourself at least one or two months to build a wall properly.","└ Wild Grylls: One or two months? I’m making it out of wood.","_ Passing Dwarf: If you don’t believe me, go make one right now.","└ Wild Grylls: Fine, I will.","Thud!","Was he serious?","Even as I looked at the post with suspicion, I got to work. Actions spoke louder than words.","Trees were everywhere nearby, so acquiring materials would be easy. I had also bought an axe specifically for logging.","’This axe is heavier than I expected.’","Even holding it with both hands, I could feel its considerable weight.","I stood in front of a moderately sized tree.","It grew straight upward without bending, making it ideal for building a defensive wall.","Still, one month was ridiculous.","Confidently, I swung the axe.","’As expected of a new axe. It feels great in the hands.’","At this rate, it wouldn’t take long at all.","Passing Dwarf had seriously underestimated me.","\"Huff... Huff...\"","I take that back.","He hadn’t underestimated me. His assessment had been extremely objective.","Panting heavily, I stared at the tree.","Despite chopping at it with all my strength, I hadn’t even cut halfway through.","The outer layers had been manageable, but the closer I got to the center, the harder the wood seemed to become.","’I have a newfound respect for lumberjacks.’","The woodcutters who appeared all the time in fairy tales had actually been incredible people.","No wonder so many of them had several children to support.","I wiped away the sweat pouring down my face and stared at the half-cut tree.","If cutting down a single tree was this difficult, there was no way I could build an entire defensive wall.","Humans truly were helpless when working alone.","In the end, I had no choice but to postpone building the wall.","Just as Passing Dwarf had said, setting traps would be better.","Title: F—, Why Is This Tree So Hard?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a slightly chopped tree)","This is killing me.","└ It’s hard now that you’ve actually tried it, isn’t it?","_ Did you think logging was a joke?","└ You had it easy all this time because other people did the hard work for you, huh? LMAO.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m sorry. I’ll never act cocky again.","└ SwordMaster: Learning a mana cultivation technique would make it somewhat easier.","_ Heavenly Demon: The one above speaks the truth. Hurry and begin by practising the lotus position.","_ Wild Grylls: O-Okay. I will.","_ Did all his confidence just disappear?","_ That’s better than acting recklessly and getting himself killed.","_ Passing Dwarf: See that you do not get cocky again.","└ Wild Grylls: Yes, brother.","└ He suddenly became so respectful, LMAO.","Thanks to them, I was able to settle on a clear course of action.","I would create traps near the cave entrance that only I knew about.","The defensive wall could wait until after I trained in whatever internal-energy or mana cultivation technique they were talking about.","At my current level, it consumed far too much stamina.","’Digging will take a long time too.’","Having completed military service, I knew all too well how exhausting it was to shovel dirt.","It usually took three or four people working together an entire day to construct a single defensive position.","Moreover, considering the size of the owlbear I had seen, I would have to dig much deeper than my own height.","’This is seriously hopeless.’","Nothing was easy.","Humans were far too powerless in the wilderness.","But did that mean I would give up?","Absolutely not.","Little strokes fell great oaks. If I kept working steadily, my efforts would eventually bear fruit.","’First, I’ll dig deeply around the entrance. I can work on the surrounding area later. I can also buy some fabric from the auction house to use as camouflage.’","Thinking about traps gave me another good idea.","Rather than relying only on traps, I could dig up the ground around the entrance and the cave itself.","Like the moats that surrounded castles in the old days, it would be enough as long as it prevented outside intruders from approaching.","For now, I could also use the excavated soil to form a temporary wall.","Later, I could slowly replace it with a wooden one.","’Good. Let’s start immediately.’","Nothing would happen if I only made plans.","I began designing the area around the cave entrance.","I marked where I would dig the moat, where I would pile the earth to make a temporary defensive wall, and finally, where I would leave an entrance for myself.","It was far from perfect, but it should at least help protect me.","Thud!","I drove the shovel into the ground.","Thanks to the rain early that morning, the soil was somewhat soft.","Logging had been difficult, but digging was at least manageable.","It would still take a long time, though.","’Let’s take it slowly, one step at a time.’","The fortress-building project that I had begun with such enthusiasm...","\"Owww... My whole body aches...\"","...rewarded me with crippling muscle pain the following day."]},{"title":"Chapter 14","paragraphs":["Mandrake (1)","It was fairly common to wreck your body while digging. Shoveling itself was work that required a terrifying amount of physical effort.","Without proper technique, it would be impossible to move normally the next day. Fortunately, I had completed military service.","I had at least some experience, so I could still move. Otherwise, I probably would have been bedridden all day.","’Isn’t there anything like a pain-relief patch?’","I massaged my tightly knotted muscles and logged into the Gallery, hoping to find something similar to a medicated patch.","Unfortunately, there was nothing of the sort. It seemed to be one of the limitations of the era.","Instead, I made a post asking whether there was any medicine effective against muscle pain.","Title: What’s Good for Muscle Pain?","Wild Grylls","I pulled a muscle digging yesterday.","_SwordMaster: Mana cultivation is good for muscle pain.","└ Wild Grylls: Mana cultivation can’t possibly cure everything. ;;","_Heavenly Demon: It appears you are unfamiliar with such matters. An internal-energy cultivation method—more precisely, circulating and regulating one’s energy—is indeed effective against muscle pain.","└ Wild Grylls: Is there any medicinal herb instead?","_SwordMaster: You should usually leave muscle pain alone. If you treat it with medicine, your muscles won’t grow as effectively.","└ Heavenly Demon: This is the first time I have heard such knowledge. Are you certain?","└ SwordMaster: Probably? I have a constitution that makes me stronger just by breathing.","└ Heavenly Demon: You are similar to this lady.","└ Wild Grylls: What the hell...?","_ A bunch of shut-ins are talking like that, LMAO.","_ Does such a constitution actually exist?","└ If it did, the government would have recruited them already.","I wished I had a constitution like that.","I let out a sigh.","In the end, it seemed best to endure the muscle pain. It wasn’t so severe that I couldn’t move at all, so I could probably tolerate it.","Still, working today would be difficult. If I pushed myself any further, my urine might turn cola-colored tomorrow.","’Forget the muscle pain. I just want to wash.’","I hadn’t washed in three days, and the grimy feeling was driving me insane. Oil was practically streaming down my face.","But I couldn’t go to the river either.","I couldn’t trade my life for a shower.","At least the forest was cool and not very humid. If this had been a jungle, it would have been unbearable.","’For now, I should buy some water. It feels wasteful, but I have no choice.’","I needed to maintain a minimum level of cleanliness to avoid harming my health. At the very least, I had to wash my hands.","I purchased a large quantity of water from the Gallery auction house.","It was painful to spend the money, but I had no other option until I found another river.","The water arrived with a bucket. Before washing, I tested its quality.","’Since I bought it from the auction house, I can’t just trust it blindly.’","Fortunately, it was exactly as the reviews had described: perfectly ordinary water.","It had been drawn from a well.","I used it to wash my face, hands, feet, and finally the areas where sweat tended to accumulate.","I also used soap. Following yesterday’s advice, I chose one with almost no fragrance.","Once I had roughly cleaned myself, I wiped down thoroughly with a towel I had purchased from the auction house.","It wasn’t a proper shower, but even that made me feel considerably refreshed.","Crunch. Crunch.","\"Ugh... Bitter. So bitter.\"","Then came breakfast.","My face twisted naturally as I chewed the disgustingly bitter fasting pills.","These fasting pills were truly fascinating. I only had to chew a few, yet almost all sense of hunger disappeared.","Just as the Heavenly Demon had said, perhaps they really were made from medicinal herbs that were good for the body. I didn’t feel hungry at all.","Of course, considering their tiny size, I couldn’t expect to feel full.","Even so, I was fairly satisfied.","’Meat is a luxury for someone in my position.’","I should be grateful that no carnivorous beast had come to this cave yet.","After finishing breakfast, I looked inside the pouch containing the fasting pills.","There were still plenty left, but they wouldn’t last forever.","I could ask the Heavenly Demon for more, but she had said they were made from valuable medicinal herbs. Asking would only burden her.","’I can’t depend on the Gallery. I need to keep reminding myself of that.’","Ordinarily, accessing the Gallery from the Forest of Four Seasons was impossible.","For reasons unknown, I was able to do so.","Put another way, there was no telling when I might suddenly lose access.","I needed to improve my own abilities in preparation for that possibility.","It was a resolution I made over and over again.","’Today, let’s go in the opposite direction from the river.’","It was the area where I had abandoned the mad dog’s corpse and where the owlbear had appeared.","Because of the owlbear, I hadn’t dared to set foot there for some time.","But that was no longer an option.","Even if it only raised my chances of escape by 0.01 percent, I needed to take risks and explore.","I intended to use this place as a base and create a safe zone around it. I had no intention of living as a complete wilderness hermit forever.","Choosing to live here in the first place was already the worst possible option.","Even if it took time, I still held on to the hope of escaping.","’I’ll take the sword and shield.’","I left the crossbow behind.","It was too large, and in an emergency, it would be less useful than a sword.","Most importantly, reloading after a single shot took far too long. That delay alone could cause serious trouble.","Besides, I needed to practise the basic swordsmanship SwordMaster had posted.","I had been studying it little by little whenever I had time.","’When bracing myself, I put my left leg forward...’","Before setting out, I checked my stance.","A sword-and-shield warrior was an exceptionally well-balanced combat class.","The reassuring weight of the shield gave me such a strong sense of security that I didn’t have to worry about being overwhelmed by an opponent’s presence.","Shields were so absurdly effective that I had once heard ancient gladiators were sometimes forced to fight without them because they were considered too unfair.","’Let’s go.’","With slight nervousness, I stepped outside the cave.","The unfinished hole I had begun digging yesterday remained near the entrance.","Once I returned from exploring, I would have to start shoveling again.","Just imagining it was horrifying.","But I couldn’t simply leave it unfinished.","Being alone was truly miserable.","Title: Heading Out to Explore","Wild Grylls","(Photo of me looking into the forest while holding a sword and shield)","Today, I’m going in the opposite direction from the river.","For reference, it’s where the owlbear appeared.","_Heavenly Demon: Is that not dangerous? You still have many fasting pills, so I believe it would be best to master an internal-energy cultivation method before going.","└ SwordMaster: The Heavenly Demon is right. Wouldn’t it be better to train inside first?","└ Starlight Princess: You’re not actually going to make your life as fragile as a fly’s, are you...?","└ PraiseTheSun: I went through the trouble of giving you that shield. It would be rather upsetting if you died.","_ Passing Dwarf: My crossbow weeps... It weeps...","└ Wild Grylls: Can’t you all just cheer me on...? I’ll run away immediately if an owlbear appears.","└ He’s sulking, LMAO.","_ We can’t help it. We’re genuinely worried about you, LOL.","└ That just means everyone cares about you.","└ The Gallery will be sad if you die.","\"...\"","It felt nice to know that so many people cared about me, just as the comments said.","Was this why people became addicted to browsing the Gallery?","Unlike genuine attention seekers, I desperately needed conversations with other people.","How would I have survived the loneliness if I hadn’t had the Gallery?","’No, that’s wrong. The mad dog would have killed me.’","With that thought, I headed toward the area where the owlbear had appeared before.","When I reached the place where I had discarded the mad dog’s corpse, I found it surprisingly clean.","Some bones, scraps of flesh, and part of the head remained, but it was far better than leaving the entire corpse untouched.","If the owlbear hadn’t dealt with it, the body would have been swarming with maggots and insects while giving off a terrible stench.","’Still, I shouldn’t get close.’","Using the mad dog’s corpse as a landmark, I turned right.","The trees were densely packed in that direction.","Open terrain was somewhat dangerous. If I encountered the owlbear there, I might not be able to escape.","Of course, considering its house-sized body, it could probably knock the trees down while chasing me.","But I still had to increase my chances of survival, even if only slightly.","\"There are quite a lot of trees.\"","As I pushed through them, I made sure to mark the trunks with my sword.","If anything about the terrain felt strange, I intended to turn around immediately without looking back.","Space twisted and tangled here as badly as my own life, so I needed to remain especially cautious.","\"Heave-ho. Huh?\"","When I emerged from the densely packed trees, a clearing spread out before me.","It was quite large and covered with thick weeds.","’...Is a boss monster going to appear?’","In games, places like this were exactly where boss monsters tended to jump out.","Just in case, I walked back toward the trees.","The location might suddenly change, so I had to be careful.","After observing the area for a while, however, I realized that the likelihood of it shifting was low.","The clearing was somewhat large, but I couldn’t find anything visibly unnatural about it.","Most Gallery users concluded that the plants were radishes.","To be honest, they did look like radishes.","Apparently, radishes bore fruit as well.","In that case, wouldn’t it be fine to pull one out?","Judging by the ring of trees surrounding the clearing, perhaps this place was simply unusual.","’Why? Why is the boundary here so distinct?’","It wasn’t unnatural, but the boundary was clearly defined.","Without lowering my guard, I examined the supposed weeds in the clearing.","Upon closer inspection, they weren’t weeds at all. They were fruit-bearing plants.","Bright red fruit hung from them like raspberries.","They might have been poisonous, so I had no intention of eating them.","Instead, I took a photo and posted it in the Gallery.","Title: Anyone Know What This Is?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a plant bearing raspberry-like fruit)","Does anyone know what this is? There are tons of them here.","└ Aren’t those raspberries?","└ They look more like radishes. Look at the leaves.","└ Radishes bear fruit?","_ They do, but I think these look a little different.","└ Allfather: Oh? You must not pull those out carelessly. This is only a guess, but they may be mandrakes.","└ Wild Grylls: What’s a mandrake?","└ Allfather: A plant that screams when its root is pulled from the ground. Hearing the scream will not kill you, but it will cause severe damage to your hearing.","└ Doesn’t hearing the scream kill you?","└ That’s what I heard too.","_Allfather: That is a distorted version of the truth. A mandrake’s scream induces temporary confusion, but it is not fatal.","└ Then where did the story about people dying come from?","└ Allfather: Human greed. Mandrakes are exceedingly rare plants. Many people have killed one another while trying to claim them. In most such cases, their actions were treated leniently because they had supposedly been affected by the confusion.","_ Humans are scarier than the mandrakes. ;;","└ Typical damn humans.","_ Why are humans suddenly getting blamed?","└ Whenever something like this happens, it always turns out to be humans, LOL.","└ Damn, this bastard’s being racist against an entire species.","In any case, pulling one out would only be somewhat noisy.","It wouldn’t put my life in danger.","Still, hearing damage would be troublesome, so I needed to prepare properly.","└ Seriously. Does he think mandrakes are weeds? LOL.","└ It’s the Forest of Four Seasons. They might actually be real.","└ It won’t be too late to decide after he pulls one out.","└ If those really are mandrakes, that’s an incredible find.","└ Wild Grylls: Are mandrakes expensive?","└ What kind of question is that? They’re one of the main ingredients used to make elixirs.","└ They’re also insanely difficult to harvest, so the auction house would go wild if you listed one.","└ Allfather: (Photo of the plant) (Photo of a human-shaped root)","_ Allfather: It should be easier if you compare it with these.","While everyone argued back and forth, Allfather uploaded some pictures.","I compared them with the plant in front of me.","Its outward appearance was identical to the one in the photograph, but the fruit was different.","The fruit in Allfather’s picture was green, whereas the ones before me were red.","’Are the fruits ripe?’","Just in case, I purchased a pair of earplugs from the auction house.","They looked similar to ones from Earth.","The description claimed they were also used by soldiers, though I didn’t know much about that. As long as they sealed my ears tightly, that was enough.","Since the root was supposedly shaped like a person, it shouldn’t be difficult to identify.","└ Wild Grylls: Do I just pull it out? There’s no chance I’ll hear the sound.","_ Allfather: If you are fully prepared, simply pull it out firmly, just as you would pull up a radish.","└ Wild Grylls: Okay.","So I only had to grab it and pull with all my strength.","I immediately got to work.","Now that I was wearing earplugs, I should be fine even if it screamed.","The product description claimed they could even block the sound of cannon fire.","That might have been an exaggeration, but the reviews suggested they were highly reliable.","After letting out a nervous breath, I pulled with all my might.","\"Heave... ho!\"","Pop!","I felt it catch on something halfway through, but I managed to pull it out without much trouble.","I immediately examined the plant’s root.","According to the Gallery, mandrakes were shaped like humans.","Not exactly human, but close enough to resemble one.","\"Huh?\"","However, what I had pulled out was far stranger than that.","To be more precise, it looked like an actual person.","It didn’t merely have a humanoid shape. Its proportions were exactly the same as a person’s.","Its arms and legs were clearly defined, and even its facial expression was distinct.","It even had fine, beard-like hairs growing along its chin.","Rather than merely resembling a person, it looked as though someone had copied an actual human appearance onto the root.","To make matters stranger, it stood with its arms crossed, looking unbearably dignified.","’And why is it so red? Is this a mandrake or red ginseng?’","It resembled a mandrake, but there were far too many differences.","I would have to ask the others directly.","Flash!","Just as I was about to log into the Gallery, the root, whose eyes had been closed, suddenly snapped them open.","Because its entire body was red, I didn’t realize at first that it had opened its eyes.","Only when it slowly uncrossed its arms did I finally notice.","\"Huh?\"","\"Huuuuup...!\"","While I stood there in confusion, the root began drawing in an enormous breath.","That was when I felt something was wrong.","I hurriedly tried to release it, but the situation Allfather had warned me about unfolded first.","[UWOOOOOOOOOOOOH!]","A scream—no, a monstrous roar—pierced straight through the earplugs.","Without them, my hearing wouldn’t merely have been damaged. My eardrums would have burst.","I grimaced and stumbled backward.","Because I had clapped both hands over my ears, I ended up dropping the mandrake.","Was it going to burrow back into the ground?","I cautiously opened the eyes I had squeezed shut.","Why was it just standing there?","It had merely let out one roar before crossing its arms again.","Because it looked so much like a person, it seemed to be staring up at me with a deeply displeased expression.","According to Allfather, it should have continued screaming until it was replanted.","So what exactly was this?","Rumble—!","While I was still wondering, an earthquake suddenly struck.","I nearly lost my balance.","First a monstrous roar, and now an earthquake.","That didn’t seem like a good sign.","’Let’s just grab this one and leave.’","I hurriedly seized the mandrake.","To stop it from roaring again, I forcefully clamped my hands over its mouth.","The root itself was so thick that covering its mouth was difficult, but using both hands made it possible.","\"Mmph! Mmph! Mmph!\"","Apparently, it hadn’t expected me to gag it, because it began struggling violently.","That was what it got for standing there with its arms crossed.","All I had to do was return to the cave.","Without wasting another moment, I started moving.","Pop! Pop!","\"Huh...?\"","What the hell were those things?","I stopped before I could take another step.","Red, human-shaped figures were emerging from the ground all around me.","The entire clearing churned as though corpses buried in a graveyard were rising from the dead.","The creatures emerging from the earth looked exactly like the mandrake that had just roared.","There were men, women, children, and elderly figures mixed among them, but since every single one was red, they were undoubtedly mandrakes.","’I’m screwed.’","This was bad.","No, it went beyond bad. It felt ominous.","Still holding the mandrake, I turned my back on them.","I had a rough idea of what they were about to do.","Hadn’t the golden poison frogs done something similar only yesterday?","The difference was that I could block the frogs’ poison with my shield.","Sound was another matter.","My only option was to run as far away as possible.","Worse still, I was using both hands to keep the mandrake’s mouth shut.","\"Hiss!\"","\"Huuup!\"","By the time I reached the densely packed trees—","[UWOOOOOOOOOOOOH!]","An enormous shock wave slammed into my back.","***","Title: What Should You Do After Being Hit by a Sound Attack?","Wild Grylls","A whole group of mandrakes screamed at once. Does anyone know how to treat this?","└ Heavenly Demon: A sound attack and a scream? Were you struck by a Lion’s Roar?","└ Wild Grylls: Something similar.","└ Heavenly Demon: How badly were you injured?","└ Wild Grylls: My ears keep ringing.","└ Heavenly Demon: Then it seems you were struck properly. Have you lost your hearing, or is there blood coming from your ears?","_ Wild Grylls: Fortunately, no. I was wearing earplugs.","└ Heavenly Demon: Then your hearing is unlikely to have suffered permanent damage. With sufficient rest, you should recover quickly. However, you will likely suffer from tinnitus for a while, so I shall obtain medicine for you.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you. Have you ever been hit by a Lion’s Roar, Heavenly Demon?","└ Heavenly Demon: I have. This lady tore out the bastard’s throat so that he would never shout again for the rest of his life.","└ Wild Grylls: Sh-Shiver...","└ What the hell did you do to make a whole group of mandrakes scream?","_ Wild Grylls: I pulled one out, and when it roared, all the others came out of the ground on their own.","└ ??? I’ve never heard of that happening.","└ Are you sure those were mandrakes?","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll upload a picture.","Title: Is This Really a Mandrake?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a battered red mandrake)","It really does look like a person, but why is its body so red?","└ What happened to it? Its face looks like it got beaten to hell.","└ Wild Grylls: It kept making noise, so I grabbed it by the head and slammed it into a wall. I also stuffed dirt into its mouth.","└ That’s seriously cruel, LOL.","_ Silence magic—physical edition, LMAO.","_ Aren’t mandrakes plants? Can they even feel pain?","└ They’re closer to monsters, so they do feel pain. But this is the first time I’ve heard of someone beating one until it shut up, LOL.","└ Do mandrakes normally look like that, though?","└ I heard they resemble people, but that thing is practically human.","└ At that point, isn’t it just a monster rather than a mandrake?","└ Normal mandrakes look vaguely human, which makes them unsettling. That one looks exactly human, so it feels even stranger.","└ Maybe it’s some kind of hundred-year-old mandrake?","└ LOL, what is this, wild ginseng?","└ I looked it up in a book. Apparently, red mandrakes are a superior species of mandrake.","└ What book did you check?","_ An encyclopedia of medicinal herbs. It says they’re incredibly rare.","└ How rare?","_ It says they’re even more valuable because they’re a superior species.","└ LOL, wasn’t that book written by some quack?","└ LMAO.","└ It was written by a highly respected scholar. ;;","└ Don’t elixirs use mandrakes as an ingredient? Could that thing be used too?","└ Yeah. That’s why only magic towers are allowed to cultivate mandrakes.","└ If that’s a superior species, how powerful would it be?","While everyone continued arguing over the red mandrake—","└ Allfather: Oh. By Aragon, no. I believe that is a fully matured mandrake.","Fatheremon—no, Allfather—responded with something close to outright shock."]},{"title":"Chapter 15","paragraphs":["Mandrake (2)","└ An adult?","└ You mean a fully grown mandrake?","_ Allfather: Yes. Once a mandrake finishes growing, its body turns red. I even wrote a paper on the subject.","_ Then what are the mandrakes we’ve known until now? Are you saying they were immature?","_ Allfather: According to my past research, yes. Did it pause before roaring?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. When I pulled it out, it was standing there with its arms crossed. Then it roared afterward.","└ Allfather: That makes it even more certain. Just as human infants do little more than cry, mandrakes are the same. Their grotesque appearance is likely because they have not finished growing.","Allfather’s explanation was roughly as follows.","For a mandrake to mature, it needed soil so rich in mana that it practically overflowed, as well as an environment free from outside threats.","However, lands rich in mana were extremely rare, and the mandrake was highly likely to lose out to other competing organisms.","If the conditions were any less ideal, humans, monsters, or wild beasts would inevitably chew, eat, or tear it apart before it could grow.","In other words, a mandrake could only reach adulthood if every condition was perfectly met.","Artificially raising one was practically impossible as well, because it had to be continuously supplied with an enormous amount of mana.","└ I get that it’s a fully grown mandrake, but is it more effective than an ordinary one?","└ Allfather: Yes. A single adult specimen can be used to create a highest-grade elixir. Considering that a normal highest-grade elixir requires ten mandrakes, that is remarkable.","└ He struck medicinal gold.","└ Grylls is about to make a fortune again.","└ Are you planning to sell it?","I wasn’t sure.","At the question of whether I intended to sell it, I looked at the mandrake.","It had made such a racket that I had slammed it against the wall several times, after which it became quiet.","Though \"quiet\" was probably less accurate than \"unconscious.\"","I wasn’t sure whether it was even appropriate to sell something like this.","’Maybe it would be easier to think of it as hundred-year-old wild ginseng.’","I researched mandrakes a little more to find out exactly what they were.","From what I learned, they were one of the main ingredients used in elixirs and countless types of potions.","Their roots, leaves, and stems could all be used as medicinal herbs, so practically no part went to waste.","They were plants seemingly born for the sole purpose of becoming potion ingredients.","Alchemy was essential, however, if one wanted to draw out their full effectiveness.","’Should I give it to SwordMaster?’","He had given me an elixir before, so this seemed like an appropriate way to repay him.","If I harvested more later, I could give some to the Heavenly Demon and the other regular users.","It would be especially good for the Heavenly Demon, since she was an elderly woman.","Hadn’t she even given me a valuable medicinal herb when my body was in terrible condition?","PraiseTheSun had also given me a shield for free, so I intended to return the favor without asking for payment.","First, though, I would repay SwordMaster.","I could always harvest another mandrake later.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m not selling it. I’m going to give it to SwordMaster. He gave me an elixir before, so I want to repay him.","└ SwordMaster: I don’t need it.","└ Wild Grylls: Think of it as a health supplement.","└ SwordMaster: I’m already healthy.","└ Wild Grylls: There’s nothing wrong with becoming even healthier, is there?","└ SwordMaster: I don’t want to become any healthier than I already am. ;;","_ Wild Grylls: Why not? Why wouldn’t you want to become healthier...?","└ Someone who doesn’t want to be healthy, LOL.","└ Why doesn’t he want it? LMAO.","└ Ah, whatever. He just doesn’t want to be healthier, LOL.","└ I really don’t understand, LMAO.","└ Allfather: Even if an adult mandrake were simply decocted and consumed, it would greatly increase one’s mana.","└ SwordMaster: Hearing that makes me want it even less.","└ Wild Grylls: Why in the world...?","_ Starlight Princess: Excuse me, but could you give that mandrake to me? I will compensate you generously.","It was Starlight Princess.","She was the person who posted every day praying for a complete recovery.","Come to think of it, there was someone who needed it far more than SwordMaster did.","I replied to her comment.","I still couldn’t understand it.","Were there really people in this world who didn’t want to become healthier?","SwordMaster might not have been as old as the Heavenly Demon, but he still seemed close to adulthood.","Despite having the occasional eccentricity typical of a Gallery user, he was generally quite composed.","’If he refuses that firmly, I can’t force it on him.’","That left the Heavenly Demon.","She had promised to give me both an antidote and medicine effective against tinnitus, so I could trade it to her in exchange.","Just as I was about to send her a trade request, another comment caught my eye.","└ Wild Grylls: You gave me a compass before, so you don’t need to compensate me. But can a mandrake actually treat your illness?","└ Starlight Princess: It should improve my condition to some extent. Mandrakes contain yang energy.","I remembered.","When I had found the New Moon Spirit Herb, Starlight Princess had said that she needed yang energy.","Considering that her posts praying for a full recovery had continued for so long, there was a high chance that her illness was quite severe.","The Heavenly Demon seemed to have reached the same conclusion.","└ Heavenly Demon: If your illness requires yang energy, do you suffer from the Nine Yin Severed Meridians?","└ Starlight Princess: According to the physician, yes. Are you familiar with it as well, Heavenly Demon?","_ Heavenly Demon: Of course I am. It is the most famous of all severed-meridian conditions. How could I not know of it?","└ Starlight Princess: Then you must know its symptoms as well.","└ Heavenly Demon: How unfortunate. Stay strong.","└ Wild Grylls: Is it a serious disease?","└ Heavenly Demon: It is an illness that exchanges a heaven-reaching talent for one’s lifespan. Even those who survive for a long time rarely live past twenty.","└ Starlight Princess: You know it well. Recently, my body has grown so weak that I can no longer leave my bed. I suppose I am beginning to enter the dangerous stage.","└ Wild Grylls: ;;;","└ Is she suggesting they die together? LOL.","└ Talk about dragging someone down with you, LMAO.","└ I’m actually curious which of them will die first.","└ You really are an awful person. ;;","I felt like I needed to give it to her immediately.","Her illness was far more serious than I had expected.","Perhaps because a cure was difficult to find, her posts praying for complete recovery had continued without end.","She had said she needed a medicinal herb on the level of the New Moon Spirit Herb to be fully cured, so finding one must have been like plucking a star from the sky.","I was a little taken aback, but then realized that she was joking and gave a bitter smile.","She had probably made the remark to break the uncomfortable atmosphere.","It was a kind of self-deprecating joke.","Whenever I saw situations like this, I was reminded that good health truly was the most important thing.","Health was an asset that could not be exchanged for anything else.","└ Wild Grylls: I didn’t realize it was that serious. I’m sorry.","_ Starlight Princess: It’s all right. You’re also someone who could die at any moment, Mr. Grylls.","└ Wild Grylls: Ma’am?","└ Starlight Princess: I’m joking.","└ That didn’t sound like a joke, LOL.","└ Wild Grylls: In any case, would an adult mandrake be effective against the Nine Yin Severed Meridians?","_ Allfather: I cannot say for an ordinary mandrake, but an adult specimen should have some effect.","└ Starlight Princess: Even some effect would be valuable. Mandrakes are already rare plants to begin with.","└ Heavenly Demon: It seems it is not potent enough to cure the Nine Yin Severed Meridians completely.","└ Is there no cure for it?","└ There is. Usually, there are three methods. One is to take medicine, another is for a physician to open each meridian individually, and the last is for a man to directly transfer his energy into her.","└ The first two sound fine, but what’s with the last one? Is it what I think it is?","└ Yeah. But the man also has to be sufficiently powerful.","└ Oh. I’m strong. Could I do it?","└ How strong are you?","_ I beat everyone in my village at arm wrestling. LOL.","└ LMAOOOOO.","This lunatic had just sexually harassed a patient.","I stared at the comments with a thoroughly unimpressed expression.","Because the Gallery guaranteed anonymity, people often threw around obscene remarks like that.","It might have been tolerable in a lighter atmosphere, but doing it at a moment like this made me feel genuinely uncomfortable.","└ Starlight Princess: Come if you are confident. However, if you fail to meet the requirements, I will cut it off. Keep that in mind.","└ Cut it off? You mean his johnson?","└ Starlight Princess: What else did you think I meant? If you dislike that option, shall I cut off your head instead?","_ I’m sorry. I will never act cocky again.","Apparently, she was used to dealing with this sort of thing, because Starlight Princess struck back even harder.","The third method could be discarded for obvious reasons, while the second was closer to surgery.","And an exceptionally difficult surgery at that.","Even Earth’s medicine, with all its advanced science, would struggle with such a procedure. How much harder would it be here?","In practice, the first method was the only realistic answer.","But that method was also incredibly difficult.","_ Heavenly Demon: The Nine Yin Severed Meridians can only be cured by consuming spiritual treasures such as a Solar Fire Carp, a Ten-Thousand-Year Fire Carp, or a Solar Flame Herb.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ve never heard of any of those. Are they rare?","└ Heavenly Demon: They are comparable to the New Moon Spirit Herb you gave me.","└ Wild Grylls: So they’re incredibly rare.","_ Heavenly Demon: This lady was exceedingly fortunate. That is why you are both my fateful opportunity and my benefactor.","└ Wild Grylls: I was lucky too, though. Anyway, would even an adult mandrake be unable to cure her completely?","_ Allfather: It may not be entirely impossible. The problem is the quantity.","└ Wild Grylls: The quantity?","└ Allfather: Yes. An adult mandrake may not quite qualify as a true spiritual treasure, but it belongs to the tier immediately below one. Therefore, if six or seven adult mandrakes were refined into a single elixir, she should recover.","Six or seven?","That sounded manageable.","I thought back to the place where the adult mandrakes lived.","I had been fleeing in such a panic that I hadn’t counted them carefully, but there had been far more than ten.","No.","Forget ten.","There had been at least several dozen of them.","In any case, there were a lot.","’And once I pull them out, I can just beat them until they quiet down.’","I turned my head and looked at the adult mandrake.","It was still hanging limply, unconscious.","I had heard that even if it looked dead, it would become fresh and lively again once planted in soil.","Of course, I had no intention of planting it. I was going to give it to someone else.","Pulling it out again would only cause more trouble.","For now, I should tell them.","While I was at it, I might also be able to get something I wanted from Starlight Princess.","└ Starlight Princess: Huh?","Apparently not.","It seemed she had been too stunned to leave a proper comment.","_ Starlight Princess: To think I would need that many... It would be difficult to obtain all of them, wouldn’t it?","_ Allfather: I have only seen three in my entire life. Even if one were found, someone would probably have consumed it already.","_ Starlight Princess: That’s unfortunate. Ah, you never even said you would give one to me, Mr. Grylls. I suppose I became too greedy.","└ Wild Grylls: There are tons of them here, though.","└ Starlight Princess: You’re lying, aren’t you? If you’re trying to tease me, it won’t work.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m serious. I told you earlier that a whole group of mandrakes screamed at once.","└ Starlight Princess: You mean all of them were adults?","└ Wild Grylls: Every single one was red.","└ Starlight Princess: I won’t believe you until you show me a picture.","└ Wild Grylls: Give me a moment.","Adult mandrakes were practically scattered everywhere around here.","That was what I meant by my comment.","After that, she didn’t respond for quite some time.","I wondered whether she had temporarily closed the Gallery to do something else.","Taking a picture was easy enough.","I roughly packed my equipment and headed toward the mandrake colony.","It wasn’t far away, but I remained cautious in case a wild beast suddenly appeared.","\"Huh?\"","When I arrived at the colony, I stared at the changed landscape in confusion.","Its location hadn’t shifted.","However, several adult mandrakes had climbed out of the ground even though no one had pulled them up.","They were looking around as though standing guard.","Apparently, reaching adulthood had also granted them intelligence.","’This makes things a little difficult.’","The moment they noticed me, the sentries would roar.","Then I would be struck by the same Lion’s Roar as before.","I had no choice but to wait until they returned underground.","Still, this was enough proof.","Title: Adult Mandrakes Standing Guard","(Video of adult mandrakes standing guard)","I wasn’t lying. Starlight Princess, please watch the video and respond.","└ Why is this actually real? LMAO.","└ Why the hell is it real? LOL.","└ Do mandrakes normally act like that?","_ Of course they don’t, LMAO.","└ Allfather: Oh! Adult mandrakes standing guard...! This is worthy of an academic paper! Are all those plants mandrakes?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. I took one of their friends earlier, so it looks like they’re standing guard now.","└ Allfather: Would you be willing to observe them continuously?","└ Wild Grylls: I’m sorry, but I don’t have that kind of free time.","└ Allfather: What a shame.","While I was speaking with the academically passionate Allfather, Starlight Princess finally left a comment.","└ Starlight Princess: Those are all adult mandrakes... correct?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes.","└ Starlight Princess: It looks as though there are dozens of them buried in the ground.","└ Wild Grylls: Yes.","└ Starlight Princess: What exactly are you?","I pondered her question.","Would she tell me to stop joking if I said I was from the Miryang Park clan?","But I didn’t have any proper answer to give her.","I had no idea why I had ended up here either.","While I hesitated, comments began pouring in.","└ Correct answer! A man with the lifespan of a fly!","_ Correct answer! A castaway in the Forest of Four Seasons!","└ Correct answer! A beggar!","└ Correct answer! A motherless bastard!","└ DontAbandontheHero: Correct answer! A strange person!","└ Wild Grylls: F—, forget the others. What’s with the head mod?","└ DontAbandontheHero: I was bored! By the way, the person who insulted your parents has been banned for one hour!","└ But Grylls really doesn’t have a mother. Why ban him?","_ DontAbandontheHero: It sounds wrong! And even if someone has no parents, telling them that can still hurt deeply!","└ Wild Grylls: You’re even worse.","└ DontAbandontheHero: Ah! I’m sorry!","└ LMAOOOOOOOO.","The money Allfather had given me was enough.","I would only ask for food in an emergency.","There was only one thing I currently needed.","Perhaps it was second only to food in importance.","└ Wild Grylls: Starlight Princess, your family is wealthy, right?","└ Starlight Princess: You could say that.","└ Wild Grylls: Then if I send you mandrakes, can you immediately turn them into an elixir?","└ Starlight Princess: It would take some time, but yes. I am highly knowledgeable in alchemy.","└ Wild Grylls: Then I have one request.","This worked out perfectly.","Starlight Princess could provide exactly what I needed most.","The fact that she was also skilled in alchemy was the icing on the cake.","As expected, these people were ruthless.","I chuckled, then asked Starlight Princess again.","└ Wild Grylls: So, do you want them? I can give you the first one for free, but the next ones won’t be free.","└ Starlight Princess: What do you want? I’ll give you anything I can obtain. Do you need money?","└ Wild Grylls: No. I don’t urgently need money right now.","└ Wild Grylls: Once you recover completely, could you supply me with elixirs? I never know when I might get injured. It would feel wrong to only receive things, so I’ll give you mandrakes from time to time.","└ Starlight Princess: I will give you an elixir every time we trade mandrakes. If I can recover completely, I would give you my position, my wealth, or even my body.","_ Wild Grylls: Would you like to come to where I am? LOL.","└ Starlight Princess: Ah. That would be a little...","└ Wild Grylls: You’re a bad person.","└ Even she’d rather die than enter the Forest of Four Seasons, LOL.","└ Imagine finally curing yourself only to commit suicide by going there, LMAO.","_ Judging by the fact that she can offer elixirs, she must genuinely be rich.","└ Not potions but elixirs? She’s definitely a noble.","This was enough.","All that remained was to give her the mandrakes.","To do that, I first had to capture them.","I stared at the mandrakes standing guard.","’They call it guarding, but the security isn’t that strict.’","Even if they were monsters, they were still plants.","Moreover, their vigilance had already decreased compared to earlier.","As plants, they had no choice but to return underground eventually.","I waited until only one remained.","Pop! Pop!","Several mandrakes burrowed back into the ground.","When the last one began preparing to descend as well, I saw my chance and sprinted forward.","The mandrake noticed me, flinched in surprise, and opened its mouth wide.","I had to catch it before it roared.","But the distance between us was too great.","Fortunately, I had prepared for this.","I picked up the fist-sized rock I had found earlier.","\"Uwo...!\"","Whoosh!","Just before it could scream, I threw the rock.","I had played baseball in the past, so my aim was accurate.","Thud!","\"Guehk!\"","The rock struck the mandrake directly in the head, forcing a strange cry from its mouth.","Now all I had to do was grab it.","Before long, I caught the mandrake with both hands.","And then—","Thud! Thud! Thud!","Holding the stem attached to its root, I punched it repeatedly.","I couldn’t allow it to make another sound.","I also forcibly stuffed dirt into its mouth.","If its mouth was packed full, it wouldn’t be able to scream.","Thanks to my efforts, the mandrake soon went limp.","It had lost consciousness.","’Is this really the proper way to catch one?’","Well, all’s well that ends well.","A perfectly executed improvised method wasn’t much different from the orthodox approach.","’I should give some to Starlight Princess and one each to the others.’","With this, I should be able to repay at least some of the favors I owed."]},{"title":"Chapter 16","paragraphs":["Health (1)","There were many things in the world that money could buy, but there were also many things it could not.","Health, the heart, time, and so on. Most were abstract concepts, yet they occupied an enormous place in a person’s life.","Among them, health was especially important because it was often directly tied to life itself.","No matter how high one’s status, how vast one’s wealth, or how great one’s fame, all of it was meaningless without good health.","Most people lived without understanding the importance of their health, only realizing it after it was too late.","And by the time they tried to cling to it, the opportunity had already passed.","Even an emperor who reigned with absolute dignity was no more than an ordinary human before illness.","Worse still, once one’s health deteriorated, it was rarely easy to restore.","As the ages passed and medicine and technology advanced, new methods of preserving health emerged, but they remained limited.","Sometimes, when one part of the body felt uncomfortable, the actual problem lay somewhere entirely different. Others were simply born with ailments.","From the moment people were born, their health was destined to decline little by little.","Humans were beings who received the promise of death at the same moment they were granted life.","Yet cruelly, there were some for whom that cycle was exceptionally short.","Some were sentenced to death from the moment they were born.","\"Cough! Cough!\"","A woman lying in bed erupted into a fit of violent coughing.","She hurriedly covered her mouth with a handkerchief.","Her hair and eyes were as white as snow, and her skin was deathly pale.","Her entire appearance evoked untouched snow, giving her an air of mystery.","\"Haa...\"","After coughing harshly, the woman slowly lowered the handkerchief from her lips.","Dark red blood stained the pure white cloth.","Her condition looked grave even at a glance, but she appeared unconcerned as she held the handkerchief out to the side.","A young brown-haired maid stood beside her.","\"Mary. Take care of this for me.\"","\"My lady.\"","The brown-haired girl looked anxiously between the handkerchief and the woman.","Her large eyes resembled those of a deer.","The white-haired woman seemed to read the emotion in those innocent eyes and gave a faint smile.","Or rather, she attempted to smile.","No smile actually appeared.","Her expression remained rigid and cold, as though frozen in place.","\"Wouldn’t it be better to inform His Grace again?\"","\"It happens often. Don’t make a fuss.\"","\"But lately, you’ve been coughing far too—\"","\"I said I’m fine. Hurry and give me another one.\"","The woman spoke in a cold, blunt voice.","The maid, Mary, hesitated before taking the handkerchief and placing it into a basket atop the drawer.","The basket was filled with bloodstained handkerchiefs.","It showed just how much blood she had coughed up.","\"...We’re running low on handkerchiefs. I’ll bring more.\"","\"Fine. Bring tissues if there aren’t any.\"","\"Yes, my lady.\"","Even as Mary left the room, she could not tear her worried gaze away.","The white-haired woman merely stared back without expression.","Once Mary had finally gone outside, the woman turned her head forward.","The room was filled with a chill as cold as her face.","\"Haa...\"","The woman, Selena, let out a long sigh and leaned back against the bed.","Her expression was still stiff, but a trace of gloom had entered it.","She raised one arm and stared at her wrist.","It was so slender that it looked as though it might snap from the slightest touch.","Her skin was so unnaturally pale that it appeared powdered white.","As the blood on the handkerchief had made obvious, Selena’s health was extremely poor.","In truth, even calling it extremely poor was an understatement.","’I don’t have much time left.’","Selena thought this without changing her expression.","A congenital, incurable illness.","It did not merely shorten her lifespan. It openly predetermined it.","She was guaranteed to die by the time she reached adulthood.","According to a physician from the Central Plains, it was called the Nine Yin Severed Meridians, one of the worst illnesses imaginable.","It was a disease in which an excessive amount of yin energy completely destroyed the body’s balance, gradually ruining it from within.","Its defining symptom was that the meridians—in other words, the mana circuits—became blocked one by one.","Mana circuits were essential for human survival.","They were especially closely tied to the health Selena desired so desperately.","People occasionally collapsed from heart attacks.","Such incidents occurred when the mana circuits near the heart were blocked by disease or declining health.","In the past, nothing could be done once a heart attack occurred, but recently, cardiopulmonary resuscitation at least made emergency treatment possible.","’The gods are too cruel.’","But the Nine Yin Severed Meridians was different.","If only one particular region were blocked, like in a heart attack, that would have been one thing.","This was practically the same as having every mana circuit in the body blocked.","The vessel had a fixed capacity, yet it contained so much that even the vessel itself began to shatter.","In exchange, it granted strength far beyond that of an ordinary person.","Back when Selena had still been able to move freely, she had been called a genius.","In magic especially, she was said to possess talent that no one else could rival.","Her mind was also exceptionally sharp, to the point that even her father, Theodore, sought her advice.","’All of it is meaningless.’","As time passed, everything began to feel increasingly pointless.","She had been born into the most prestigious ducal house in the Messiah Empire and possessed extraordinary talent, yet she was still dying helplessly.","Before poor health, everything else seemed small and pathetic.","As the days passed, there was only one thing she desired.","To leave her bed and run proudly on her own two feet.","Selena knew perfectly well that it was impossible.","Despite receiving every form of support available, her health showed no sign of improving.","There were three methods of treating the Nine Yin Severed Meridians.","One could consume a spiritual treasure overflowing with yang energy, receive direct treatment from a physician, or take yang energy directly into the body.","The first method was practically impossible, even with the ducal family’s authority, wealth, and intelligence network.","They had monitored the black market constantly, but all they ever found were drugs, human trafficking, and similar filth. There were no spiritual treasures.","Every physician had abandoned the second method.","The operation was impossibly difficult, and none of them had the confidence to deal with the consequences if it failed.","As for the third method...","She would rather die.","She would bite her tongue before sleeping with a man she had never met.","She had no desire to prolong her life at the cost of her chastity.","’Besides, men capable of it are rare.’","To ensure success, the man would need to be someone worthy of being called the strongest.","However, most of the people frequently mentioned in discussions about the current strongest were women.","There was Kadir, known as the King of Magic, but he was already old.","Worse still, rumors described him as an eccentric, which made the idea deeply unpleasant.","’I don’t want to die like this, but...’","Death frightened her.","That was why she had gathered every piece of knowledge she could find.","She taught herself alchemy and medicine in hopes of extending her life even a little.","Yet the more knowledge she accumulated, the more firmly she reached the same conclusion.","There was no cure.","Could anything be more despairing?","There had been a time when she cried until her voice gave out.","Her parents also felt the full weight of their helplessness, and their expressions worsened with each passing day.","Little by little, emotion disappeared from Selena’s face as well.","She had reached the stage where she was slowly accepting despair rather than clinging to hope.","She could no longer remember the last time she had laughed without restraint.","’It’s still better than doing nothing.’","Even so, she hated the idea of simply giving up and waiting for death.","Selena raised her head and looked into the air.","A window appeared before her eyes.","The Gallery, which she had only begun accessing after accepting her death.","’I used to hate even looking at it.’","Anyone could access the Gallery as long as they met the conditions, regardless of age or gender.","That was precisely why many people avoided it.","Some disliked places stained so heavily by human desire.","Selena had once been one of them, but her thoughts changed after her health deteriorated.","\"So much time has passed.\"","She became absorbed in the Gallery at around the same time her condition worsened dramatically.","Unable to leave her bed, she spent all day browsing it.","At first, she merely lurked because she had nothing else to do.","Then, thinking she should at least leave some kind of record behind, she began posting messages counting down the days.","It had already been five months.","Put another way, her health had been worsening for five straight months.","’Not everyone there is terrible.’","When she was first criticized and mocked, she had thought, Of course. What else did I expect?","But as time went on, people seemed to realize that it was not an act and began sincerely encouraging her.","The head moderator was strange, but fundamentally just. Any abuse that crossed the line earned an immediate ban.","Thanks to that, Selena could now access the Gallery with a more relaxed heart than before.","People became endlessly free the moment they accepted death.","Selena gradually grew accustomed to the Gallery, that pit of human desire, and evolved into an excellent user herself.","A small portion of her dried-up emotions even returned.","Amusingly, most of those emotions were envy or resentment.","’Those idiots get to live with perfectly healthy bodies, so why am I...?’","It was deeply ironic.","Even so, she could not stop using the Gallery.","Recently, an especially unusual regular user had appeared, making it impossible not to pay attention.","’Wild Grylls... Why did this person fall into the Forest of Four Seasons?’","Anyone who explored the Gallery long enough would eventually witness things that defied common sense.","Recently, someone had appeared who claimed to have fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons.","The Forest of Four Seasons was a region where space changed constantly and access to the Gallery was impossible.","Yet he could connect without issue and had provided proof multiple times, attracting more attention than anyone else.","└ Wild Grylls: Three fasting pills.","_ Have you ever eaten meat? LOL.","└ Wild Grylls: No...","└ Want some?","└ Wild Grylls: Change your username first, LOL.","Title: Anyone Want to Bet on How Long Grylls Lasts?","I say about two weeks. LOL.","└ Even two weeks is generous.","_ He might die tomorrow.","_ A true fly’s lifespan.","└ I think the gods hate Grylls.","└ Wild Grylls: You awful bastards. I’m going to survive until the end.","_ So what are you eating today?","At first, Selena had merely thought of him as someone pitiful.","Her opinion changed after trading with him.","He could have simply kept the compass without consequence, yet he insisted on returning it.","At the very least, that meant he was not a shameless person.","’And the fact that his life is as fragile as a fly’s gives me a strange sense of kinship.’","Selena was terminally ill, while Grylls had the lifespan of a fly.","That peculiar comparison had gradually become established within the Gallery.","Occasionally, arguments broke out over which of them would die first, but those comments quickly disappeared.","The head moderator had probably decided that such discussions went too far and banned the users involved.","They were weighing human lives against each other, so they deserved it.","’If the first herb he had discovered had been something else...’","Selena had this thought every time she read one of Grylls’s posts.","The rare medicinal herb he had discovered by chance—the New Moon Spirit Herb.","Unfortunately, the New Moon Spirit Herb specialized in stabilization rather than any particular type of energy.","She could not describe how disappointed she had been.","Had it been an herb overflowing with yang energy, she would have pursued it by any means necessary.","’Would the Heavenly Demon have been in danger then?’","She could infer the answer from the behavior of the Heavenly Demon, who had presumably received the New Moon Spirit Herb.","The Heavenly Demon was one of the Gallery’s more famous regular users.","Selena was therefore familiar with her general behavior.","’For someone with such overwhelming self-esteem to treat him that respectfully, she must have received the New Moon Spirit Herb.’","The Heavenly Demon was famous for constantly posting nonsense.","No matter what others said, she continued without the slightest concern.","Through those posts, Selena had been able to infer her personality.","She was someone with exceptionally high self-esteem and confidence.","Her self-esteem in particular was strong enough to be obvious.","Anyone who posted whatever nonsense they pleased while ignoring everyone else clearly followed their own path.","’Was \"Gal!\" a word from the Central Plains meaning to rebuke someone?’","Yet during the incident involving the New Moon Spirit Herb, that same person had openly displayed urgency.","After receiving it, she even began treating Grylls with exceptional respect.","It was clear that the Heavenly Demon had been unwell and had received help from him.","’This Grylls person... seems like a bit of a pushover.’","Selena analyzed Grylls with her usual expressionless face.","His personality could be summed up in a single saying:","Treat others well, and they will treat you well in return.","His actions reflected that principle too.","Even though receiving help was crucial after being stranded in the Forest of Four Seasons, he still tried to repay every favor to the very end.","’There really are all kinds of strange animals in the world.’","Selena checked Grylls’s posts frequently.","Partly because his fly-like lifespan gave her a strange sense of kinship, but more than anything, because she felt uneasy.","If his posts suddenly stopped, it would most likely mean that he had died.","’That only makes me more curious.’","She became increasingly curious.","What strange animal would he encounter next, and how would he overcome the hardship it brought?","Thanks to him, she even began leaving comments despite rarely doing so before, and her days became somewhat enjoyable.","Tiny ripples had begun to spread across Selena’s heart.","\"Cough! Cough!\"","Splatter!","If only her body had not continued worsening with each passing day.","A sudden coughing fit seized Selena, and she hurriedly covered her mouth with her hand.","Mary had gone to fetch more handkerchiefs, leaving Selena with no other choice.","\"...\"","Fighting off the dizziness, she lowered her hand and looked at it.","Seeing blood pooled in her palm rather than on a handkerchief made death feel even more vivid.","It was a sign that she was finally nearing her limit.","Click—","\"My lady, I brought the handkerchiefs... My lady?!\"","Mary returned at just the right moment.","The instant she saw Selena, she rushed toward her in alarm.","\"...Mary.\"","\"I’ll call the attending physician immediately. There’s so much blood today...\"","\"No. It’s all right. There’s no need anymore.\"","\"My lady?\"","At Selena’s refusal to summon the physician, Mary stared at her with a look of dreadful realization.","Selena read the meaning in her face and nodded.","\"I truly don’t think I have much time left.\"","\"M-My lady, you mustn’t give up so quickly...\"","\"I know quite a bit about medicine myself. I understand my body better than anyone.\"","At one point, Selena had studied every piece of medical knowledge she could find in order to survive.","But she had gained nothing from it.","All she had obtained was certainty that her life was coming to an end.","Mary stared at Selena with trembling eyes, but Selena remained resolute.","\"Thank you for the handkerchiefs. You should go rest as well. I’ll call if I need anything.\"","\"...My lady.\"","\"I want to be alone. Go.\"","At Selena’s cold dismissal, Mary reluctantly left the room.","Even until the last moment, she did not stop looking back with concern.","Selena felt warmth in her heart at the girl’s kindness.","Her expression, however, remained as cold as ever.","’I should ask Father to adopt Mary.’","It would be both her final request and a reward for the girl who had stayed by her side until the end.","With that thought, Selena leaned back against the bed.","The dizziness had eased slightly, but her body was growing heavier.","Even taking a single step outside the bed had become difficult.","’Is Mr. Grylls... all right?’","As death drew closer, one particular person came to mind.","If Selena could be described as drawing infinitely closer to death, then Grylls was someone who constantly wandered directly before its gates.","She forced her dimming eyes open and accessed the Gallery.","’An adult... mandrake? What is that now?’","As expected of Grylls.","He had discovered yet another strange thing.","It was a plant rather than an animal this time, but that only made it more interesting.","’Mandrakes are known to contain yang energy...’","Would one improve her condition, even slightly?","With that thought, she left several comments and learned something astonishing.","’It might be possible to treat me with adult mandrakes.’","There was a condition, however.","An absurdly difficult one.","She would need at least six adult mandrakes.","Seeing even one in an entire lifetime was difficult, yet she needed six.","It was nothing more than false hope.","Just as she was about to give up completely, a comment appeared that she could not ignore.","└ Wild Grylls: There are a ton of them here, though.","└ Starlight Princess: Huh?","She had been so startled that she left a strange reply.","At first, she could hardly believe it.","Even for the Forest of Four Seasons, wasn’t that too much?","But after seeing the post and video Grylls uploaded shortly afterward, her thoughts changed.","’Maybe...’","Perhaps with Grylls’s help, she could escape this hellish illness.","Selena had made elixirs before.","She had devoted her entire life to curing herself, after all.","As luck would have it, Grylls wanted elixirs rather than money.","If she recovered completely, supplying him with elixirs whenever he needed them would be easy.","’Was this how the Heavenly Demon received his help too?’","Did Selena suspect he was a fraud?","Not at all.","The Heavenly Demon herself was living proof, openly treating him as a benefactor.","Of course, Selena did not know whether adult mandrakes would truly be effective against the Nine Yin Severed Meridians.","But she was desperate enough to grasp at any straw.","’Can Mr. Grylls capture them all in time?’","She was not merely at risk of dying in a few days.","She could die as soon as tomorrow.","Had Grylls discovered them even a little earlier, she might have had more time.","\"Harvesting mandrakes should take a long time... Will he be all right?\"","Just as anxiety began to overwhelm Selena, a trade request suddenly arrived.","For an instant, hope flared within her.","Had he already gathered all of them in such a short time?","Then she shook her head.","’He is probably only sending the one he caught earlier.’","That was the reasonable conclusion.","She should not raise her hopes unnecessarily.","Suppressing her expectations, Selena accepted the request.","[Wild Grylls has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","It was Grylls.","Selena stared at the trade window and blinked.","[Wild Grylls: Hello, Starlight Princess. I gathered seven adult mandrakes.]","[Starlight Princess: Huh?]","The moment she accepted, Grylls’s words left her completely stunned.","She only blinked with her usual expressionless face, but she was stunned nonetheless.","’No. He already gathered all of them? How?’","She had expected it to take at least a full day, but he had completely defied her expectations.","[Starlight Princess: You already gathered them all? Is that even possible?]","[Wild Grylls: They quiet down if you punch them before they scream. I also stuffed dirt into their mouths, so they should be safe.]","[Starlight Princess: ;;;]","Selena felt deeply conflicted.","She blinked twice.","Was that truly how one was supposed to harvest mandrakes?","Normally, the best method was to use silence or sleep magic.","’Is this what the Gallery calls magic—physical edition?’","In any case, he claimed to have gathered them all, so she only had to accept them.","Selena swallowed hard and continued the conversation.","Although her expression remained stiff, her written responses were far more varied.","[Starlight Princess: What if you’re lying?]","[Wild Grylls: Then you can stop trading with me next time.]","It was an absurdly gullible way of thinking.","If it turned out to be false, then so be it.","Selena let out a faint breath of disbelief before returning to her expressionless state.","Still, the corners of her lips rose ever so slightly.","No wonder the Heavenly Demon was so devoted to him.","Even if he occasionally did strange things, he was fundamentally kindhearted.","[Starlight Princess: Are you truly all right with this? These are incredibly valuable. Are you sure you can give all of them to me...?]","[Wild Grylls: You seemed very sick.]","[Starlight Princess: Thank you. Truly. But this is so sudden that I don’t think I can give you an elixir immediately. Is that all right?]","[Wild Grylls: Just send me a trade request later. That’s fine.]","[Starlight Princess: Thank you. Thank you so much.]","The tiny ember of hope that had remained within her slowly began to grow into a flame.","Selena filled her heart with hope, then suddenly became curious.","Grylls was someone who, like her, stood closer to death than almost anyone.","It would not be strange if he died tomorrow.","[Starlight Princess: Mr. Grylls, may I ask you one thing?]","[Wild Grylls: What is it?]","[Starlight Princess: What would you do if you knew you were going to die tomorrow?]","There was a famous saying:","Even if the world ended tomorrow, I would still plant an apple tree today.","It was such a predictable answer that it had become almost tiresome.","Selena expected Grylls to say something similar.","His reply, however, was completely different from what she had imagined.","[Starlight Princess: Then what would you do?]","[Wild Grylls: I’d think about what I need to do to live today.]","[Wild Grylls: Why would I think about dying tomorrow?]","Think about how to live today.","Those words pierced deeply into Selena’s heart.","Once, she too had desperately wanted to live.","But this cursed body had shattered that desire.","Afterward, she had done nothing but wait for the day she would die.","’But now...’","She stared blankly at her lap.","The trade had just ended, and several crimson mandrakes now lay there.","’I want to live.’","Ding!","Without hesitation, Selena pressed the call bell.","The moment she did, Mary, who had been waiting outside, hurried into the room.","\"Do you need something, my lady?\"","\"Mary. Take me to the laboratory.\"","\"The laboratory?\"","\"Yes.\"","Selena made another request of the bewildered maid.","\"Bring these too.\"","She pointed at the adult mandrakes.","Mary tilted her head as she looked at them.","\"What are those ugly plants? Where did they come from?\"","\"Hmm...\"","Selena considered how to explain, then quietly opened her mouth.","\"It’s a long story.\"","For now, she had no choice but to brush the question aside."]},{"title":"Chapter 17","paragraphs":["Health (2)","This was her final hope—her last desperate struggle.","That was Selena’s resolve when she arrived at her private laboratory.","Her laboratory was equipped with everything one might find in a Magic Tower’s research facility.","It was evidence of just how desperately she had struggled to find some way to heal her body.","Her health had deteriorated so severely that she could barely enter the laboratory anymore, but today was different.","\"Mary. You only need to do exactly what I tell you. Understood?\"","\"Yes! I’ll do my best!\"","\"It isn’t anything diffi—cough! Cough! Cough!\"","When a violent cough suddenly burst from her throat, Selena hurriedly covered her mouth with a handkerchief.","Mary flinched and rushed toward her, but Selena raised a hand to stop her.","\"Haa...\"","Once the fit had passed, Selena slowly lowered the handkerchief from her lips.","A pool of black, dead blood had gathered in it.","Usually, the handkerchief merely became damp.","But for enough blood to collect into a puddle meant—","If not today, then tomorrow.","She did not have much time left.","Selena clenched the handkerchief tightly.","The blood pooled inside slowly spread through the cloth.","Then she looked at the worried Mary and nodded.","With her body in this condition, Mary would have to serve as her hands and feet.","\"We don’t have time, so let’s begin immediately. First, bring me that extractor over there.\"","\"Yes!\"","\"Next, connect the extractor to the charger, and...\"","Selena continued giving Mary one instruction after another.","Mary fumbled at first, perhaps because of the urgency, but she made no mistakes.","Though not quite on Selena’s level, Mary was rather intelligent herself.","Considering that she had been born a commoner, her ability was quite remarkable.","Perhaps I should consider sending Mary to the Academy.","Before long, Mary had finished preparing everything exactly as Selena instructed.","All that remained was to extract the essence from the mature mandrakes.","After the extraction, they would need to dilute and refine it with various medicinal herbs so that the human body could withstand it.","\"Next, you need to—cough! Cough! Kgh!\"","Just as they were approaching the final stage, Selena erupted into another coughing fit.","She did not even have time to raise the handkerchief to her mouth before black blood poured from her lips.","\"Y-Your Ladyship!\"","\"Kgh... H-Hurry...\"","\"B-But...!\"","\"Hurry... Do it...! Cough!\"","\"Y-Yes!\"","She was struggling to breathe from the coughing and the blood filling her throat.","Selena forced herself to endure it and continued giving instructions.","She had come too far to give up now.","She desperately clung to her vision as darkness began creeping into its edges.","\"Y-Your Ladyship! Th-There’s a problem!\"","\"What... cough! What problem?\"","\"Th-That thing...!\"","As if matters were not bad enough, something had gone wrong with the mandrake.","Selena struggled to steady her ragged breathing and looked toward it.","Just as Mary had said, the mandrake that had been unconscious moments earlier was beginning to twitch.","It was waking up.","That was extremely troublesome.","I was in too much of a hurry to bring the flowerpot...!","A mandrake had to remain unconscious during extraction to prevent an accident.","If the extraction began while it was conscious, its scream could even destroy the extractor.","Normally, one would use magic to silence it or plant it in a flowerpot to keep it calm.","But Selena’s body had deteriorated so badly that she could no longer use magic.","And in her haste, she had forgotten to bring a flowerpot.","It was truly a moment of crisis.","Fortunately, only one of the mandrakes was waking up.","As Selena wondered what to do, a brilliant idea suddenly came to her.","He said it would quiet down if you hit it, didn’t he?","It was the method Grylls had taught her.","He had said that after punching the mandrake, it had quickly gone silent.","It was rather barbaric and had not been scientifically proven, but this was an emergency.","\"Mary! Cough! Beat it until it stops moving!\"","\"What? You want me to hit it?\"","\"Yes! Hit it! If punching it is too difficult, grab the stem and smash it against the floor! Cough! Cough!\"","Her breathing had somewhat steadied, but blood sprayed from her lips whenever she spoke.","Mary stared back and forth between Selena and the mature mandrake in bewilderment.","She looked unsure of what she should do, but ultimately decided to obey Selena’s command.","Grab!","\"Hm?\"","The moment Mary seized the mature mandrake by its stem, it quietly opened its eyes.","The creature had fine hairs growing around its chin like a beard.","Thud! Smack! Slam!","\"Kuegh?! Kuek! Kueeegh!\"","It had no choice but to close its eyes again.","Mary had grabbed it by the stem and repeatedly smashed it against the floor.","It screamed during the process, but not loudly enough to cause confusion or disorientation.","\"I-It worked!\"","\"Then let’s begin the extraction... cough! Start extracting it.\"","\"Yes!\"","Following Selena’s instructions, Mary began extracting the mandrake essence.","As the process started, the mature mandrakes inserted into the extractor gradually shriveled.","Drip. Drip.","Golden liquid fell one drop at a time into the glass bottle connected to the machine.","As Selena watched the liquid, hope began to rise within her.","Just looking at the brilliantly glowing essence already made her feel healthier.","\"Cough! Cough!\"","\"Your Ladyship, here’s a handkerchief...\"","\"No. I’m fine now.\"","Of course, that feeling was merely wishful thinking.","After coughing, Selena looked down at her clothes.","They were now drenched in dark-red blood.","Every time she coughed, what seemed like an entire bowlful of blood poured from her mouth.","Drip—drip—","As time passed, nearly all the essence had been extracted from the mature mandrakes.","Their bodies had shrunk until they were barely the size of a baby’s palm.","Even their formerly crimson color had turned pure white.","Every last trace of essence had been extracted from them, leaving them completely devoid of vitality.","\"I think it’s almost finished. What should I do next?\"","\"All that remains is... cough! Cough! Hup...!\"","Selena’s eyes widened.","She could endure the coughing itself.","The problem was the suffocation that came afterward.","She tried desperately to control her breathing, but nothing worked.","Her vision began to black out, and pain washed over her as though even her brain had stopped functioning.","No. I can’t...!","Even Mary’s frantic cries sounded like distant echoes as Selena’s consciousness began to fade.","Barely holding on, Selena reached out.","Her hand stretched toward the essence they had only just finished extracting.","She gestured for Mary to give it to her immediately.","Drinking the essence without refining it was practically suicide.","But with her life hanging by a thread, Selena was in no position to be selective.","Gulp! Gulp! Gulp!","Realizing what Selena wanted, Mary poured the essence directly into her mouth.","Selena felt the blazing energy of the essence flow down her throat.","Could something so hot truly heal her?","It was hope flaring back to life like a dying ember.","She could not give up.","I-I need to circulate my mana...","Even as her consciousness faded, she forcibly attempted to circulate her mana.","However, there was no way her mana circuits, which had long since become completely blocked, would respond.","It was bitter and unfair, but Selena refused to give up.","The final thread of her survival instinct continued to drive her onward.","Then, just before her consciousness was severed completely, she heard—","Thump!","The vivid beating of her heart.","***","\"Your Ladyship! Lady Selena! Wake up! Your Ladyship!\"","Mary shook Selena’s shoulders as she lay collapsed on the floor, trying to determine whether she was conscious.","Selena had originally been sitting in her wheelchair, but she had lost consciousness and fallen.","Had Mary not been there, Selena might have struck her head and suffered a serious injury.","But Selena showed no sign of waking, leaving Mary with no choice but to panic.","I-I need to call someone first!","Standing around in panic would accomplish nothing.","As a precaution, Mary turned Selena’s head to the side.","If she vomited blood again, it might flow backward into her airway.","Mary then rose to her feet and was about to run out of the laboratory when—","Crack!","A strange noise pierced her ears.","Mary froze.","The sound had not come from the laboratory equipment.","It had come from Selena.","Mary turned toward her with an anxious expression.","Crack! Crack!","\"Wh-What...?\"","Mary was utterly bewildered.","A bizarre phenomenon was unfolding before her eyes.","Selena’s skin was as white as snow.","However, it was an unhealthy whiteness.","Her mana circuits had become so thoroughly blocked that even her blood could no longer circulate properly.","But now, that skin was slowly peeling away, and new skin was growing beneath it.","It was no longer deathly pale.","Instead, it was fair and luminous, as though it had simply never been exposed to sunlight.","Most remarkable of all were the blood vessels slowly becoming visible beneath her skin.","It was proof that Selena’s previously blocked mana circuits had begun circulating again.","Crack! Pop!","And it was not only her skin.","Selena’s bones and muscles were also visibly changing.","Her body had been afflicted by the Nine Yin Severed Meridians, leaving her incapable of even ordinary exercise.","But now, the energy inside her—in other words, her mana—had begun to harmonize, changing everything.","The immense mana was reconstructing a vessel capable of containing its power.","In the language of the Central Plains, this phenomenon was known as Reforging the Bones and Cleansing the Marrow.","Normally, such a transformation could occur only when vast mana was accompanied by profound enlightenment.","However, Selena’s body had suffered from the Nine Yin Severed Meridians.","The mana itself had always been abundant. It had merely failed to achieve harmony, while her talent supplied the enlightenment she needed.","Crack! Pop!","Every trace of her sickly appearance vanished, and the curves of a mature woman became pronounced.","Her snow-white hair repeatedly fell out and regrew, but before long, it stabilized at its original length.","The pure white strands shone like moonlight, enhancing her beauty even further.","The final change was her face.","She had already been beautiful, but after undergoing Reforging the Bones and Cleansing the Marrow, her beauty blossomed to an entirely different level.","Although many aspects of her body had changed, Selena’s condition could be summed up in a single word.","She had obtained a far more \"healthy\" body than before.","\"Mm...\"","As the brief yet seemingly endless transformation came to an end, Selena regained consciousness.","When Mary heard Selena groan, she snapped out of her daze and urgently asked,","\"Your Ladyship! Your Ladyship! Are you awake?!\"","\"...Mary?\"","\"Yes! It’s me, Mary!\"","\"What in the world happened... Huh?\"","Selena unconsciously sat up, only for her eyes to widen.","Since she had been lying down, the first thing she could inspect was her own body.","And the first thing that caught her attention was her chest.","It was naturally the first part she saw when she lowered her head, making it impossible to overlook.","Were my breasts always this large?","Selena tilted her head while touching her chest.","Her body had once been pitifully frail.","She had believed it possessed none of the charms of a woman.","But now, soft mounds of flesh filled her vision and rested beneath her hands.","In terms of size alone, they were large enough to inspire envy in others.","It isn’t only my chest. My arms, too...","As though entranced, Selena examined her arms.","They were no longer skeletal but properly filled out like those of an ordinary person.","Even her skin was no longer deathly pale. It was white with a distinctly healthy glow.","The faint outline of blood vessels could be seen beneath it, giving her complexion genuine color.","\"...\"","\"Your Ladyship? Could you say something...?\"","Spring!","Mary had just spoken carefully when Selena suddenly leapt to her feet.","Mary was startled at first, but then stared in shock when she realized Selena had stood up on her own.","\"Your Ladyship! You shouldn’t overexert your—!\"","Tap-tap!","Mary could not finish her sentence.","Selena, standing firmly on both legs, had suddenly begun to run.","She did not walk.","She ran.","She had skipped learning to walk and started with sprinting instead.","And she was barefoot.","Mary felt as though her heart had dropped into her stomach.","\"Your Ladyship! Where are you going?! Your Ladyship!\"","Selena paid no attention to Mary’s frantic cries behind her.","She simply ran.","She ran and ran and kept running.","From time to time, she heard startled exclamations from the mansion’s servants.","Selena ignored them.","She merely continued running.","I can run. I can actually run!","She did not stop.","Even when she occasionally stumbled, she continued onward.","When had she last run like this?","She could not even remember.","No.","Perhaps she could not remember because she had never run before.","Even walking had once been difficult for her, yet now she could run without strain.","Feeling as though she had gained the entire world, Selena dashed out of the mansion.","Her expression, stiffened from years of illness, remained rigid, but the corners of her lips had visibly risen.","\"S-Selena?! Y-You...!\"","\"Dear! Where are you going?!\"","Selena’s parents, who had just returned, recoiled in shock upon seeing her.","It was an understandable reaction.","Their daughter, who had been unable to leave her bed, was now running around like a wild horse.","To make matters worse, her clothes were covered in dried blood.","To put it bluntly, she looked like a madwoman.","\"Haa!\"","Ignoring them, Selena stopped in the mansion courtyard and steadied her breathing.","Despite running so much, she did not feel tired at all.","The only thing she could clearly hear was the beating of her heart.","I’m not coughing, either.","Even the cough that had plagued her for her entire life had completely disappeared.","She could not feel anything wrong with her body.","The absence of pain felt so unfamiliar that it was almost uncomfortable.","My mana is circulating perfectly as well.","More than perfectly.","It was moving incredibly quickly.","In the past, it had always felt as though everything inside her was completely blocked.","Now, the mana that had achieved harmony flowed through every corner of her body.","Nothing hurts.","A miracle had occurred.","What else could she possibly call it?","Selena closed her eyes and raised her face toward the clear sky.","Thank you, Mr. Grylls.","He was the person who had given her both a miracle and a new life.","A benefactor who had willingly helped her despite never having met her face-to-face.","What kind of person was he?","She found herself growing increasingly curious about him.","Her facial muscles relaxed naturally, and a happy smile appeared on her face.","\"Selena!\"","\"Dear! Are you all right?!\"","\"Your Ladyship!\"","Just as Selena was savoring the new life she had obtained, her parents and Mary called out urgently from behind her.","Hearing their voices, Selena opened her eyes and turned around.","The family she loved more than anyone was staring at her with worry.","\"Yes. I’m perfectly fine now—bleargh!\"","Splash!","Selena abruptly lowered her head in the middle of speaking.","Something poured from her mouth.","It was black, dead blood.","And it was not merely one bowlful.","She vomited enough to fill at least two bowls.","\"Urgh! Kuegh!\"","Thud! Plop!","Blood was not the only thing she expelled.","Black, congealed lumps also fell from her mouth.","They were impurities that had not yet been discharged during Reforging the Bones and Cleansing the Marrow.","Her previous physical condition had been so terrible that the accumulated waste had clumped together into solid masses.","\"Ah...\"","\"D-Darling! Pull yourself together!\"","To her family, who knew nothing of what had happened, the sight was beyond horrifying.","Selena’s mother fainted, and her father barely managed to catch and support her.","Even Mary, the last one still standing, turned deathly pale at the grotesque sight.","\"Cough. Cough. Ugh.\"","Selena’s brow twitched.","The stench from the rotten blood and impurities pouring out of her mouth was unbearable.","She wanted to grimace, but her facial muscles still did not move very well.","I need a bath.","Now, she could bathe without Mary’s assistance.","The thought alone filled Selena with anticipation.","But first, she needed to clear up her family’s misunderstanding.","Selena approached her confused family and spoke quietly.","With the blood still smeared around her mouth and her usual expressionless face, she looked rather terrifying.","\"Mother. Don’t worry. I’m healthy now—bleargh!\"","Selena vomited black blood with a perfectly blank expression.","At the bizarre sight, her family recoiled in horror once again.","\"Ahhh...\"","\"P-Pull yourself together! You cannot leave me as well!\"","She still had a long way to go.","***","Meanwhile, in the gallery—","Title: Grylls, thanks.","Passing Dwarf","(Photo of mature mandrakes being steeped in alcohol)","Looks like I’ll finally get to drink some infused liquor again.","└ Wild Grylls: You insane dwarf bastard! You turned something that expensive into alcohol?","└ Passing Dwarf: Is there a problem?","└ Wild Grylls: I told you that thing was insanely expensive! And you used it to make liquor?","└ Passing Dwarf: It’s mine. You mad?","└ Wild Grylls: From now on, sharpen your knives with gold, you damn bastard.","└ He told him to sharpen his knives with gold, lololol.","└ Can’t blame him for getting pissed, hahahahaha.","└ Come on, you can’t resist infused liquor, lololol.","The gallery was peaceful once again."]},{"title":"Chapter 18","paragraphs":["Health (3)","As I mentioned before, capturing a mandrake was surprisingly simple.","First, pull it out of the ground. Then, if it looked like it was about to scream, beat it like a dog on the hottest day of summer.","If it still stubbornly tried to scream? Stuff its mouth with dirt. It couldn’t do anything after that.","Using that method, I first harvested the most urgent request—the Starlight Princess’s—and then slowly gathered enough for the other gallery regulars as well.","The next person I gave one to was the Heavenly Demon.","She had helped me more than anyone else.","[Wild Grylls]: Take this and replenish your vitality. Are you feeling all right now?","[Heavenly Demon]: I was only in danger back then. I’m perfectly fine now. I’m more worried about your condition.","[Wild Grylls]: Aside from my stomach hurting a few times a day—probably because of the Bigu Pill—I’m okay.","[Heavenly Demon]: That’s proof your body is expelling impurities. You never underwent Reforging the Bones and Cleansing the Marrow, so they’re leaving your body that way instead.","[Wild Grylls]: So that’s a good thing?","[Heavenly Demon]: Of course. If you want, I can give you more. You gave me something beneficial as well, after all.","[Wild Grylls]: I’m fine. Just the antidote and the medicine for tinnitus that you mentioned before are more than enough.","[Heavenly Demon]: I feel guilty, as though I’m always the one receiving.","[Wild Grylls]: That’s exactly what I should be saying.","Every time I talked to her, I couldn’t help but think how admirable the Heavenly Demon was.","Everyone teased her for being an old-timer, but whenever someone gave her something, she always repaid the favor.","This was what a true adult should be like.","Though I still had no idea why someone like her spent time in this gallery.","Then again, judging from her usual posts, she was every bit as much of a gallery addict as the rest of us.","Maybe she simply got bored living such a carefree life.","So this is the antidote... and this one treats tinnitus.","After finishing our trade, I checked the items she’d sent.","The labels were written in characters that looked similar to Chinese, so I was confused at first, but the Heavenly Demon explained them.","The gallery automatically translated conversations, but only inside the gallery itself.","Every country still had its own language.","Come to think of it, who on earth had created this gallery and even implemented automatic translation?","It was a strange world in many ways, but that wasn’t something I needed to worry about right now.","[SwordMaster]: But... I told you I don’t want to become healthier.","[Wild Grylls]: Just consider it repayment for the elixir you gave me before. If you don’t want it, you can give it to someone who’s sick. Or sell it.","[SwordMaster]: Hmm... All right. Since you put it that way, I guess I can’t really refuse.","[Wild Grylls]: Thank you.","I practically forced SwordMaster into accepting it.","I couldn’t understand why anyone would refuse something that could make them healthier.","Isn’t he going to regret this someday?","Countless people had neglected their health and paid the price.","Health was something you couldn’t simply take care of whenever you wanted.","You had to look after it consistently before problems appeared.","[PraisetheSun]: So this is that precious herb?","[Wild Grylls]: Yep. I heard it’s really valuable. You gave me that shield before, so this one’s a gift.","[PraisetheSun]: Does it... happen to improve stamina? You know, that kind of thing?","[Wild Grylls]: Uh... Since it’s an ingredient for elixirs, I guess it probably does?","So he was a guy.","Well, his username should’ve tipped me off.","[PraisetheSun]: Thanks. I’ll give you an amazing gift later.","[Wild Grylls]: You’ve already given me the shield. If I find anything else that’s good for your health, I’ll bring it to you.","[PraisetheSun]: You’re too kind. Then let’s do this—every time you give me a mandrake, I’ll give you one thing you want. Sound good?","[Wild Grylls]: Works for me.","I had more than enough mandrakes.","The colony was large enough that I could keep supplying the regulars for quite a while.","Still, I wasn’t planning to harvest them recklessly.","If I ran out when I truly needed them, I’d regret it.","It was better to think of them as an emergency reserve.","After finishing my trade with PraisetheSun, I contacted CheongguPrincess.","She’d helped me before, too, so I wanted to give her one as a gift.","[Wild Grylls]: CheongguPrincess, here’s one for you.","[CheongguPrincess]: Thank yooou! I’ll send you another uniform in return!","[Wild Grylls]: Thanks! Whose is it this time?","[CheongguPrincess]: It’s Gioni Sader, the legendary goalkeeper of Chayu!","I still had no idea who that was.","Still, a gift was a gift.","When I’d first received one of her uniforms, I’d wondered whether it would be useful at all.","Surprisingly, it had been incredibly helpful.","The material was so elastic that it never felt restrictive.","[Wild Grylls]: Thanks. Was it the Champions League? I hope you win it.","[CheongguPrincess]: Not the Champions League—the Challengers Cup! But thank yooou!","[Wild Grylls]: Right, the Challengers Cup. That’s the tournament where every club in Mephisto competes, right?","[CheongguPrincess]: Yep! It’s the greatest competition in the world! Clubs from other countries compete too, not just Mephisto’s!","I didn’t have a favorite team, but I did enjoy soccer.","Watching underdog South Korea defeat powerhouse Germany had felt like witnessing a miracle.","And when Argentina won the World Cup, all I could think was, Wow... they actually did it.","Soccer was the kind of sport where even the greatest players and strongest teams could become victims of a miracle.","Its unpredictability alone was enough to make it the world’s most popular sport.","Especially in this world, where there wasn’t much entertainment besides the gallery.","No wonder sports were so popular.","I wonder if they have something like the World Cup.","According to CheongguPrincess, the Challengers Cup—or simply the Challs—allowed clubs from other nations to participate alongside Mephisto’s.","Apparently, there were domestic tournaments as well as international competitions.","In the distant past, things had been different.","But now every team consisted of multiple races, turning competitions into battles over club pride rather than national identity.","There didn’t seem to be anything resembling a World Cup, where people rooted for their country instead of a club.","Not that it’s any of my business.","I already had enough problems of my own.","Even if I was interested in soccer, I didn’t have the luxury of worrying about it.","Still, curiosity was curiosity.","I figured I’d look into it later.","From what I’d heard, humanity’s influence had been growing stronger by the day, even beginning to shake Mephisto’s position as the founding nation.","Maybe I’ll make a post asking about it.","The gallery really was convenient at times like this.","I wanted to ask CheongguPrincess more questions, but unfortunately, time was limited.","Apparently, only the head moderator could adjust private chat time.","Maybe I should submit a suggestion.","[Allfather]: Oh! Thank you very much. How much should I pay you?","[Wild Grylls]: You gave me valuable information, so you don’t have to pay anything. By the way, have you made any progress on the antidote for the Golden Poison Frog?","[Allfather]: May I answer honestly?","Seeing those words left me puzzled.","May I answer honestly?","That didn’t sound very encouraging.","[Wild Grylls]: Thanks. Go Chayu!","[CheongguPrincess]: Thank yooou! Hope you survive another day!","Our conversation ended with me cheering for Chayu.","The only regulars left were Allfather and Passing Dwarf.","[Wild Grylls]: Hello, Allfather. I’d like to give you a mature mandrake.","[Wild Grylls]: Did the results turn out badly?","[Allfather]: Yes. Especially for you, Mr. Grylls, this information is important.","[Wild Grylls]: Hmm... Please explain.","[Allfather]: The Golden Poison Frog’s venom is far stronger than we anticipated. My laboratory nearly dissolved because of it.","[Wild Grylls]: Whoa... Are you okay?","As everyone knew, the Golden Poison Frog’s venom was extraordinarily potent.","It wasn’t even acidic, yet it could melt wood.","That alone spoke volumes.","I’d warned Allfather beforehand, but the fact that his laboratory had almost been destroyed showed just how dangerous it truly was.","If I could somehow make use of that substance, my body might eventually develop resistance to it.","[Allfather]: Yes. Fortunately, there was no accident. But the more important issue is that the poison is so powerful that even the antidote failed to neutralize it.","[Wild Grylls]: Then... ?","Did that mean I’d have to buy the Water of Life after all?","Just as that thought crossed my mind, Allfather continued.","[Allfather]: But it wasn’t a complete loss. While researching the poison sac, I discovered something else.","[Wild Grylls]: That sounds a lot more promising.","[Allfather]: Yes. If this goes well, you may be able to develop resistance to poison.","Allfather’s explanation went something like this.","After researching the Golden Poison Frog’s venom sac, he had discovered a special substance inside it.","[Wild Grylls]: Wouldn’t that be even better?","[Allfather]: However, you will need to ingest it for at least two weeks. Only then will you be able to develop resistance even to the Golden Poison Frog’s venom.","[Wild Grylls]: That sounds like you’re telling me to catch more frogs.","[Allfather]: You really are perceptive.","Good grief. The nerve of this man.","I let out a dry laugh at Allfather’s shamelessness.","Still, it was well worth trying.","He was talking about gaining resistance to poison itself. For someone in my situation, that would be especially useful.","Right now, insects are more dangerous than the frogs.","At least the Golden Poison Frog’s venom could be blocked with a shield or avoided.","But snakes, venomous insects, and poisonous plants could appear from anywhere.","I was also particularly susceptible to rashes from plants, which made Allfather’s proposal even more appealing.","[Wild Grylls]: It doesn’t sound bad. But I’d appreciate it if you finished making the medicine from what I gave you before first.","[Allfather]: I do have some sense of shame. I’ll prepare the proper dosage and send it to you within two days.","[Wild Grylls]: Thank you.","Considering how much money he possessed, his skill was probably the real deal.","Now the only one left is Passing Dwarf.","Lastly, I gifted a mandrake to Passing Dwarf.","And then that bastard turned it into liquor almost immediately.","I was utterly dumbfounded when I saw it.","I could at least have understood if he had sold it for money.","My conversation with Allfather had ended, but I still felt somewhat uneasy.","He had said it worked by gradually acclimating the body to poison rather than acting as a direct antidote.","That meant the effects would not appear immediately.","It was exactly the kind of thing that could come back to bite me.","For now, I’ll have to rely on the antidote the Heavenly Demon gave me.","I did not think Allfather intended to scam me.","If he had wanted to, he would have done it when I first handed over the Golden Poison Frog.","└ Passing Dwarf: I’m rich, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: Yeah, good for you. Your shit must be huge.","└ Passing Dwarf: Thanks for the compliment.","└ Wild Grylls: You bastard, lol.","└ I’ve got nothing to say to that, hahaha.","I should have known better than to argue.","Some people were so sick they could die any day, while others soaked valuable medicine in alcohol and called it a day.","The world really was unfair.","Though the fact that I had been dropped into the Forest of Four Seasons was unfair enough on its own.","In any case, now that I had sent gifts to all the regulars who had helped me, I moved on to my next task.","Thud! Thump!","\"Ugh. This is killing me.\"","Digging traps near the cave entrance.","I had a feeling I would regret it if I kept putting the work off, so I needed to do a little every day.","My whole body would ache the next morning?","That was still better than dying.","Times like this really make me want a shower.","For now, I had no choice but to endure it.","Even after the threat of the Golden Poison Frogs disappeared, showering every day would probably be difficult.","The problem was not disposing of the water.","It was my clothes.","To minimize contact with insects and plants, clothing was not optional.","But wearing the same clothes every day would create hygiene problems of its own.","That meant I needed to wash them from time to time, which naturally required a large amount of water.","I’m going to need a lot of soap.","In a place like this, hygiene was especially important.","If I came down with an illness, things could become dangerous very quickly.","It was not as though every sickness disappeared the moment you took medicine.","Perhaps that was why, once the sun began to set, I stopped working and bought some water.","I had been sweating, so I should at least wash the parts that needed cleaning.","Once you experienced that refreshing feeling, it was difficult to forget.","The money felt wasteful, but compared to the price of my life, it was cheap.","Is this my second day?","After giving myself a rough wash, I connected to the gallery.","I had finished everything for the day and wanted to leave a record.","I would probably end up making one every day, just like the Starlight Princess.","Title: Survival, Day 2","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a campfire)","Day two of survival complete! See you tomorrow.","└ Heavenly Demon: Rest well.","└ SwordMaster: Good work. I gave the mandrake to my mother.","└ CheongguPrincess: Thank yooou for the gift. Stay healthy!","└ PraisetheSun: Post something first thing tomorrow. I’ll be worried otherwise.","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: Good work today!","Even the head moderator had left a comment.","Apparently, I was attracting more attention than I had thought.","I did not pay much attention to anonymous users.","Most of them were too busy venting their own desires.","└ Passing Dwarf: Hey. I made liquor with what you gave me, and now I can’t sleep, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: Just die already.","└ Passing Dwarf: Hic—hahaha!","└ Damn, I can smell the alcohol through the post, hahaha.","Maybe I had grown somewhat close to the regulars.","Most of the comments were well wishes, telling me I had worked hard.","There was one useless bastard among them, but he was still helpful, so I let it slide.","He might talk like this, but he was also the same guy who had once felt bad enough to send me alcohol as an apology.","Come to think of it, I wonder what happened to the Starlight Princess.","The lack of news was making me anxious.","I hoped she would at least make a post tomorrow.","I slowly lowered myself onto the ground.","It felt a little soft instead of completely hard.","That was thanks to the mat and pillow I had purchased from the auction house.","Apparently, they had been stuffed with straw.","It really is... kind of soft.","Perhaps because of the exhaustion from the day and the soft bedding, drowsiness slowly began to wash over me.","Unable to resist it, I gradually closed my eyes.","All while hoping that the next day would bring only good things.","***","Around the time Grylls finished his work and fell asleep, the gallery remained active regardless of day or night.","Normally, it overflowed with all kinds of pointless posts.","But lately, things had changed.","The topic was Wild Grylls, the man who claimed to have fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons.","Once it became certain that he really was there, countless people began paying attention to him.","Even the incident involving the mature mandrake, which had seemed like nothing more than a minor commotion, was beginning to take on a different meaning.","Title: Gallery User Is Screwed in Real Time ;;","My friend is a knight, and one of his superiors traded with Grylls and ordered him to bring back a mature mandrake ;;","└ Really?","└ Yeah. The guy’s pretty high-ranking.","└ This feels way too sudden.","└ Apparently, they’d been watching quietly all along. The post that dwarf made seems to have convinced them.","└ Hahahaha. At this rate, won’t even the emperor order someone to bring one back?","└ I’m more curious about how the Magic Tower will react.","└ Why the Magic Tower?","└ They control the mandrake monopoly. They’re probably watching this more closely than anyone.","└ Come on. Would they really make a big deal over something this small?","└ Don’t you remember the incident with the head moderator from two terms ago?","└ What happened?","Someone from another territory made a secret agreement with the Dwat Territory and began sending goods there without tariffs. That nearly drove the other territory into bankruptcy.","└ But Grylls doesn’t have enough supply, does he?","└ The Magic Tower lacks supply too, if you look at it that way. They don’t cultivate mandrakes. They only manage them.","└ So they have to obtain them from elsewhere too?","└ I heard they have enormous authority and monopoly rights, so their abuse of power is pretty severe.","└ Then from the Magic Tower’s perspective, Grylls must be rather inconvenient.","The atmosphere was beginning to take a strange turn."]},{"title":"Chapter 19","paragraphs":["Health (4)","As ridiculous as it sounded, even the highest levels of society kept a close eye on the gallery.","It was useful for gathering intelligence, monitoring leaks, assessing the political climate, and even observing daily life in foreign countries.","The gallery was filled mostly with nonsense posts, but every so often, something incredibly valuable could be found there.","More importantly, it was one of the few places where those in power could gauge public opinion .","Given the era, accurately understanding public sentiment was nearly impossible, making the gallery their only real window into it.","Of course, relying solely on the gallery had its drawbacks.","There had been many occasions when people in power trusted gallery opinion too much, only for protests and rebellions to erupt in the opposite direction.","Since then, they had learned to be wary of the \"loud minority\" and to separate useful information from noise.","Even so, no one could deny the gallery’s influence.","After all, everyone used it—young and old, nobles and commoners alike.","One famous story involved a noble who constantly criticized the gallery, only to be exposed as a hardcore gallery addict himself.","Status did not erase human desires.","If anything, those who had to maintain an elegant public image often vented their stress in the gallery instead.","That was why the upper class went to great lengths to hide the fact that they used it.","Even when caught, they usually insisted they only lurked without posting.","Almost nobody believed that excuse, but personal privacy was still respected.","As a result, there was an unspoken rule among nobles:","Never bring up the gallery.","Unless you were speaking privately with someone you trusted.","\"Your Highness, we cannot simply ignore this matter.\"","\"I know that. But that man is living on borrowed time. Isn’t this a bit too hasty?\"","The man speaking wore golden hair and blue eyes.","With his handsome features and well-built physique, he lacked for nothing in appearance.","Yet even he sounded reluctant.","Across from him, a middle-aged man with graying hair answered in an urgent tone.","\"That is precisely why we must secure as many mature mandrakes as possible before he dies.\"","\"Count Gorgon. I thought you were usually the cautious one.\"","\"There are times when decisive action must be taken.\"","The blond prince fell silent, considering the advice of his loyal retainer, Count Gorgon.","He was Arnold Louis Messiah, the future Emperor of the Messiah Empire.","With the current emperor bedridden due to chronic illness and overwork, Arnold was serving as acting emperor.","\"If we can establish trade with him, we can greatly weaken the Magic Tower’s influence. We could even pressure the Kingdom of Iris.\"","\"That’s an awfully optimistic scenario. The elves have been behaving unpredictably lately. We have no reason to provoke the Magic Tower as well.\"","\"But, Your Highness...\"","\"Enough. I have no desire to discuss someone who may die tomorrow.\"","\"If we supported him, wouldn’t that change the situation?\"","Count Gorgon refused to give up.","Though unusually stubborn, Arnold did not rebuke him.","Count Gorgon was famous for his remarkable foresight.","It was almost amusing to see someone like him influenced by rumors from the gallery.","That alone showed how much influence the gallery truly wielded.","\"If we support him, he may survive longer. But let me ask you something. Who exactly will handle this matter?\"","\"I know someone.\"","\"Not you?\"","\"...\"","Arnold’s blunt question immediately silenced Count Gorgon.","The count merely blinked in surprise.","Arnold chuckled to himself before waving a dismissive hand.","\"So you planned to take advantage of the gallery’s anonymity. You’re rushing this. That will be all.\"","\"Your Highness...\"","\"If you insist, I’ll leave it to your discretion. Just don’t complain when everyone assumes you’re the one buying mature mandrakes in bulk.\"","\"...\"","\"You haven’t been insulting me on the gallery, have you?\"","\"Absolutely not.\"","Yeah, right.","Arnold didn’t believe him for a second.","People cursed even their king whenever no one was listening.","The gallery was obviously no exception.","He himself had been showered with insults more than once simply because of unpopular policies.","\"It’s only been three days since this Grylls fellow entered the Forest of Four Seasons. Be patient.\"","\"...Understood. I may have been too hasty.\"","\"Good. Now go. I have work to attend to.\"","At Arnold’s dismissal, Count Gorgon quietly left the room.","Soon, Arnold was alone.","Leaning back in his chair, he stared thoughtfully at the ceiling.","It’s not as though I’m unconcerned either...","His gaze drifted toward the gallery.","At the moment, it was ablaze with rumors.","The spark had been Passing Dwarf’s photo of the mature mandrake.","Although Grylls had gifted mandrakes to those who had helped him, none of them had posted proof.","There was no reason to.","Doing so only risked revealing their identities.","As a result, many people had remained skeptical.","But Passing Dwarf’s post convinced them.","To make matters even worse, Grylls had previously uploaded a picture of an entire colony of mature mandrakes.","Anyone following the gallery naturally reached the same conclusion.","If you help Grylls, you’ll receive a mature mandrake.","This realization had spread within only a few hours after Grylls went to sleep.","***","Title: There Are Way Too Many Similar Posts for This to Be Just a Rumor","My friend serves in the Imperial Guard, and the Emperor supposedly ordered them to bring back a mature mandrake lol.","└ Seriously?","└ Yeah. The rumor’s already spread everywhere.","└ They’re probably holding meetings about it by now.","└ Come on. There’s no way that’s real.","Arnold smirked as he read the thread.","It sounded absurd.","Yet it was difficult to dismiss outright.","Count Gorgon himself had just pleaded the exact same case.","If even someone as cautious as Gorgon felt that way, many other nobles were probably thinking the same thing.","They would all try to establish trade with Grylls and earn his favor.","***","Title: Has the Magic Tower Said Anything Yet?","The Magic Tower monopolizes mandrakes. Haven’t they reacted?","└ Not yet, but they probably will soon.","└ Isn’t the Magic Tower in the Kingdom of Iris?","└ Could this end up causing conflict with the Empire?","└ Over one mandrake? Seriously?","└ Maybe not a war, but they’re bound to say something. Besides, I doubt the Magic Tower likes this situation.","└ Why not?","└ Because they have a monopoly.","***","Title: Current Situation Summary","Mandrakes are extremely rare and are essential ingredients for elixirs.The Magic Tower has traditionally managed all known mandrakes.Their monopoly generates unimaginable profits.Grylls has discovered not only mature mandrakes, but an entire colony of them.A single mature specimen is enough to make a top-tier elixir.Rather than accepting unfavorable deals with the Magic Tower, it would be far better to buy directly from Grylls.","└ Sure, but Grylls can’t keep supplying them forever. Once he harvests them all, that’s it.","└ The same applies to the Magic Tower. They don’t cultivate mandrakes—they only manage existing ones.","└ So they source them from the wild too?","└ Exactly. Their job is preserving mandrakes so they’re always healthy enough to be turned into elixirs.","└ And they built a monopoly around that? What a bunch of crooks, lol.","└ One more thing: Grylls is in the Forest of Four Seasons, so no one’s in a position to pressure him.","└ I can’t believe this is actually happening. Damn...","If someone could establish trade with Grylls and secure a steady supply of mature mandrakes, the rewards would be immeasurable.","The problem was Grylls himself.","He was far too unstable.","Living inside the Forest of Four Seasons meant he could die at any moment.","And it isn’t something money can solve...","What Grylls needed was not wealth.","He needed supplies to survive.","Since he had recently received a fortune from the regular known as Allfather, money was probably no longer a priority for him.","That meant bartering was the only viable option.","And that, too, made the situation unpredictable.","For now... it’s better to simply watch and wait.","It would be the worst of both worlds if they acted rashly.","If even one factor had been stable, it might have been worth considering, but everything about the situation was uncertain, making it difficult to commit.","Still, obtaining even a single one would be worthwhile...","If it were for personal reasons rather than official business, that was another matter entirely.","They see one thing but miss another.","Arnold shook his head.","With the Emperor’s health declining rapidly, the temptation was unavoidable.","Even the Imperial Palace’s budget struggled to afford a top-grade elixir.","If a mature mandrake could restore the Emperor’s health, Arnold’s position would become unshakable.","It wasn’t as though his siblings were competing for the throne.","Arnold had two younger brothers and two younger sisters.","One might expect at least one of them to covet the crown, but surprisingly, none of them did.","I suppose I’ve been fortunate...","His second brother was deeply interested in culture and had become the Minister of Culture.","His third brother was devoutly religious and had entered the clergy. According to rumor, he had become a Holy Knight.","As for his two younger sisters, they both married into noble families, naturally removing themselves from the line of succession.","It would be far better if Father handed me the crown himself than merely approved my succession.","Unless the Emperor personally passed on the throne, there would always be those looking for excuses to question Arnold’s legitimacy.","To prevent that from happening, he needed at least one mature mandrake.","Even so, Arnold hesitated.","It wasn’t because approaching Grylls made him uneasy.","With a sigh, he looked at his gallery username.","A name he had created in his youth, unable to restrain his childish impulses.","[UltimateZZoneArnoldRocks]","\"...Sigh.\"","It was embarrassing just to look at.","Why had he ever chosen a name like that?","He should have stayed anonymous from the very beginning.","No matter how many times he thought about it, he could not understand his younger self.","Fortunately, no one knew the truth.","If anyone ever found out, he would have abandoned his position as Crown Prince and fled long ago.","Can’t I at least change my username?","The gallery was a civilization far ahead of its time, but it was not perfect.","Over countless revisions, numerous conveniences had been added.","Changing your username, however, remained impossible.","Was there a way to become anonymous again?","There was exactly one.","Completely expel every trace of mana from your body and refill it with new mana.","It was essentially the same as completely replacing your body.","Even someone who underwent Reforging the Bones and Cleansing the Marrow couldn’t accomplish such a feat.","Once a username was registered, it was yours for life.","If I obtain a mature mandrake or help Father recover... people will inevitably figure it out.","And once that happened, his username would naturally be exposed.","He didn’t even want to imagine it.","Nor could he simply wait.","Managing mature mandrakes was extremely difficult.","There was a reason the Magic Tower had taken responsibility for preserving them.","At least he had deleted all of his old posts.","If the gallery hadn’t allowed users to delete their own posts, they would have remained as permanent black history.","Should I make my brother do it instead...?","Arnold folded his arms and pondered.","His second brother might officially be the Minister of Culture, but in reality he spent most of his time loafing around.","Whenever he had free time, he went to watch soccer or baseball.","He claimed it was far better than taking on a position that involved nothing but hard work.","For now, it’d be best to keep watching the gallery... and see who ends up with the mature mandrakes.","At the moment, that seemed like the wisest course of action.","Only three days had passed.","It was too early to make a fuss.","As Arnold browsed the gallery, he thoughtfully stroked his chin.","Still, I should at least familiarize myself with the culture.","The easiest way to do that would be by making a post.","Although his username embarrassed him, asking a simple question couldn’t hurt.","***","Title: Hello. Nice to meet you.","UltimateZZoneArnoldRocks","I’m new to the gallery. How does this place usually work?","└ Newbie?","└ UltimateZZoneArnoldRocks: Yes, I am.","└ Then stop using polite speech, dumbass.","└ You’re a newbie and you’re using honorifics?","└ Look at that username, lol.","Arnold’s eyes filled with confusion.","\"...Ugh...\"","I stretched, working the stiffness out of my body.","Thanks to the mat and pillow I’d bought at the auction house, I didn’t wake up sore all over.","I should’ve bought them sooner.","At least I realized it before it was too late.","The gallery...? What the...? Why are there so many trade requests?","My eyes widened.","A surprisingly large number of trade requests had arrived while I was asleep.","Once you logged out of the gallery, you received no notifications whatsoever.","That was great for getting a good night’s sleep, but it still left me puzzled.","Most of these are from regulars I don’t even know. Are they all asking for mature mandrakes?","That seemed likely.","Passing Dwarf had uploaded his post yesterday.","Even a single mature mandrake was worth an enormous amount.","If someone could genuinely help me survive, I was willing to trade.","One at a time.","Not in bulk.","My own survival came first.","There was no point supplying everyone else if it cost me my life.","[A Typical Gallery Initiation][118]","\"Hm?\"","One particular post caught my attention.","Not only were there a mountain of comments, it had an impressive number of upvotes as well.","What happened while I was sleeping?","I guess all the entertaining things really did happen while you were asleep.","[I’m the Crown Prince, you bastards.]","[What is wrong with you people?]","[Seriously.]","[I didn’t even do anything wrong.]","[Why is everyone insulting me?]","[No, listen to me first.]","[Is this really normal here?]","[This gallery is pretty rough.]","[Hello. Nice to meet you.]","Read from the bottom up.","***","Title: A Typical Gallery Initiation","[Welcome back, buddy.]","└ Talk about adapting fast, lol.","└ What’s with that username?","└ Looks like another old-timer wandered into the gallery.","└ Sounds like something my dad would come up with.","└ If your username has words like \"Ultimate,\" \"Zone,\" or \"Rocks\" in it, you’re probably old.","└ These days, some people actually choose names like that on purpose.","It was just another peaceful day in the gallery."]},{"title":"Chapter 20","paragraphs":["Owlbear (1)","Title: A Bright and Energetic Morning!","(Photo of a raised thumb)","If anyone asks who I am, tell them I’m Grylls!","└ Heavenly Demon: You’re awake. Did anything happen during the night?","└ Wild Grylls: No. I slept like a log. Did you sleep well, Heavenly Demon?","└ Heavenly Demon: Given my cultivation level, I have no need for sleep.","└ Wild Grylls: Ah. Right.","Even if something interesting happened while I was asleep, what I had to do remained the same.","Report that I was still alive.","It was a post announcing the beginning of another day.","The Heavenly Demon and the other familiar regulars each left greetings.","Quite a few anonymous users commented as well.","└ Grylls, did you see the posts from dawn?","└ Wild Grylls: What posts?","└ The ones saying they wanted to buy mature mandrakes from you. There were tons of them.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh, I saw those. I got a lot of trade requests too.","└ Are you going to sell them?","I wasn’t sure.","As I had already said, I didn’t have that kind of leeway.","I wasn’t short on money, nor was there anything I urgently needed.","I could buy most things through the auction house.","The people I had traded with so far had helped me out of pure goodwill, so I had gladly returned the favor.","[User XXX has requested a trade.]","[User @@@ has requested a trade.]","[User ○○ has requested a trade.]","Before long, even more requests flooded in.","I stared at them for a moment, then searched the usernames.","Most of the accounts had never made a post, and many had been created only recently.","They were probably trying to obtain mature mandrakes from me.","First, reject them all.","Then I needed to make a post.","If I simply ignored them, they might become even more annoying later.","I also wanted the head moderator to see what was happening.","***","Title: To Everyone Who Sent Me Trade Requests","Wild Grylls","I assume you’re after mature mandrakes, but I have no intention of trading them right now.","Given my current situation, I can’t afford to act carelessly, and I have no idea what you intend to offer.","So instead, make a post explaining what you want to trade.","I’ll look through them and send trade requests myself if anything interests me.","Also, please don’t ask for regular shipments.","I could die tomorrow.","└ Wait, so the rumors were true?","└ The mature mandrakes were real, so I guess it makes sense.","└ \"I could die tomorrow,\" hahaha.","└ At least he has an accurate view of his situation, lol.","└ Everyone will understand if he puts it like that.","└ PraisetheSun: If anyone tries to buy one with money, tell me. I’ll pay more than them, lol.","└ Damn, he’s rich.","└ Look at that confidence, hahaha.","└ Rich Dark Elf bro is built different.","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: Hmm! I think I understand what’s happening! I’ll keep an eye on things!","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you. Do you need a mandrake too, Head Mod?","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: Huh?! I haven’t done anything to help you!","└ Wild Grylls: A bribe, lol.","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: Absolutely not!","└ He just openly called it a bribe, hahaha.","Now that the situation was more or less settled, I began my daily routine.","First, I sat cross-legged to improve my flexibility.","Three days ago, it had felt as though my entire body were being twisted apart.","Now, it was slowly becoming bearable.","I should be able to learn from the Heavenly Demon soon.","An internal cultivation method—or perhaps a mana cultivation technique.","If I could learn one, it would surely improve my condition.","The Heavenly Demon wouldn’t teach me anything dangerous.","It should make chopping wood and digging easier too, right?","The most important task at the moment was reinforcing my shelter.","I wanted to cut trees with the Heavenly Demon’s sword instead of an axe.","But if I damaged the blade, I would be in serious trouble, so I had no choice but to use the axe.","The same went for the shovel.","Every task here involved backbreaking labor.","There aren’t any interesting posts either.","Nothing particularly noteworthy had appeared since I made my post.","As usual, I ate a Bigu Pill for breakfast.","I’ll dig traps today.","After deciding to adapt to life in the Forest of Four Seasons, my routine had become simple.","In the morning and afternoon, I either explored the surroundings or repaired the shelter.","Yesterday had mostly been spent exploring because of the mature mandrake incident.","Today was for repairs.","Though \"repairs\" consisted of little more than chopping nearby trees and digging holes.","Ten minutes of either was enough to make my whole body ache, but it was necessary for my safety.","Maybe I’m lucky. I haven’t seen any sign of the owlbear.","Every time I heard something rustle, I flinched, but nothing happened.","This place was far from where the owlbear had appeared before, but I still couldn’t let my guard down.","According to the gallery, owlbears were extremely territorial.","Anything that entered their territory—beast or human—would be torn apart.","Considering that they were as large as houses, encountering one would almost certainly mean death.","Unless I can lure it back to the cave.","I stopped digging and looked toward the cave entrance.","It was just large enough for Mad Dog to pass through.","An owlbear the size of a small mountain would never fit inside easily.","With the trap I had laid near the entrance, I might even be able to kill it if I was lucky.","It would be better to know the limits of its territory first, though.","I continued digging until I checked the depth of the pit.","This should be deep enough.","Now all that remained was camouflage.","Why didn’t I place sharpened stakes or weapons at the bottom?","Because I might fall into it myself.","This wasn’t some trap far from camp.","It was directly in front of the cave and meant to serve as a final line of defense.","There should be something in the auction house I can use instead of a tarp...","I bought a piece of cloth to cover the top.","Then I stretched it tightly across the pit, held the edges down with stones, and covered it with dirt.","With that, one trap was complete.","A sense of satisfaction welled up inside me.","Why am I so proud of something like this?","A moment later, I sighed at my own situation.","It was too early to celebrate after finishing only one task.","The hardest work—logging—still remained.","Just thinking about it made the future look bleak.","Rustle—","Then I heard bushes moving nearby.","I flinched and instinctively hunched over.","Turning toward the source of the sound, I watched carefully.","\"...\"","Had I imagined it?","Nothing happened, no matter how long I stared at the bushes.","I let out a relieved sigh and entered the cave.","Naturally, I jumped over the trap before going inside.","Maybe I should put down a plank.","Having to jump over it every time could cause an accident in an emergency.","This was how I would slowly learn through trial and error.","I slung the logging axe over my shoulder and went back outside.","I have a whole new respect for lumberjacks.","How had people cut down so many trees in an age without chainsaws?","They had even used the timber to build wooden houses and ships.","Every day, I gained a greater appreciation for civilization.","That feeling would probably only grow stronger as time passed.","Could I ask the dwarf to make me a chainsaw?","The pointless thought crossed my mind, but I quickly dismissed it.","He had been drinking yesterday, so he was probably suffering from a hangover by now.","Besides, I was more curious about the Starlight Princess’s condition than the dwarf’s.","Thud! Thump!","I started with the tree I had left unfinished yesterday.","It was too thick to saw through easily.","Still, no tree could withstand being struck forever.","If I kept chopping, it would eventually fall.","I should make it fall toward the cave.","To do that, I also needed to cut into the opposite side.","After catching my breath, I walked around the tree.","Rustle—","Once again, the sound of moving grass reached my ears.","This time, there was no mistaking it.","I tensed and slowly turned around.","Rustle. Rustle.","It wasn’t my imagination.","The bushes were definitely moving.","The sound was also growing louder.","Something was approaching.","I slowly backed away, preparing to flee into the cave at any moment.","Push—","At last, the source of the sound crawled out from the dense undergrowth.","The instant I saw its face, my breath caught.","Sharp, vicious golden eyes.","A savage beak unique to a bird of prey.","And finally, a body as large as a house.","\"Grr?\"","It was an owlbear.","My body stiffened from the tension.","Fortunately, it did not attack immediately.","Perhaps this was its first time seeing a human in the Forest of Four Seasons.","It seemed to be observing me first.","I slowly stepped backward.","\"Grrrr...\"","\"Haa...\"","I glanced behind me, estimating the distance to the cave.","If I provoked it unnecessarily, I wouldn’t merely get hurt.","I would die.","Fortunately, the owlbear was so enormous that it probably couldn’t enter the cave.","I need something to distract it...","I searched my pocket and felt something round.","It was a Bigu Pill I had kept as emergency food.","Maybe I could use it to draw the creature’s attention.","Carefully, I tossed the pill onto the ground near the owlbear.","\"Sniff. Sniff.\"","\"...\"","The owlbear began smelling the pill.","Taking advantage of the distraction, I managed to reach the area near the cave entrance.","Apparently deciding that the scent was harmless, the owlbear picked up the Bigu Pill in its beak.","It spent a moment savoring the taste.","Then—","\"Kuegh! Kueeegh! Screeeech!\"","It let out a hideous shriek at the Bigu Pill’s distinctive bitterness.","The instant I heard that scream, I realized one thing.","If I didn’t get inside the cave immediately, I would be torn limb from limb.","\"Couldn’t you tell from the smell?! I thought bears had good noses!\"","As I ran, I felt a terrifying pressure behind me.","Was this what killing intent felt like?","My knees nearly gave out.","Tap!","Remembering the trap near the cave entrance, I dove over it.","My legs and knees would probably be badly scraped, but that was better than dying.","Boom!","\"Screeeeeech!\"","A tremendous impact sounded behind me.","The owlbear’s furious roar followed.","I hurriedly pushed myself up as every hair on my body stood on end.","\"Huff... Huff...\"","\"Screeeech! Screech!\"","Scrape! Scratch!","The owlbear’s razor-sharp claws tore at the ground. I watched it while gasping for breath.","Half of its enormous body had made it through.","In other words, it was stuck.","If the cave entrance had been even slightly larger, it probably would have squeezed through.","On top of that, thanks to the trap, its short bear-like legs couldn’t seem to reach the ground.","Th-This is my chance.","I didn’t have time to stand around watching.","Instead of the axe, I immediately grabbed another weapon.","The crossbow I had received from Passing Dwarf.","I loaded it with an ordinary bolt rather than a harpoon.","Even a normal bolt should be effective enough since it was dwarf-made.","Twang! Thud!","There was no need to aim precisely.","I simply fired, and the bolt struck its face.","\"Screeeeeech!\"","The owlbear thrashed violently as the bolt buried itself in its eye.","Just how strong was this thing for its movements to shake the entire cave?","My brief relief vanished when I saw the cave entrance slowly beginning to crumble under the owlbear’s monstrous strength.","I’m screwed...!","The moment the entrance collapsed, my life would be over.","Thud! Thunk! Smack!","Without hesitation, I fired the crossbow again and again.","The more bolts lodged in its face, the more violently the owlbear rampaged.","It showed no sign of calming down.","Does this bastard not have a brain?","I fired not only ordinary bolts but also the tethered harpoon.","The final harpoon struck its remaining eye.","With that, the owlbear lost its sight completely.","However, it was thrashing so wildly that approaching it was still impossible.","A spear! Right, I should buy a spear!","I hurriedly connected to the gallery and purchased a spear from the auction house.","I didn’t bother checking reviews or comparing prices.","As long as it was a spear, that was enough.","I stared at the still-rampaging owlbear and gripped the weapon with both hands.","\"Hraaah!\"","Stab!","Then I drove the spear into the owlbear’s head.","Perhaps I was lucky, because the spearhead struck the exact center of its forehead.","Before the owlbear could thrash even more violently, I pressed down with all my strength.","\"Keeeeeegh!\"","Crack!","But a spear was still a spear.","The spearhead might have been metal, but the shaft was wooden.","The owlbear’s swinging claw snapped it in half.","I nearly lost my balance, but managed to steady myself at the last second.","Rumble!","\"W-Whoa?\"","Then the thing I had feared finally happened.","The cave entrance almost completely collapsed.","While I stood there in shock, the owlbear forced its way inside.","I’m screwed.","I’m really screwed.","Even as the thought crossed my mind, I grabbed the Heavenly Demon’s sword and the Golden Shield.","The worst-case scenario had arrived, but the owlbear was already close to death.","If I waited for the right opportunity, I still had a chance.","\"Screeeeeech!\"","Boom!","With bolts and a spearhead embedded in its face, the owlbear charged straight at me.","Startled, I hurriedly raised the shield to protect myself.","SwordMaster’s post flashed through my mind, allowing me to brace in time.","Crash!","\"Kgh!\"","Even with the shield, there was no way I could completely stop an owlbear’s charge.","The difference in weight was too great.","I was a frail human, while the owlbear was still a bear.","Thud!","My feet left the ground, and I was sent flying.","Fortunately, I merely landed on the floor rather than crashing into the cave wall.","But it was too early to feel relieved.","I never took my eyes off the owlbear.","\"Screeeeeech!\"","It charged at me while I was still lying on the ground.","Even without its sight, it could probably estimate my location by sound.","That meant its attacks would be less accurate.","I focused until the very end.","...Left paw!","The owlbear raised its left foreleg.","All that remained was to determine where it intended to strike.","I opened my eyes wide and watched its attack.","The raised paw came down directly toward my left shoulder.","Bang!","I twisted my body just enough to avoid it.","Still, the deafening impact right beside my ear left me with a slight ringing sensation.","I already suffered from tinnitus, so I didn’t pay much attention to it.","What mattered was the counterattack that followed.","\"Uaaaaah!\"","With a shout, I thrust the Heavenly Demon’s sword toward the owlbear’s jaw.","I desperately hoped this would be the final attack.","Stab!","As expected of the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","It pierced through the owlbear’s jaw and drove all the way into its skull.","The moment its brain was struck, the owlbear merely convulsed.","It could no longer struggle.","Its brain had been destroyed so thoroughly that its body could no longer receive signals.","Boom!","\"Urgh!\"","The owlbear’s enormous body collapsed on top of me.","It was absurdly heavy.","Groaning and straining, I crawled out from beneath it.","As I did, I finally noticed the condition of my legs.","They’re completely scraped raw.","It was probably because of that desperate dive earlier.","Both knees had been badly torn up.","Calling them mere scrapes didn’t do the injuries justice.","The flesh had been peeled away so deeply that the muscle was nearly visible.","If the wounds had been even slightly deeper, I might have seen something white beneath them.","\"Ow... Ow...\"","As the adrenaline slowly faded, pain spread through my entire body.","That single dive had left wounds not only on my knees but all over me.","If I hadn’t been wearing clothes, my upper body would probably have been badly injured as well.","First, an elixir... Right. I don’t have one.","I would have to buy a potion.","Normally, I would have traded with the Starlight Princess for an elixir.","But she still hadn’t made a survival post.","The cooldown on trade requests hadn’t expired either, so I couldn’t contact her.","Drip—","\"Ugh...\"","I bought a reasonably priced potion from the auction house and poured it over my wounds.","True to the classic image of a potion, it was bright red.","At the very least, I could expect it to disinfect the injuries.","Afterward, I wrapped strips of cloth I had purchased separately around the wounds like bandages.","Since I was injured in so many places, I ended up wrapping cloth around each of my arms and legs.","Now all that remains is dealing with the owlbear.","Countless bolts were embedded in its face.","A bolt and a harpoon protruded from its eyes in particular.","Looking at the corpse alone made it seem a little pitiful, but it had tried to kill me.","***","Title: I Killed an Owlbear","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the owlbear’s corpse)","I seriously thought I was going to die fighting it ;;","I’ll put it up on the auction house soon, so do whatever you want.","└ Whoa. How did you kill it?","└ Wild Grylls: The cave entrance was narrow, so I lured it there. Then I wrecked its face with a crossbow.","└ Hahahaha, look at its face. It has a bolt and a harpoon where its eyes should be.","└ Are you really an ordinary person?","└ He killed an owlbear and still calls himself ordinary. Damn.","└ Heavenly Demon: Were you injured?","└ Wild Grylls: Other than a lot of scraped wounds, I’m fine.","└ Heavenly Demon: That is fortunate. Whenever I see posts like this, I feel that your basic combat ability is remarkably good. Am I mistaken?","└ Wild Grylls: I wouldn’t have been able to finish it off without the sword you gave me.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hearing that pleases me. Is there any weapon you require?","A weapon I needed.","I definitely thought having a proper spear would be useful.","Still, I had no intention of asking the Heavenly Demon for one.","As I had said many times before, depending too heavily on someone else was never a good idea.","└ Wild Grylls: Not yet. Oh! I’m getting used to sitting cross-legged now. Could you teach me an internal cultivation method?","└ Heavenly Demon: That is wonderful news. I have been organizing one in a way that will be easy for you to understand.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you.","└ SwordMaster: That was impressive. You said you lured it to the cave entrance, correct?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes.","└ SwordMaster: You seem surprisingly quick-witted.","└ Wild Grylls: Haha, thank you.","└ SwordMaster: Someday, you’ll be able to face one head-on in a fair one-on-one fight.","└ Wild Grylls: Is there a method for fighting owlbears?","└ SwordMaster: They’re quite easy. Their claws are their main weapon, so you simply cut off their legs. When they raise a foreleg to strike, sever it as it comes down. Easy, right?","└ Wild Grylls: ;;;","It was probably easy only by her standards.","How could an ordinary person possibly understand a genius?","After scrolling through the gallery’s reactions, I dealt with the owlbear first.","The moment I listed the corpse on the auction house, it vanished.","Bidding began immediately.","The auction period was twenty-four hours.","I wonder if it’ll sell for a lot.","I had no idea.","What I needed now was rest.","Before that, though, I had to inspect the trap.","The owlbear had damaged it, so repairs were essential.","\"Hm?\"","\"...\"","But the moment I stepped outside the cave, I came face-to-face with something strange.","Bright, round golden eyes.","A bird-like beak.","A body about the size of a medium-sized dog and a face overflowing with curiosity.","\"Kyuu?\"","A baby owlbear stood before me, tilting its head."]},{"title":"Chapter 21","paragraphs":["Owlbear (2)","Every animal is cute when it’s young.","People even say that their cuteness is what earns them mercy from predators and helps them survive.","No matter how fierce the species, most animals are irresistibly adorable as babies.","\"Kyuu?\"","Just like the baby owlbear standing in front of me.","All it did was tilt its head, yet it dealt a critical hit straight to my heart.","If I had to describe the baby owlbear...","It looked like a fluffy ball of fur staring at me with wide, round eyes.","The adult owlbear had a face that was terrifying beyond words, but this little one’s face was incredibly gentle.","Still, this was the wilderness. Even an owlbear cub would have a hard time surviving here alone.","So what should I do?","\"Here, here. Come on.\"","\"Kyuu.\"","What else?","Pet it, of course.","I beckoned with my fingers, and the baby owlbear tilted its head before cautiously waddling over.","It pressed its nose against my hand and began sniffing it, acting on pure instinct.","While it was busy smelling me, I slowly raised my other hand.","Pat... pat...","\"Kyung?\"","The one thing four-legged animals could never do for themselves—","Having someone gently stroke their head.","The baby owlbear blinked in surprise at the unfamiliar sensation and looked up at me with wide eyes.","Its huge round owl-like eyes...","The little tufts of feathers sticking up from its head...","How could something this adorable even exist?","It was only about the size of a medium-sized dog, so it wasn’t particularly intimidating.","\"Grrr... rrr...\"","Apparently my petting felt good.","The baby owlbear closed its eyes and let out a strange, contented rumble.","While continuing to rub its head, I quietly opened the Gallery.","***","Title: Found a Baby Owlbear","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the baby owlbear.)","(Another photo of the baby owlbear.)","(Video of me petting the baby owlbear.)","(Video of the baby owlbear smiling.)","Killed its mom, then found this little guy. Seriously adorable.","LOL it’s so cute.","Look at that fluffy fur.","└ Completely different from the adults.","Wait... you killed the mother of something this cute? You’re evil.","The Orphan Maker strikes again.","LMAO Orphan Maker.","Wild Grylls: Excuse me?","The moderator’s authority is unstoppable.","Tyranny!","LOL.","Can I post my face too? I’m cute.","Don’tAbandonTheHero: Posts that cause psychological damage will be banned!","Look how serious they are. LOL.","?","PrincessChaenggu: What the hell? If you’ve got a problem, fight me.","Heavenly Demon: Sacrilegious. I feel like hugging it until it bursts.","Don’tAbandonTheHero: Three-hour ban.","Wild Grylls: ??? Wait, why?","Don’tAbandonTheHero: Cute things require at least ten photos and three videos.","Wild Grylls: That was a rule?","Don’tAbandonTheHero: I just made it.","Grylls, you’re an orphan too. Did you really have to make another one?","Wild Grylls: Its mom was trying to kill me. I wanted to live too.","Fair enough. Survival comes first. LOL.","Heavenly Demon: It truly is adorable. I’d like to hold that little ball of fluff at least once.","└ PrincessChaenggu: I know, right? Just like me.","...Heavenly Demon?","?","Most of the comments were filled with praise for the baby owlbear.","Honestly, anyone’s heart would melt at the sight of such a fluffy little creature.","But the wilderness was always cruel.","One particular comment caught my eye.","Who cares if it’s cute? You’ll have to kill it eventually anyway.","Why would you kill something this adorable?","Boo! Trash!","No, seriously. If you don’t kill it, are you going to raise it? The moment it gets hungry it’ll eat Grylls first.","I heard about this. A noble who raised an owlbear went on vacation and got eaten when he came back.","You can even raise one?","As long as you keep it well-fed, its loyalty is incredible. Stop feeding it, and you become the meal.","Besides, this is the wild. How are you supposed to raise it out here?","Do you really have to kill it? It’s so cute.","Judging by its size, it looks like it was just born.","After reading those comments, I looked down at the owlbear.","It was happily rubbing its face against my hand.","Just watching it made all the gloom in my heart melt away...","But a wild animal was still a wild animal.","Especially an owlbear.","Apparently they were notorious for their enormous appetites.","They even ate their own owners on a regular basis.","\"Kyuu... Kyuu...\"","This little guy?","I looked at it with a heavy heart.","To be rational, the safest option would be to kill it myself.","Some people might ask why I couldn’t just raise it...","But I was barely surviving as it was.","Even wealthy nobles struggled to keep one.","How was I supposed to?","’And it’s not like you can easily buy food for something like this at the auction.’","If it were that easy, I would’ve bought it long ago.","It was a shame, but there was no helping it.","Still...","Killing it left a bad taste in my mouth.","It would be better to release it back into the wild.","I made up my mind.","Wild Grylls: I’ll just let it return to the wild. I’m barely feeding myself as it is.","So you have no sense of responsibility?","Wild Grylls: Its mom tried to kill me. What responsibility?","...Fair point.","Fastest agreement ever. LOL.","Just buy meat at the auction. Aren’t you rich now, Grylls?","Wild Grylls: If it were that simple, I’d have bought meat for myself already.","Come on, you’ve got money. Can’t even feed one baby?","Wild Grylls: Why should I raise it? I’m trying to save money in case something happens.","How much money do you even have?","Let’s see...","After getting paid so generously by Allfather, I did have a comfortable amount of money.","But raising an animal cost a fortune.","Especially not a dog or cat—","A bear .","Even if it was still a cub, its appetite would only get worse.","Wild Grylls: I do have money, but spending it on this is...","Are you an idiot? Just keep the owlbear as your bodyguard.","Wild Grylls: What are you talking about?","You know how strong adult owlbears are. Once it grows up, nothing beats having one beside you. Treat it like your personal knight.","...That’s actually convincing.","Not gonna lie, that’s a really good idea.","Yeah, raising it sounds better.","The argument was surprisingly persuasive.","I looked at the baby owlbear.","This adorable little puffball would eventually grow into that terrifying monster.","And as long as I kept it well-fed, it would supposedly be fiercely loyal.","...It would be nice to have company, too.","The Gallery was nice, but it wasn’t the same as interacting with a living creature.","The baby owlbear stared back at me with curious eyes.","Maybe...","Keeping it as a companion wasn’t such a bad idea after all.","If I ever ran short on money, I could always sell a mandrake or hunt more golden poison frogs.","’But... what does this thing eat?’","Bears were omnivores that would even eat carrion.","But this wasn’t an ordinary bear.","It was an owlbear.","To find out what it liked to eat, I made another post.","***","Title: What Do Owlbears Eat?","Wild Grylls","Pretty much anything.","Yeah, same as the comment above. Their diet’s basically identical to a regular bear’s.","Wild Grylls: Do they like honey?","They absolutely love it. LOL.","Perfect.","Then I’d test it myself.","I opened the auction house and searched for honey.","Just to be safe, I carefully read the reviews.","Apparently the seller’s family had been running an apiary for three generations.","Their proof was... something else.","How do we even know that’s real honey?","(Photo of the seller’s face swollen from countless bee stings.)","...Alright. I’ll buy two jars.","Now that’s convincing proof. LOL.","Something like that.","Thanks to those reviews, I bought it without hesitation.","After purchasing the honey, I also bought a large wooden spoon.","I scooped up a spoonful of honey and held it out to the baby owlbear.","\"Kyuu?\"","\"Go on. It’s delicious.\"","\"Sniff... sniff...\"","The little owlbear hesitated, apparently seeing honey for the first time.","Watching the thick honey drip off the spoon felt almost wasteful.","Still, its keen sense of smell soon won over its caution.","Before long, it slowly opened its mouth wide.","\"Yum.\"","\"Is it good?\"","\"...\"","After taking a bite of the honey, the little creature froze for a moment.","\"Kyuuuuuu!\"","\"H-Huh?\"","\"Kyuaaaa!\"","It let out a bizarre cry and began devouring the honey in a frenzy.","Startled, I set the jar on the ground and backed away a couple of steps.","\"Chomp, chomp, chomp, chomp!\"","It sure knew how to make food look delicious.","It was also fascinating to see such a long tongue emerge from that short beak.","The baby owlbear was completely entranced by the sweetness of honey, something it had never tasted before.","I hadn’t even gotten a single bite.","Had I known this would happen, I would’ve tasted some first.","Anyway, it seemed to like it, so that was a relief. It would take a while to finish the whole jar.","’What should I name it?’","I had decided to raise it for the sake of my survival and mental well-being.","I’d never owned a pet before, but even I knew that choosing a name was important.","’It’s a fluffy ball of fur, so... Fluffy?’","Was that too lazy?","Still, no other name suited it better.","Asking the Gallery to name it seemed like a bad idea.","They would probably come up with all sorts of ridiculous names.","\"Fluffy.\"","\"Chomp, chomp, chomp!\"","\"Fluffy?\"","\"Chomp, chomp, chomp!\"","Was it ignoring me because it was too busy eating honey?","Well, I’d already decided on the name. I could slowly teach it to respond later.","Before that, I had to upload a picture.","How could I possibly keep something this cute to myself?","***","Title: Decided on a Name","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the baby owlbear eating honey.)","Its name is Fluffy because its fur is fluffy. Objections will not be accepted.","You really put zero effort into that name. LOL.","How is that any different from naming a dog Brownie? LOL.","LMAO.","Wild Grylls: Then you guys come up with something.","Heavenly Demon: Since it is a round ball of fur, how about Wonmo, meaning \"Round Fur\"?","Wild Grylls: Ma’am?","Of course the old-timer would suggest something like that. LOL.","It does roll off the tongue, though. Wonmo!","Your name is Wonmo from now on. LOL.","SwordMaster: Fluffy isn’t bad. It’s cute.","Wild Grylls: Can’t you think of anything else?","SwordMaster: Is it male or female?","Wild Grylls: Give me a second.","The moment I read that, I cautiously moved behind the owlbear.","Then I lowered my head and spotted two round balls.","It was unmistakably male.","There was no more reliable way to check.","Wild Grylls: Male.","SwordMaster: Alexander II. What do you think? Sounds cool, right?","Wild Grylls: ...","Isn’t that the name of a general?","Yeah, a famous general from Messiah. LOL.","If it were female, she’d have named it Alexandria. LMAO.","PrincessChaenggu: How about Naldo?","Who’s Naldo?","Some famous football player.","PrincessChaenggu: You caught me.","Caught you doing what? LOL.","Look at how shameless she is. LOL.","PraiseTheSun: Sultan VII. You can tell at a glance that he has the face of a king.","What part of that fat thing looks royal?","PraiseTheSun: Pigs have traditionally been considered one of the faces of royalty.","Really?","PraiseTheSun: Absolutely. I swear on my son.","Why are you betting your son on it? LOL.","Naturally, my opinion was ignored, and they started a vote without me.","See?","All kinds of bizarre combinations were already appearing.","It would be better to simply call him Fluffy than let the Gallery decide.","Unfortunately, the Gallery users had other plans.","There are too many names. We should settle it with a vote.","So the five choices are Fluffy, Wonmo, Alexander, Naldo, and Sultan?","Any more suggestions? If not, I’ll post the poll right away.","Shouldn’t Grylls be the one to post it?","No way. He’ll obviously rig it so Fluffy wins.","Wild Grylls: ??? I’m the owner! Why are you deciding this without me?","***","Title: Vote for the Baby Owlbear’s Name","Fluffy: 1%Wonmo: 39%Alexander: 21%Naldo: 19%Sultan: 20%","By the principle of majority rule, his name is officially Wonmo! Decision finalized!","This was absurd.","I was the one raising him, so why were they naming him however they pleased?","But who were the Gallery users?","A bunch of people who never listened to anyone else.","Heavenly Demon: Everyone has excellent taste. I am pleased.","SwordMaster: Why did Wonmo win? That name sounds so old-fashioned.","PrincessChaenggu: I refuse to accept this.","PraiseTheSun: What a shame. He truly has the face of a king.**","Wild Grylls: I keep telling you, he’s my pet. Why are you deciding his name?","Heavenly Demon: If you dislike it, then use whatever name you desire. This lady shall respect your decision.","You can feel the disappointment radiating from that comment.","Grylls, the elder is asking so nicely. You’re not really going to refuse, are you?","If you refuse, you’re seriously a terrible person.","Wild Grylls: ...","What a rotten situation.","Now I had no choice but to name him Wonmo.","The Heavenly Demon had helped me many times, so it was hard to reject her suggestion.","I rubbed my face and sighed.","Why was I letting the Gallery control me like this?","’Still, Wonmo isn’t that bad of a name... is it?’","Wonmo.","It sounded like the sort of name people used in old countryside villages.","It felt rustic to the point of sounding a little dim-witted.","’At least they didn’t name him Dolsoe.’","Although...","Would Dolsoe have been better?","I honestly couldn’t tell anymore.","I looked at the baby owlbear, who was still eating honey and had now somehow become Wonmo, before quietly calling out.","\"Wonmo.\"","\"Kyuu?\"","Wait.","You didn’t look up when I called you Fluffy.","Why did you immediately react to Wonmo?","I stared at the baby owlbear—Wonmo—with an incredulous expression.","The longer I gazed into those round eyes, the calmer I felt.","’Ah, whatever.’","I approached him.","Honey was dripping from his beak.","I stroked his head and firmly imprinted the name into his mind.","\"From now on, your name is Wonmo. Got it?\"","\"Kyuu!\"","He gave me a bright smile, as though he loved it.","But why?","***","Meanwhile, at around the same time...","\"Hehe.\"","The Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol, smiled proudly.","The name she had suggested, Wonmo, had become the baby owlbear’s official name.","The Gallery was already clamoring for more pictures of Wonmo.","That alone proved how powerful Wonmo’s appeal was.","What could possibly be more satisfying than this?","’To think the name received such an enthusiastic response even in the Gallery. Grylls must be delighted as well.’","Had Grylls heard that, he would have started foaming at the mouth."]},{"title":"Chapter 22","paragraphs":["Owlbear (3)","Now that the name had been decided, all that remained was to bond with Wonmo.","Giving him honey had raised his affection toward me considerably, but he was still only a cub.","He couldn’t yet tell right from wrong, and with his mother dead, I would have to take care of him.","But then the biggest problem occurred to me.","’How am I supposed to raise him?’","Even back home, I had never owned a single pet.","I had barely been able to take care of myself, so raising an animal had never even crossed my mind.","At least I had seen enough dogs and cats to have some idea of how to handle them.","An owlbear, however, was a completely different matter.","Aside from the fact that they had enormous appetites and were extremely ferocious, I knew absolutely nothing about them.","’The most important thing is making him recognize me as his owner.’","I watched Wonmo scurry around the cave.","Perhaps because he was still young, he was overflowing with curiosity.","\"Sniff. Sniff, sniff.\"","He wandered around the place where his mother had died for quite some time.","Judging by the way he kept sniffing the ground, he seemed to remember her scent.","Unfortunately, the mother owlbear had already been shipped off to America...","No, to the auction house.","People were still steadily bidding on it, so I would soon receive a large sum of money.","’But that tiny thing is really going to grow that big?’","The mother owlbear had been, with only slight exaggeration, about the size of a house.","But look at Wonmo.","The round little fellow was only the size of a medium-sized dog.","Even the pale color of his fur suggested that, just as the Gallery users had said, he had only recently been born.","\"Kueeeek!\"","\"Oh dear.\"","He was far too curious for his own good.","Why would he try eating the fasting pills inside the sack?","With his sharp sense of smell, he should have noticed their bitter scent.","Why had he still eaten one?","\"Kuaaaak!\"","Rip!","Yet even as a cub, his ferocity remained intact.","The moment Wonmo swung his claws, the sack tore open.","I nearly screamed when the fasting pills inside came spilling out.","\"Hey! Park Wonmo! You can’t do that!\"","\"Kyuu? Kyuu?\"","\"No matter how bad they taste, you can’t just tear the sack apart!\"","Even as I scolded him, I hurried to deal with the mess.","I laid the torn sack on its side so the remaining pills wouldn’t spill out.","Then I bought another sack of a suitable size from the auction house and transferred them into it.","’Didn’t they say owlbears would even eat rotting corpses?’","Just how disgusting were these fasting pills for every animal to react the same way?","I had grown used to them, but apparently animals couldn’t tolerate them.","’First, I need to make him understand that this is his home...’","That raised another question.","Why had the mother owlbear brought her cub here?","Owlbears were highly territorial animals, which meant they were extremely sensitive about their domains.","In other words, they normally avoided entering another creature’s territory.","Even if she had been scouting the area, there was no reason for her to bring along a newborn cub.","’Did something drive them out of their original territory?’","No.","That probably wasn’t it.","The mother owlbear had been in perfect condition when she encountered me.","She hadn’t immediately tried to tear me apart either. She had first examined the area.","Perhaps they had simply been moving...","I couldn’t be sure.","The best way to find out would be to locate their nest.","’That’s impossible right now.’","Just look at that ball of fur staring at me with those huge round eyes.","He was sitting on the straw-filled mat, gazing blankly at me.","\"Come here, you little cutie.\"","\"Kyuu.\"","He was so adorable I could hardly stand it.","How could anything be this cute?","I showered Wonmo with affection, scratching beneath his chin and stroking his head to my heart’s content.","Right.","How could I possibly leave him behind?","Even if I did go somewhere, I couldn’t leave the cave unattended until he understood that this place was his home.","’Then repairing the cave is probably my best option...’","It was a little disappointing, but it wasn’t a bad choice.","The greatest problem, however, was still water .","I could manage my own hygiene, but Wonmo was another matter.","There was no telling what kind of disease he might bring back, so bathing him was essential.","’Washing him in the creek would be difficult.’","The golden poison frog wasn’t the issue.","The problem was that I had no idea where Wonmo might run off to.","If he crossed to the opposite bank, it would be a disaster.","And if the terrain changed at the exact moment he crossed, it would become an even greater disaster.","’Isn’t there a better way?’","I stared at Wonmo, who was watching me blankly, then silently picked him up.","His fur was this fluffy, yet I hadn’t been allowed to name him Fluffy.","I’m sorry, little guy. Your owner failed you.","As though he understood my feelings, he rubbed his face against me.","Grrrrumble.","Then a strange noise reached my ears.","It definitely hadn’t come from my stomach.","I slowly set Wonmo down and stared at his face.","\"Kyuu...\"","\"Are you hungry?\"","\"Slurp.\"","Don’t lick your lips while staring at me.","That’s terrifying.","Before Wonmo could go berserk, I hurriedly opened the auction house.","It sold all kinds of goods, so I could easily buy some suitable meat.","’They even sell monster meat?’","Orcs, goblins, gnolls, trolls, and more.","I had no idea why anyone would list that sort of thing at the auction house.","Apparently monster meat was so tough and foul-tasting that nobody ate it unless they were desperate.","The sellers had probably listed it simply because they didn’t know what else to do with it.","Its price was also comparatively low.","\"Here. Try this.\"","\"Sniff, sniff, sniff.\"","I bought some orc meat and placed it in front of Wonmo.","He sniffed it curiously before taking a huge bite.","\"Nom, nom, nom.\"","\"Is it edible?\"","\"Nom, nom, nom, nom. Crunch! Chomp!\"","He ate it without hesitation.","As expected of an owlbear, his diet appeared to be close to that of an ordinary bear.","I placed a bowl of water beside him, then went outside.","It would take him a while to finish all that, so I intended to complete the rest of my work.","Thwack! Thwack!","After chopping away with the axe for some time, the tree had begun to wobble slightly.","The sound was no longer a dull thud but closer to the noise of splitting firewood.","After checking the tree’s position relative to the cave, I kicked it hard.","The tree slowly tipped over before collapsing with a series of loud cracks.","Craaaack!","Thud!","It was so massive that merely falling produced an enormous amount of noise.","Surely that wouldn’t irritate any nearby animals.","Fortunately, the greatest threat in the area—the owlbear—had already been sold through the auction house.","’Should I cut it into three sections?’","I walked over to the fallen tree and estimated its size.","A tree this large could probably provide enough material for three or four sections of barricade.","The problem was that I still had to split and shape the thick trunk.","’Why did I do this?’","One problem after another.","There was still an overwhelming amount of work left.","I should have learned an internal energy cultivation technique first, just as I had originally planned.","I had gotten bored, started doing something unnecessary, and only created more work for myself.","After letting out a deep sigh, I decided to begin by removing the smaller branches.","There were so many that I wouldn’t have to worry about firewood for quite some time.","Once I had roughly cleared away the branches, I planned to cut the trunk into smaller sections.","’A sword probably won’t work. I’ll need to buy a saw...’","Just thinking about sawing through it made me dizzy.","Still, I couldn’t give up now.","Before buying the saw, I returned to the cave to rest.","\"Grrrrr...\"","When I entered the cave, I found Wonmo asleep on the mat.","He had completely finished the monster meat I had given him earlier.","No matter the species, babies tended to spend most of the day sleeping.","I watched Wonmo, curled up into a ball, then silently opened the Gallery.","***","Title: Our Wonmo Is Sleeping","Wild Grylls","(Photo of Wonmo curled into a ball while sleeping.)","Isn’t he adorable?","Ah... This is so healing...","More! Give us more!","He really looks like a ball. LOL.","The more I see it, the more I think Wonmo was the perfect name.","I seriously want to hug him at least once.","The responses were overwhelmingly positive.","Anyone who could look at this and remain unaffected couldn’t possibly be human.","As I proudly read through the comments, one in particular caught my attention.","Passing Dwarf: Is that emergency food? Looks tasty.","Wild Grylls: Are you insane?","Passing Dwarf: I drank yesterday and just woke up. What happened?","It was Passing Dwarf.","Apparently he had only just woken up after drinking himself to sleep.","How could anyone look at Wonmo and call him emergency food?","I thought the dwarf was an idiot in more ways than one, but the other Gallery users were even worse.","So Grylls became a pet servant. LOL.","I’m telling you, the moment he gets hungry, he’ll eat you first. LOL.","Wild Grylls: You people are seriously insane.","Right.","This was the Gallery.","I let out a hollow laugh.","Since Passing Dwarf was here, I decided to ask him something.","Wonmo isn’t Grylls’s emergency food. Grylls is Wonmo’s emergency food. LOL.","Passing Dwarf: Really? So you’ve taken in a master.","Wild Grylls: Dwarf, can you get me a good saw?","Passing Dwarf: A saw? Oh, did you cut down a tree?","Wild Grylls: Yeah. But just thinking about sawing it makes my balls tremble.","Passing Dwarf: Unless it’s made of adamantium, one saw is about as good as another. It’s better to chop into it with an axe first, then start sawing.","Wild Grylls: That’s still too exhausting.","Passing Dwarf: Did you think it would be easy? That kind of work normally takes at least two people.","It was infuriating, but I couldn’t argue with him.","Nothing was ever easy.","The best option would be to learn an internal energy cultivation technique from the Heavenly Demon.","If I could use mana, surely the work would become easier somehow.","Until then, I had no choice but to brute-force it through sheer effort.","Passing Dwarf: Or sell the log at the auction house and buy a fence or barricade. Wouldn’t that solve it?","Wild Grylls: There aren’t any.","Passing Dwarf: Why not?","That wasn’t the only strange thing.","Why weren’t there any?","I had searched too, but couldn’t find what I needed.","There were a few fence-like structures, but none in the form I wanted.","Wild Grylls: Why are you asking me? If there aren’t any, there aren’t any. And wouldn’t they be expensive?","Passing Dwarf: Even if they are, they’d still be cheaper than the log you cut down. Do you have any idea how valuable wood grown in the Forest of Four Seasons is?","Wild Grylls: Of course I don’t. I told you I came from another world.","Passing Dwarf: Wasn’t that just drunken nonsense?","Wild Grylls: You bastard. LOL.","Hard to blame him for not believing you. LOL.","LMAO.","Wild Grylls: Why didn’t you tell me sooner?","Passing Dwarf: So you’d suffer a little.","Wild Grylls: You son of a bitch.","Passing Dwarf: Sawing isn’t the end of it. You need to dry out the moisture, plane the wood, and do a bunch of other things.","Wild Grylls: What happens if I don’t remove the moisture?","Passing Dwarf: Mold everywhere!","Wild Grylls: Ha...","Looks like reality just hit him. LOL.","At least you gained knowledge. Have a drink!","No.","Why did everyone seem so untrustworthy?","I really wanted a drink now.","Had I known this, I would’ve at least asked the Gallery before starting.","Just as the dwarf said, it seemed better to list the log at the auction house.","’In that blocky world, they made things so easily.’","That was only because the protagonist over there had absurd abilities.","As long as he had the materials, he could instantly craft anything from a sword to a pickaxe.","That was what made him incredible.","Why had I been dropped into this hellish world without a single useful ability?","The situation made me want to sigh endlessly, but at least I had the Gallery.","’Should I ask the dwarf to make it?’","He was irritating, but no one I knew was better at this kind of work.","After thinking for a moment, I asked Passing Dwarf.","Passing Dwarf: Except when I’m drunk. LOL.","Wild Grylls: What are you holding right now?","Passing Dwarf: Beer.","Wild Grylls: You son of a...","Passing Dwarf: It’s basically a soft drink to a dwarf. Got a problem?","That is technically true. LOL.","It’s the kind of truth that deserves a beating. LOL.","Wild Grylls: Then if I give you the log, can you make me a suitable barricade?","Passing Dwarf: Just buy one at the auction house. I checked earlier and saw a few. Drying the wood alone takes several weeks.","Wild Grylls: The auction house doesn’t have the kind I want.","Passing Dwarf: Fair enough. They might sell fences, but probably not proper barricades. I’ll see what I can find.","Wild Grylls: You’re not messing with me, are you?","Passing Dwarf: I don’t joke about this kind of work.","That was a relief.","My head was spinning.","What kind of alcoholic lunatic was this?","Still, he didn’t seem to be joking, so I looked through the auction house again.","As expected, there were no barricades in the shape I wanted.","Once a barricade was built, it tended to remain in place, so demand was probably low.","Even if someone needed one, they would likely cut and process nearby timber rather than buy it.","’I should list the log first.’","I registered the fallen log at the auction house.","I had no idea how much it would sell for, but I hoped it was as valuable as the dwarf claimed.","If it fetched a high price, every tree around here would become a savings account.","’I’ll have to wait for the barricade.’","The dwarf said he would list one soon, so I could buy it when he did.","Until then, I planned to improve the area around the cave little by little.","’It’s not like I’m going to live here forever, but...’","First, I marked the trees that needed to be cut down.","I planned to dig a moat after installing the barricade.","Once I had roughly marked the trees with my axe, I returned to the cave to rest.","Wonmo was still deep in dreamland.","He was truly adorable.","I smiled warmly and opened the Gallery again.","Many more comments had appeared in the meantime.","Among them, a comment from the familiar named user PraiseTheSun stood out the most.","PraiseTheSun: Hey. Have you brushed Wonmo’s fur?","Wild Grylls: Why would I need to brush him?","PraiseTheSun: Animals with thick fur need regular brushing. Either that or a bath. Try brushing him once.","I didn’t really understand, but I should probably follow the advice.","It seemed that PraiseTheSun also raised animals.","I bought a fine-toothed comb from the auction house and approached Wonmo.","Then, careful not to wake him, I gently began combing through his thick fur.","\"...What is this?\"","Now I understood why PraiseTheSun had brought it up.","Something was wriggling between the teeth of the comb.","It looked absolutely disgusting.","\"T-Ticks?\"","I desperately needed water.","Right now."]},{"title":"Chapter 23","paragraphs":["Water (1)","Had I underestimated the wilderness, or had I simply been too optimistic?","The moment I saw the ticks crawling between the teeth of the comb, I realized something.","When it came to hygiene, the wilderness was far more dangerous than I had imagined.","To properly maintain cleanliness, I needed to secure a large amount of water somehow.","’Does water have some kind of personal grudge against me?’","In any case, washing Wonmo clean came first.","I should probably take a bath while I was at it.","It was fortunate that I had been wearing clothes. Otherwise, I would almost certainly have been bitten by ticks too.","First, I wanted to thank PraiseTheSun and ask for advice.","Wild Grylls: Holy crap... What are all these ticks? Things could’ve gone seriously wrong if I’d ignored them.","PraiseTheSun: At least you noticed now. Washing him with hot water should do the trick.","Wild Grylls: I’m in an environment where getting water is difficult.","PraiseTheSun: Then apply insect repellent to your body. A hot bath would still be the best solution, though.","According to PraiseTheSun, an owlbear’s hide was too thick for ticks to cause it much harm.","The real problem was me, since my skin was comparatively thin and I was constantly beside him.","I took off my clothes, shook them out thoroughly, and applied insect repellent all over my body.","Fortunately, I didn’t find any ticks on myself.","’I need to start wearing long pants.’","The uniform PrincessChaenggu had given me only had long sleeves.","For the time being, I would have to rely on insect repellent.","’No wonder people in survival documentaries always cover their entire bodies.’","Thanks to this, I finally understood the importance of proper clothing.","Long sleeves and long pants were essential.","After carefully applying the repellent without missing a single spot, I looked at Wonmo.","He was still sleeping soundly, completely unaware of what had happened.","’Right. It’s not your fault.’","I changed my clothes and thought things over.","Water had become even more urgent than before.","Unfortunately, the golden poison frogs had firmly occupied the creek, making things difficult.","Still, the creek was the closest water source, so abandoning it would be a waste.","’Should I dig a water channel instead? It’s not that far away.’","It wasn’t a bad option.","The only downside was the physical labor involved.","As I had mentioned before, the creek wasn’t very far from the cave, so perhaps it wouldn’t be that difficult.","However, I had no idea how to dig a proper channel, so I would need advice.","***","Title: Dwarf, Help Me","Wild Grylls","I’m thinking of digging a water channel. Give me some advice.","Passing Dwarf: For free?","Wild Grylls: Want one of the frogs? They’re expensive.","Passing Dwarf: I was joking. LOL.","More than anything else, I was concerned that the water might become contaminated.","There was a limit to how much joking one person should do.","Suddenly, I became curious about his age.","Considering how knowledgeable he was, he probably wasn’t young.","Yet he behaved like someone who had never fully grown up.","Passing Dwarf: Are you planning to live there permanently?","Wild Grylls: Not really, but getting water is too difficult. Those frogs are making it a nightmare.","Passing Dwarf: If you’re not settling there permanently, don’t dig a channel. The workload is insane.","Wild Grylls: Is it really that bad?","Passing Dwarf: Yeah. And if you can’t prevent erosion, you’ll end up with nothing but filthy water. Better not to do it.","Erosion was that phenomenon, wasn’t it?","The process where rock was gradually worn away by various factors.","There was no need to explain what would happen to soil, which was far softer than rock.","Wild Grylls: Then is there no other way?","Passing Dwarf: Roughly how far away is the creek?","Wild Grylls: About ten to twelve minutes on foot?","Passing Dwarf: At that distance, it’d be better to carry the water yourself.","Wild Grylls: So I can get eaten by a snake on the way? LOL.","Passing Dwarf: Hey. Wait, wait, wait.","He’s suddenly desperate. LOL.","He can’t even drink water freely. LOL.","Nothing is ever easy for him. LOL.","It wasn’t as though I hadn’t considered carrying the water myself.","But I had no idea what dangers I might encounter along the way, and drawing the water itself would be difficult.","The moment I put my hand into the creek, golden poison frogs would come swarming out.","As though I could casually collect water under those conditions.","I had hands and a functioning brain too.","But this was the wilderness.","A single mistake could cost me my life, so I had no choice but to prioritize safety as much as possible.","Passing Dwarf: There is one method, but you’ll have to build something. You okay with that?","Wild Grylls: Yeah. That’s fine.","Passing Dwarf: First, where is the creek relative to you? Uphill or downhill?","Wild Grylls: I have to go uphill to reach it.","Passing Dwarf: Oh. Then this should be easy. It might be expensive, though. Is that okay?","Wild Grylls: Could it possibly cost more than my life?","Passing Dwarf: Good. I’ll make a post soon.","Starlight Princess.","A familiar named user who had gone silent for some time.","I had been worried that something might have happened to her, so seeing the message immediately put me at ease.","[Wild Grylls: Starlight Princess? Is that really you?]","[Starlight Princess: Hello, Mr. Grylls! Yes! It’s really me!]","Passing Dwarf had said he would post an explanation, so I only needed to wait patiently.","At the same time, I felt uneasy.","If the method was complicated enough to require an entire post, it must involve a fair amount of work.","Would I really be able to secure a stable water supply?","Water always seemed to become an obstacle for me.","[Starlight Princess has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","\"Huh?\"","I had been absentmindedly browsing the Gallery when the notification appeared.","My eyes widened as I stared at the message.","Even through the text, I could feel her cheerful energy.","Once a Gallery nickname was chosen, it could never be changed.","That meant the person requesting the trade truly was Starlight Princess.","With a broad smile, I sent her a reply.","[Wild Grylls: Have you fully recovered?]","[Starlight Princess: Yes! Thanks to the gift you gave me, I made a complete recovery! Thank you so much!]","I was relieved to hear she had recovered.","I had been deeply worried that something had happened to her.","There would be no need to worry about that anymore.","Her incurable illness had been cured.","[Wild Grylls: That’s wonderful. Congratulations.]","[Starlight Princess: It’s all thanks to you, Mr. Grylls. I couldn’t post anything because I was undergoing medical examinations...]","I could roughly understand what had happened.","After finally obtaining the health she had longed for so desperately, she must have wanted to undergo a thorough examination.","The fact that she had returned after only a day meant she was almost certainly fully cured.","[Starlight Princess: Yes. Honestly, I feel like running around right now. Unfortunately, my parents won’t allow it.]","[Wild Grylls: They’re worried about you, so don’t push yourself too hard.]","[Starlight Princess: I think this every time we speak, but you truly are a kind person, Mr. Grylls. People like you are rare in the Gallery.]","I tilted my head when she called me kind.","People seemed to say that about me surprisingly often.","Considering the Gallery’s culture, perhaps it was true.","’I’m not really sure.’","Maybe it simply meant that this world was so terrible that basic decency stood out.","Given the era, human rights were probably treated like something to be chewed up and spat out.","Combine that with the Gallery’s uniquely unhealthy culture, and there was no need for further explanation.","[Starlight Princess has registered an item for trade.]","[Starlight Princess: This is the elixir I mentioned before. I kept only enough for emergencies and sent you the rest, so there should be plenty.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you so much. You’re not feeling any discomfort, are you?]","[Wild Grylls: Helping someone else ultimately means helping yourself. And you’re kind too, aren’t you? You could’ve simply ignored your promise, yet you still repaid me like this.]","[Starlight Princess: Those are wise words. Do you still wish to leave the Forest of Four Seasons?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. I want to leave immediately.]","[Starlight Princess: I may not be able to do much, but I’ll help you find a way out. I might not look it, but I’m rather intelligent.]","[Wild Grylls: Or you could just come here instead?]","[Starlight Princess: Ah. That’s a little... haha.]","[Wild Grylls: LOL.]","The words had slipped out automatically.","It definitely wasn’t because I was a hopelessly doting owner.","Wonmo really was that cute.","Of course, I had only been joking.","Who would tell someone who had been at death’s door just yesterday to come to a place where they would almost certainly die?","I had heard that no one who entered the Forest of Four Seasons had ever escaped.","That was why it was easier to treat Starlight Princess’s promise as comfort rather than something she genuinely intended to accomplish.","[Starlight Princess: Oh! That reminds me, I saw the owlbear photos.]","[Wild Grylls: Cute, isn’t he?]","[Starlight Princess: Yes. But the name is a little... questionable. Wonmo? What kind of name is Wonmo?]","[Wild Grylls: Did you have another name in mind, Lady Starlight?]","[Starlight Princess: Since it means a healthy child...]","Starlight Princess paused for a moment before revealing the name she had thought of.","[Starlight Princess: Gym Newbie. How does Gym Newbie sound?]","[Wild Grylls: Oh...]","It sounded like the kind of name that would eventually evolve into Gym Maniac.","How could every single named user have such terrible naming sense?","The more I thought about it, the more Fluffy seemed like the best name by far.","[Wild Grylls: I think I’ll have to keep calling him Wonmo for now. They held a vote without even telling me.]","[Starlight Princess: Can’t you just ignore it?]","[Wild Grylls: The Heavenly Demon chose the name, so it’s hard to dismiss it so casually.]","She was one of the named users who had helped me, and the Heavenly Demon herself had personally chosen it.","I couldn’t simply ignore that.","If she became disappointed and distanced herself from me, I would be the one losing out.","Starlight Princess seemed to understand that as well. Though she complained, she ultimately accepted it.","[Starlight Princess: That’s a shame. So what are you going to do now?]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll probably work on drawing water from the creek. The dwarf said he’d upload a post explaining how soon.]","[Starlight Princess: I see. If you ever need help, please tell me. I’ll be waiting.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you.]","[Starlight Princess: Good luck!]","Our conversation ended there.","I felt both warmth and bitterness at the same time.","I was happy that Starlight Princess had fully recovered, but nothing had changed for me.","Unless I escaped this hellish place, living an ordinary life was out of the question.","’I can escape... right?’","It was a thought that crossed my mind every day.","Could I really leave the Forest of Four Seasons?","If dangerous plants and animals were the only problem, perhaps I could somehow fight my way out.","But the forest’s greatest danger was that space itself changed constantly.","Getting lost was dangerous enough, yet even the terrain shifted unpredictably.","The thought alone was overwhelming.","’As for the elixirs... Whoa. She gave me seven?’","Starlight Princess had sent me seven elixirs in total.","Judging by their different colors, they seemed to be of different grades.","I had heard that paler colors indicated lower quality, so sorting them was easy enough.","’Wonmo might break them. I should hide these.’","I stored the elixirs inside the box Passing Dwarf had previously given me.","Just in case Wonmo went rummaging through it, I pushed the box into the farthest corner of the cave.","’Come to think of it, did the dwarf upload his post?’","Next, I checked whether Passing Dwarf had posted his explanation.","After refreshing the Gallery a few times, his post finally appeared.","***","Title: Grylls, Read This","Passing Dwarf","(A rough drawing showing how to draw water from a stream.)","(A photo of a natural-rubber hose.)","(A photo of a valve.)","Set it up like the drawing above.","Suck on the end of each hose until the water starts flowing.","Oh, and don’t lie down while sucking on it. Stay upright. The pressure difference will make the water gush out.","Attach a valve to the final hose so you can open and close it.","Understand?","Wild Grylls: I get the general idea, but what’s that mesh for? Filtering impurities?","Passing Dwarf: Yeah. You’re surprisingly quick.","Wild Grylls: Of course. I understand things instantly. LOL.","Passing Dwarf: Now I suddenly don’t want to give it to you.","Wild Grylls: I am a complete idiot.","That attitude changed fast. LOL.","Watching these two interact never stops being funny.","You two get along well. LOL.","Passing Dwarf: Anyway, connect the hoses properly and maintain the correct slope. Then it won’t be difficult.","Wild Grylls: You said it would be expensive. Is the hose the costly part?","Passing Dwarf: Yeah. It’s made of rubber, so it’s ridiculously expensive.","Rubber is expensive?","The question crossed my mind, but the answer soon became obvious.","Judging from what I had read in the Gallery, factories had only recently begun operating in this world.","Apparently, there were also locomotives powered by mana, though they weren’t commonly used.","’They said people usually just use warp gates, right?’","It was fitting for a fantasy world.","Sports such as football and baseball were widely developed, yet science seemed slightly behind.","Still, it made sense if magic filled the role of science.","Warp gates were expensive, so I had heard that commoners used locomotives instead.","’The uniform PrincessChaenggu gave me must be incredibly expensive too.’","Considering what it was made of, that was only natural.","After listening to Passing Dwarf’s various explanations, I asked the question that mattered most.","But then another problem arose.","The Gallery’s trading rules.","Once a user completed a trade, they couldn’t trade again for twenty-four hours.","Passing Dwarf had traded with someone after noon yesterday, which meant he couldn’t directly trade with me yet.","Passing Dwarf: I can list it as an instant-purchase item at the auction house, but I’ll put it up for 1,100 gold. Is that okay?","Wild Grylls: Just list it.","Passing Dwarf: LOL.","Wild Grylls: Then how much is it actually worth?","Passing Dwarf: If I’m giving you a discount, around 500 gold total. That’s including the processed rubber and the valve.","Five hundred gold was definitely expensive.","Still, I had money left from what Allfather had paid me.","It made my blood run cold, but there was no helping it.","Water was urgently needed.","This was no time to worry about money.","I might compare prices for a barricade or fence, but not for water.","I immediately opened the auction house and checked the item Passing Dwarf had listed.","[Title: Grylls Is an Idiot]","[Price: 1,100 Gold]","\"This bastard.\"","I’d remember this.","I let out a hollow laugh and bought it.","Someone else could theoretically snatch it first, but the price was so absurdly high that nobody would.","Even if someone did, I could simply buy another one from the dwarf.","\"Now that everything’s ready...\"","It was time to go get water.","As a precaution, I equipped both my sword and shield.","I slung the tightly rolled hose over my shoulder.","All that remained was the work itself.","’As soon as I get the water, I’ll wash Wonmo first.’","I looked at Wonmo, who was sleeping peacefully.","What if he woke up while I was gone?","Would he come outside looking for me?","That would be extremely dangerous.","’I need to finish as quickly as possible.’","It was time to put my practical skills to the test."]},{"title":"Chapter 24","paragraphs":["Water (2)","All the preparations for drawing water from the creek were complete, but several problems remained.","The first—and biggest—was avoiding the golden poison frogs somehow.","They leaped out the instant I put my hand in the water, making them an enormous nuisance.","The second problem was the depth of the creek.","It was deep enough to submerge more than half my arm.","That meant it would be difficult to secure the hose in place with stones.","I checked the items Passing Dwarf had given me.","’I just need to cover this with the mesh and connect it to the hose...’","I alternated between looking at the gleaming funnel and the mesh that was supposed to cover it.","Connecting the funnel to the hose was simple.","The difficult part was securing it in place.","’Do I have no choice but to dig a shallow hole with the shovel?’","That seemed like the best option.","I carried the equipment to the creek, then went back for the shovel.","Fortunately, I didn’t encounter any dangerous animals while traveling back and forth.","The Mad Dog pack had died long ago, and the owlbear had recently been shipped off to the auction house.","I probably wouldn’t encounter another predator-class creature for some time.","At this point, insects like ticks frightened me more than predators.","Shhhhhhh—","Once I had brought the shovel, all the preparations were finally complete.","I looked at the fast-flowing creek and slowly got to work.","First, I carefully began digging into the bank with the shovel.","Thud! Thump!","Fortunately, no frogs leaped out.","Still, I kept checking my surroundings between each strike, just in case.","Rushhhhh—","Eventually, I created a space large enough to insert the funnel.","To increase the force of the current, I placed stones around the area I had dug.","The water was flowing strongly enough now.","All that remained was connecting the hose.","I covered the funnel with the mesh, then attached it to the hose.","Instead of cable ties, I firmly secured the connection with metal ties.","Since plastic hadn’t been invented in this world, they apparently used iron as a substitute.","’Wouldn’t these be difficult to make too?’","The hose was made from natural rubber, so it made sense for it to be expensive.","But to me, these metal ties looked as though they should cost even more.","’Maybe it’s because a dwarf made them. Whatever.’","After confirming that everything was firmly secured, I moved to the next location.","One hose wasn’t enough.","Because of the distance, I needed to connect several hoses along the route.","\"Sluuuurp!\"","Just as Passing Dwarf had instructed, I sucked hard on the end of the hose.","When I carefully lowered it, the water began flowing much more strongly than before.","I connected that hose to another one and tightly fastened them together with a metal tie.","After repeating the same process several times, I eventually reached the shelter.","Finally, I connected the end of the last hose to the valve.","The work was complete.","Rushhhhh—","\"Perfect. This is perfect.\"","The water flowed beautifully.","Just looking at it filled me with satisfaction.","Still, the job wasn’t entirely finished.","As I had emphasized countless times, this was the wilderness.","An animal could bite through the hose, so covering it with soil was essential.","After roughly two hours of work, everything was finally done.","The fact that I no longer needed to worry about water filled me with pride.","\"Kyuu?\"","\"Oh. You’re awake?\"","Coincidentally, Wonmo seemed to have woken up.","He stared at me with his usual bright, wide eyes.","I wanted to pick him up, but his body was crawling with ticks.","’Bath first.’","I also needed to clean myself while I was at it.","I bought a large iron tub from the auction house and filled it with water.","After rinsing it several times and checking for debris, I filled it to the brim.","Then I lit a fire beneath it to warm the water.","’I should give him a dewormer too, right?’","I needed to do laundry as well.","I was incredibly busy.","Since things had come this far, I might as well set up a drying rack too.","Simply having access to water whenever I wanted greatly expanded what I could do.","While the water in the tub heated, I made a post in the Gallery.","***","Title: I’m Rich Now","Wild Grylls","(Video of water gushing from the hose.)","I’m rich in water now.","Oh. You succeeded?","LMAO.","Now you can finally take a bath.","Wild Grylls: I’m washing Wonmo first. He had a ridiculous number of ticks.","Passing Dwarf: You finished surprisingly quickly. No problems?","Wild Grylls: Nothing major. Want a mandrake later?","Passing Dwarf: Oh, I’d appreciate that. Straight into a bottle of liquor. LOL.","Wild Grylls: Screw you. You’re not getting one.","He’d use such an expensive mandrake to make infused liquor?","What kind of dwarf is this? LOL.","Heavenly Demon: Now that you have secured water, what do you intend to do next?","Wild Grylls: I’m not sure. Once I get a barricade from the dwarf, there won’t be much left. Maybe cutting trees or exploring the area?","Heavenly Demon: If that is the case, it may be time for you to learn an internal energy cultivation technique from this lady.","Wild Grylls: I’d be happy to. Let me wash Wonmo first, then I’ll contact you.","Heavenly Demon: I shall wait. This lady is looking forward to it as well.","SwordMaster: An internal energy technique is important, but have you been practicing your swordsmanship?","Wild Grylls: I’ve been studying it consistently. I still only know the basics, though.","SwordMaster: Excellent. Grow strong quickly and marry me.","Wild Grylls: Ma’am?","SwordMaster: I was joking.","That didn’t sound like a joke.","Her true feelings slip out surprisingly often.","Is she that desperate to get married? LOL.","Hmm...","As expected, the Gallery was filled with strange people.","Still, there was no denying that SwordMaster’s advice was helping me grow stronger each day.","When I fought the owlbear, recalling her posts had saved my life.","Otherwise, I would’ve died.","\"Hmm. This should be warm enough. Wonmo?\"","\"Kyuu?\"","The water in the tub had become pleasantly warm.","Steam wasn’t rising from it, but considering the forest’s temperature, it was more than sufficient.","I dragged the tub over to Wonmo.","Rather than being tall and narrow, it was wide from side to side to suit his body, making it the perfect size.","\"Get in. It’s time for a bath.\"","\"Kyuuu.\"","Could he really understand what I was saying?","Wonmo stared at the tub with his usual sparkling eyes, then cautiously placed a paw inside.","The warm water seemed unfamiliar, because he flinched at first.","Fortunately, once he realized it wouldn’t hurt him, he carefully lowered his fluffy body into the tub.","\"Kyuuuuuu...\"","\"Feels good, doesn’t it?\"","He closed his eyes and relaxed completely.","I chuckled and began washing every part of his body.","Along the way, I carefully applied insect repellent to various places and removed all the ticks.","’Won’t this become pointless once he starts roaming around again?’","I would simply have to accept that.","I scrubbed him thoroughly with soap.","Wonmo seemed to enjoy my touch, because he kept his eyes closed the entire time.","Unfortunately, the bathwater became unbelievably filthy.","That couldn’t be helped in the wilderness.","It was something I had to endure.","’Still, I can’t resist taking a picture.’","I uploaded a photo of Wonmo bathing to the Gallery.","Only his face was sticking out of the water, making him look incredibly adorable.","***","Title: Gave Wonmo a Bath","Wild Grylls","(Video of Wonmo bathing.)","Cute, right? Give me an upvote if you agree.","His face is practically cheating.","That little thing is going to become a tyrant someday?","Just watching this is healing.","Ugh, disgusting.","Your face is more disgusting.","I was talking about the water. Is your face dirty or something?","LOL.","How did twisted people appear even under a post this cute?","I had only uploaded it to show Wonmo off, so I didn’t care much.","I was still vigorously scrubbing him when—","\"Kyuuuuuuu...!\"","Shiver, shiver.","Wonmo suddenly began trembling.","The abrupt reaction startled me.","\"Wonmo? Are you uncomfortable?\"","\"Kyuuuu.\"","\"No? Then...\"","What was happening?","Just as I began wondering—","Float...","Something rose to the surface of the filthy bathwater.","It was dark brown, almost black, and round...","\"...\"","\"...Wonmo. Did you poop?\"","\"Kyuu!\"","\"GYAAAAAH! Get out right now! Hurry!\"","It seemed potty training would have to come first.","***","After washing Wonmo, I learned something important.","Whether it was a person or an animal, washing someone else was incredibly exhausting.","So much filth came out of him that I had to replace the bathwater several times.","By the time it was finally my turn to wash, the sun was already beginning to set.","\"Nom, nom, chomp.\"","\"Is it tasty?\"","After finishing Wonmo’s bath, I dried him as thoroughly as possible with a towel.","A hair dryer would have been useful, but since I didn’t have one, I had to rely on the campfire.","I also gave him a deworming medicine.","As expected of an owlbear that ate practically anything, he swallowed it without hesitation.","’Someone gets to eat meat while someone else survives on fasting pills. How unfair.’","I bought Wonmo’s meal from the auction house.","Just like that morning, it was monster meat.","Monster meat was the cheapest option available. It was practically useless, so it cost less than ten gold.","I grimaced as I put a bitter fasting pill into my mouth.","No matter how many times I ate one, it was still unbearably bitter.","’My stomach always hurts after eating these too.’","Potty training Wonmo was simple.","He was never allowed to relieve himself inside the cave.","And if he needed to go, he had to give me some kind of signal. Then I would stand guard beside him.","Strangely enough, I couldn’t tell whether Wonmo was exceptionally intelligent or whether all owlbears were naturally like this, but he understood everything.","The claim that owlbears became fiercely loyal as long as they were well-fed hadn’t been an exaggeration.","’Now that I’ve roughly finished eating, all that’s left is learning the internal energy cultivation technique.’","Sitting cross-legged no longer hurt as much either.","It hadn’t even been a week, yet I felt as though my flexibility had improved dramatically.","I wondered whether that was even possible, but decided not to question something beneficial.","Even if I thought deeply about it, I wouldn’t find an answer.","***","Title: Heavenly Demon, Are You There?","Wild Grylls","I’d like to start learning the internal energy cultivation technique. Are you here?","Heavenly Demon: I have been waiting.","Wild Grylls: ???","Whoa. The post went up ten seconds ago, but she commented after only two seconds.","Isn’t that basically stalking?","That’s a little scary.","The Heavenly Demon had often been the first to comment on my posts, but never this quickly.","’Uh... Is she really that bored?’","More likely, this was her way of repaying the favor I had done for her.","How should I put it?","She felt like a veteran player who had finally found a newbie to teach.","Thinking of it that way made me feel more comfortable.","Wild Grylls: You were here. As I mentioned before, please post the instructions as private comments.","Heavenly Demon: Very well. First, sit in the lotus position.","I was just as bewildered as everyone else.","How had she commented the instant I uploaded the post?","Following her instructions, I crossed my legs.","They still ached a little, but the discomfort was now bearable.","Only three days ago, I had screamed like a little girl while trying this.","I had already made tremendous progress.","’Can I finally use mana—or internal energy—now?’","I was genuinely excited.","I was about to wield a mysterious power that normally appeared only in fantasy stories and martial arts novels.","I hoped I would eventually be able to fire palm blasts too.","Palm blasts had always been excellent for keeping enemies at a distance.","Wild Grylls: If I train enough, will I be able to fire palm blasts?","Heavenly Demon: Why do you ask?","Wild Grylls: For ranged attacks?","Heavenly Demon: Do not do that. Only fools waste their energy in such a way.","Wild Grylls: Okay.","He sounds so disappointed. LOL.","Palm blasts are every man’s dream.","There are entire wag\"1\">"]},{"title":"Chapter 25","paragraphs":["Breathing Technique (1)","The continent had countless long-standing \"versus\" debates, not just arguments over who was the strongest.","Elves vs. demons.","Dogs vs. cats.","Summer vs. winter.","West vs. East.","There were many others, but most people avoided discussing them because they tended to cause conflict.","Of course, people only restrained themselves in everyday life.","The Gallery showed no mercy.","Whenever they had the chance, users wasted time fighting over which side was better.","When things occasionally became too heated and turned into outright hatred, the Moderator would personally step in.","And among all these disputes, one subject caused more controversy than any other.","Title: Mana Cultivation Method vs. Internal Energy Cultivation Method","Vote for whichever one you think is better.","Mana Cultivation Method: 50%Internal Energy Cultivation Method: 50%","└ Wow, how are they both exactly fifty percent?","└ None of you know anything. Mana cultivation is obviously better.","└ Cut the crap. How is it better? LOL","└ You’re from the Central Plains, aren’t you?","└ No? I’m from the Messiah Empire.","└ Then you must be a noble.","└ I’m not a noble. I’m a knight. LOL","The debate was none other than mana cultivation methods versus internal energy cultivation methods.","It had continued uninterrupted since ancient times and remained an ongoing controversy even now.","Title: The Origins of Mana Cultivation and Internal Energy Cultivation","The accepted theory is that both were taught according to the teachings of Ares, the Goddess of War and younger sister of Aragon, the God of Magic.","Of her two disciples, one took charge of the West, while the other took charge of the East.","The West gradually fragmented into many different nations, but the East still retains the name \"Central Plains.\"","However, Ares herself developed her technique by analyzing and researching the breathing method of her older brother, Aragon.","So technically, both are basically versions of Aragon’s breathing technique.","That concludes today’s mythology lesson!","└ Was Ares pretty?","└ You lunatic, LOL. Do you want to get arrested for blasphemy?","└ This is the Gallery anyway. LOL. So, was she pretty?","└ Unfortunately, there are no records saying she was beautiful. Apparently, she always wore a helmet because she was constantly at war.","└ Allfather) According to my research, the prevailing theory is that she was beautiful.","└ What evidence is there?","└ Allfather) Aragon, the God of Magic, once said this: \"She may be my damn little sister, but she is pretty.\"","└ Aren’t they just a completely normal pair of siblings? LOL","└ If a real brother admitted his sister was pretty, that says everything.","└ That suddenly sounds incredibly credible. LOL","└ Allfather) The two of them apparently fought quite often. Whenever they did, mountains were blown away and seas overturned.","└ Holy crap.","└ Gods really are something else...","└ Allfather) And every time, the Chief God smacked them both on the back.","└ So it was just a sibling quarrel on a larger scale. LOL","└ Why do they sound so human? LOL","Just as the myths suggested, mana cultivation methods were dominant in the West, while internal energy cultivation methods were dominant in the Central Plains.","However, as time passed, an interesting theory emerged.","Title: Geography Changed the Fate of Breathing Techniques in the West and East","The West is surrounded above and below by dangerous races—demons, elves, and various others—so it needed to produce as many capable fighters as possible.","That was why easy-to-learn mana cultivation methods were spread as widely as possible to strengthen the overall military force.","The problem was that this also made it easy for undesirable people to learn mana cultivation.","As a result, whenever a rebellion broke out, there were frequent cases of peasants beating knights half to death.","This was also one of the reasons the Western nations fragmented into their current state.","Meanwhile, in the East—in other words, the Central Plains—the great families tightly controlled their internal energy cultivation methods.","Their culture was also extremely conservative, and the geography was favorable enough that they faced relatively few internal or external threats.","Therefore, internal energy cultivation methods were taught only to trusted individuals, while most peasants did not even know what they were.","The academic consensus is that geography caused mana cultivation and internal energy cultivation to develop separately.","└ Oh. Knowledge gained.","└ A lot of people in the East use mana cultivation these days. Is it because of increased cultural exchange?","└ That too, and because mana cultivation is easier to learn. Its depth still seems relatively shallow, though.","└ Meanwhile, Western nobles tend to use internal energy cultivation methods. That way, they can widen the gap between themselves and commoners.","└ So internal energy cultivation is basically reserved for important people.","└ Yeah, pretty much.","└ Not necessarily. Knights are often taught internal energy cultivation methods too.","Mana cultivation methods were easy to learn but shallow.","Internal energy cultivation methods were difficult to learn but profound.","These were among the most deeply rooted perceptions surrounding the two types of breathing techniques.","They were half true, but also contained many inaccuracies.","Title: The Best Breathing Technique Is Whatever Suits You","Just look at Ash from the Messiah Empire. She reached the position of the strongest using only a mana cultivation method.","└ Isn’t she just an abnormal exception?","└ Yeah, she is. But even if the process is different, isn’t being strong all that matters?","└ Doesn’t the Hero use mana cultivation too?","└ I heard the Holy Kingdom has its own unique internal energy cultivation method for the Hero.","└ In the end, strong people are simply strong.","Title: Upvote If You’ve Ever Gotten Useful Advice from a Mana vs. Internal Energy Argument","I’ll start. LOL","└ Seriously, all kinds of useful tips come out during those arguments. LOL","└ I was stuck at a bottleneck, but thanks to them, I broke through. LOL","└ While whales fight, the shrimp get fat. LOL","└ I hope they keep arguing forever. LOL","Regardless of the method, a strong person was strong.","That was practically an absolute truth.","Even so, neither side could easily back down because the debate involved the pride and history of their respective factions.","That was why the argument turned into a versus match whenever the opportunity arose.","For those who wielded mana, the subject was especially tied to personal pride.","Perhaps because of that, whenever people argued, they often unintentionally revealed all kinds of valuable tips.","There were plenty of users who occasionally spouted nonsense, but most people knew how to filter them out.","Nothing made people expose the limits of their knowledge more easily than a discussion about breathing techniques.","’Oh. Is she finally going to teach him an internal energy cultivation method?’","Ash, the strongest person in the Messiah Empire and the current stay-at-home security guard, became curious.","As usual, she had been lying around while browsing the Gallery.","The Heavenly Demon had begun teaching Wild Grylls an internal energy cultivation method.","At first, Ash did not think much of it.","The Heavenly Demon she knew would never teach an internal energy cultivation method incorrectly.","Even if she truly were a scammer, it would not matter.","The moment Grylls posted, \"The Heavenly Demon was a fraud!\" in the Gallery, the truth would be exposed.","Of course, they also had to consider the possibility that Grylls had no talent, or that the Heavenly Demon lacked the aptitude to teach others.","From Ash’s perspective, she simply had to watch quietly and enjoy the show.","At first, that was what she thought.","└ Wild Grylls) Heavenly Demon, I followed your instructions, but my nose started bleeding.","└ Heavenly Demon) What?!","\"What?!\"","Just as the Heavenly Demon had been shocked, Ash could not help but jump in surprise.","It was extremely rare for someone to suffer a nosebleed while practicing abdominal breathing.","After questioning Grylls in detail, Ash realized something.","’Don’t tell me Grylls is the same...?’","Ash had experienced the exact same phenomenon.","She possessed a constitution that accumulated mana simply by breathing.","Every time she inhaled, several times more mana than an ordinary person’s would gather inside her mana hole—her dantian.","Because of that, merely practicing controlled breathing had been enough to give her nosebleeds, just like Grylls.","At the time, no one had understood what was happening, so the matter had been brushed aside.","After all, it was a phenomenon no one had ever heard of.","Since it happened during the most fundamental stage of training, people initially assumed she simply lacked talent.","However, once she overcame that stage, her growth became explosive.","Ash could say so with certainty because she herself had experienced it.","’Could it be true? Is he really...?’","Ash bombarded Grylls with question after question.","The more she asked, the more she realized that his constitution was similar to hers.","They were not completely identical, of course. Grylls was currently carrying mana accumulated through an elixir.","Even so, they were alike in that a massive amount of mana entered their bodies with every breath.","’Is it because he’s in the Forest of Four Seasons?’","That was probably the most likely explanation.","The mana density in the Forest of Four Seasons was several—or perhaps even dozens of—times higher than in other regions.","It was merely a hypothesis proposed by scholars, but it was highly credible.","\"The existence of a fully mature Mandrake already proves it.\"","Their environments might have been different, but the conditions were similar.","That was why Ash made up her mind.","She would raise Grylls somehow.","Judging by his actions so far, his talent did not seem particularly bad either.","More importantly, he had more than enough reasons to become stronger.","He was in a situation where he had to grasp at any straw he could find just to survive.","’What if he becomes even stronger than me...? Hehehe.’","Ash smiled wickedly.","It was a feeling she had not experienced in a long time.","Everyone she had trained until now had either failed to satisfy her or run away.","Grylls was different.","He was trapped in the Forest of Four Seasons, so there was nowhere for him to flee.","His only way out was to become stronger on his own.","It was perfect.","’First, I should teach him how to break through to the next stage.’","Grylls’s body was currently oversaturated.","When he tried to draw in more mana while in that state, his body had instinctively activated its defensive mechanisms.","Ash had intended to teach him a useful trick to resolve the problem, but an unexpected obstacle appeared.","\"This woman is seriously frustrating.\"","Ash’s beautiful face twisted slightly.","Her expression seemed to be a mixture of dissatisfaction and exasperation.","’Does she really have to be this stubborn?’","The obstacle was the Heavenly Demon.","The moment Ash offered to teach Grylls a breathing technique, the Heavenly Demon began objecting to everything she said.","Her attitude was practically, \"I already claimed Grylls, so stay away from him.\"","’I can understand it, since she’s from the Central Plains...’","People from the Central Plains were extremely sensitive about master-disciple relationships.","They even said that a master was both teacher and parent, while a disciple was no different from one’s own child.","Internal energy cultivation methods were secret arts that would never be taught to someone who was not deeply trusted.","’That must mean she trusts him that much.’","Had the Heavenly Demon stubbornly insisted on some ridiculous argument, Ash would have fought her to the bitter end.","However, the Heavenly Demon refuted Ash’s points one by one with surprisingly sound reasoning.","In the end, Ash chose to take a step back.","Fighting here would not help Grylls in any way.","Even so, they still needed to open a path for him.","That was why she made one final proposal.","└ SwordMaster) Then I’ll only teach Mr. Grylls my techniques until he can circulate his mana. In the Central Plains, you call it energy circulation and breathing, right?","└ Heavenly Demon) If thou merely intendest to aid him through energy circulation and breathing, then this lady has no objection. However, this lady shall be the one to teach him the mnemonic verses that follow.","└ SwordMaster) I have no intention of going that far either.","Ash was not lying.","That was what she said aloud, at least.","Internally, she had other plans.","Internal energy cultivation methods were difficult.","Extremely difficult.","The process was identical for both types of breathing techniques until one reached mana circulation.","However, a large difference appeared in the mnemonic verses that followed.","Unlike mana cultivation methods, internal energy cultivation methods contained rather philosophical teachings.","For example, while a mana cultivation method might simply instruct the practitioner to direct mana toward a specific area, internal energy cultivation methods were far more complicated.","’The water rising from the valley flows into the sea... Ugh, how frustrating.’","However, they did not have only disadvantages.","Just as carp raised in a river grew differently from carp raised in a lake, breathing techniques worked in a similar way.","Mana cultivation methods were severely lacking when it came to attaining \"enlightenment,\" while internal energy cultivation methods were not.","Their mnemonic verses contained various insights, making it easier to advance to the next stage.","└ Wild Grylls) Is everything the same up to that energy circulation and breathing part?","└ Heavenly Demon) Indeed. However, didst thou not say that thou hadst already sent internal energy into thy middle and upper dantians as well? That is what this lady heard earlier.","└ Wild Grylls) I’m not sure about that part, but some strange energy passed through my heart and brain, then spread throughout my entire body. After that, it returned to my lower abdomen.","└ Heavenly Demon) How peculiar. Perhaps fortune truly arose from disaster, for those pathways have already opened. It may be that thou possessest potential comparable to this lady’s own.","└ Wild Grylls) Does that mean I’ll be able to shoot hurricane-level palm strikes from my hands too?","└ Heavenly Demon) Good grief.","└ Heavenly Demon) For now, it would be best for thee to begin energy circulation and breathing. Listen carefully to the advice of this lady and that jagged stone.","└ Wild Grylls) I’ll take it to heart.","└ SwordMaster) Surely that \"jagged stone\" isn’t referring to me, right?","└ Heavenly Demon) At least thou seemest to possess a conscience.","\"Pfft!\"","Ash burst out laughing.","For the Heavenly Demon to react with such utter exasperation...","That only proved how absurd Grylls could be.","Still, it was nice to see him staying positive.","’She’s not wrong.’","Ash nodded inwardly.","However, she had no intention of giving up.","Sooner or later, Grylls would come looking for a mana cultivation method.","’He’ll definitely complain that internal energy cultivation is too difficult.’","Grylls was an ordinary person.","A polite ordinary person, but ordinary nonetheless.","By Ash’s standards, ordinary people—peasants, in other words—were people who had barely managed to learn how to read.","She did not know much about Grylls’s upbringing, but she already knew it had not been a good one.","His parents had died in an accident, leaving him to live alone.","In that kind of environment, he must have been too busy trying to survive.","There was a high chance he had never received a proper education.","That meant an internal energy cultivation method would probably be difficult for him to understand properly.","’He claims he came from another world, but could that possibly be true?’","That kind of character setting was extremely common in the Gallery.","He claimed that a single bomb from his world could destroy an entire city.","Who would believe something like that?","Apparently, Ash’s concerns had been unfounded.","Whether Grylls’s stomach was unusually weak or unusually healthy, situations like this happened quite often.","└ Heavenly Demon) Energy circulation and breathing is simple. Thou needest only repeat what thou experienced earlier.","└ SwordMaster) The same thing as before might happen again, so you should leave a longer interval between each breath.","└ Heavenly Demon) It would be best to endure it even if thy stomach begins to hurt. If thou art careless, thou mayest fall prey to an inner demon.","└ Wild Grylls) It’s a natural bodily function. You can suffer qi deviation because of that?","└ Heavenly Demon) Of course. There was once a fool who fell into qi deviation merely because someone asked him how to breathe.","└ Wild Grylls) What kind of idiot does that...?","Ash and the Heavenly Demon shared various useful tips through private comments.","Grylls appeared to begin the breathing exercise after reading them, because he stopped replying.","For a very long time.","More than ten minutes passed without a single comment.","Just as Ash grew anxious and prepared to leave another reply—","└ Wild Grylls) Ah, damn. My stomach suddenly started hurting really badly... I’ll keep going.","└ Seriously, his stomach hurts whenever he gets the chance. LOL","└ What a poop machine. LOL","It might have sounded ridiculous, but this was actually a well-known issue.","Mana circulation—energy circulation and breathing—required an extraordinary degree of concentration.","Even someone speaking to the practitioner could easily break that concentration.","└ Wild Grylls) I’ll keep trying for now. How long did you say I should continue?","└ Heavenly Demon) Until thou feelest the internal energy circulating throughout thy entire body.","└ SwordMaster) The Heavenly Demon is right.","└ Wild Grylls) Okay. Thank you.","For the first time in her life, Ash encountered an impossible problem.","\"...What kind of nonsense is this?\"","The Heavenly Demon apparently felt the same way."]},{"title":"Chapter 26","paragraphs":["Breathing Technique (2)","With the help of the Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster, I somehow managed to sense mana.","It worked fairly well when I treated it as simply repeating the phenomenon I had experienced at the beginning.","But the problem came afterward.","Every time the mana completed a full circuit after starting from my lower abdomen, my stomach began to hurt.","It might have been manageable once or twice, but the pain struck every single time the mana completed a circuit, making it impossible to endure.","It was so bad that I wondered whether I needed to build a separate toilet nearby. Going somewhere far away every time was difficult.","’Why am I sweating so much?’","I did not feel particularly exhausted, yet sweat was pouring from my entire body.","And it was not ordinary sweat.","It was pitch-black.","It looked like the filthy grime-water I had only ever heard people describe.","\"Ugh!\"","The smell was horrible too.","I nearly threw up.","It was as though every kind of waste imaginable had been mixed together.","\"Kyuueeek! Kyuueeeek!\"","Wonmo, whose sense of smell was far sharper than mine, was practically having a seizure.","The moment he caught the scent, he moved as far away from me as possible.","Judging by the way he had wedged himself into a corner of the cave and was growling, the smell must have been truly unbearable.","It seemed I would have to wash myself again.","Wonmo might kick me out of the cave otherwise.","The sun had already set, but sleeping like this might make me sick.","’What in the world is happening?’","I filled the tub with water and lit a fire beneath it.","It would take too long to wait for the water to boil, so I climbed in immediately.","The moment I submerged myself, the refreshing chill unique to stream water spread throughout my body.","After letting out a groan of relief, I decided to ask the Gallery for help.","Title: Is Mana Circulation Normally Like This?","Wild Grylls","I’m circulating mana like you advised, but every time it completes one full circuit, I need to take a dump. Is this normal?","└ Heavenly Demon) This is the first time this lady has heard of someone needing to relieve himself whenever he practices energy circulation and breathing.","└ SwordMaster) Same here. Isn’t there simply something wrong with your intestines?","└ Wild Grylls) I haven’t eaten anything. And it’s not even diarrhea.","└ Ugh. Disgusting.","└ I’m eating curry, and you’re talking about poop.","└ The truth is, you’re eating poop that tastes like curry. LOL","└ Oh, come on—","It was admittedly a filthy topic, but I was being serious.","Had it been diarrhea, I could have understood it to some extent.","That would have meant I was sick.","But it was not, so I could not help becoming suspicious.","The only thing I had eaten until now was fasting pills.","Still, I explained that the two seemed to have a complementary relationship, so it was probably better to take care of my body.","└ Heavenly Demon) The only explanation that immediately comes to mind is that thy body is expelling accumulated impurities.","...Is there perhaps something wrong with thy body?","└ Wild Grylls) Well, I’m not a pig, at least.","To be honest, my body was close to being overweight.","I was neither skinny nor noticeably fat.","However, because I had lived almost entirely on instant noodles to save money, I had probably accumulated a fair amount of visceral fat.","└ Heavenly Demon) Aside from that, are there any other symptoms?","└ Wild Grylls) I’m sweating black liquid, and it smells horrible.","└ Heavenly Demon) It truly does seem that impurities are being expelled from thy body.","└ Wild Grylls) Is that a good thing?","└ Heavenly Demon) It goes beyond merely being good. It is abnormal. Normally, one must reach at least the Supreme Realm before such a thing occurs.","└ Wild Grylls) It isn’t bad, right?","└ Heavenly Demon) It is not bad, but just in case, it would be best for thee to focus only on energy circulation and breathing for the time being.","└ Heavenly Demon) Considering what happened whenever thou consumed the fasting pills, that is the only explanation this lady can think of at present.","└ SwordMaster) Or it may genuinely be caused by your constitution.","└ Wild Grylls) Does the same thing happen when fat people learn breathing techniques?","└ If that were true, I would have learned one ages ago. LOL","└ You can become healthy just by breathing? I’d start immediately. LOL","Apparently, learning a breathing technique did not alter one’s physique.","Changing the body’s shape fell under external cultivation, while breathing techniques belonged to internal cultivation, or something along those lines.","In the end, my training came to a halt at mana circulation.","They said they would teach me the mnemonic verses later.","I had no reason to object, so I accepted it without complaint.","My stomach hurt every time I completed a circuit of mana.","There was nothing I could do about that.","’It isn’t nutrients being expelled instead of impurities, is it?’","The thought made me anxious enough to want another fasting pill.","However, doing that might make my Johnson explode, so it was probably better to resist.","\"Whew.\"","Why did nothing ever go according to plan?","Then again, the real problem was being dropped into this damn forest in the first place.","After lamenting my situation for a while, I raised my head and looked at the sky.","The night sky was breathtaking, embroidered with countless stars.","’...Right. There’s no need to rush.’","The water was gradually warming.","I scrubbed every part of my body thoroughly with soap and finished washing.","I planned to dispose of the water left in the tub the next day.","It was too dark to do so safely now.","After drying myself completely with a towel, I browsed the Gallery while waiting for my hair to dry.","Even late at night, the Gallery remained lively.","Most of it was overflowing with pointless posts.","[Gallery User Is Screwed in Real Time]","[I Really Want to Quit My Job]","[This Counts as a Blue Ocean, Right?]","[The River Water Is Warm These Days]","[Those Damn Elves Planted Trees Again]","[EMERGENCYYYY!]","It was all like this.","I was so accustomed to it that I had even begun to feel fond of it.","After browsing the Gallery for a while, I uploaded a simple post.","As always, it was the post that marked the end of my day.","Countless comments appeared immediately, but I skimmed through them and closed the Gallery.","Perhaps because I had learned a breathing technique today, sleepiness overwhelmed me.","’Where should I go tomorrow? Repair work? Breathing practice? Exploration?’","Whatever I chose, one thing was certain.","I would suffer.","Before closing my eyes, I checked on Wonmo.","He was lying right beside me, preparing to sleep.","At least having him around made me feel less lonely.","’I’ll have to gather plenty of wood, even if only for the money.’","I slowly closed my eyes.","As drowsiness washed over me, my thoughts stopped functioning properly.","I had worked hard today, so I should rest comfortably for tomorrow.","’I’ll be able to get out... right?’","I held on to the hope that was gradually fading away.","***","Sleep was extremely important to every animal.","Humans were no exception.","The desire for sleep far surpassed both hunger and sexual desire.","Failing to sleep properly was enough to ruin the entire following day.","Conversely, a full night of deep sleep meant waking up feeling more refreshed than ever.","Title: Another Strong and Energetic Morning!","Wild Grylls","If anyone asks who I am, I’m Wild Grylls!","└ Heavenly Demon) Thou art awake. Is there anywhere in thy body that feels uncomfortable?","└ Wild Grylls) Not at all. I actually feel much more refreshed than usual.","└ SwordMaster) It’s probably because of the breathing exercise. It should be even more effective if you do it as soon as you wake up.","└ Heavenly Demon) It is likely due to the breathing exercise. It would be beneficial to practice once before sleeping and once after waking.","└ Heavenly Demon) Thou insolent wretch. This lady was about to say that first.","└ SwordMaster) You were too slow.","└ Heavenly Demon) Faster is not always better. Accuracy is what matters.","└ SwordMaster) I agree with that part, but speed is more important.","└ Heavenly Demon) Those who pursue speed are the ones who fall into qi deviation.","└ Starlight Princess) You’re awake. Does anything hurt?","└ Wild Grylls) Not really. You’re truly all right now, aren’t you?","└ Starlight Princess) Yes. I went outside the estate and ran as soon as I woke up.","└ Wild Grylls) You really have recovered.","└ So Grylls is the only one left now?","└ What will poor Grylls do all alone? LOL","└ Will he break the young lady’s record?","└ Starlight Princess) You people are truly awful. I’ll help make sure he does not break that record, so please do not worry too much.","The Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster began bickering first thing in the morning, while the now-healthy Starlight Princess left a comment of her own.","I tried to remember how many recovery-wishing posts I had uploaded for the Starlight Princess.","As far as I could recall, it had been around 110 days.","That was roughly three or four months.","Would I be able to escape by then?","’At that point, I won’t be adapting anymore. I’ll just be living here.’","I browsed the Gallery for only a little while before checking on Wonmo.","He was still a baby, so even though I had woken up, he remained fast asleep.","Moving around carelessly might wake him, so I checked the auction house first.","’Let’s see... The things I listed yesterday...’","The items I had put up yesterday were the owlbear’s corpse and some wood.","I had listed both through bidding.","Because of the brutal fees, auctions were structured so that the seller usually ended up losing out.","But fees or not, selling them mattered more to me, so I was simply curious.","[Owlbear Corpse: 200 taels of silver]","[Wood from the Forest of Four Seasons: 10 gold]","\"Oh?\"","They had fetched surprisingly high prices.","The wood was valuable enough, but the owlbear’s price was especially impressive.","Silver taels were the currency of the Central Plains, and I had heard that one tael of silver was roughly equivalent to ten gold.","That meant the owlbear’s corpse was worth around two thousand gold.","’Why is it so expensive? Because of the gallbladder?’","An owlbear was still a kind of bear, so its gallbladder was probably valuable.","Even if that was not the reason, I did not care as long as it sold for a high price.","’The wood is pretty expensive too.’","Ten gold every time I chopped down a tree?","I was confident I could become an environmental criminal.","’Though I’d probably wreck my body first.’","At the very least, I would need to become strong enough to fell a tree with a single swing of an axe.","Until then, I planned to avoid logging purely for money.","’I need the wood for the barricade anyway.’","After roughly organizing what I needed to do, I sat down cross-legged.","Following the advice of the Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster, I began breathing.","Once in the morning, once at noon, once in the evening, and once before bed.","Apparently, practicing about four times a day was standard.","There was one exception.","Whenever one consumed an elixir.","Since the elixir’s energy had to be properly gathered and refined, circulation was absolutely necessary.","’Then do I have to do this every time I eat?’","The fasting pills were said to be equivalent to elixirs, so it was probably mandatory.","I closed my eyes and practiced the breathing technique just as I had learned the day before.","’Starting from the lower abdomen and making one full circuit through the entire body...’","At first, controlling the mana had been difficult, but after that it became easier.","The problem was that every completed circuit caused my stomach to hurt sharply.","I was worried that the same thing might happen today.","’Through the heart and head, then back to the lower abdomen.’","The Heavenly Demon had told me that it was dangerous for a beginner to pass energy through the heart and head.","Apparently, those pathways could normally be opened only after one reached a certain level.","Yet mine had opened from the very beginning.","I had suffered a nosebleed because of it, but I had never fallen into any truly dangerous situation.","’Back to the lower abdomen.’","The mana that had circulated through my entire body returned to my lower abdomen.","Unlike yesterday, my stomach did not hurt at all.","Perhaps everything that needed to be expelled had already left my body.","I completed several more circuits before slowly ending the exercise.","\"Whew.\"","I exhaled and gradually opened my eyes.","The first thing I saw was a pair of bright golden eyes.","As I stared into them, the furry creature tilted its head.","\"Kyu?\"","It was Wonmo.","He must have watched me the entire time I was breathing.","The fact that he had not disturbed me showed that he was quite perceptive.","I stared at Wonmo for a moment, then chuckled and asked,","\"Are you hungry?\"","\"Kyu!\"","\"It almost feels like you understand everything I say.\"","\"Kyu?\"","\"Maybe not?\"","Either way, it did not matter.","I bought a suitable piece of meat from the auction house.","When I gave it to Wonmo, he devoured it with great enthusiasm.","He might be thirsty too, so I decided to give him some water.","Drip, drip, drip—","\"Hm?\"","But the water was barely flowing.","It was coming out, but the pressure was far too weak.","Something must have happened to the hose overnight, or perhaps there had been some change in the river.","\"What a pain.\"","I was not going up there immediately.","Water was still coming out, at least.","I gave Wonmo some water and ate a fasting pill for breakfast.","From now on, I would eat one per meal instead of three.","The bitterness was exactly the same even with just one.","One might actually be better.","’I can test it right away, can’t I?’","The moment I activated the cultivation method, a different reaction occurred.","Something clumped together inside me broke apart and merged with the mana.","That dissolved substance was probably the energy of the fasting pill.","I circulated the mana in that state.","Nothing changed dramatically.","My stomach did not hurt, and I felt completely fine.","’Maybe my body got used to them because I ate too many before.’","That could be it.","In any case, breakfast was done, so it was time to go repair the hose.","I equipped my sword and shield, then looked at Wonmo.","As though he knew I was leaving, he stared back at me.","\"You have to stay here. Got it?\"","\"Kyu.\"","\"Oh, and if your stomach hurts, do it outside. Don’t poop inside the cave.\"","\"Kyu.\"","Wonmo answered adorably.","His response sounded almost as if he understood.","Even if he did not, there was no need to rush.","I could potty-train him gradually.","After petting Wonmo several times, I stepped outside the cave.","’Do the sword and shield feel lighter? Or am I imagining it?’","Perhaps it was because I had slept well, but both weapons felt lighter than before.","Not only that, my entire body felt remarkably good.","The change was so sudden that I could not help thinking of the internal energy cultivation method I had practiced yesterday.","Still, it might only be temporary.","I should not get my hopes up too much.","’I wish I felt like this every day.’","With that thought, I headed toward the river.","When I arrived at the place where I had set up the hose, what I saw was—","Splash! Splash!","\"What is that now?\"","A single red fish was completely blocking the waterway.","’It looks like Magikarp.’","That was more or less what it resembled."]},{"title":"Chapter 27","paragraphs":["Thief (1)","I stared at the red fish completely blocking the channel.","I had placed stones around the channel to control the current.","Since I had dug the makeshift waterway myself with a shovel, it was not very deep.","It seemed the fish had entered the channel by sheer bad luck and then failed to escape.","The current itself was extremely strong, and its body fit the passage almost perfectly, so getting back out would have been difficult.","’Why is it so huge?’","It was large enough to fill the entire channel.","When I first saw it, I thought it was a catfish rather than an ordinary fish.","However, aside from its red body, it looked like a perfectly normal fish.","Most fish were relatively narrow, but even this one’s width was enormous.","I would need both hands to lift it.","I did not know much about fish, but I could say with certainty that it was not a catfish.","’It should be safe to eat, right?’","I watched the fish as it continued to thrash around.","It desperately flopped about in an attempt to escape, but unfortunately, the water was too shallow.","Judging by the way its mouth protruded above the surface and opened and closed repeatedly, it seemed to be having trouble breathing.","Flop! Flop! Flop!","\"You’re pretty strong too.\"","I wrapped both arms around the violently struggling fish and lifted it.","It was nearly as large as my torso, making it difficult even to keep my balance.","It would be troublesome if it managed to leap back into the river, so I moved as far away from the water as possible.","For now, I planned to carry it back to the cave with both hands and keep it inside the tub.","’I should run, just in case.’","Running into a wild animal along the way would be a serious problem.","If that happened, I would use the fish as bait and escape.","Fortunately, nothing like that occurred, and I returned safely.","\"Kku?\"","\"No. You already ate.\"","Wonmo immediately showed interest when he saw me carrying the fish.","I pushed him back and placed the fish inside the tub.","Since the tub was empty, I did not forget to fill it with water.","Once I added water, the red fish finally calmed down somewhat.","Seeing it like this made its size even more impressive.","The tub was normally large enough for either Wonmo or me to bathe in, yet the fish nearly filled it by itself.","Title: Caught a Monster","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a red fish about the size of a shield)","The water wasn’t flowing properly through the hose today, so I went upstream and found this thing blocking it.","It’s seriously huge.","I already ate breakfast, so I’m planning to have this guy for lunch.","Looks like I’ll finally get to feast again after a long time. Haha.","└ Heavenly Demon) Oh my. It is indeed enormous. Judging only by its size and color, it is comparable to a Sunfire Carp.","└ Wild Grylls) What’s that?","└ Heavenly Demon) A spiritual creature containing the energy of the sun. It is exceedingly rare. However, this lady merely said that it looks similar. The chances of it truly being one are low.","└ Wild Grylls) How do I check whether it’s real?","└ Heavenly Demon) Thou shouldst first determine whether it possesses an inner core.","└ Seriously, a spiritual creature appears every time he does anything. LOL","└ Is that actually a Sunfire Carp?","└ Who knows? Grylls has to check.","└ Wasn’t there something similar to a Sunfire Carp too?","└ Heavenly Demon) If thou art referring to the Ten-Thousand-Year Fire Carp, then yes. As the name suggests, it is a carp that has lived for ten thousand years.","└ Starlight Princess) In the past, I would have told you to cut it open immediately, but there is no need for that anymore.","└ By \"the past,\" don’t you mean yesterday?","└ Starlight Princess) It feels like the distant past to me. Every day felt like an entire year.","└ I guess it could feel that way.","└ Maybe it feels like she was born again?","└ Waaah. I’ve been reborn. Feed me.","An inner core—wasn’t that something similar to the way oysters produced pearls?","I was not entirely sure, but I imagined it had effects similar to an elixir.","Of course, I did not truly believe this fish was a spiritual creature.","Even if it was, I did not care.","I had already decided that it would be today’s lunch.","└ Starlight Princess) You people never change. You are all such idiots~","But right now, it was my lunch.","No matter what anyone in the Gallery said, this fish was going to become my meal.","That meant it would probably be better to spend the morning repairing the shelter rather than exploring.","Wonmo might eat the fish while I was gone.","Even now, he was staring intently at the metal tub containing it, clearly waiting for an opportunity.","\"Hey!\"","I warned Wonmo just as he was about to reach for the fish.","Wonmo looked up at me with eyes so wide they were practically bulging.","His expression seemed to ask what he had done wrong.","His innocent face made him look even cuter.","\"You can’t eat that. I’ll give you honey after lunch.\"","\"Kyu.\"","\"That’s right. Our Wonmo is such a good boy.\"","I stroked Wonmo’s head several times and looked around.","If I wanted to build a defensive wall, clearing the trees had to come first.","Perhaps because of that, my chest already felt tight.","How long would it take me to clear all of them?","’They say small efforts eventually become a mountain. I have to do it.’","Grumbling inwardly, I walked toward a tree.","Why did it have to be so thick?","Still, I felt good today.","I gripped the axe tightly and swung it with all my strength.","After swinging it several times before, I had apparently learned the proper technique, allowing me to use the strength of my waist more smoothly.","Crack!","\"Huh?\"","The moment the axe struck the tree, a puzzled sound escaped my mouth.","The reason was simple.","The situation was far too different from yesterday.","Yesterday, I had needed to hack at the tree repeatedly before the axe could barely penetrate its surface.","Today was different.","The axe blade sank deeply into the trunk.","Even the sound was different.","’What is this? Is this tree weaker than yesterday’s?’","The axe could not have changed overnight.","I was in unusually good condition today, and perhaps this tree was also weaker.","That still did not answer all my questions, but since the situation benefited me, I decided not to dwell on it.","’A good thing is a good thing.’","Crack! Crack! Thunk!","After striking the tree about three more times, I examined the middle of the trunk.","Amazingly, I had almost cut straight through its center.","It looked as though the tree would fall if I only chopped the opposite side.","’Already?’","Until yesterday, I had spent the entire day swinging an axe just to cut down a single tree.","Then I had encountered the owlbear and nearly lost my life.","It was difficult to dismiss all these doubts by simply saying that this was a different tree or that I happened to feel better today.","However, there was one obvious difference between yesterday and today.","’Is it really because of the breathing technique?’","That seemed highly likely.","It was the only thing that had changed since yesterday.","There was no downside to becoming stronger anyway.","In an environment like this, physical strength was especially important.","’I’ll have to practice even harder from now on.’","It was amazing that a single breathing technique could shorten my working time this much.","What a strange world.","The world was a fitting mixture of fantasy and martial arts, and it was filled with superhumans capable of blowing up mountains.","Yet these people refused to believe that a single bomb could wipe out an entire city.","Their very existence was basically equivalent to a nuclear warhead.","’I really am curious about the outside world.’","The world shown through the Gallery was narrow.","It was also extremely subjective.","Though the poor reputation of Albenheim, the elven nation, seemed to be universal across every country.","After letting my thoughts wander, I moved to the opposite side of the tree.","If I chopped only this side, the tree should fall in the direction I wanted.","Crack! Crunch! Creak!","After several swings, the tree began to sway.","I checked the direction and shoved it with my foot.","The towering tree slowly began to fall with a loud creak.","Boom!","I had felled an entire tree in less than ten minutes.","The work speed was absurdly fast.","I stared at the fallen tree and checked my condition.","I was slightly tired, but not enough to need a break.","’I’ll do a little more before resting.’","After cutting down one more tree, I finally began to feel somewhat tired.","But it was only a sense of fatigue.","Cutting down another tree would not have been too difficult.","In the end, I felled three trees in total and finished listing them at the auction house.","’The area is starting to open up.’","Perhaps because I had cut down four trees in total by now, the space around the cave had become noticeably wider.","I smiled with satisfaction for a moment before entering the cave to take a proper rest.","Huff... huff...","When I entered, Wonmo was taking a nap.","As I had mentioned before, Wonmo was still a baby.","He would probably sleep most of the day.","’The fish is still fine too.’","It remained quiet inside the metal tub, no longer thrashing around.","I set down the axe and accessed the Gallery to see whether anything had happened while I was working.","Nothing particularly notable stood out, but one thing caught my attention.","’The Moderator has been less active.’","The Moderator, who managed the Gallery, had been unusually inactive.","Normally, posts containing explicit images, grotesque pictures, or excessively abusive language would be deleted immediately, and the users responsible would be banned.","[Photos of Older Sisters]","[All Elves Should Die]","[Warning: Graphic—Photo of My Hand]","Those posts were still up even though ten minutes had passed since they were uploaded.","Normally, they would have been removed instantly.","The users saw this as an opportunity and began unleashing their desires without restraint.","Pretending not to care, I discreetly opened one of the posts too.","Since I was stranded in the wilderness with nothing around me, the Gallery was my only source of entertainment.","Of course, it was not an urgent need.","It was merely something pleasant to look at.","I was too busy struggling to survive to have time for anything beyond that.","[Mr. Grylls, Please Read This.]","After refreshing the page several times, a title caught my eye.","’Allfather?’","Normally, I might have ignored it, but the author was a familiar named user.","I opened it immediately.","Title: Mr. Grylls, Please Read This","Allfather","The item I promised you is ready. Please initiate the trade whenever it is convenient.","It seemed the medicine he had mentioned before was finally complete.","The medicine made from the Golden Poison Frog.","He had said that consuming it would permanently grant resistance to poison, so I absolutely needed it.","└ Wild Grylls) Have you finished the medicine you mentioned before?","└ Allfather) Yes. I have prepared enough for ten days. I believe I will need more specimens for the remainder.","└ Wild Grylls) I’ll send you another Golden Poison Frog as soon as I catch one.","└ Allfather) Thank you. I shall await it.","If I gained resistance to poison, my chances of survival would increase dramatically.","To accomplish that, I would need to hunt another Golden Poison Frog.","I had already rested at just the right time, so I picked up the crossbow resting against the wall.","The arrows I had embedded in the owlbear’s head last time were still in perfect condition.","’It really is strange.’","I had been in such a hurry at the time that I listed the entire corpse at the auction house with the arrows still stuck in its head.","However, the arrows apparently had not been considered part of the corpse, because they had fallen out on their own.","I had nearly lost the arrows and harpoon bolts that I had worked so hard to obtain.","Creak—","I pulled back the crossbow string.","It drew back easily.","Before, I had needed to use all my strength.","Now, all it took was gritting my teeth slightly.","’My strength really has increased.’","That confirmed it.","I had not simply happened to choose weaker trees.","My physical strength had genuinely increased.","All because of a single breathing technique.","The change was so dramatic that I felt more confused than impressed.","It would be best to post about it in the Gallery soon and ask the Heavenly Demon or SwordMaster for advice.","’Everything is ready...’","I checked on Wonmo, who was sleeping soundly, and the fish inside the metal tub.","There did not seem to be any problems.","All I had to do now was hunt the Golden Poison Frog.","Just in case, I also took my sword and shield with me.","I did not forget to put several fasting pills in my pocket either.","After finishing all my preparations, I stepped outside the cave.","’Surely no thief will break in, right?’","With that pointless thought in mind, I headed toward the river.","***","It was after Grylls had left for the river to hunt.","The only sounds inside the cave were the occasional splashing of the fish and the soft breathing of the adorable baby owlbear.","Aside from those noises, the surroundings of the cave were perfectly still.","Birdsong could occasionally be heard, but it was nothing worth paying attention to.","Rustle—","At that moment, a sound came from between the dense trees.","At first, it seemed like nothing more than the wind.","But it was not.","Slowly—","An animal emerged from between the closely packed trees.","Its arms were unusually long compared to its short legs.","Long, vicious claws extended from the tips of its hands.","The creature, covered from head to toe in fur, moved forward very slowly.","Extremely slowly.","Using its long arms to support itself against the ground like a gorilla, it headed toward a very clear destination.","Splash! Splash!","The metal tub containing the fish.","Its advance was painfully slow, but no one was standing guard.","No matter how long it took, it would eventually reach the tub.","The animal moved with the same leisurely pace suggested by its relaxed-looking face.","\"What are you?\"","That was, had Grylls not returned after realizing he had forgotten the antidote.","The animal had nearly reached the metal tub when it heard his voice and turned its head.","Even the act of turning its head was unbearably slow.","Standing face-to-face with the unexpected thief, Grylls muttered quietly,","\"...A sloth?\""]},{"title":"Chapter 28","paragraphs":["Thief (2)","A sloth.","An animal whose name was associated with both trees and laziness.","True to its name, it was famous for how painfully slow every one of its movements was.","Apparently, sloths were so slow that even zoologists who had studied them for two years became frustrated enough to give up.","At first glance, that seemed like an enormous disadvantage in the wild, but sloths were surprisingly efficient animals.","It was the beauty of slowness.","Moving slowly meant consuming less energy.","’But this is the Forest of Four Seasons.’","I had no idea whether that philosophy of slowness worked in the Forest of Four Seasons.","Even now, it had come face-to-face with me, yet it was still moving at a leisurely pace.","The thing it had been after was clearly the fish inside the tub.","However, I was not sure whether sloths were omnivores.","This was exactly when the Gallery came in handy.","Title: What Is This Thing?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a sloth caught trying to steal the fish)","I went up to the river and came back down, and this thing was here.","It looks like I caught it trying to steal my fish. Do sloths eat meat?","└ Heavenly Demon) Its very expression exudes composure. Be careful.","└ ??? You don’t know what a sloth is?","└ She’s telling him to be careful of a sloth. LOL","└ This is ridiculous. LOL","└ Heavenly Demon) Thou fools will regret thy mockery only after being pierced by those vicious claws.","└ Allfather) I did not know sloths lived in the Forest of Four Seasons. They should normally inhabit jungles.","└ Wild Grylls) Sloths don’t eat fish, right?","└ Allfather) Their primary diet consists of leaves. Furthermore, sloths cannot walk and must crawl. Yet that specimen is supporting its body with both arms like a gorilla. It may not actually be a sloth.","└ Wild Grylls) (Video of the sloth moving extremely slowly)","└ Allfather) It is a sloth. What the hell is that thing?","└ Wild Grylls) I don’t know either.","└ Even the professor is suffering cognitive dissonance after watching the video. LOL","└ It’s a species even he’s never seen before. Damn.","└ Isn’t this basically a new research subject?","└ Allfather) It certainly is, but please be careful. Every plant and animal inhabiting the Forest of Four Seasons possesses at least one weapon of its own.","Both the Heavenly Demon and Allfather warned me to be careful.","The difference was that Allfather’s warning came from caution toward the unknown, while the Heavenly Demon seemed to be relying on instinct.","Either way, it did not hurt to be careful around this absurdly slow sloth.","’To be honest, I could just catch it.’","It was slow enough that I could grab it with my bare hands.","Still, I had no intention of doing so.","Touching it unnecessarily might expose me to disease or parasites.","Wonmo was fine because I had scrubbed him thoroughly, but this creature was different.","’I should chase it away first.’","Since it had gone after my fish, I had no intention of letting it off without doing anything.","Still, killing it felt a little excessive, so I planned to frighten it away.","\"Shoo. Shoo. Go away.\"","I tapped it lightly with the back of my sword rather than the blade, and the sloth slowly backed away.","Even the act of retreating was so sluggish that watching it made me feel frustrated.","However, that fish was meant to be my lunch.","I could not give it away, even to a sloth.","\"Go eat leaves. That’s what you normally eat, isn’t it?\"","\"You look like you don’t want to. Why not? Go climb a tree. There’s plenty of food up there.\"","The sloth’s perpetually relaxed expression changed slightly.","Its face shifted so subtly that it almost looked annoyed.","It seemed to be saying through its expression, You’re the one who cut down the trees.","If that was really what it meant, then I was sorry.","But I still was not giving it the fish.","\"Making that face won’t help. Hurry up and leave.\"","\"...\"","\"Tsk. This isn’t working.\"","Now, even when I pushed it with the back of my sword, it refused to retreat.","I looked around and picked up a suitable branch.","Poke. Poke. Poke.","When I prodded it with the branch and told it to leave, the sloth finally began backing away again.","Perhaps if I pushed it all the way to a tree, it would return to where it belonged.","Grab—","\"Huh?\"","But the world rarely went the way I wanted.","The sloth caught the end of the branch with one hand.","After a brief moment of surprise, I pulled backward to retrieve it.","Grip—","\"What kind of strength is this...?\"","It would not come free.","The sloth was far stronger than it looked.","Perhaps that was only natural for an animal that spent its life climbing trees. Its arms had to be powerful.","Rather than getting into a pointless contest of strength, it would probably be easier to find another branch.","’Or should I just put on my gloves and pick it up?’","That might actually be better.","The gloves were inside my pocket.","I put them on and moved behind the still-slow sloth.","It barely moved before I got behind it.","Even when I grabbed its back, it reacted no faster.","\"Heave-ho.\"","The moment I lifted it, the sloth’s expression shifted into surprise.","Even its facial expressions changed as slowly as its movements.","It was fascinating that such a relaxed-looking face could make an expression like that.","After carrying the sloth to a tree and setting it down, the matter finally seemed settled.","Now I only had to retrieve the antidote and leave to hunt the Golden Poison Frog.","’Surely it isn’t coming back this way.’","Feeling doubtful, I turned around.","Sure enough, it was approaching me with all its might.","It was moving so earnestly that I almost felt sorry for it.","What was so special about that fish that it was this obsessed?","A sigh escaped me.","’...This won’t do.’","Words—if they could even be called that—were clearly not enough.","I needed to threaten it more convincingly.","After all, this sloth was a thief trying to steal my precious meal.","I aimed the crossbow at the sloth as it carefully crawled toward me.","Killing it outright felt wrong, so I planned to shoot the ground and frighten it.","Slowly... slowly...","’...This is driving me insane.’","I was wasting this much time because of one sluggish animal.","Had I been more ruthless, I would have put a hole through its head already.","However, the sloth had not directly harmed me.","Every animal I had killed until now had threatened my life first.","I aimed the crossbow at the ground and fired far enough away that the sloth would not be hit.","Twang! Thunk!","The bolt shot forward at high speed and embedded itself in the dirt.","The sloth slowly lowered its head.","It stared calmly at the bolt sticking out of the ground, then raised its head again.","Slowly... slowly...","\"This is driving me crazy.\"","What in the world was inside that thing’s head?","Even after all this, it showed no intention of retreating.","In the end, my frustration drove me to ask the Gallery for help.","Title: Someone Tell Me How to Chase This Thing Away","Wild Grylls","(Video of the approaching sloth)","It keeps trying to take my fish.","I picked it up and carried it back to a tree, but it’s still doing this.","I even threatened it with the crossbow, yet it keeps coming. Any advice?","└ Heavenly Demon) What extraordinary perseverance. Thou shouldst learn from it.","└ SwordMaster) Why not just give it the fish? It looks like it’ll keep bothering you otherwise.","└ Wild Grylls) Teachers, I want to eat a proper meal too. Wonmo eats better food than I do.","└ That’s genuinely pitiful. LOL","└ Why the hell is that thing acting like that? Is there something special about the fish?","└ Wild Grylls) I think it’s because I destroyed its home.","└ Why did you destroy its home?","└ Wild Grylls) I cut down a tree, and apparently that was its house.","└ That sloth can talk?","└ Wild Grylls) No, it’s just a hunch. LOL","└ So you were just talking nonsense. LOL","└ Grylls, are you really going to become a man who loses to a sloth?","└ Wild Grylls) No, but killing it feels a bit much.","└ Just kill it and eat it, or feed it to Wonmo. That would be better.","└ Wild Grylls) Does it taste good?","└ I heard it tastes terrible. That’s probably why it survived humans.","└ Allfather) I have never seen a sloth behave like that before... Fascinating.","└ Even you’ve never seen one like this, Professor?","└ Allfather) I do not know much about the Forest of Four Seasons either. Nor would I ever want to go near it.","There was not much useful advice.","Most people simply suggested killing the sloth.","However, sloths supposedly tasted awful, and their hides were worthless, so I would not be able to sell it either.","It might be fine if Wonmo ate it, but dealing with the remains afterward would be troublesome.","’Still, I can’t give it the fish.’","Judging by that idiotic persistence, it would steal the fish eventually, no matter how long it took.","I finally had a chance to eat a proper meal after so long, and they expected me to give it up?","Not a chance.","I loaded another bolt and aimed at the sloth.","This time, I would not shoot the ground.","I intended to make the threat unmistakable.","No matter how slow it was, surely it would understand the danger if a bolt passed right beside its head.","’If I accidentally kill it...’","I would probably feel a little guilty.","I aimed beside the head of the slowly approaching sloth.","The moment it took another step, I pulled the trigger without hesitation.","Twang!","The bolt narrowly grazed past the side of its head.","Despite nearly dying, the sloth’s expression remained as relaxed as ever.","Did it genuinely not realize how close it had come to death, or was even its reaction simply slow?","Its shamelessness was becoming almost comical, and a hollow laugh escaped me.","’This isn’t working.’","I abandoned the idea of frightening it away.","Perhaps it would only come to its senses after I put a hole through its body.","I needed to hunt the Golden Poison Frog, and this had already delayed me far too long.","I steadied myself and aimed at the sloth’s shoulder.","The bolt was already loaded.","All that remained was to fire.","’Don’t come back again.’","I muttered the words inwardly and pulled the trigger.","There was no hesitation.","I had already given it plenty of chances.","Twang!","The bolt shot forward like lightning, heading directly for the sloth’s shoulder.","A single hit had been powerful enough to drive even an owlbear into a frenzy.","Since this creature’s hide was much thinner, the bolt would probably pass straight through it.","At least, that was what should have happened.","Whoosh!","The sloth twisted its body slightly and dodged.","It moved at the very last moment, just before the bolt could strike.","There was nothing slow about it.","Its movement had been astonishingly agile.","\"Huh?\"","Having witnessed it in real time, I could only let out a stupid sound.","What had I just seen?","Had I really watched a sloth dodge a crossbow bolt?","After a brief moment of stunned disbelief, I hurriedly loaded another bolt.","The first time must have been a coincidence.","Perhaps it had moved so slowly that I had simply misjudged its path.","I reassured myself and aimed the crossbow again.","The sloth had already returned to its usual sluggish movements.","Twang!","Another bolt flew.","Swish!","As if to prove the first time had not been an illusion, the sloth dodged again with a burst of lightning-fast movement.","That alone was absurd enough, but what it did next was even more unbelievable.","As though nothing had happened, it resumed its painfully slow approach toward me.","’...This thing is dangerous.’","I narrowed my eyes and raised my guard.","It was absolutely not something I could take lightly.","It had seen the bolts coming and dodged them.","And it had done so with barely any movement.","A bolt launched from a crossbow traveled extremely fast.","Reacting after seeing it was nearly impossible.","Title: Can Anyone Here Dodge an Arrow After Seeing It?","Wild Grylls","Isn’t that extremely difficult?","Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster, please don’t answer.","└ Heavenly Demon) Why art thou excluding this lady?","└ Wild Grylls) Because if I ask you, you’ll probably just say it’s easy.","└ Heavenly Demon) Thou hast come to understand this lady well. How gratifying.","└ SwordMaster) It’s surprisingly easy. You just watch it and dodge.","└ Wild Grylls) Sigh...","└ You don’t really dodge after seeing the arrow. You predict its trajectory.","└ Yeah, and you watch the archer’s hands. That makes it easier than you’d think.","└ Easy, my ass. LOL. It hits you almost the instant the archer releases the string.","└ Most people calling it easy are probably holding shields. LOL","└ You caught me. LOL","└ Why are you asking, anyway?","└ Wild Grylls) The sloth dodged a bolt after seeing it.","└ What?","└ ???","└ What kind of nonsense is that now?","└ Wild Grylls) I wish it were nonsense too.","Even the Gallery agreed that it was difficult.","They said an ordinary human could not visually track an arrow once it left the string.","And when I told them a sloth had done exactly that, none of them believed me.","’I saw it with my own eyes, and I still don’t believe it.’","While I was distracted, the sloth drew even closer.","Judging by the distance, it was now about ten meters away.","At this range, dodging after seeing the bolt should be impossible.","I aimed the loaded crossbow at the sloth.","Now that I knew it was dangerous, there would be no more mercy.","’This time, I’ll aim for the head.’","Without the slightest hesitation, I pulled the trigger.","The instant I did, the sharp bolt shot directly toward the sloth’s head.","At this rate, it would pierce the center of its skull and kill it instantly.","But this was the Forest of Four Seasons.","A place inhabited by every kind of bizarre and extraordinary plant and animal.","Grab!","\"...Holy shit.\"","The sloth caught the bolt aimed at its face with one hand.","It slowly lowered the hand covering its face and stared calmly at me.","Its unbearably relaxed expression seemed to be saying only one thing.","Too slow."]},{"title":"Chapter 29","paragraphs":["Thief (3)","The sloth—or rather, I should start calling it the Speed Sloth now.","The Speed Sloth looked at me with an expression that radiated leisure and quiet disdain.","Oddly enough, I didn’t feel angry.","Instead, my sense of danger shot through the roof.","Snap!","The arrow it had caught in one hand broke cleanly in half.","What worried me far more than that were its claws.","Those vicious, overgrown claws.","The moment those hit me, my life is over.","There was no way I couldn’t be tense.","I don’t know when it’ll attack.","If it possessed that kind of agility, why did it usually move so slowly?","Maybe it was something like this.","\"I knelt only to build up momentum!\"","Ordinary sloths move slowly to conserve energy.","That’s what Allfather had explained.","But surviving in the Forest of Four Seasons probably made that impossible, so perhaps they’d evolved in another direction—","Displaying overwhelming speed only when faced with danger.","It was a surprisingly plausible theory.","This world was seriously insane.","Shuffle... Shuffle...","The Speed Sloth began moving again.","After witnessing that explosive burst of speed earlier, even its sluggish movements looked different now.","It wasn’t slow.","It was composed.","There had been a reason both the Heavenly Demon and Allfather warned me to be careful.","Can people really tell something’s this dangerous just by watching a video?","I wasn’t sure.","But one thing was certain.","Their instincts had been right.","So... how am I supposed to deal with this thing?","I lowered my crossbow.","Even if I fired, it’d either dodge the bolt or catch it with its hand.","There was no point.","Hand-to-hand... honestly, I think I’d lose.","It completely outclassed me in speed.","It had caught an arrow with its bare hand.","Me?","I could barely even follow an arrow’s trajectory with my eyes.","There was no choice but to stay on edge.","The moment I let my guard down, those claws might punch straight through my throat.","...No.","If it wanted to pierce my throat, it would’ve done it already.","That left only two possibilities.","Either this Speed Sloth was a pacifist...","Or it simply had no intention of killing me.","The first option would be great.","The second was potentially even more dangerous.","Something that fast and agile would always be a threat.","...Or maybe it’s just playing with me.","Maybe it was acting so relaxed because it didn’t see me as any threat at all.","As I watched the Speed Sloth slowly approaching, I glanced behind me.","Inside the iron barrel were the fish I’d caught this morning.","Maybe I should just give them to it and let it leave peacefully.","It wasn’t a bad option.","The odds of winning a fight were practically nonexistent.","I’d received an elixir from Starlight Princess, but that only mattered if I wasn’t instantly killed.","If those claws struck a vital spot, the elixir probably wouldn’t save me.","After agonizing over it, I slowly picked up my shield.","Not my sword.","I had a different plan in mind.","Keeping the shield pointed at the creature, I carefully walked toward the iron barrel.","Even then, the Speed Sloth continued approaching at its usual slow pace.","Scrraape... Scrraape...","Before long, I was dragging the heavy barrel full of fish with one hand.","It really seemed like the creature wanted the fish.","The Speed Sloth continued its signature slow approach toward me.","Yeah.","It definitely wanted the fish.","But that only raised another question.","Why?","I’d heard sloths mainly lived on leaves.","So why was it after fish?","Had the animals of the Forest of Four Seasons evolved different diets as well?","Or... is there something special about the fish?","Something the Heavenly Demon had once said suddenly came back to me.","The fish I’d caught resembled spirit beasts —","The kind that possessed internal cores.","I still didn’t know if that was actually true.","After thinking it over, I dragged the barrel all the way inside the cave.","It made quite a racket.","Even so, Wonmo slept through it like nothing had happened.","One of us was facing a life-or-death crisis...","The other was sprawled out sleeping peacefully.","Life really wasn’t fair.","Well... he’s still just a baby.","Meanwhile, the Speed Sloth entered the cave.","There was nowhere left to run.","I gripped my sword and shield, remaining on full alert.","There was only one chance.","Attack the moment it reached for the fish.","I had no idea when those murderous claws might come for my throat.","I intended to finish it before that happened.","\"...\"","Then—","The Speed Sloth suddenly stopped.","It had never stopped before.","Slow, yes.","But never completely still.","Naturally, I found it strange.","The creature stared intently at something.","I followed its gaze.","It was looking...","At the sack containing my fasting pills.","Shuffle... Shuffle...","\"H-Huh?\"","Not the fasting pills.","Anything but those.","Panicking, I rushed toward the sack.","The moment I grabbed it, the Speed Sloth quietly looked up at me.","Tap... Tap...","Without changing its expression, it casually flexed those terrifying claws.","Anyone could tell what it meant.","It wanted one.","And if I didn’t hand one over...","It looked suspiciously like a death threat.","\"...Should I give you one?\"","\"...\"","It simply stared at me.","Honestly, I preferred this.","If its attention had shifted from the fish to the fasting pills...","And I still had plenty of pills left...","Then maybe this wasn’t so bad.","Carefully, I took out a single fasting pill.","\"T-This?\"","\"...\"","Tap... Tap...","\"...You want another one?\"","\"That might be a little diff—\"","Whoosh!","Without a sound—","(Not that it could talk in the first place.)","Its claw stabbed straight into the fasting pill.","Then it slowly carried it to its mouth.","Even that action was agonizingly slow.","Watching it somehow made me nervous.","\"...Hmm.\"","The Speed Sloth slowly moved its jaw as though savoring the flavor.","Even the owlbear—and Wonmo—had spat the fasting pills out immediately because they were so bitter.","Heck, even I only forced myself to eat them to survive.","Never because they tasted good.","Yet this thing carefully chewed every bite.","Its relaxed expression never changed.","Just as I was about to complain that I barely had enough food for myself—","The Speed Sloth’s claw was suddenly inches from my throat.","Had it moved even a little farther...","There would’ve been a gaping hole in my neck.","Every drop of blood in my body turned ice cold.","I hadn’t even seen it move.","Tap... Tap...","As I swallowed hard, the Speed Sloth gestured with its other hand.","The meaning was obvious.","Hand it over... or die.","\"...Ha. Fuck.\"","What a miserable world.","Cursing under my breath, I reluctantly handed over another fasting pill.","Only then did it retract its claws.","After eating the second pill, it looked completely satisfied.","Thankfully, two seemed to be enough.","It didn’t ask for a third.","It also seemed to have completely lost interest in the fish.","I quietly let out a sigh of relief.","Shuffle... Shuffle...","\"Huh? Wait... what are you doing?\"","But the Speed Sloth wasn’t done surprising me.","Without warning...","It started climbing onto me.","It was careful not to stab me with its sharp claws, so it didn’t hurt at all.","\"...\"","\"...\"","Finally—","The Speed Sloth rested its chin on top of my head.","Did it think I was some kind of tree that grew leaves?","I was so dumbfounded that I couldn’t even speak.","I wanted to shake it off, but I couldn’t.","I’d only hurt myself if I tried to force it off.","Those vicious claws alone made it impossible to remove the creature by force.","At least it barely weighed anything.","Strangely enough, it didn’t smell bad either.","If anything, it smelled pleasant.","This thing probably has ticks too...","Still, I should wash it just in case.","I let out a deep sigh.","It hadn’t even been a week, yet I’d already gone through all kinds of bizarre incidents.","There was only one place where I could vent about this.","Title: Getting Mugged by a Sloth in Real Time","Wild Grylls","I’m the registered user who posted the sloth earlier. This bastard ate a fasting pill, then threatened me with its claws and demanded more. TTTT","What a miserable world. Never thought I’d live to see the day I got mugged by a sloth.","└ Heavenly Demon: You yielded merely because it pointed its claws at you?","└ Wild Grylls: This bastard can see and catch arrows... It nearly stabbed me in the throat at that speed too.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. In that case, I can understand to some extent. It may even make an excellent sparring partner.","└ Wild Grylls: You want me to spar with a sloth?;;","└ Heavenly Demon: You said you were slower than the sloth, so it would not be a poor choice.","└ Wild Grylls: Ha...","└ SwordMaster: What’s the sloth doing right now?","└ Wild Grylls: It’s hanging from my back.","└ SwordMaster: What kind of bullshit is that?","└ Wild Grylls: Sounds like bullshit, right? It’s true. I’ll upload a picture later.","└ Never thought I’d hear about a sloth mugging someone and then clinging to them. Hahahaha","└ This is legendary. Hahaha","└ Is that thing even really a sloth?","└ Wild Grylls: I decided to call it a Speed Sloth. ᄋᄋ","└ Speed Sloth. Kekeke","└ Better than Fluffy. Hahaha","└ Wild Grylls: What’s wrong with Fluffy?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: It’s lame!","└ The Moderator is here?","└ Appears out of nowhere and drops facts. Hahaha","└ Wild Grylls: Where have you been all this time?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: I was being chased, so I had to run away for a while! I’m safe now! Though I still have to sleep outdoors!","└ Ah...","└ Aah...","└ Aaaaah...","└ Wild Grylls: Why not come here instead? It’s surprisingly abundant here.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: I’m sorry! The Goddess would never forgive suicide!","└ Wild Grylls: That’s too harsh.","└ Allfather: A Speed Sloth... Perhaps you have discovered an entirely new species. Scholars may take an interest in it.","└ Wild Grylls: Normal sloths have lots of ticks too, right?","└ Allfather: They don’t have ticks. Instead, moths and beetles live in their fur and eat the ticks.","Ah.","Fuck.","└ Allfather: Furthermore, the fungi growing on it are probably protecting it from infection.","└ Wild Grylls: So none of that benefits me in the slightest?","└ Allfather: Correct. It’s filthy. Extremely so.","So I had to wash it somehow.","But I wasn’t sure whether the creature would willingly climb down.","At least it didn’t feel particularly unpleasant.","As I said earlier, it didn’t smell bad either, so it was tolerable.","For now, I guess I’ll have to catch the Golden Frog like this.","I’d catch the Golden Frog, trade with Allfather, and eat fish for lunch.","The sudden appearance of the Speed Sloth had thrown my plans off a little, but things were fine now.","With the Speed Sloth still on my back, I gathered my equipment.","Normally, I would sling the crossbow over my back, but the Speed Sloth was in the way—","Slide.","\"Hm?\"","When I tried to put the crossbow on, the creature quietly shifted aside.","Once the crossbow was secured, it climbed back on top of it.","It really was an intelligent animal.","I’d sensed it when it threatened me earlier, but it seemed to possess fairly high intelligence.","Does it understand what I’m saying, like Wonmo does?","Probably not.","It was likely just smart.","I carefully adjusted the crossbow so that the Speed Sloth couldn’t accidentally pull the trigger.","Perhaps it understood my intention, because it moved toward the front and hung there in a way that wouldn’t interfere with me.","Thanks to that, I ended up face-to-face with it.","Its expression looked undeniably stupid.","And yet this was the same creature that could catch a flying arrow.","The Forest of Four Seasons was truly bizarre.","Hissss...","I was making my way toward the river where the Golden Frog lived when an ominous sound reached my ears.","It sounded like a snake flicking its tongue.","I’d already suffered badly at the fangs of a Steel-Scaled Snake, so I immediately scanned my surroundings.","But I couldn’t see anything.","For a moment, I wondered whether I’d imagined it.","\"Shaaa!\"","Something brown that had clearly looked like a tree branch suddenly opened its jaws wide.","At the same time, its brown body turned green.","Two razor-sharp fangs protruded menacingly from its mouth.","It wasn’t a branch.","It was a venomous snake.","A-A chameleon?!","A snake imitating a chameleon’s camouflage?","What kind of grotesque combination was that?","I was so startled that I failed to react properly.","I’d genuinely mistaken it for a branch, so I hadn’t noticed it at all.","Slash!","However, there was an animal that moved before I did.","It happened so quickly that I couldn’t follow the process.","But I saw the result clearly with my own two eyes.","\"Shaaa! Shaaa!\"","\"...\"","Claws even more vicious than the snake’s fangs had pierced straight through its head.","The venomous snake trembled violently, its skull impaled on the claw.","It wrapped its body around the claw in a desperate attempt to escape, but the effort was pointless.","It was considerably smaller than the Steel-Scaled Snake I’d encountered before.","And the moment its head was pierced, its fate had already been sealed.","Riiip!","The Speed Sloth grabbed the snake with its free hand and pulled hard.","The venomous snake’s head split vertically.","Thud.","The snake was thrown to the ground, still twitching.","Its vertically torn head was utterly revolting.","Just in case, I stabbed it with my sword so it couldn’t bite me.","Before long, the snake’s body went limp.","Its torso occasionally twitched, but there was no doubt that it was dead.","I looked at the Speed Sloth hanging behind me.","As always, it wore its calm, leisurely expression.","It looked so peaceful, as though nothing had just happened.","\"...Want another fasting pill?\"","Node.","The Speed Sloth nodded.","As expected, even that movement was painfully slow."]},{"title":"Chapter 30","paragraphs":["Inner Core (1)","Thanks to the Speed Sloth’s help, I made it to the riverside safely.","The first thing I did after arriving was check the hose.","I looked to see whether another fish had been caught like before, and sure enough, my prediction was right.","Splash! Splash!","\"Another one got caught.\"","Another fish had been trapped in that short span of time.","This one was red too.","It was about the same size as the fish from earlier.","Judging by that, this seemed to be the average size of the fish inhabiting this river.","I’ll deal with this one later.","The Golden Frog was more important right now.","My trade with Allfather came first.","That meant I needed to get the Speed Sloth off my back.","I patted it on the back and asked,","\"Can you get down for a moment? This is urgent.\"","\"...\"","Shuffle... Shuffle...","As though it understood me, the creature slowly climbed down.","Then it stared at me with that stupid-looking face.","It almost felt like it was urging me to hurry up.","That was probably just my imagination.","Time to lure out a Golden Frog.","The one that seemed to be their leader had appeared the moment I dipped my hand into the river.","Would the others react the same way?","I carefully placed my hand in the water.","About three seconds later, I heard a splash from the middle of the river.","\"Croak.\"","A Golden Frog.","It climbed onto a rock in the middle of the river.","It was smaller than the one I’d seen before, but still quite large.","The moment it appeared, I retreated without hesitation.","I also remembered to raise my shield, just in case.","\"Kyaaaak!\"","The Golden Frog tilted its head back.","It even made a sound like it was gathering phlegm.","It looked ready to spit poison.","But I had already moved far away.","The only one still sitting there blankly was the Speed Sloth.","\"Hey! What are you—?!\"","\"Ptooey!\"","Before I could finish shouting, the Golden Frog spat its poison.","A glob of purple mucus shot forward at high speed.","Its target was the Speed Sloth.","The Speed Sloth calmly watched the poison coming toward it.","Then it tilted its head slightly.","Sssssss!","The poison narrowly passed beside its face.","It struck a tree and immediately began melting the bark.","I’d more or less expected it, but its agility was still incredible.","Now.","While the Golden Frog’s attention was focused on the Speed Sloth, I prepared my crossbow.","I loaded a harpoon bolt and aimed at the Golden Frog.","\"Kyaaaak!\"","\"Kyaaak!\"","\"Croooak!\"","Meanwhile, more Golden Frogs climbed onto the rocks.","I had already hidden myself, but the Speed Sloth remained seated there without the slightest concern.","Even if it was the Speed Sloth, dodging several consecutive attacks should be diffic—","\"Ptooey!\"","\"Ptui!\"","\"Ptoo!\"","Whoosh—Whoosh, whoosh!","...Apparently not.","Even though it stayed in the same spot, it avoided every attack merely by twisting its body with effortless ease.","Its expression was so relaxed that it looked like some reclusive master.","Does that bastard have Observation Haki or something?","There was no other explanation.","I let out a breath of disbelief.","Still, that was that, and this was this.","My preparations were complete.","I aimed at one of the Golden Frogs and pulled the trigger.","Twang! Thud!","The harpoon pierced the Golden Frog cleanly, knocking it into the rushing river.","I immediately began pulling the rope.","The other Golden Frogs didn’t attack me in the meantime.","They seemed greatly shocked that one of their companions had been struck.","Of course, that was only my guess.","But judging by the way they all stopped attacking at once, they at least seemed capable of understanding what had happened.","Every creature living in the Forest of Four Seasons was extraordinary in one way or another.","Splash!","Perhaps deciding to retreat, the group of Golden Frogs leaped back into the river.","They probably wouldn’t pose a threat for a while.","All that remained was cleaning up.","I pulled hard on the rope connected to the harpoon.","Previously, it had felt like I was locked in a tug-of-war.","Now, I only needed to exert a little strength.","\"Heave-ho.\"","The Golden Frog I dragged out of the water was quite large.","Not as large as the one I’d caught before, but about the size of a small puppy.","All that remained was trading it to Allfather.","Before that, though, I needed to deal with the fish.","I’ll tie this to my waist for now.","This was something Allfather had taught me.","If purple liquid began pouring out, it meant the poison sac had ruptured.","No purple liquid was leaking right now.","That meant it was safe.","With the frog hunt finished, the only thing left was the fish.","I had no idea what it ate to grow so large.","Today’s haul is generous.","With this, both lunch and dinner were secured.","I lifted the fish, which was still thrashing wildly.","There’s no way I could catch this thing with a fishing rod.","It was so strong that it was still trying to slap me in the face with its fins.","Afraid I might drop it, I hugged the fish tightly with both arms.","Had my strength not increased, I would’ve lost my grip long ago.","Shuffle... Shuffle...","The Speed Sloth climbed onto my back again, completing my preparations to return.","\"It’d be nice if you tasted good, but that’s probably asking too much.\"","Taste didn’t matter.","In my situation, caring about flavor was a luxury.","Besides, I could buy seasoning from the auction house, so it would probably be fine.","Splash!","After returning to the cave, I placed the fish inside the iron barrel.","It was still so powerful that the barrel trembled slightly.","It was probably better not to try catching one of these with a fishing rod.","At this rate, I might end up being the one dragged into the water.","A trap or fish basket seemed like a safer option.","Just looking at the two massive fish made me feel secure and happy.","Time to trade with Allfather.","After organizing my belongings, I made a post in the Gallery.","I wrote that Allfather should send me a trade request if he was online.","[Allfather has sent you a trade request. Would you like to accept?]","It didn’t take long for him to contact me.","I gave the Speed Sloth another fasting pill and accepted the request.","[Allfather: Hello. I saw your post and sent a trade request.]","[Wild Grylls: Hello. I’ll put the item up right away. The poison sac hasn’t ruptured.]","[Allfather: Thank you. This should make my research much easier.]","[Wild Grylls: That’s good to hear. Ah, there’s also something I’m curious about.]","[Allfather: Go ahead.]","[Wild Grylls: The Speed Sloth climbed onto me and refuses to get off. Do you know why?]","[Allfather: Are you referring to the sloth that supposedly caught an arrow?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. Hard as it is to believe, it really did catch one.]","[Allfather: To be honest, I don’t know either. No such specimen has ever been documented in academia.]","Even Doraemon Allfather didn’t know what species it was.","Just what kind of place was the Forest of Four Seasons?","As I sighed inwardly, Allfather offered his own theory.","[Allfather: Still, I can make a guess. You said in your post that it extorted you?]","[Wild Grylls: It didn’t take money, but it did steal my fasting pills.]","[Allfather: Perhaps it thinks of you as a tree.]","[Wild Grylls: A tree?]","[Allfather: Is it still hanging from you?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. It doesn’t seem interested in getting off.]","[Allfather: Then yes. To it, you may simply be a tree that produces food.]","[Wild Grylls: That sounds kind of...]","[Allfather: Ridiculous, yet strangely plausible? I think so too.]","Allfather said it exactly as it was.","Even he seemed to find the theory absurd.","Still, it was reasonable enough that there wasn’t any better explanation.","[Allfather: Since it doesn’t seem hostile, keeping it might not be a bad idea.]","[Wild Grylls: I don’t completely dislike it either. I almost got bitten by a snake today, and this guy helped me.]","After chatting about this and that, Allfather and I completed the trade.","I gave him the Golden Frog’s corpse, and he gave me a pill that would increase my resistance to poison.","[Allfather: It would be best to take it after a meal. Proper digestion is important.]","[Wild Grylls: Should I absorb this using the breathing technique too?]","[Allfather: Yes. You can think of it as a kind of inner core.]","An inner core.","I remembered the Heavenly Demon’s explanation.","A crystal formed when energy accumulated inside the body of a spirit beast.","The mention of inner cores made me curious about something, so I asked Allfather.","[Wild Grylls: Have you ever eaten an inner core before?]","[Allfather: I’ve never eaten an inner core, but I have consumed a Dragon Heart.]","[Wild Grylls: What’s that?]","[Allfather: Exactly what it sounds like. The heart of a dragon. It contains an immense amount of mana.]","I had a rough idea of what dragons were.","They were mentioned in the Gallery from time to time.","They were powerful enough to treat humanity as insignificant, though they weren’t completely unrivaled.","More importantly, I’d heard their numbers were so low that they were considered endangered.","Could there be dragons in the Forest of Four Seasons too?","If there were, they’d be disasters incarnate.","I was only a weak human.","How was I supposed to catch something that could fly freely through the sky and breathe fire?","[Allfather: Thank you, as always, for another excellent trade. Feel free to ask me whenever you encounter an unusual animal.]","[Wild Grylls: I saw something that looked like a cross between a chameleon and a snake too.]","[Allfather: What was that?]","[Wild Grylls: I thought it was a tree branch, but it turned out to be a snake. It changed the color of its body in an instant.]","[Allfather: Oh! This place truly is overflowing with fascinating creatures!]","[Wild Grylls: Want to come here?]","[Allfather: This old man’s knees aren’t what they used to be. I’ll have to decline.]","[Wild Grylls: TT]","That was where our conversation ended.","Apparently, even Allfather wanted nothing to do with the Forest of Four Seasons.","Well, who would willingly come to a hellhole like this?","I was lucky, at least.","Most other people trapped here couldn’t even access the Gallery.","\"Hmm.\"","I stared at the pill resting on my palm.","It was round and pale purple.","This was the medicine I’d received from Allfather.","According to his explanation, eating it would grant me resistance to poison.","I should eat lunch first.","I placed the pill in my pocket and walked over to the iron barrel containing the fish.","There were only two fish inside, yet they filled the entire barrel.","How am I supposed to cook these?","I’d lived alone back home, so I knew how to cook.","But that was with ingredients that had already been cleaned and prepared.","I’d never had to butcher a fish myself.","There was only one thing to do in situations like this.","Ask the Gallery.","It was better to gain at least a little knowledge than charge ahead blindly.","Title: Need Help Cleaning a Fish!","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the fish inside the iron barrel)","Anyone have advice? These things are fucking huge too.","└ Professionals pierce the brain with a knife or awl to kill it instantly. If you’re inexperienced, just cut the whole head off.","└ Hit its head with the back of a knife before cutting it. That’ll stun it. Make your move then.","└ Removing the guts is easy. Just cut open the belly.","Since I was inexperienced, I decided to use the method of striking its head first.","I was going to grill it immediately anyway, so there was no need to worry about aging the meat or anything like that.","\"Kyuu.\"","\"Wonmo, wait just a little longer.\"","Wonmo had woken up with perfect timing the moment lunchtime arrived.","Just look at those bright, expectant eyes demanding food.","I wanted to toss him a chunk of meat immediately, but cleaning the fish came first.","I wrapped both arms around one of the fish and lifted it out of the barrel.","Flop! Flop!","The fish thrashed wildly as if demanding that I release it, but that wasn’t happening.","I placed it on the stone slab I’d prepared in advance.","The fish was so large that even the broad slab looked small beneath it.","They said to hit the head hard, right?","Because of its size, an ordinary knife wouldn’t be enough.","This was exactly when I needed the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","I wasn’t using the blade, so I swung it down without holding back.","Bang! Bang! Bang!","After striking it three times in succession, I got a reaction.","Just as the Gallery comments had said, its mouth and gills opened wide.","It had been properly stunned.","I immediately began cleaning it.","Since I might injure myself, I used an ordinary dagger rather than the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","The dagger was quite sharp, so it sliced through the fish’s flesh easily.","\"Wonmo, want this?\"","\"Kyuu!\"","I cut off the head and gave it to Wonmo.","He ate it with great enthusiasm.","He could eat rotting corpses, so a fresh fish head was probably nothing to him.","The Speed Sloth was more interested in fasting pills than fish, so I didn’t need to worry about it.","Now to cut open the belly.","Whenever blood came out, I rinsed it away with water.","I slowly sliced open the belly of the now-silent, headless fish.","The sensation against my fingertips wasn’t pleasant, but it was something I’d have to get used to.","Would Wonmo eat the organs too?","With the belly opened, I could see the densely packed organs inside.","I just needed to remove all of them and wash the cavity with water.","I reached inside to pull them out.","\"Hm?\"","My hand caught hold of something.","At first, I thought it was the heart.","But it was far too hard to be one.","I fumbled around and finally managed to pull it out.","It was a small bead roughly the size of one segment of my finger.","Its color was red, just like the fish.","What’s this? Could it really be an inner core?","Surely not.","Spirit beasts that possessed inner cores couldn’t be that common.","Still, considering that fully grown Mandrakes were practically lying around here, I couldn’t completely dismiss the possibility.","I’d even discovered a New Moon Spirit Herb right at the beginning.","Hmm...","I stared at the red bead for a while before making a decision.","It would be best to ask the Gallery.","More specifically, an expert.","And the obvious expert was the Heavenly Demon, the first person who had mentioned inner cores to me.","She wasn’t the type to secretly steal it either, so I could ask her without worry.","Title: Heavenly Demon, I Have a Question","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the red bead)","I found this while cleaning a fish.","It looks similar to the inner core you mentioned before. Can you tell what it is?","If the photo isn’t enough, I can send it to you through a trade.","└ Heavenly Demon: You found it inside a fish?","└ SmartCultist: Ha...","└ SwordMaster: Aren’t pearls made by shellfish, not fish?","└ Exactly. She’s confidently saying something completely ignorant. Hahaha","└ Even for an old fossil, that’s a bit much.;;","└ Isn’t she just stupid?","└ I’m embarrassed just reading this.","She replied only three seconds after I posted.","Her response speed was truly terrifying.","The sudden discussion of the Heavenly Demon’s lack of basic knowledge made me slightly uneasy.","Still, she was the person who had taught me the breathing technique, so I could trust her with this.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll send you a trade request. You only need to check whether it’s an inner core.","└ Heavenly Demon: If it truly is an inner core, what do you intend to do with it?","└ Wild Grylls: Eat it, obviously. You said it was good for the body, didn’t you?","└ Heavenly Demon: I do not recommend that. As I told you before, your internal energy is already oversaturated. Consuming an inner core as well may cause serious trouble.","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. I found it while removing the organs.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. It is difficult to tell from the photograph alone. It may simply be a pearl.","└ Wild Grylls: Can fish make pearls too?","└ Heavenly Demon: I was under the impression that they could.","I nodded at the Heavenly Demon’s advice.","Too much of a good thing could indeed be harmful.","Eating an inner core in my current state might cause a serious problem.","That left only one option.","Give it to the Heavenly Demon.","SwordMaster would probably refuse, claiming that she didn’t want to become healthier.","└ Wild Grylls: Then would you like to eat it?","└ Heavenly Demon: Inner cores can no longer raise my cultivation. I passed that stage long ago.","└ Wild Grylls: Then what should I do with it?","└ Heavenly Demon: The answer is simple.","The Heavenly Demon’s response was straightforward.","└ Heavenly Demon: Why not put it up for auction?","What an incredibly carefree suggestion.","Should I?","And I found myself gradually leaning toward that carefree idea."]},{"title":"Chapter 31","paragraphs":["Inner Core (2)","The daily life of the Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol, was so simple that it bordered on monotonous.","She sat upon the highest throne of the Heavenly Demon Divine Cult, a seat meant only for the heavens themselves.","From there, she browsed the Gallery and organized whatever enlightenment she had gained.","That was all.","She had no need to sleep.","She had no need to bathe either.","At her level of cultivation, her body always remained in perfect condition.","And so, every single day, she sat on her throne and browsed the Gallery.","One might ask what kind of ridiculous lifestyle that was, but reality was reality.","Anyone who saw it might have asked a question like this.","Title: Does the Heavenly Demon Have a Job?","If she does, what kind of work does she even do? I’m kind of curious.","└ What job would an old fossil who browses the Gallery all day have? Hahaha","└ Even if she has one, isn’t she basically role-playing as an unemployed shut-in?","└ Judging by the way she talks, maybe she’s some kind of adviser?","└ Heavenly Demon: I sit upon the throne.","└ That’s it?","└ Heavenly Demon: My majesty is displayed through that alone.","└ So you’re just unemployed. Kekeke","└ How is that any different from being a shut-in? Hahaha","└ Heavenly Demon: Do not compare me to those who abandon their duties and hide away. I am at least revered as the heavens themselves.","└ What a load of bullshit. Hahaha Does she think she’s some kind of god? Hahaha","└ Wouldn’t that get her arrested for blasphemy?","└ Heavenly Demon: I personally crush the heads of those who mock me.","└ Damn, this role-play is seriously intense.;;","└ Just leave her alone. She’s always been like that.","Wasn’t the Demonic Cult a place that regarded the Heavenly Demon as the heavens themselves?","Then how was she any different from a shut-in?","The problem was that they literally worshipped her as the heavens.","What was the sky?","A symbol of divinity that had existed since humanity first came into being.","Very few people could face such an existence directly and plead for their wishes.","Even those who wished to make a request had to go through the Demonic Brain, the true administrator of the cult.","At first glance, that might make the Heavenly Demon seem like a mere figurehead.","But that couldn’t have been further from the truth.","Even the Demonic Brain would not escape unharmed if he displeased her.","The moment one fell out of favor with a Heavenly Demon who had surpassed the Transformation Realm and reached the Profound Realm, it was over.","Title: Can Usernames Be Duplicated?","A lot of registered users have surprisingly simple names.","The Heavenly Demon is especially famous throughout the Central Plains, right?","Did no one ever claim that username before?","└ Usernames probably can’t be duplicated. Semi-registered accounts can use them, though.","└ Even semi-registered accounts can’t use one if a registered user already claimed it.","└ What’s the difference between semi-registered and registered accounts? Is it that yellow mark beside the name?","└ That’s part of it, but registered users can also list items in the auction house and conduct private trades.","└ The Moderator can track their location too, though. Hahaha","└ The former former former Moderator did that, killed someone, and went to prison.","└ Damn, that’s terrifying.","└ So because the Heavenly Demon claimed it as a registered username, no one else can use it?","└ ᄋᄋ Exactly.","└ You’re saying no one had ever registered the name Heavenly Demon before?","└ Someone probably did, but they were likely all semi-registered accounts. Who in their right mind would register Heavenly Demon as a permanent username? Hahaha","└ The current Moderator is nice. The former former former one would’ve sold your address for money. Hahaha","└ But what if she turned out to be the real Heavenly Demon?","└ Then the Demonic Cult would’ve been ruined for a completely different reason.","└ Heavenly Demon: There is no need for concern. As long as I exist, the Demonic Cult will never fall.","└ That’s exactly the problem, ma’am.","└ If someone like that were really the Heavenly Demon, the cultists would have an existential crisis. Hahaha","└ How is she browsing the Gallery twenty-four hours a day?;;","So that she could reply the moment her benefactor made a post.","Most matters concerning the Demonic Cult were handled by the Demonic Brain, leaving her with little to do.","All sorts of rumors circulated about her, but it was true that Yu Sowol had become completely immersed in the Gallery.","Recently, she had even encountered a benefactor who could only be described as a fortuitous encounter.","Worried that something might happen to him, she remained in the Gallery at all times.","As always, she was browsing through the Gallery.","Yu Sowol sat idly upon her throne, staring intently at something.","A tiny red bead rested between her slender fingers.","It was the item Wild Grylls—her benefactor and fortuitous encounter—had traded to her so she could determine whether it was an inner core.","Having surpassed the Transformation Realm and entered the Profound Realm, identifying it was easy.","It is an inner core.","The red bead Grylls had given her was indeed an inner core.","Though it looked like an ordinary marble, the energy contained within it was anything but ordinary.","However, it is lacking in many respects.","For an inner core, it was deficient in several ways.","First, the absolute amount of energy it contained was too small.","Normally, consuming an inner core could allow a Supreme Peak martial artist to enter the Transformation Realm.","This one contained only enough energy to raise someone from the Peak Realm to the Supreme Peak Realm.","It was likely the inner core of a spirit beast that had lived for several centuries rather than several millennia.","Still, it is not bad.","To Yu Sowol, who had already entered the Profound Realm, it was little more than a medicinal treasure beneficial to the body.","Of course, that was only from Yu Sowol’s perspective.","To anyone else, it was an object surpassing treasure.","Considering how rare even Supreme Peak martial artists were, its true value was easy to imagine.","If this were released onto the market—especially through the Gallery’s auction house—it would undoubtedly cause an uproar.","It is too much for my benefactor to consume. What a pity.","But Yu Sowol did not dwell on that.","There was something more important.","Grylls had only just begun learning an internal cultivation technique.","By some stroke of fortune, he had opened both his middle and upper dantians, but he was still inexperienced.","If he consumed the inner core as well, his body might be unable to withstand it and burst apart in the worst-case scenario.","Even if he survived, he would likely suffer from fever and pain for several days.","That was not an outcome someone focused on survival like Grylls would prefer.","But leaving the inner core unattended was not an option either.","The energy within an inner core dispersed over time.","Since it had originally existed inside the body of a spirit beast, that was only natural.","What a remarkable forest. To think that fish containing inner cores can be caught so easily.","A New Moon Spirit Herb.","A fully grown Mandrake.","And now, even a fish containing an inner core.","Each one alone would be enough to shake the entire world, yet the Forest of Four Seasons seemed to have them lying around everywhere.","Even so, entering the forest was no different from suicide.","The space itself constantly shifted, and access to the Gallery was normally impossible.","Grylls was surviving only because, for some strange reason, he could still access it.","An ordinary person wouldn’t last two days.","Was that how the Demonic Brain explained it?","Yu Sowol stared at the inner core for a moment before accessing the Gallery.","Now that she had confirmed its quality, all that remained was to inform Grylls.","Because they had just completed a trade, she could not immediately return it.","Still, there were ways to preserve the energy within an inner core, so there was no need to worry.","Title: Benefactor, Read This","Heavenly Demon","As you requested, I have verified the authenticity of the inner core.","It is genuine.","└ Isn’t she trying to scam him?","└ So she can sell it at a higher price. Hahaha","└ Now even inner cores are appearing. Hahaha","└ Heavenly Demon: Believe me or not as you please. I have not spoken a single falsehood.","She ignored all the pointless comments.","The only person who mattered to Yu Sowol was Grylls.","Still, playing along with the others for a moment didn’t seem so bad.","Unlike her, who remained in the Gallery at all times, Grylls was busy.","As she idly traded jokes with the other users, Grylls finally left a comment.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh. It’s actually real?","└ Heavenly Demon: Indeed. What will you do with it now?","└ Wild Grylls: What would happen if I ate it?","└ Heavenly Demon: In the worst case, your body may burst. Even if that does not happen, there is a high chance you will suffer from a severe fever for several days.","└ Wild Grylls: So basically, I have to give it to someone else.","└ If it’s real, give it to me. I’ve hit a wall and I’m still stuck at First-Rate.","└ Give it to me. I’m stuck at Intermediate Expert.","└ Give it to me give it to me give it to me give it to me give it to me","└ Cultistcultistcultistcultistcultistcultist!","└ Heavenly Demon: What a pathetic spectacle.","Perhaps he needed time to think, because Grylls did not reply for a while.","Or perhaps something else had happened in the meantime.","The Heavenly Demon waited silently.","She could already predict what kind of comment would appear.","He will most likely choose to give it either to me or to someone else.","└ Wild Grylls: Then you can eat it, Heavenly Demon, or give it to someone around you.","└ Heavenly Demon: Is there anything you desire in return?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. Could you give me more fasting pills?","Just as expected, Grylls left such a comment.","He was proposing to exchange the inner core for fasting pills.","At his suggestion, Yu Sowol unconsciously smiled.","It was a smile worthy of a painting, but unfortunately, there was no one there to see it.","The Heavenly Demon sat alone upon the throne in the audience hall.","└ Heavenly Demon: An inner core is a precious medicinal treasure. Though this one is somewhat lacking, an inner core is still an inner core. Even if it takes time, it would be better for you to consume it eventually.","└ Wild Grylls: But I don’t know when that will be. If necessary, I can just catch another one.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm? There is another one?","└ Wild Grylls: I caught one just now. I don’t know whether it has an inner core, but since it looks exactly the same, there’s probably a good chance, right?","└ Heavenly Demon: What a wondrous forest.","└ He caught another one? Is that for real?","└ Wild Grylls: ᄋᄋ I’ll probably install a fish trap soon.","└ Won’t the fish tear the trap apart?","└ Wild Grylls: Then I’ll just ask the dwarf for help.","└ Passing Dwarf: Why me?","└ Wild Grylls: Did you make the barricade?","└ Passing Dwarf: Forgot. Kek.","└ Wild Grylls: You fucking bitch.","└ Passing Dwarf: What?","└ Wild Grylls: ...Is what I obviously shouldn’t say, right?","└ Look at this shameless bastard. Hahahahaha","└ This lunatic. Hahahahahahaha","Fasting pills.","Yu Sowol fell into thought.","She had previously given him an entire sack, so could he already be running low?","That was unlikely.","Even if he ate three per meal, she had packed plenty for him.","He probably intended to keep more as emergency rations.","That was the most reasonable explanation.","He must be accounting for the sloth as well.","With another mouth to feed, his supplies would naturally be depleted faster.","Grylls was likely preparing for that.","└ Considering the fully grown Mandrake, there’s a ninety-nine percent chance it’s real.","└ He could’ve coordinated the story with the Heavenly Demon.","└ Then they’d simply be scammers. Hahaha","└ Grylls doesn’t really have any reason to scam people, though. ᄋᄋ","└ Heavenly Demon: Wait here. I shall ask one of my close aides.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you. If it’s difficult, you don’t have to do it.","└ Heavenly Demon: It is a request from my benefactor. I cannot simply refuse. If it cannot be done, then I shall make it possible.","└ Wild Grylls: That’s kind of burdensome. Still, don’t pressure them too much if they say it’s difficult. I don’t want them to hate me for no reason.","└ Heavenly Demon: What will you do if they say it is impossible?","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll trade with someone else. Or list it in the auction house.","└ The auction house is about to explode. Kek.","└ Is that thing really an inner core?","A strange sense of anticipation was already spreading through the Gallery.","Hadn’t the incident involving the fully grown Mandrake happened only two days ago?","Naturally, posts flooded in claiming that the inner core must also be real and begging to receive it themselves.","Getting excited over nothing.","Yu Sowol snorted as she read them.","No one had even said they would give it away, yet they were already getting their hopes up.","Seeing those comments only strengthened her resolve.","She would exchange the inner core for fasting pills no matter what.","Coincidentally, the Demonic Brain was a master standing between the Peak and Supreme Peak Realms, making it a fair trade.","[Demonic Brain, are you listening?]","Yu Sowol summoned the Demonic Brain through a voice transmission.","He was probably busy at the moment, so calling him in this manner was more convenient.","[There is something I require. Come to me.]","No answer came back.","The audience hall was far from the place where the Demonic Brain currently was.","Ever since Yu Sowol entered the Profound Realm, her senses had long since surpassed the boundaries of humanity.","She no longer saw merely through her eyes.","Her perception was closer to looking down upon the world from the heavens.","Even with all this, the Forest of Four Seasons remains difficult. Nature truly is mysterious.","At the same time, she realized once again how extraordinary nature was.","The closer one drew to it, the farther away it seemed.","That perfectly described Yu Sowol’s impression of nature.","Putting that aside...","Until the Demonic Brain arrived, the Heavenly Demon continued browsing the Gallery.","Her reverence for nature was not the only thing that had grown after reaching the Profound Realm.","Is it truly impossible to interfere with the Gallery?","She had begun questioning whether she could interfere with it directly.","Aside from the Moderator, no user was capable of altering the Gallery’s structure.","She wanted to interfere with it somehow, but attempting to do so was like smashing her head against an unyielding wall.","Accessing it itself is not difficult. Just who created this strange civilization?","The origins of the Continental Integrated Gallery were unclear.","Some claimed that it had existed since ancient times, while others said it had appeared only recently.","Watching posts appear in real time, Yu Sowol thought,","In order to aid my benefactor...","Normally, this was not something she would have cared about.","But things had changed after receiving Grylls’s help.","The Heavenly Demon—the exalted sky of the Demonic Cult seated upon her throne—could now face him through the Gallery.","\"I greet the heavens of the Demonic Cult.\"","\"Take it.\"","Yu Sowol skipped over the trivial formalities and tossed the inner core.","As though he had anticipated her action, the Demonic Brain caught it easily without raising his bowed head.","He then slowly looked up, revealing his confusion.","\"Heavens, this is...?\"","\"It is an inner core. Though somewhat lacking, it belonged to a spirit beast that lived for several centuries.\"","She would find some way to interfere with the Gallery and aid Grylls.","Although she had yet to understand its basic structure, interference was not necessarily impossible.","Was it called... a Vice Moderator?","Just as Yu Sowol reached toward an unknown realm she should perhaps never have touched—","[Heavens, I have answered your summons.]","The Demonic Brain’s respectful greeting sounded from outside.","The moment Yu Sowol heard him, she closed the Gallery and spoke calmly.","\"Enter.\"","It was not the command of Yu Sowol the human.","It was the command of Yu Sowol the Heavenly Demon.","At her words, the tightly sealed doors of the audience hall slowly opened.","A young man dressed in the traditional attire of the Demonic Cult appeared beyond them.","The Demonic Brain.","Perhaps nervous, his expression was slightly stiff as he slowly raised his head.","Confusion soon became evident on his face.","He examined the red inner core from various angles before speaking in a reluctant tone.","\"It certainly is an inner core. Where did you obtain it?\"","\"I received it through a trade. Therefore, I have something to ask you.\"","\"Please give your command.\"","\"The fasting pills that were prepared for my cultivation. How many more can you produce?\"","Yu Sowol went straight to the point.","It meant that no further explanation was necessary.","The Demonic Brain thought for a moment before carefully answering.","\"The fasting pills produced for the heavens were made using precious medicinal herbs.\"","\"I know.\"","\"If you are referring to those, then it is possible.\"","\"How many days will it take?\"","\"We must prepare the ingredients, and you appear to require a large quantity. It will take approximately one week.\"","\"Good. Begin preparing them at once. You may consume the inner core.\"","\"I am grateful for your grace, Heavens.\"","The Demonic Brain bowed deeply in gratitude.","It was fortunate that his head was lowered.","Otherwise, Yu Sowol might have noticed the corners of his lips twitching upward.","The Demonic Brain soon turned around and departed from the audience hall, leaving Yu Sowol alone once more.","The moment she sensed that he had gone outside, she immediately accessed the Gallery.","[Ah. Fuck, why is my body heating up?]","\"Hm?\"","The instant she entered the Gallery, a certain title caught her eye.","It had been posted by Grylls.","Yu Sowol hurriedly opened it.","Title: Ah. Fuck, Why Is My Body Heating Up?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a fish that had been eaten clean, with even the bones picked bare)","My body started heating up the moment I ate this. What’s going on?","Don’t tell me it was poisonous?","\"Oh no.\"","Yu Sowol realized her mistake the moment she saw the post.","The energy of a spirit beast was not necessarily concentrated solely within its inner core.","The spirit beast itself was essentially another inner core.","Every piece of its flesh would contain powerful energy.","I was careless.","Yu Sowol hurriedly left a comment.","She was deeply worried that something might happen to Grylls."]},{"title":"Chapter 32","paragraphs":["Inner Core (3)","There was something I had realized over the course of my life.","The loneliest and most miserable moment in the world was when you were sick.","After my parents passed away, I once spent several days bedridden with illness.","I couldn’t remember how much I had cried back then.","Had even one of them still been alive, they would have taken care of me.","Loneliness and fever were the perfect combination for wearing a person down.","That was exactly how I felt now.","I’d finally eaten my fill for the first time in ages, only to collapse with a fever immediately afterward.","\"Kyuu.\"","At least I had the adorable Wonmo with me.","Without him, I think it would’ve hurt even more.","Perhaps the Speed Sloth could read the mood, because it climbed off my back the moment I began suffering.","\"You should just leave.\"","But because of its natural expression, it wasn’t comforting at all.","Its relaxed face was normally fine, but right now, it almost looked like it was mocking me.","Surely not.","I felt bad for taking my frustration out on an innocent Speed Sloth.","The sudden fever was clouding my judgment.","I panted from the heat burning throughout my entire body.","Every breath carried scorching air out of my mouth.","At this rate, I might start breathing fire like a dragon.","I don’t understand why this is happening.","It was ridiculous that eating a single fish had given me a fever.","I wondered whether I’d been infected by a parasite, but that was unlikely.","I’d cooked it thoroughly just in case.","The first possibility that came to mind was poison.","Could it have contained toxins like a pufferfish?","I took the medicine immediately, but I don’t know if it’ll work.","Just in case, I had swallowed the pill Allfather gave me.","Normally, I should’ve immediately circulated it using the internal cultivation technique, but I was in no condition to do so.","I could probably do it after the fever subsided a little.","Before that, I should check the Gallery.","I’d made a post just before the fever began, so there should be comments by now.","Title: Ah, Fuck. Why Is My Body Heating Up?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a fish eaten completely clean, with even the bones picked bare)","My body started heating up the moment I ate this. What’s going on?","Don’t tell me it was poisonous?","└ Is there even a poison that raises your body temperature?","└ There are some. I’ve heard of poisons that kill by causing a severe fever.","└ Allfather: Did you take the medicine I gave you?","└ Wild Grylls: I did, just in case.","└ Allfather: If it were poison, you should have recovered immediately. Strange. It probably isn’t poison.","└ Heavenly Demon: You should regulate your internal energy immediately. Since you consumed a spirit beast, your body must now be filled with energy.","└ Wild Grylls: But I didn’t eat the inner core.","└ Heavenly Demon: A spirit beast is called a spirit beast for a reason. Even without the inner core, its flesh would still contain a considerable amount of energy.","└ SwordMaster: Nothing works better than a mana cultivation technique when you’re sick. Taking a sip of elixir beforehand helps too.","└ Heavenly Demon: It is an internal cultivation technique, not a mana cultivation technique.","└ SwordMaster: Same thing, really. Hehe. Until you teach him the mnemonic formula, aren’t they all basically identical?","└ Heavenly Demon: I feel like tearing out that wicked tongue of yours.","└ SwordMaster: Go ahead and try. Kek.","└ Heavenly Demon: What an ugly sight, hiding in your room and doing nothing but running your mouth. I can practically see you wasting away with age and idleness.","└ SwordMaster: What did you just say?","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. Perhaps I should begin becoming more active myself. I would hate to become as unsightly as you.","└ Why did the Heavenly Demon suddenly attack all of us too?","└ That was some wide-area provocation. Fucking hell. Hahahaha","└ Suddenly, I want to support SwordMaster.","Come to think of it, I had an elixir.","The sudden fever had made me completely forget about it.","Enduring the steadily rising heat, I crawled forward.","Eventually, I reached into the storage box and grabbed one of the elixirs.","A brilliantly glowing golden liquid filled the bottle.","Different grades had different colors, but I was in too much pain to care which one I picked.","I’ll just take one sip first...","Even removing the cork was difficult.","Should I buy some fever medicine from the auction house?","I struggled to pull out the cork and drank a mouthful of the elixir.","A strangely bitter yet refreshing sensation flowed down my throat.","Now all that remained was the breathing technique.","Before beginning, I checked the comments again.","Just before closing the Gallery, I’d seen the Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster start arguing.","└ Heavenly Demon: Struggle all you wish. I am the one who will teach my benefactor his internal cultivation technique. Now begone.","└ SwordMaster: What if Grylls can’t understand the mnemonic formula?","└ Heavenly Demon: That will not happen. I shall explain every detail to him one by one.","└ SwordMaster: Sorry, but that’s realistically difficult. You’re not beside him. It’s hard to learn the practical nuances of a mana cultivation technique through a mnemonic formula alone.","└ Heavenly Demon: Does the same not apply to you? If he can understand merely from written explanations, then my benefactor is already a genius.","└ SwordMaster: Have you even read my posts? Do you have any idea how good I am at explaining things?","└ Her explanations really are good. The continent’s average combat strength rose because of her.","└ She covers everything from the basics to advanced applications, so both beginners and experienced fighters can use them.","└ The Heavenly Demon only posts garbage anyway. Hahaha","I should probably stop them here.","Perhaps thanks to the elixir, some of my dizziness had subsided.","└ Wild Grylls: SwordMaster, that’s enough. It’s true that your posts have helped me, but I don’t want to break my promise to the Heavenly Demon.","└ SwordMaster: I’m sorry. I got carried away.","└ Heavenly Demon: Pay no heed to someone who seeks to break trust with her wicked tongue.","└ Wild Grylls: SwordMaster was only trying to help me too.","SwordMaster’s posts really were useful.","Even someone like me, who knew absolutely nothing, had managed to grasp the basics because of them.","Perhaps that was why most people were more sympathetic toward SwordMaster than the Heavenly Demon.","The Heavenly Demon only kept replying because she marched entirely to the beat of her own drum.","An ordinary person would’ve had their spirit crushed by now.","Thankfully, the argument seemed mostly settled.","Had I not intervened, my entire post might have been buried beneath their fight.","Besides, SwordMaster had started it this time.","Though the Heavenly Demon had certainly taken the bait.","I should sit down now...","Even the elixir hadn’t completely brought the fever down.","Its pain-relieving effect had only reduced the suffering.","I forced my increasingly hot body upright and assumed the lotus position.","Before beginning the breathing exercise, I asked the Heavenly Demon for guidance.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m about to start cultivating. Could you teach me that mnemonic formula or whatever it’s called?","└ Heavenly Demon: I can, but as a precaution, I shall teach you only the first formula. A mistake could cause you to suffer qi deviation.","└ Wild Grylls: Understood. Please post it as a private comment.","└ Heavenly Demon: The heavens are the supreme existence revered by all creation. Reach out your hand and grasp them within it. If you look upward, then look downward. That is the nature of the heavens...","I had expected some ordinary piece of advice, only for a poem to suddenly appear.","It was archaic and, in a way, perfectly suited to a martial arts world.","Which meant I couldn’t understand it at all.","There was a reason SwordMaster had criticized internal cultivation formulas as poetry rather than practical guidance.","How is this supposed to help me?","Besides, the mnemonic formula wasn’t just a single line. It was fairly long.","The Heavenly Demon’s comments continued appearing one after another.","After feeling bewildered for a moment, I memorized every line she had posted.","My head was spinning from the fever, but not so badly that I couldn’t memorize it.","\"Hoo...\"","I began by controlling my breathing, imagining that I was gathering the heat inside my body.","I also repeated the Heavenly Demon’s formula in my head.","I just had to picture it somehow.","This was closer to emotion and intuition than actual interpretation.","Still better than Gwandong Byeolgok.","It was far better than that dreadful poem.","Imagining the mnemonic formula the Heavenly Demon had taught me, I began circulating my internal energy.","The heat scattered throughout my body seemed to gather in my lower abdomen.","The heavens are the supreme existence revered by all creation...","And after continuing the internal cultivation technique while reciting the formula—","\"Khrrr...\"","I fell asleep without even realizing it.","\"Ugh!\"","The sensation of falling from a great height made me bolt upright.","It felt like suddenly jerking awake after dozing off in class.","Except this sensation was several times more intense.","I became fully alert in an instant.","\"...\"","I blinked.","What kind of dream had I just been having?","I remembered flying freely through the sky, but nothing after that.","It was difficult to explain.","It almost felt as though my soul and body had separated.","Still, it had been a pleasant dream.","For the first time in a long while, I had experienced genuine freedom.","\"Kyuu...\"","While I sat there in a daze, a sorrowful sound reached my ears.","I turned toward it and saw a fluffy ball of fur staring at me.","It was Wonmo, the baby owlbear.","Wonmo gazed at me with sorrowful eyes.","Grrrrumble—","At the same time, an alarm sounded from his stomach.","I’m hungry. Feed me because I’m hungry. I’m sad because I’m hungry.","That was roughly what his expression seemed to say.","Feeling awkward, I checked the time.","No.","There was no need to check.","Looking outside the cave was enough.","...It’s already night?","The outside world was filled with complete darkness.","It had been around lunchtime when the fever struck after I ate the fish.","That meant I had slept for at least six hours.","No wonder Wonmo looked so miserable.","\"Wonmo, I’m sorry. I’ll feed you right away.\"","\"Kyuu!\"","\"Wonmo aside, where did Speedy go...?\"","The moment I turned my head, Speedy was right there.","The creature stared at me with its now-familiar expression.","Judging by the way its mouth was moving, it had eaten some fasting pills while I slept.","...It didn’t eat too many, did it?","With a growing sense of unease, I counted the remaining pills.","Thankfully, the number hadn’t decreased much.","In that case, feeding Wonmo came first.","I accessed the Gallery.","As always, it was noisy, but Wonmo’s meal was more important right now.","\"Here you go.\"","\"Kyuoooo!\"","The moment I bought him a chunk of meat, his eyes lit up with delight.","When I stroked his head because he was so adorable, he became even happier.","How could I possibly dislike him?","Just looking at him made me smile.","The fever seems to be gone, and nothing feels wrong with my body. I should be fine.","As expected, sleeping deeply was the best cure for a fever.","Still, my body felt damp from all the sweat.","That couldn’t be helped.","Since it was already late, I thought I should at least wash myself quickly.","The iron barrel still contained the fish, so taking a proper bath would be difficult.","\"Hm?\"","Just as I removed my clothes and stepped outside the cave, I noticed something strange.","I could see far too clearly.","My night vision had always been fairly good, but this was on an entirely different level.","It wasn’t as clear as daylight, but I could move around without any difficulty.","What’s going on?","I wondered about it briefly, then finished removing my clothes so I could wash.","There was no need to light a campfire.","Why would I need one when I could see perfectly well?","I would still need it when sleeping, though.","I could still feel the cold.","Flake.","Before washing, I ran a hand over my body and heard a strange sound.","I looked down and found myself facing something unexpected.","A layer of skin had peeled away.","It was different from the peeling caused by sunburn.","The skin underneath was soft and even slightly glossy.","I frowned when I saw it.","There was only one possible explanation.","How did I accumulate this much grime?","I’d thought I was washing myself properly, but apparently not.","I would have to be more thorough from now on.","For today, I could wash quickly and take a proper bath tomorrow.","If I soaked in warm water, the grime would probably come off more easily.","I can cook the fish for breakfast while I’m at it.","Surely eating it wouldn’t give me another fever.","Then the next morning came, and when I cleaned the second fish—","\"This came out again.\"","Another inner core appeared among its organs."]},{"title":"Chapter 33","paragraphs":["Inner Core (4)","The Heavenly Demon had told me that an Inner Core was one of the greatest treasures in existence.","She said that if even a single one appeared on the market, it would shake the entire world.","Martial artists devoted countless years to reaching the next realm.","Unless they possessed extraordinary talent, it was nearly impossible to obtain power that transcended the limits of time.","That was why everyone coveted Inner Cores.","With just one, they could leap straight into the next realm.","***","Title: Got Another Inner Core","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a red Inner Core.)","I slept like a log yesterday because I was sick.","Woke up, cleaned myself up, and started preparing today’s fish. Then this popped out.","Another Inner Core? Should I just put it up for auction?","Heavenly Demon: Have you awakened? You hadn’t posted for quite some time yesterday, so I was worried.","Wild Grylls: The moment I finished memorizing the cultivation verse, I blacked out and fell asleep. Is that normal?","Heavenly Demon: That is the first time I have heard such a thing. If I had to guess, your body was unable to withstand the internal energy and instinctively protected itself.","Wild Grylls: Well, my body’s completely fine now, so I guess everything worked out.","Heavenly Demon: If you say you are well, then I shall believe you. What do you intend to do with that Inner Core?","How much do you want for it?","Gimme gimme gimme gimme gimme.","How do we even know it’s real? I’ll eat it and confirm it.","Heavenly Demon: You treat an Inner Core so casually. Have you truly reached such a lofty realm?","SwordMaster: Yep.","Heavenly Demon: ...You’re so confident that I have nothing more to say.","SwordMaster refused it because he didn’t want to become healthy.","Then what about everyone else?","I waited for the others to reply.","That was the problem.","Who should I give this Inner Core to?","Ideally, I wanted to give it to one of the familiar regulars.","But even that wasn’t easy.","Wild Grylls: I should prioritize the people who’ve helped me.","SwordMaster: I’m fine.","Wild Grylls: Except you, SwordMaster.","SwordMaster: ?","Wild Grylls: Just kidding lol. So... do you want it?","SwordMaster: I don’t want to get healthier. The Mandrake can go to someone else, but an Inner Core isn’t something I can pass along, so don’t bother.","Wild Grylls: The regulars that come to mind are Passing Dwarf, Starlight Princess, Princess Chaenggu, Praisethesun, and Allfather.","Starlight Princess: I’ve already received so much from you... I think someone else should have it.","Starlight Princess was the first to comment.","She wasn’t as active as the Heavenly Demon, but she was one of the regulars who consistently left comments.","After reading that she didn’t need the Inner Core, I replied.","Wild Grylls: Are you sure? Don’t you want to improve your health even more?","Starlight Princess: I’m already more than satisfied. Taking care of my body is more important than increasing my mana.","Wild Grylls: Taking care of your body?","Starlight Princess: Yes. I started working out yesterday. It’s something I’ve never really been able to do before, and I think I’m going to get completely hooked.","She’d wanted to name Wonmo \"Gym Newbie,\" and now it looked like she was turning into a gym fanatic herself.","She’d said she’d spent most of her life confined to a bed, so it made sense she’d be eager to exercise.","Anyway, after Starlight Princess declined, I waited for the others.","Princess Chaenggu: I’m not really interested either. It’s awkward to sell, and it’s awkward to give to someone else.","Wild Grylls: You’re not going to use it yourself?","Princess Chaenggu: I don’t really need it. If anything, I’d rather give it to the Chaeyu players.","You might actually get arrested if you do that.","Wouldn’t an Inner Core count as performance-enhancing drugs?","Not exactly. But if someone suddenly experiences a huge jump in mana, they’ll probably be investigated.","But aren’t Inner Cores legal?","Princess Chaenggu: They’re legal, but it wouldn’t be ethically right. Besides, what good is more mana? Using mana is prohibited in sports.","She’s right. More mana isn’t automatically a good thing.","Haven’t there been athletes who awakened and then went into a terrible slump?","Why would getting stronger make them worse?","Because it throws off their body’s balance. Some athletes have even been disqualified after unconsciously using mana during competitions.","Wild Grylls: Then... could you at least give me some clothes?","Princess Chaenggu: I don’t really have a use for it anyway. Sorry. I’ll just give you the clothes.","Wild Grylls: Do you happen to have any long pants...?","Princess Chaenggu: Not right now, but I can get some if you want. Do you want something made from uniform fabric?","Wild Grylls: Yeah. Then let’s trade for that.","Princess Chaenggu: Just cheering for Chaeyu is enough.","Wild Grylls: Go, Chaeyu! Wishing you the championship!","Princess Chaenggu: Perfect! Haha.","Chaeyu winning? LOL.","King Leor: LMAO.","King Leor: Wild Grylls, do you even know what place Chaeyu is in right now?","Wild Grylls: What place?","Princess Chaenggu: Be quiet before I come over there and beat you up.","King Leor: Ooooh, scary. Anyway, what place is Chaeyu in? Eighth!","Wild Grylls: That’s a bit low. How many matches are left?","Princess Chaenggu: Five. It’s okay, though. We probably won’t make the Champions League, but we’ll at least qualify for the Master Cup.","King Leor: Talk after you actually make the Champions League lol.","There they went again.","Those two argued surprisingly often.","King Leor especially seemed to pick a fight every time Princess Chaenggu showed up.","Personally, I didn’t like it.","She’d helped me before, after all.","Allfather: I’d rather receive another rare creature than the Inner Core.","Praisethesun: Just auction it off. And don’t think about squeezing money out of me.","Wild Grylls: I wasn’t planning to...","Praisethesun: Relax, I’m joking. I’m not interested anyway. The mature Mandrake you gave me before is more than enough.","Wild Grylls: Got it. So you really don’t need it, Princess Chaenggu?","Princess Chaenggu: Nope. I can’t give it to the players anyway.","Wild Grylls: Understood. Go, Chaenggu!","Princess Chaenggu: Thank you. Haha.","King Leor: Cheer for Leor too!","Wild Grylls: I’m not the type to play both sides. Haha.","Princess Chaenggu: I like you even more now. I’ll go find those pants as soon as I can.","Since Princess Chaenggu also turned it down, I moved on to the others.","Allfather: As I mentioned before, my body isn’t capable of making use of an Inner Core. Please give it to someone else.","Wild Grylls: Understood.","Both Allfather and Praisethesun refused.","They were the type who only asked for things they truly needed.","That left only Passing Dwarf.","Passing Dwarf: Just give me more Mandrakes. I wanna brew more liquor.","Wild Grylls: Yeah... Asking you was my mistake. Almost finished making the barricades?","Passing Dwarf: We’ll trade at lunch. If you’re short, let me know.","Wild Grylls: You don’t want the Inner Core as payment?","Passing Dwarf: I said bring me booze.","Wild Grylls: ;_;","The dwarf was hopeless.","Maybe it was because he was a dwarf, but he absolutely loved alcohol.","In the end, every regular I knew turned it down.","The Heavenly Demon said she didn’t need another one since I’d already given her one before.","Apparently she’d already received too much from me.","Whatever.","I didn’t think about it for long.","I listed the Inner Core in the auction house.","The fish were more important than the Inner Core right now.","I gave the head and innards to Wonmo, then cleaned the fish thoroughly like I had yesterday.","Today the hose wasn’t clogged, and water poured out freely.","It did taste good.","I’d eat a hearty breakfast, then use that energy to reinforce my base.","At lunchtime, I’d install the barricades the dwarf had given me.","Sizzle—","The fish browned nicely in the cast-iron pan I’d bought from the auction house.","I’d removed all the scales and seasoned it with salt.","I also cut the meat into bite-sized pieces.","Eating it whole yesterday had been a pain.","\"Here, Wonmo. Eat up.\"","I didn’t keep it all to myself.","I picked up a few pieces of the freshly cooked fish with my chopsticks and handed them to Wonmo.","I didn’t just shove the whole pan in front of him.","Being Korean, chopsticks felt far more natural than a fork.","\"Kyuu!\"","Wonmo’s eyes sparkled as he eagerly devoured the fish.","Considering his size, this was nowhere near enough.","For a human, it would’ve barely counted as an appetizer.","I’d give him some meat later.","\"Want some too?\"","I held out a piece of the well-cooked fish toward the Swift Sloth.","I knew it was a herbivore...","But maybe it’d still be interested.","Nod.","The Swift Sloth slowly nodded and accepted.","I thought it only ate plants, but apparently not.","Then again, it had originally tried to steal the fish, so it wasn’t entirely surprising.","I picked up a well-cooked piece of fish with my chopsticks and held it near its mouth.","Slowly... ever so slowly...","\"Could you eat a little faster?\"","How could even opening its mouth be that slow?","And yet this same creature had threatened me at the fastest speed imaginable.","No matter how hard I tried, I simply couldn’t understand it.","Now that I’d given both of them some fish, all that remained was filling my own stomach.","\"...\"","After dividing it evenly, there was much less left than yesterday.","But that was fine.","Yesterday, while I had been feasting alone, the two of them had stared at me.","Their gazes seemed to say, You’re really eating all that delicious food by yourself?","It had made me feel guilty.","There’s plenty anyway.","The fish was so large that I had to wrap both arms around it.","Giving away a few pieces wasn’t going to leave me short.","Maybe yesterday’s fever had actually been caused by overeating.","Though, as the Heavenly Demon had said, it was probably because too much energy had surged into me at once.","\"Delicious.\"","After finishing the fish, my stomach felt comfortably full.","Instead of a toothpick, I used a fish bone to remove the bits of food stuck between my teeth.","Not a single part went to waste.","Disposing of the remains was a little troublesome, but all I had to do was bury them.","Time to get moving.","I couldn’t afford to relax too much.","I wasn’t planning to live here forever. It would be a problem if I became lazy already.","But first, I should circulate the cultivation method.","Since I’d eaten a hearty breakfast, I used the internal-energy cultivation method to refine my mana.","I also remembered to recite the verse the Heavenly Demon had taught me yesterday.","The poetic language made it difficult to understand, but imagining the imagery made it somewhat easier.","If the first verse is already this bad, how difficult will the second one be?","Surely all of them together wouldn’t form a poem as long and complicated as Gwandong Byeolgok .","If they did, even memorizing it would be an ordeal.","Still, I’ll have to learn it.","I focused while guiding the mana inside my body with the cultivation method.","It might have been my imagination, but the energy felt stronger and more domineering than yesterday.","Rather than a calm river, it felt like waves rushing violently forward.","That wasn’t necessarily a bad thing.","Thanks to that powerful force, the circulation speed had increased dramatically.","\"...\"","After completing the entire circulation, I slowly opened my eyes.","The first thing I saw was the Swift Sloth’s drowsy face directly in front of me.","\"Whoa! You scared me!\"","\"...\"","\"Seriously... Don’t sneak up on people like that.\"","I nearly had a heart attack.","I let out a sigh.","It was good that it hadn’t disturbed me, but anyone would be startled to find it sitting right in front of them.","Wonmo is... already asleep.","Our adorable ball of fur was deep into his afternoon nap.","Since he was still a baby, it seemed all he knew how to do was eat, sleep, and poop.","Fortunately, he did the last one outside the cave, so it wasn’t a problem.","Crawl... crawl...","When I prepared to move, the Swift Sloth climbed onto my back.","I was gradually becoming used to it, but then I suddenly remembered its hygiene.","This thing hasn’t taken a bath, has it?","I needed to heat some bathwater immediately.","Otherwise, it might make me sick.","Allfather had said that while it didn’t have any ticks, various other insects lived in its fur.","He had even said there was a high chance that mold was growing on it.","It needed to be scrubbed clean just as thoroughly as Wonmo.","I’ve finished eating the fish, and the timing is perfect.","I immediately cleaned the iron tub and filled it with water.","Now all I had to do was wait for it to heat up.","I could worry about adjusting the temperature later.","While waiting, I used a shovel to dig out the places where I intended to install the barricades.","I planned to surround the cave entrance with barricades in a square formation.","Thud! Thud!","Why is this so easy to dig?","I’d noticed it while logging, but shoveling didn’t feel exhausting at all.","Normally, even the shovel itself should have felt somewhat heavy, but I couldn’t feel its weight.","This had to be thanks to the internal-energy cultivation method.","Manual labor would be easy from now on.","\"...I’m already finished?\"","The problem was that it had become too easy.","Less than thirty minutes had passed, yet the groundwork was already complete.","All I had to do was place the barricades inside the neatly dug trenches and fill them back in with soil.","A few trees were in the way, but I could gradually cut those down.","Bang! Bang! Crack!","Even the logging was finished within thirty minutes.","It was unbelievably fast.","Before, it had felt like I was chopping trees.","Now it was closer to smashing them apart.","Once I destroyed the center, the trees lost their balance and easily toppled over.","All I had to do was break the middle and push them with my foot.","I was more bewildered than pleased by how suddenly I’d become stronger.","Well, there’s no point complaining about something good.","I scratched my head while looking at the devastated trees, then shrugged.","I listed all but one of the felled trees in the auction house.","The remaining one would be used as firewood.","Thinking about firewood reminded me of the bathwater I had heated earlier.","I worried that it might be boiling, but fortunately, only gentle steam was rising from it.","\"All right. It’s your turn to wash.\"","Crawl... crawl...","Perhaps it understood me, because the Swift Sloth climbed down from my back.","At first, I thought it was going to enter the bath on its own.","But instead, it headed into the cave.","It seemed to be running away because it didn’t want a bath.","Despite being so ridiculously slow.","\"Hey. Not that way. Come over here.\"","\"...\"","In the end, I picked it up myself and tried to place it inside the iron tub.","No.","More precisely, I attempted to place it inside.","Grip!","Before I could, it clung tightly to my arm as though refusing to let go.","It was even trembling.","It seemed frightened.","That made even less sense, considering it could see an arrow coming and snatch it out of the air.","\"...Hey.\"","\"Do you hate baths?\"","There was no response.","It couldn’t speak in the first place.","But the fact that it refused to budge made its feelings perfectly clear.","Even so, I couldn’t simply give up on hygiene.","I tried forcing the Swift Sloth into the tub.","Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh!","Each time, it darted across different parts of my body with lightning-fast movements.","It slipped around me as though my body were a tree.","And it did so at an astonishing speed, as if entering the tub would kill it.","\"Ah, seriously! Do whatever you want! I’ll take the bath myself!\"","\"...\"","I finally gave up.","Only after hearing my declaration of surrender did the Swift Sloth begin moving slowly again.","\"...Did you really think I’d say that and mean it?\"","\"?!\"","It was a fake-out, you bastard.","I seized the Swift Sloth’s arm while its guard was down.","Now that I’d restrained one arm, it would have no choice but to enter quietly.","Sure, it still had one arm free, but there was no way it could do anything with just that.","Splash!","I had been completely mistaken.","The Swift Sloth swung its remaining arm toward the iron tub.","The tub was cleanly sliced into several pieces, spilling the warm water everywhere.","It wasn’t that it couldn’t do anything.","It absolutely could.","In the silence that followed, I stared at the Swift Sloth.","It stared back at me.","Its expression seemed to say:","—What exactly do you think you can do about it?","Another defeat for me today."]},{"title":"Chapter 34","paragraphs":["Assistant Moderator (1)","After suffering yet another defeat at the hands of the Swift Sloth, I finished cleaning up the mess.","Losing the iron tub was a shame, but they were everywhere in the auction house, so replacing it wouldn’t be difficult.","Besides, I had sold the owlbear’s corpse and the logs, so my finances were in fairly good shape.","I’d just listed the Inner Core as well, so my wallet would probably be even fuller tomorrow.","I wonder how much the Inner Core will sell for.","The Heavenly Demon had said that it was difficult to put a price on one.","That might actually cause people to underestimate its value.","After all, an Inner Core was an incredibly rare elixir.","People regularly posted about being scammed in the auction house, so naturally, buyers would be even more suspicious of an Inner Core.","It was fortunate that I’d built up some credibility by now. Otherwise, I couldn’t have complained if people accused me of being a scammer.","It’s not like I personally tested the Inner Core’s effects.","The benefits I’d experienced had come from eating the fish, not the Inner Core itself.","Even that wasn’t completely certain.","I had only just taken my first step into the worlds of mana and internal energy.","The Heavenly Demon and several other regulars possessed expertise, but none of them were here beside me.","Something even they didn’t understand was happening inside my body, so it was difficult to draw a definite conclusion.","Still, I’m certain that it had some effect.","In less than a single day, my strength and stamina had increased dramatically.","Even simple physical labor like logging and digging had become effortless.","I didn’t know the exact reason, but I had undoubtedly grown stronger through that process.","That much, I could guarantee.","I still have some time. Should I explore the surrounding area?","The repairs to my base were complete.","All that remained was receiving the barricades from the dwarf.","Before then, I planned to decide which area to explore next.","I entered the cave.","Inside, Wonmo was sleeping soundly.","How could even his sleeping form be so adorable and lovable?","I had to take a picture and upload it.","***","Title: A Round Ball of Fur","Wild Grylls","(Photo of Wonmo sleeping while curled into a ball.)","(Video of Wonmo sleeping peacefully.)","Seriously, every time I look at him, I feel completely at peace.","How can something be this cute?","Wow. He really is adorable.","I’ll admit he’s cute if you still say that after he grows up lol.","Don’t animals grow really quickly?","Most of them are probably fully grown within a year.","Wild Grylls: Hey, you bastards. Are you telling me to stay here for an entire year?","This is the Forest of Four Seasons. Can you even escape? Lol.","Wild Grylls: I have to try. I’m planning to start exploring now.","You’re going to leave Wonmo here alone? What if something attacks him?","That was a good point.","It would be dangerous to leave Wonmo alone while I explored.","Ideally, I wanted to take him with me, but Wonmo was weaker than I was.","Even the last time I’d gone to the river, the Swift Sloth had suddenly appeared.","It had been fine because I’d returned quickly, and the Swift Sloth wasn’t actually hostile.","Should I take Wonmo with me?","There was another option.","I could leave the Swift Sloth in the cave.","Honestly, that was probably the best solution.","The downside was that I would be putting myself in greater danger.","The Swift Sloth had saved me when the chameleon viper nearly got me last time.","Its overwhelming visual acuity and agility would also make it incredibly useful during exploration.","This is difficult.","Should I leave Wonmo alone and go exploring?","Or should I leave the Swift Sloth here with him?","After thinking about it for some time, I spoke to the creature hanging from my back.","\"Swiftie.\"","The Swift Sloth slowly tilted its head at my call.","\"You’ll have to guard the cave.\"","\"If you protect it until I return, I’ll give you a fasting pill.\"","Upon hearing that, the Swift Sloth slowly climbed down from my back.","It definitely understood what I was saying.","It was truly fascinating.","There was absolutely nothing strange about me, so the Swift Sloth had to be the unusual one.","Wonmo could also understand me, but I decided not to think about that.","Questions and their answers were luxuries for times when one had room to spare.","When survival was the priority, they were nothing more than meaningless distractions.","\"When Wonmo wakes up, tell him where I went. Understood?\"","Nod, nod.","The Swift Sloth nodded to show that it accepted my request.","Now that I had assigned him a reliable bodyguard, all that remained was preparing for the expedition.","As always, I brought the Heavenly Demon’s sword and the golden shield.","I also wore clean clothes.","They were the ones I’d washed when I bathed Wonmo earlier.","Princess Chaenggu said she’d give me long clothes later, right?","I didn’t know how long that would take, but it probably wouldn’t be long.","She had been willing to give me a high-quality uniform without hesitation, after all.","I also packed an elixir and some fasting pills in case of an emergency.","Now all that remained was setting out.","Should I try going this way today?","I had been gradually exploring in all four directions around the cave.","The river where the Golden Poison Frog appeared was to the northeast, while the mature Mandrake habitat was to the northwest.","Of course, I didn’t have a compass, so I couldn’t be certain those directions were accurate.","They were based entirely on my sense of direction.","This time, I planned to travel toward what I believed was west.","I should return before lunch.","After exploring, I planned to receive the barricades from Passing Dwarf and reinforce the base.","In less than a week, my overall physical abilities had improved dramatically.","Manual labor was no longer particularly difficult.","Exploration would probably become my main daily activity before long.","\"I’m heading out. Guard the house properly.\"","\"...\"","As I left the cave, the Swift Sloth slowly waved its hand at me.","It was clearly telling me to have a safe trip.","No matter how I looked at it, it seemed more like a person than an animal.","Chirp, chirp— Chirp, chirp—","I headed in a completely new direction, away from both the river and the Mandrake habitat.","The deafening sounds of insects pierced my ears and heightened my tension.","To avoid getting lost, I marked the path at regular intervals.","I can’t trust everything I see.","The chameleon viper had taught me that I could never let my guard down.","From time to time, I struck tree trunks with the back of my blade or swept aside bushes.","I moved as cautiously as possible.","It might slow my progress, but it was safer.","Even though I had an elixir, I needed to conserve it.","\"Hm?\"","I had been advancing little by little when something on the ground caught my eye.","It was completely black, so at first I thought it was charcoal.","But judging by the flies swarming around it, it definitely wasn’t.","It’s poop.","Animal droppings.","I had no idea what kind of animal had left them.","In the civilized world, people would simply dismiss feces as something filthy.","But things were completely different in the wild.","Animals often used their droppings to mark their territory.","It was essentially a warning:","This is my territory. Enter, and you’ll die.","The flies make it look fairly old. Could it belong to the owlbear?","I wasn’t an expert, so I couldn’t tell what animal it came from.","For now, I guessed it belonged to the owlbear that had been sent to America.","Wonmo’s droppings were different in size, but their overall appearance was similar.","Still, asking the Gallery was the best option.","I should add a content warning, right?","I needed to be careful, or I might get banned.","Without lowering my guard, I wrote a post on the Gallery.","***","Title: Mildly Graphic—Whose Is This?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of animal droppings.)","Found this while exploring today.","Does anyone know what animal left it?","If it’s from the owlbear, I’ll keep exploring. If it belongs to something else, I’ll reconsider.","Ugh, that’s fucking disgusting.","Damn, it really left a massive pile lol.","Mix some rice into that and you’ve got yourself a full meal lol.","Fuck this. I’m blocking you. That’s disgusting.","Wild Grylls: Enough nonsense. Does it belong to an owlbear or not?","Looks like it. Aren’t owlbears the only ones that leave poop that black?","Don’t normal bears also leave droppings like that?","Allfather: It is indeed owlbear excrement. Judging from its size, I believe it came from the specimen you killed previously.","As expected of Fatheremon.","He was the only intelligent person among this crowd of idiots.","Since it was Allfather saying it, I could trust the answer.","I thanked him and continued walking.","Just in case, I deleted the post afterward.","The Moderator might see it and ban me.","Maybe it would have been fine if he were flexible, but he had a tendency to follow the rules rather strictly.","It was better to be safe.","I’m surprised the Heavenly Demon didn’t leave a comment.","The Heavenly Demon probably disliked filthy things too.","Understandable.","In any case, now that the droppings had been confirmed to belong to the owlbear, it should be safe to continue exploring.","Oh. Are those wild raspberries?","While exploring, I discovered some delicious-looking berries.","They were red and plump, unmistakably resembling wild raspberries.","But this was the Forest of Four Seasons—a demonic hell where even ordinary plants could be poisonous.","Even before coming here, I had been highly susceptible to rashes from poisonous plants, so I decided to ask the Gallery before gathering them.","I wanted to avoid dropping dead after thoughtlessly eating something.","***","Title: Is This Safe to Eat?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of berries resembling wild raspberries.)","They look delicious. Can I eat them?","Aren’t those wild raspberries?","Do wild raspberries even grow in this forest?","Aren’t raspberries usually round? Why are those so long?","Try one. Eat it and tell us how it tastes.","Wild Grylls: I don’t trust anything you bastards say.","Then why did you ask?","Wild Grylls: Give me a proper explanation.","Allfather: Do not eat them. They are jack-in-the-pulpit berries, which are sometimes used for suicide. They contain a deadly poison.","Wild Grylls: Thank you. ;;","Allfather: Wild raspberries are round, so they should be fairly easy to distinguish.","Damn, that was close lol.","What a shame.","You seriously deserve to get banned.","I stared at the raspberry-like berries before crushing them underfoot.","It would serve as a directional marker.","A sign showing that I had already passed through this path.","Every little marker mattered.","Should I buy some paint?","That wasn’t a bad idea.","It would be useful when I traveled farther away like this.","I continued making my way through the forest, pushing aside vegetation and weaving between the trees.","I never forgot to be careful not to lose my way.","I wandered around for some time before finally encountering something that could serve as a proper landmark.","\"Wow. That’s enormous.\"","I looked up in amazement.","The sight naturally made my jaw drop.","A massive mushroom stood directly in front of me.","It was no ordinary mushroom.","Even its height far exceeded mine.","Calling it gigantic didn’t seem sufficient.","It was a colossal mushroom.","What the hell was this thing?","It looks like a matsutake mushroom, though.","I could probably use this mushroom as a landmark from now on.","I could explore the surrounding area using it as a reference point.","There’s quite a lot of open space around it. Why?","Before approaching the mushroom, I examined the surroundings.","No matter how large it was, the fact that it stood completely alone was suspicious.","Perhaps it had absorbed the nutrients meant for all the nearby plants.","I first needed to identify it, so I uploaded a post to the Gallery.","Wow. It’s as big as my dick.","Wanna see?","You fucking lunatic.","Allfather: You should be careful around that mushroom. It may be a Mushroom Man.","Wild Grylls: A Mushroom Man?","Allfather: Yes. It is a creature formed from the fusion of a monster and a mushroom. They do not normally grow anywhere near that large, but I suppose this is the Forest of Four Seasons.","Wild Grylls: Is it strong?","Allfather: Honestly, not particularly. However, it scatters spores, so you will need fire.","***","Title: Found a Fucking Huge Mushroom","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the colossal mushroom.)","It’s taller than me. You can estimate its size by comparing it to the trees beside it.","Does anyone know what this thing is?","Fire, huh?","I nodded.","I had the ignition stone the Heavenly Demon had given me, but there was no reason to provoke it unnecessarily.","It wasn’t like I planned to eat it.","There was no need to waste my strength.","I was about to circle around the mushroom when—","\"Hm?\"","I noticed a cave behind it.","The mushroom completely blocked the cave entrance, making it impossible to enter.","I suddenly became curious about what might be inside.","It’s like some kind of dungeon gatekeeper.","Curiosity aside, I valued my life.","Having already survived several life-threatening situations, I was able to abandon the idea without hesitation.","Rrrrrumble!","But the world refused to leave me alone.","I was startled by the sudden vibration, but quickly realized where it was coming from.","The colossal mushroom was shaking violently, as though it were about to rip itself out of the ground.","Ah, shit.","This always happened.","I slowly backed away.","I didn’t have fire prepared, but I planned to gauge how strong it was before fleeing.","Even if I fought it, the only reward would be getting to see the inside of that cave.","Crack! Craaack!","The earth split apart, revealing the mushroom’s true form.","Allfather had described the body shape of a Mushroom Man like this:","Extremely short limbs that looked disproportionately tiny compared to its bloated body.","He had said that even if it grew larger, its proportions should remain roughly the same.","\"Kuuk.\"","He was completely wrong.","Its arms and legs were long, almost like a human’s.","Long limbs alone would have been manageable.","But they were also packed with bulging muscles like those of a bodybuilder.","Its body was long and mushroom-like, while its limbs resembled those of a muscular human.","It was bizarre beyond words.","No, bizarre wasn’t enough.","It was grotesque.","The Mushroom Man kicked off the ground and closed the distance between us in an instant.","It seemed to take only one step, yet suddenly it was right in front of my face.","That much was manageable.","It wasn’t particularly fast.","I could see it move and react.","It was far slower than the Swift Sloth.","Let’s try blocking one hit.","The Mushroom Man’s right fist shot toward my abdomen.","I raised the golden shield.","Considering the shield’s performance and my recently increased strength, I should have been able to withstand it.","\"Kuooooh!\"","The Mushroom Man let out a powerful roar.","BOOOOM!","\"Guh?!\"","A tremendous impact struck the shield, sending my body flying backward.","***","Wow. Of all the things I’ve experienced...","After fleeing back to the cave, I lamented inwardly and stared at the front of the golden shield.","A clear fist-shaped dent had been left in it.","I had only escaped unharmed because of the shield.","Without it, that single punch would have killed me.","Afterward, I had fled without even looking back.","Fortunately, the Mushroom Man didn’t pursue me.","Why the hell does a Mushroom Man know the One-Inch Punch?","Its muscular limbs had given me some idea of what to expect, but I hadn’t imagined it would be that powerful.","Had I taken the punch directly, it would have punched straight through my stomach.","Either that, or everything inside me would have come bursting out of my mouth.","I sighed in relief and uploaded another post to the Gallery.","***","Title: Got Hit by a Mushroom Man’s One-Inch Punch","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the shield with a distinct fist-shaped dent.)","That bastard used a One-Inch Punch on me and did this to my shield.","Thank God I had it, or I would’ve been completely fucked. ;;","Damn. Look how clear that dent is. If you’d taken that barehanded, it would’ve punched through your stomach.","A Mushroom Man is that strong? What the hell did it look like?","Wild Grylls: Its limbs were seriously muscular. They were completely jacked.","I can’t picture it. Upload a photo.","Wild Grylls: (Photo of the muscular Mushroom Man.)","LMAOOOOO, what the hell is that?!","Holy shit lol. Its body is better than mine.","That thing looks fucking strong lol.","Can that truly be called a Mushroom Man?","Praisethesun: What the hell happened to my shield? That thing is seriously high-quality. ;;","Wild Grylls: You mean I would’ve died without it, right? Thank you so much, brother.","Praisethesun: You don’t need to thank me. Still, that’s surprising. What the hell did you fight?","Wild Grylls: A mushroom.","Praisethesun: The world truly is a strange place.","Allfather: Fascinating. Did you notice anything else unusual?","Wild Grylls: No. All I know is that it was ridiculously strong.","Allfather: Hmm... I do not know. I genuinely have no idea. What kind of place is that forest?","While I was organizing my thoughts, one particular comment caught my eye.","Heavenly Demon: What an intriguing tale. A fist powerful enough to dent a shield, even one made of gold... Its strength would not be inferior even when compared to mine.","Even Allfather didn’t know what it was.","The other users could do little more than express their amazement.","Apparently, this was abnormal even by the standards of the people in this world.","That showed just how far outside common sense the Forest of Four Seasons truly was.","Though a sloth that could see a fired arrow and snatch it out of the air was equally absurd.","Why was that thing blocking the entrance to the cave?","The way it stood guard like a guardian deity only made me more curious.","But the Mushroom Man was far too strong.","A direct confrontation was impossible.","I would need to use some kind of trick to get past it.","The Heavenly Demon.","She was normally the regular who replied first to nearly every one of my posts.","The fact that she was late today suggested she had something else to do.","But something else caught my attention even more.","Wild Grylls: Hello, Heavenly Demon. But... you are the Heavenly Demon, right?","Heavenly Demon: If you are asking whether this is indeed me, then yes. Why do you ask?","Huh? Why did her name suddenly turn blue?","Why the hell is she blue now?","Wait. Why did she suddenly turn blue?","Users who noticed it before I did flooded the post with comments.","Most of them were confused.","Naturally so.","Beside the Heavenly Demon’s username was a blue badge that had never been there before.","Heavenly Demon: Ah. I nearly forgot. From now on, you may address me as the Assistant Moderator.","The Heavenly Demon had returned as an Assistant Moderator."]},{"title":"Chapter 35","paragraphs":["Assistant Moderator (2)","In the Gallery, the term armband usually referred to either the Moderator or an Assistant Moderator.","They were administrators granted the authority to manage the Gallery.","That made it sound as though they were expected to work hard at managing it, but that wasn’t actually true.","It was perfectly acceptable for the Moderator to manage the Gallery carelessly.","Everyone had their own circumstances, after all.","In such cases, the Moderator could appoint an assistant manager—an Assistant Moderator—and share some of their authority.","***","Title: What’s Good About Being an Assistant Moderator?","Genuinely asking.","You can delete Gallery posts and ban users.","And?","That’s it lol.","Then why would anyone become one?","Exactly. That’s why nobody does.","If you manage the Gallery like shit, you can get fired too lol.","Isn’t that also true for the Moderator?","The Moderator is fine as long as they occasionally log in. Assistant Moderators don’t even get that privilege lol.","That’s basically how serfdom started lol.","Fuck, talking about group projects reminds me of the academy. Being a commoner was miserable.","These days, nobles are practically forced to become group leaders. Apparently, nobles are supposed to set an example lol.","Society has finally improved.","The problem was that the rewards were pitiful compared to the authority granted.","It was practically unpaid volunteer work.","That was why users tried their hardest to avoid being appointed as an Assistant Moderator.","Even when they disliked the Moderator, a single question—","Do you want to turn blue?","—was enough to silence them.","***","Title: This Moderator Really Doesn’t Appoint Any Assistants","Isn’t managing everything alone exhausting?","Yeah, that’s why everyone keeps telling them to appoint an Assistant Moderator—as long as it isn’t them lol.","Infinite selfishness at its finest lol.","Would you want to be an Assistant Moderator?","I’d do it if they paid me lol.","Basically, Assistant Moderator equals group-project leader. Understand now?","An Assistant Moderator was a necessary position that nobody wanted for themselves but desperately wanted someone else to take.","The authority to delete Gallery posts and ban users?","Even that wasn’t much.","No reward came with doing the job well.","***","Title: This Reminds Me of the Old Days","Remember when the Moderator and Assistant Moderator met up in real life to fight and both died?","Oh, I remember that lol. It was fucking hilarious.","The surprising part was that one of them was a noble lol.","Why did they fight?","I think the Assistant Moderator demanded the Moderator’s armband. Said they did all the work while the Moderator did nothing.","Fair reason.","So the Moderator said they’d hand it over if the Assistant Moderator won the fight lol.","And then they both died lol.","***","Title: What Authority Does the Moderator Have?","Everything an Assistant Moderator has, but better. They can also make trades whenever they want. I think they can have private one-on-one conversations too.","Can’t they track users’ locations as well?","Yeah. Someone once threatened to attack the Emperor, and the Moderator revealed their location so they could be executed. I think the Moderator even received a reward.","That’s a dangerously powerful ability.","That’s why one Moderator stalked some noble lady, had his eyes gouged out, and got thrown in prison lol.","It really was dangerous lol.","The Moderator’s authority, on the other hand, was extremely powerful.","They weren’t restricted by the rule preventing another trade for twenty-four hours after completing one, and they could interfere with various systems.","As a result, the atmosphere and direction of the Gallery largely depended on whoever held the Moderator position at the time.","The current Moderator, Don’t Abandon the Hero , was somewhat scatterbrained but principled and generally righteous.","To put it less kindly, he was stubborn and old-fashioned.","Fortunately, he possessed at least a little flexibility.","For some reason, however, he would occasionally disappear for long periods, causing the Gallery to descend into chaos.","An Assistant Moderator was needed precisely for situations like that, yet he had never appointed one.","***","Title: Why Won’t the Moderator Give Anyone an Armband?","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I can handle all the difficult work myself! Assistant Moderators don’t even get paid!","Doesn’t the Moderator also work for free?","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I receive transaction fees! I’m using them to improve the Gallery!","What exactly does \"improving the Gallery\" mean?","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I should be able to add minigames soon!","Moderators really do have all kinds of interesting abilities. So you’re still not appointing an Assistant Moderator?","Don’t Abandon the Hero: You’re right above me at the moment!","I’m not even a registered user lol.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I can use the transaction fees to purchase the authority to appoint someone by force!","I’m sorryI’m sorryI’m sorryI’m sorryI’m sorry.","LMAOOOOOO.","***","Title: How Does Someone Become the Moderator?","If the Moderator appoints Assistant Moderators, then who appoints the Moderator?","According to previous Moderators, it just happened one day. They suddenly received a notice saying they’d become the manager of the Continental Integrated Gallery.","So it’s completely random?","Yeah.","Then how does someone else become Moderator?","When the current Moderator doesn’t access the Gallery for a long time. Or when they die.","I’m pretty sure getting imprisoned also strips you of the armband.","One needed either an extraordinarily strong mentality or an absurd amount of free time and boredom.","As it happened, someone who satisfied those conditions had appeared.","There had always been interest in the armband, but nobody clearly understood how it worked.","Even the current Moderator had admitted that he didn’t fully understand the Gallery’s systems, which said everything.","Most authority in the Gallery was concentrated in the Moderator’s hands, while Assistant Moderators were practically slaves.","Who would willingly become both the leader of a group project and a serf under a feudal system?","It was a thankless position where doing well earned nothing and doing poorly invited endless abuse.","Anyone who genuinely wanted the role had to be one of two things.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: Are you really certain?! I can handle all the difficult work alone!","Heavenly Demon: This Queen has already decided. However, only if you accept my condition. Are you not busy yourself? You do not seem to have visited the Gallery often lately.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I’ve shaken off my pursuers, so I’m fine for now! And if I accept that condition, everyone else will criticize you!","Heavenly Demon: Do not worry. This Queen does not care.","It was a conversation between the Moderator, Don’t Abandon the Hero, and the Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol.","Yu Sowol waited patiently for the Moderator to continue.","On the surface, it looked like they were negotiating a trade.","In reality, it was something similar.","The only difference was that this was not a transaction chat window, but a private one-on-one conversation.","The Moderator possessed every restricted authority.","Therefore, if the Moderator initiated the request, a private conversation became possible.","To make that happen, the Heavenly Demon had repeatedly sent him trade requests.","She had done it so often that even the Moderator could no longer ignore her.","Heavenly Demon: Rather than hiding it, I intend to reveal it openly. It is better to endure the criticism sooner rather than later.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I see! I understand what you mean!","Heavenly Demon: Then, will you grant me the armband?","If she slowly investigated this authority, she was certain to find some kind of opening.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: Very well! I’ll give you the armband! However, if you abuse your power, I will revoke it immediately!","Heavenly Demon: Do not concern yourself. This Queen shall govern with great tolerance. Besides, are private conversations not visible to you as well?","Yu Sowol waited in anticipation.","Would the Moderator truly grant her the armband?","She had two goals.","The first was to have private one-on-one conversations with Grylls.","Every time she left a comment, some fly-like wench named SwordMaster would swarm in, so she had decided that speaking privately would be better.","Her second goal was to understand the Gallery’s structure more clearly.","An Assistant Moderator possessed less authority than the Moderator, but it still had some privileges.","Every private conversation in the Gallery was visible to the Moderator.","Normally, this referred to trade conversations between registered users, but the Heavenly Demon was about to receive administrative authority.","That meant the profound cultivation verses of the Heavenly Demon Divine Art might also be exposed to the Moderator.","However, she wasn’t particularly worried about that.","The Moderator has already seen them once.","The Moderator even possessed the privilege of reading private posts.","There were no secrets one could hide from the Moderator.","In that case, it was better to speak openly through private conversations instead.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: That’s right! It’s unavoidable, even if only to prevent crimes! Is that a problem?!","Heavenly Demon: It matters not. In exchange, I shall grant you the honor of contemplating the profound meaning of the Heavenly Demon Divine Art.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I’m fine! I already have a blessing from the Goddess!","When their conversation ended, a blue badge appeared beside the Heavenly Demon’s username.","The moment she received it, she checked Grylls’s post first.","Something seemed to have happened while she was persuading the Moderator.","The Heavenly Demon smiled in anticipation and left a comment.","Besides, nobody would believe her anyway.","Yu Sowol knew exactly how people regarded her in the Gallery.","She was a famous registered user who posted nonsense or shitposts every single day.","The important part was that those seemingly meaningless posts actually contained the enlightenment of the Heavenly Demon.","Nobody believed that.","The Moderator was no exception.","Yu Sowol had already taken that into account.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I look forward to working with you, Assistant Moderator!","Heavenly Demon: Likewise.","Heavenly Demon: Ah. I nearly forgot. From now on, you may address me as the Assistant Moderator.","Why all of a sudden?","What the hell happened?","We’re fucked. They gave the armband to someone with nothing but free time. ;;","EMERGENCYYYYY!","Excellent reactions appeared one after another.","Everyone seemed utterly shocked that Yu Sowol had become an Assistant Moderator.","This feels strangely satisfying.","Yu Sowol’s chin lifted slightly.","Look at them trembling in fear.","Normally, they treated her like some outdated martial-arts old-timer.","But look at them now.","The moment she obtained great power—the blue badge—the Gallery users began quaking in terror.","In reality, the Heavenly Demon Yu Sowol could wipe out entire groups with a single gesture.","Yet receiving this sort of treatment in the Gallery made her strangely happy.","It felt as though she had stepped out of the shell of the Heavenly Demon and obtained power and authority as an ordinary human being.","This was why she couldn’t quit the Gallery.","For Yu Sowol, whose days had once been endlessly dull, it was an enormous source of stimulation.","I should proudly announce my emergence.","In the martial world, it was customary to openly declare one’s name and origin when making an entrance.","The Gallery was no different.","She happily announced her emergence.","However, she restrained her arrogant tone as much as possible.","She might otherwise upset the Moderator.","***","Title: Hear Me, My Subjects","Heavenly Demon","By the grace of the Moderator, this Queen has received the armband.","However, merely possessing the armband does not mean I intend to oppress you like an emperor.","I shall only ban those for justified reasons, so you need not worry.","Ask whatever you wish. For today alone, I shall graciously permit it.","She really got the armband? The world is ending. ;;","Why did the Moderator give it to that old fossil?","Isn’t she going to ban anyone she dislikes?","The Moderator wouldn’t have appointed her if she were like that.","Should we start begging for mercy now?","SwordMaster: Why did you become an Assistant Moderator? I don’t understand.","She could ignore the other comments, but not SwordMaster’s.","Yu Sowol began writing a response, then quietly deleted it.","An amusing idea had occurred to her.","After thinking for a while, she smiled and replied.","Heavenly Demon: You may ponder that question yourself.","SwordMaster: ??? You told us to ask questions. ;;","Heavenly Demon: I said I would answer. I never said I would give you the answer you wanted.","SwordMaster: Are you messing with me right now?","Heavenly Demon: This Queen is entirely serious.","SwordMaster: I already want to impeach you. ;;","That was something she could worry about when the time came.","She possessed time in abundance, like the vast sea.","There was no shortage whatsoever.","Then the Heavenly Demon noticed another comment.","What color are your panties today?","\"Hehe.\"","This was the experience she had been waiting for.","Yu Sowol let out a faint laugh.","Truthfully, she wanted to inflict heavenly punishment—meaning a permanent ban—upon SwordMaster.","That registered user was constantly filling her benefactor’s head with strange ideas.","But she endured it.","With mercy as vast as the heavens, she refrained from delivering divine punishment.","The initiative was now hers anyway.","There was no longer any need to concern herself with SwordMaster.","Unless that woman also receives a blue badge.","The urge to deliver heavenly punishment surged again.","But who was she?","\"Hehe.\"","Yu Sowol forgave her with boundless generosity.","Compared to the others, that comment was relatively mild.","This place truly is overflowing with idiots.","Once again, she realized just how extraordinary the Gallery was.","***","The news that the Heavenly Demon had become an Assistant Moderator spread throughout the entire Gallery.","With the blue badge displayed prominently beside her username, it was impossible not to notice.","To make matters worse, she had even created a post, and the comment section was overflowing.","The problem was that a considerable number of those comments were idiotic.","Questions about the color of her panties were practically mandatory.","That was normal everyday behavior in the Gallery, but the appearance of a new Assistant Moderator seemed to attract even more people than usual.","She must be lonely in her old age.","Judging by all the strange posts she regularly made, that seemed likely.","I’d heard that old people tended to spend their days reminiscing about the past.","Otherwise, there was no explaining how she managed to attract so much attention.","Or maybe she’s starved for attention.","In that case, I should treat her with a little more courtesy from now on."]},{"title":"Chapter 36","paragraphs":["Assistant Moderator (3)","The news that the Heavenly Demon had become an Assistant Moderator spread like wildfire.","She had already been a well-known registered user, so it was only natural that the Gallery would erupt into an uproar.","An Assistant Moderator might be an inferior version of the Moderator, but they were still a manager.","Anyone who broke the rules or angered the Heavenly Demon now faced a high chance of being banned.","The Heavenly Demon probably won’t do that, though.","She had a strong tendency to follow her own path.","No matter what anyone said, she simply continued forward without wavering.","You could call it a mentality of steel.","Or perhaps it was the tolerance that came with old age.","To genuinely anger the Heavenly Demon, someone would probably have to hurl insults too vile to repeat.","And if someone did that, they couldn’t complain about getting banned.","In any case, from my perspective, it was little more than an ordinary incident.","The Heavenly Demon becoming an Assistant Moderator probably wouldn’t change much.","It simply meant that the Gallery had gained another manager.","Since I was acquainted with her, I might receive a few minor conveniences.","Not that I intend to rely on her.","If I depended too heavily on the Heavenly Demon, I would inevitably grow lazy.","I was already receiving plenty of help.","Rather than clinging to her, it was better to become stronger on my own.","Now that she’s an Assistant Moderator, she’ll probably be busy.","Assistant Moderators were essentially volunteers.","Unpaid slaves.","Yet if they neglected their duties, they could lose the position and even get banned.","The Moderator was especially rigid and placed great importance on rules and principles, so she couldn’t afford to be careless.","\"I should focus on my own work.\"","I had escaped from the muscular mushroom, and the Heavenly Demon had become an Assistant Moderator, but I still had things to do.","I needed to receive the barricades from Passing Dwarf and reinforce my shelter.","He had said he would send them around lunchtime, so the trade request should arrive soon.","After I finish installing the barricades...","Just as I began thinking about what to do afterward—","Passing Dwarf has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?","A trade request arrived from the dwarf.","Apparently, speaking of the devil really did summon him.","I accepted.","Passing Dwarf: You accepted immediately. Guess you’ve got some free time?","Wild Grylls: I was waiting for you.","Passing Dwarf: Ah, sorry. I’m into women. It’s hard being this popular.","Wild Grylls: You lunatic lol. Did you finish the barricades?","Passing Dwarf: I did, but there are a lot of them, and they’re big. Do you have somewhere to store them?","At his question, I looked around.","Perhaps because the Mad Dog pack had once lived here, the area surrounding the cave was surprisingly spacious.","The interior was large as well.","Three enormous beasts had once lived inside it, after all.","If necessary, I could store some of the barricades inside the cave after installing a few outside.","I admired the photos the dwarf sent.","One showed an ordinary wooden defensive wall.","It consisted of sharpened wooden posts placed tightly beside one another.","The other was closer to a barricade.","A wall and a barricade were technically similar, but their shapes were different.","The wall stood vertically, while the barricade leaned at an angle.","It consisted of pointed wooden stakes arranged diagonally and tightly bound together.","Wild Grylls: I have space. About how big are they?","Passing Dwarf: Look at these first.","Passing Dwarf: (Photo of a wooden wall.)","(Second photo of a wooden barricade.)","Passing Dwarf: Which one looks better?","\"Oh?\"","Passing Dwarf: You’re not planning to live there permanently. If you only need something temporary, the spikes are probably better. They’re easier to install too.","Wild Grylls: Those do look better. I dug all those fucking holes for nothing lol.","Passing Dwarf: Just bury them roughly. I’ll make the rest in this style.","Wild Grylls: How long will it take to make more?","Passing Dwarf: What I’ve already sent should provide decent protection. If that’s not enough, make some yourself. They’re easy as long as you know how to tie rope.","Wild Grylls: I’ll think about it. Can you send these now?","Passing Dwarf: Yep.","Passing Dwarf has registered the trade items.","Passing Dwarf: Take them.","Wild Grylls: Is there anything you need?","Passing Dwarf: Just give me booze lol.","Wild Grylls: Can’t give you alcohol, but I’ll find you something to eat with it. Fish okay?","Passing Dwarf: Not bad. Don’t you need a fish trap to catch them?","Wild Grylls: It’d be useful, but the fish are so huge that I think it’d be difficult.","Passing Dwarf: I’ll make one. You’d better give me the food. Deal?","Wild Grylls: Deal.","The items the dwarf had sent arrived as soon as the trade ended.","I had assumed the barricades wouldn’t be very tall.","I was wrong.","Even when placed diagonally, they stood slightly taller than I did.","If anything, building them this way must have required even more effort.","They’re bigger than I expected.","There was no time to stand around in surprise.","More barricades would arrive shortly.","Fortunately, the delay between each delivery allowed me to position them one at a time.","Their size probably caused them to take longer to transfer.","Or perhaps there wasn’t enough open space for them to appear all at once.","\"Whew.\"","After some time, I finished placing and adjusting everything.","I didn’t know exactly how the system determined where traded items would appear, so the process was somewhat awkward, but no accidents occurred.","There’s no inventory system or anything like that, is there?","Large deliveries like these would probably cause trouble every time.","It would be convenient if there were a separate space where traded items could be stored temporarily.","***","Title: Work Finished!","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the shelter with the barricades installed.)","Finally finished installing the barricades. I still have more to do, but this feels satisfying.","By the way, isn’t there some kind of space for temporarily storing traded items? They kept appearing out of nowhere, and positioning them was a pain.","Good work. That feature actually used to exist, but it’s restricted now.","Wild Grylls: Why was it restricted?","Smuggling. People used to complain that the system handled things like the military, but then the Moderator from two generations ago ruined an entire territory with it, so the feature was blocked.","Isn’t that restriction meaningless for the Moderator? They can do whatever they want.","Yeah. The Moderator could remove the restriction. But do you really think the current one would?","Wild Grylls: Couldn’t they allow storage for just ten minutes? That would be enough.","There are people who hide drugs up their asses to transport them. Like hell the Moderator will approve that lol.","They might make an exception for you, Grylls. But is there even a system for removing restrictions for only one registered user?","No. Maybe for an Assistant Moderator. And even then, you’d have to suck up to the Moderator lol.","One thing’s certain: the current Moderator is an old-fashioned hard-ass, so he won’t allow it.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I’m not old-fashioned! I merely value rules and principles! Calling someone old-fashioned just because they uphold order is the other person’s fault! The technical term for that is antisocial behavior!","The Moderator’s here?","Moderator, why not remove the restriction, then? You can decide now, can’t you?","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I’ve actually been considering it! I’ll review the matter positively, so please wait! Now, if you’ll excuse me!","He was reviewing it positively.","Perhaps there was reason to hope.","Even being able to store items for five minutes would help.","Although I had arranged the barricades, they were still scattered around somewhat messily.","No. I’m asking for too much. What am I thinking?","I quickly shook my head.","This wasn’t good.","I had resolved to reduce my dependence on the Gallery, yet here I was becoming annoyed by a minor inconvenience.","Its functionality was truly like a drug.","No wonder people couldn’t stop using the Gallery.","I could only grow by overcoming difficulties myself.","I renewed my resolve.","First, I should inspect the barricades properly.","Someday, I might have to build barricades by myself.","Perhaps something would happen to the dwarf, or I might lose access to the Gallery.","I needed to understand the structure of the barricades in preparation for that possibility.","He carved grooves into the wood and fitted the stakes into them. Then he secured everything tightly with rope, just in case.","When I had some free time, it might be a good idea to practice by making a small barricade.","There were trees everywhere, so I would never run out of materials.","The only thing lacking would be my craftsmanship.","Whatever I made would probably be far inferior to the dwarf’s work.","Aren’t dwarves supposed to be short? He made all of this by himself?","The dwarf’s physique suddenly came to mind.","The barricades stood slightly taller than I did.","It was surprising that a dwarf had built defensive structures this tall all by himself.","He constantly pestered me for alcohol, but perhaps Passing Dwarf was actually someone important.","\"Kyuu.\"","\"Are you hungry?\"","Wonmo approached and looked up at me with his bright, round eyes.","While I was installing the barricades, lunchtime had arrived before I knew it.","There was no fish left, so I would probably have to settle for a fasting pill today.","I gave Wonmo a large piece of meat that I had bought through the Gallery.","His eyes sparkled, and he immediately began devouring it.","I also need to learn how to set traps.","The problem was whether ordinary animals would fall for ordinary traps.","The only small animals I had seen so far were squirrels and rabbits.","Even those were considerably larger than normal.","The rabbits were about the size of medium-sized dogs.","They were also incredibly fast, fleeing the instant they sensed my presence.","Then I’ll just make the traps bigger.","It was a simple but effective solution.","Instead of setting a trap for a rabbit, I could build one as though I were trying to catch a wild boar.","While chewing on the bitter fasting pill, I glanced behind me.","I had felt something climbing onto my back, and sure enough, it was the Swift Sloth.","\"Do you want one too?\"","\"...\"","It nodded at its usual painfully slow pace.","I handed it a fasting pill and browsed the Gallery.","After taking a brief rest, I planned to circulate the cultivation method.","Heavenly Demon has requested a private conversation! Would you like to accept?","\"Huh?\"","A message caught my eye while I was browsing.","The Heavenly Demon hadn’t sent me a trade request.","She had requested a private one-on-one conversation.","As far as I knew, ordinary users and even registered users couldn’t use private conversations.","Apparently, the feature had been restricted to prevent cliques from forming.","So why could the Heavenly Demon use it?","Is it different for an Assistant Moderator?","I had my doubts, but I couldn’t exactly reject a request from the Heavenly Demon.","I accepted.","A window similar to the trade interface appeared.","Heavenly Demon: Benefactor, can you see my message?","Wild Grylls: Hello. I can see it clearly. Can Assistant Moderators use private conversations?","Heavenly Demon: Normally, they cannot. However, I persuaded the armband holder to grant me this authority. I must be the one to initiate the conversation, though.","Wild Grylls: I see. How are you finding the Assistant Moderator job?","Heavenly Demon: There are many images that please the eye. However, those with shallow enlightenment like yourself would fall prey to inner demons upon seeing them.","I roughly understood what she meant.","The last time I had wandered in without knowing anything, I had been thoroughly blinded by what I saw.","But the Heavenly Demon was a true Gallery addict among Gallery addicts.","She would easily brush such things aside.","In a way, she possessed all the qualities of an excellent Assistant Moderator.","She had plenty of free time, was immune to inner demons, and possessed a rock-solid mentality.","From the Moderator’s perspective, appointing her had probably seemed like a good idea.","Wild Grylls: Sounds like you’re having a hard time. Is there no time limit on private conversations?","Heavenly Demon: There is none. However, the entire conversation will be visible to the Moderator. That does not concern me. What I intend to teach you is only the foundation.","Wild Grylls: The foundation? Didn’t you already teach me everything? You said I’d even opened something called the upper dantian.","Heavenly Demon: That is true. However, the problem is that you opened it far too quickly. Without a proper foundation, one will inevitably become unstable. Even a bridgehead that appears sturdy will eventually collapse if it was built carelessly.","The language was clearly related to martial arts, yet strangely enough, I understood it.","The part about shoddy construction especially resonated with me.","This must have been what people called wisdom.","She was an excellent teacher.","Wild Grylls: That makes perfect sense. You’re saying my body could collapse because it was built carelessly, right?","Heavenly Demon: Correct. From now on, I intend to teach you the fundamentals. No matter how sturdy the stem may be, it will quickly wither if its roots are weak.","Wild Grylls: Thank you. I’m just not sure I’ll be able to understand everything.","Heavenly Demon: Do not worry. I shall explain it in terms you can understand. First, sit in the lotus position.","I followed her instructions and sat cross-legged.","Perhaps because I had grown accustomed to it, the posture no longer hurt.","It actually felt refreshing.","Later, I should practice other positions as well.","There was no downside to becoming more flexible.","Heavenly Demon: Good. However, I would prefer that you call it internal energy rather than mana. It is not necessarily incorrect, but hearing you call it mana bothers me for some reason.","So it bothers her.","She must have taken tremendous pride in internal-energy cultivation.","Well, she was an old woman who had experienced everything the world had to offer, so her pride was understandable.","It was something I ought to respect.","I would have to be more careful from now on.","Heavenly Demon: Ah, there is one thing I wish to ask. What did it feel like when you circulated the cultivation method? Did you feel any obstruction at the crown of your head?","Wild Grylls: Not at all. It just felt like the energy traveled throughout my entire body and completed a full circuit.","Heavenly Demon: Then it seems you truly have opened the Gate of Life and Death. Your internal energy appears to flow freely through the Governing and Conception Vessels.","I had no idea what any of that meant.","Still, I could tell she was impressed.","Wild Grylls: That’s a good thing, right?","Heavenly Demon: It is exceedingly good. In terms of cultivation, you have reached the late stage of the Peak Realm. However, your advancement was far too abrupt, so you likely cannot even manifest sword energy properly.","Wild Grylls: Sword energy? You mean putting mana into a sword?","Heavenly Demon: Internal energy.","Wild Grylls: I’ll be careful. Anyway, I can’t do it. This is the first time I’ve heard of it.","Heavenly Demon: You would likely struggle not only to manifest sword energy, but even to reinforce your own body. That is precisely why the fundamentals are important.","Wild Grylls: I see. Understood.","Heavenly Demon: Therefore, understanding the route will make matters easier. Read carefully. When circulating your cultivation method, the internal energy flows through the lower dantian, the perineum, the coccyx...","The Heavenly Demon’s lesson continued.","At considerable length.","I could only stare blankly with my mouth hanging open.","I didn’t understand a single word.","It felt like I had started with the basics of one plus one, only for her to suddenly throw calculus at me.","The Heavenly Demon’s intensive tutoring continued.","Heavenly Demon: If this is too difficult, I can show you through a drawing.","Wild Grylls: Can you do that?","Heavenly Demon: (A rough diagram of the circulation route.) How is it? Can you see it clearly?","I could certainly see it.","It was roughly a side view of a human body with the internal circulation route drawn inside.","What language is this?","The problem was that I couldn’t understand any of the writing.","At least the route itself was illustrated, so I could more or less guess where it went.","Is this really going to be okay?","It was far too difficult.","Meanwhile—","SwordMaster: Moderator, you traded with the Heavenly Demon, didn’t you?","Don’t Abandon the Hero: Huh?!"]},{"title":"Chapter 37","paragraphs":["Assistant Moderator (4)","At present, SwordMaster—Ash—is what people would call an unemployed bum who gets smacked on the back by her mother practically every day.","An unemployed bum who spends all day browsing the gallery and snickers whenever something amusing happens.","However, she was someone who had, strictly speaking, experienced \"working life.\"","And not just ordinary working life, but life in the political world, where conspiracies, schemes, and power struggles were everyday occurrences.","Since ancient times, politics had gradually developed as a means of keeping overwhelming power in check.","Ash, in particular, had been nothing more than a commoner until the Emperor bestowed a title upon her.","Until then, she had worked hard at navigating society so she would not find herself in politically troublesome situations—watching the moods of nobles, flattering them, agreeing with them, and so on.","In truth, marriage would have been the easiest option, but because Ash was simply too strong, every attempt had fallen through.","And after she became captain of the Imperial Guard, there was no longer much room for political problems to arise around her anyway.","In any case, Ash had experience with society—and, more specifically, with the dark and murky world of politics.","That was why the Heavenly Demon becoming a sub-mod set off a few alarm bells in her head.","She definitely made some kind of deal. There’s no way that old fossil would’ve become a sub-mod otherwise. Same goes for the head mod.","The instant Ash heard that the Heavenly Demon had become a sub-mod, she started thinking.","Unlike certain people, she actually had experience dealing with society.","She grasped the situation faster than anyone else.","What kind of deal did she make?","Ash had been a regular fixture in the gallery for a long time. In terms of seniority alone, she had been around for nearly ten years.","Unlike the previous head mod, the current head mod placed great importance on principles and rules.","On top of that, they had such a strong self-sacrificing streak that they would never force the sub-mod position onto somebody else.","For someone like that to appoint a sub-mod—and a well-known fixed-nickname user at that—meant there had to be something behind it.","The Heavenly Demon was probably the one who proposed the deal first...","In truth, the Heavenly Demon becoming a sub-mod was not much of a problem for Ash.","What if the Heavenly Demon started abusing her authority however she pleased?","Her privileges would be stripped immediately, and she would probably be banned for several weeks.","The Heavenly Demon knew that as well, so on the surface, she seemed to be diligently doing her job.","But Ash tried to discern the intention hidden beneath it.","Why had the Heavenly Demon decided to become a sub-mod at this particular moment?","The timing is way too convenient.","Ash had clashed with the Heavenly Demon quite a few times recently.","They had bickered over whether mana cultivation was better or whether an internal energy cultivation method was superior.","Though, to be fair, it had been closer to Ash picking fights one-sidedly, so Grylls had sided with the Heavenly Demon.","Ash was aware of how embarrassing her own behavior had been, so she limited herself to giving advice and stopped interfering beyond that.","Still, what a waste...","That did not mean she intended to give up easily.","It was simply too much of a waste. It had been a long time since she had seen someone with that much potential.","Ash had once trained countless disciples.","Of course, the reason had been the thoroughly impure intention of finding someone suitable to marry, but that was beside the point.","Regardless, she was confident in her ability to judge people.","All of those disciples had eventually fallen for other women and gotten married, but Grylls was different.","As she had said before, his life might constantly be in danger, but at least there was no need to worry about him getting distracted by women.","Even the ones I personally trained weren’t this exceptional. I have to teach him somehow.","Whenever she looked at Grylls, Ash felt as though she were looking at her past self.","A constitution that accumulated mana simply by breathing.","Because of his unusual environment, Grylls accumulated mana just by breathing.","And for mana to circulate throughout the entire body was ordinarily something that should only become possible after reaching the intermediate level of Sword Expert.","But I really don’t want to become a sub-mod.","Even so, becoming a sub-mod herself was something she absolutely wanted to avoid.","It was not as if the gallery was free of politics.","If anything, it was full of something even worse than politics: \"gallery politics.\"","And what was the difference?","Gallery politics consisted of agitation, fabrication, trolling, and finally, infighting.","Sub-mods, in particular, attracted far more attention than ordinary fixed-nickname users.","Just look at the Heavenly Demon.","The moment she became a sub-mod, she was subjected to all sorts of attacks.","She had managed to brush them all off thanks to her uniquely domineering personality.","Besides, mental fortitude was not an issue for Ash.","She simply hated it.","Ash just hated being a sub-mod!","Whatever the case, that makes me the latecomer.","In the end, Ash could only let out a small laugh.","The Heavenly Demon had put her in a perfect bind.","Who could have predicted she would become a sub-mod?","Still, Ash could not suppress her curiosity.","She wanted to know what had possessed the head mod to place the Heavenly Demon in that position.","I should find out.","The method for contacting the head mod was extremely simple.","All she had to do was send a trade request.","Only fixed-nickname users could send trade requests anyway, so the head mod usually accepted them.","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: Hello! What can I do for you?!]","The moment the request was accepted, the head mod greeted her energetically.","Ash smiled at the head mod, who never seemed to lose that energy, and spoke.","[SwordMaster: Head mod. You made a deal with the Heavenly Demon, didn’t you?]","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: W-What?!]","Despite her smile, Ash’s question went straight for the throat.","The head mod must have been thoroughly flustered, considering the bizarre response.","The head mod Ash knew was terrible at lying.","That remained true even in a gallery where anonymity was the norm.","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: How did you know?! Did the sub-mod tell you?!]","[SwordMaster: No. I just figured something like that had probably happened and took a shot in the dark. Then you confessed. So, what kind of deal did you make?]","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: She asked me to make one-on-one conversations possible!]","[SwordMaster: Oh.]","So that was it.","What a greedy woman.","Ash nodded at the head mod’s painfully honest answer.","Thanks to that, she was able to piece together the whole story.","As expected, the Heavenly Demon had become a sub-mod for Grylls.","But couldn’t she just use private posts? That seems way too simplistic.","Yet one question still remained unanswered.","What was the point of private posts, then?","Ash wanted to know the reason.","[SwordMaster: Aren’t one-on-one conversations still visible to you, head mod?]","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: Yes! I’m watching right now too!]","[SwordMaster: What are they talking about? The internal energy cultivation method?]","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: I can’t tell you the details, but I can answer \"yes\" to that!]","That much was within her expectations.","But she still did not understand.","The reward was far too small compared to the responsibilities that came with being a sub-mod.","Then again, was the Heavenly Demon the sort of person who would recklessly abuse authority?","No.","The Heavenly Demon was the type to say what she wanted to say and nothing more.","She was not easily swayed by other people’s opinions.","If anything, she was similar to the head mod in that she was not the type to become tyrannical simply because something displeased her.","And with the head mod still above her, she did not even have the conditions necessary for that.","Suspicious. Way too suspicious. What is she actually after?","Ash’s thoughts grew longer.","It was difficult to figure out the Heavenly Demon’s intentions.","Still, the conversation had not been entirely fruitless.","Ash nodded and thanked the head mod.","[SwordMaster: Thank you, head mod. Is there anything you want in return?]","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: I don’t need a bribe! If you want to become a sub-mod, you can just tell me!]","[SwordMaster: No, I’m fine without being a sub-mod. That’s not why I contacted you. I was just curious about why she was acting like that.]","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: I see! Understood!]","Their conversation ended there.","Ash slowly organized her thoughts.","It doesn’t seem like she has any political motive.","Given the Heavenly Demon’s personality, she almost certainly had no political intentions.","Becoming a sub-mod was probably partly to make it easier to help Grylls, while also serving some other purpose.","Ash did not know what that purpose was, but at the very least, it was unlikely to harm her.","Was I worrying for nothing?","The Heavenly Demon becoming a sub-mod was a massive issue in and of itself.","Especially since Ash had even gotten into a war of nerves with her recently.","There was no way she could simply ignore it.","This is complicated. Really complicated.","Maybe she was overcomplicating things.","She had never abandoned the idea of helping Grylls, after all.","She could simply step in quietly whenever he ran into trouble.","Internal energy cultivation methods contain a lot of terms that are difficult to understand unless you’re from the Central Plains. He’ll definitely make a post saying it’s too hard.","That would be her chance to give him tips on mana cultivation.","Since mana cultivation methods were specialized for training others, there were plenty of useful tricks she could teach him.","She just had to wait for the right timing.","Ash focused on the gallery.","She refreshed the page once every ten seconds, waiting for Grylls to make a post.","[Internal energy cultivation is way too hard.]","There it is!","Before long, Grylls made a post.","And the title was exactly what Ash wanted to see.","A post complaining about how difficult internal energy cultivation was.","She immediately opened it.","Title: Internal energy cultivation is way too hard","Wild Grylls","I’m learning an internal energy cultivation method from the Heavenly Demon, but there are so many words I don’t know that it’s really hard.","She says this is just the basics, but if even the basics are like this, I’m scared of what the advanced stuff will be like ;;","└ The Heavenly Demon taught you? How? She didn’t even make a post.","└ Wild Grylls) She requested a one-on-one chat with me?","└ Sub-mods can do that too? The head mod allowed it?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah. She said the head mod gave permission. Also said she didn’t care if people knew.","└ Wow ;; look at that special treatment. I’m already getting jealous.","└ Lmao, makes me want to start trolling.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) If you want, I can appoint you as a sub-mod too!","└ That threat doesn’t work anymore lol. We figured out anonymous users can’t become mods.","└ Anonymous users can’t do it anyway lol.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) Then I’ll come find you in person and threaten you!","└ Sorrysorrysorrysorrysorry","└ Damn, when the head mod says that it actually sounds scary lmaoooo.","└ Reminds me of when the head mod used to stalk people back in the day lol.","└ Police? Open up?","└ SwordMaster) Which part are you having trouble with?","└ Wild Grylls) It’s hard to understand the route. The Heavenly Demon even showed me a diagram while explaining it, but maybe I’m just too dumb because I still can’t get it.","└ SwordMaster) I understand what you mean. I can help you with that.","└ Wild Grylls) Thank you.","Ash stared at the post, unable to hide her sense of emptiness.","She had gone so far as to initiate a trade with the head mod just to figure out what was going on, yet the person involved had simply revealed everything himself.","It made all the effort she had put in feel pointless.","Then again, perhaps that was just like the Heavenly Demon.","...I should just teach him some tips.","Still, there was work to be done.","Ash pulled herself together.","Then she started typing comments so she could pass on various useful tricks.","She smiled when Grylls thanked her so politely.","Unlike internal energy cultivation, mana cultivation was a breathing method specialized for training others.","It was perfect for teaching the fundamentals in painstaking detail.","But why isn’t the Heavenly Demon interrupting me?","Normally, she should have butted in by now.","Yet there was not even a glimpse of her.","Just what was she plotting?","Ash remained suspicious as she continued typing.","└ SwordMaster) Mana cultivation and internal energy cultivation may have different branches, but they share the same roots. Start with your breathing first.","└ Wild Grylls) I already am.","└ SwordMaster) While maintaining that state, send the energy in your lower abdomen toward the perineum. You know where the perineum is, right?","└ Wild Grylls) More or less?","└ SwordMaster) \"More or less\" isn’t enough. Since you’re a man, Grylls, just think of it as the area between your testicles and your anus. Send the energy there and you should feel something.","└ Wild Grylls) Hmm... yeah. I can feel it. It’s itchy though. Can I scratch it a little?","Could this be why the Heavenly Demon did it too?","Her reasonable suspicion steadily grew.","***","This was strangely frustrating.","Ash furrowed her elegant brows.","It was not because Grylls was having trouble understanding.","Nor was it because she had to cram so much text into the narrow comment section...","└ Teach us too~","└ Why are you keeping all the good tips to yourselves?","└ SwordMaster, I’ve hit a wall in my cultivation recently. Could you help me too?","└ Unlocktheprivatecommentsunlocktheprivatecommentsunlocktheprivatecomments","The jackals had smelled something sweet and come running.","They were getting in the way of her concentration.","They kept invading Grylls’s comment section, making it harder for her to teach him properly.","Meanwhile, at that very moment, in the Demonic Cult—","I can feel her frustration from here.","Yu Sowol smiled as she read SwordMaster’s private comments.","The moment she had been given a moderator badge, she had gained the authority to view private comments as well.","It was only natural.","That meant Yu Sowol could also see all the useful tips SwordMaster was passing on.","Calling these \"tips\" is somewhat generous.","SwordMaster’s advice could barely even be called advice.","Because it was no different from what Yu Sowol had already taught him.","This problem stemmed from SwordMaster—Ash—being far too talented herself.","Unlike swordsmanship, which she had built up from the very bottom, she had possessed a constitution that accumulated mana merely by breathing.","She might have been exceptional at swordsmanship, but she had very little talent when it came to teaching breathing methods.","I suppose it only works because the benefactor’s potential is exceptional.","Still, geniuses had ways of understanding other geniuses.","Grylls gradually absorbed what SwordMaster considered \"useful tips.\"","Even though Yu Sowol herself had dismissed the method, Grylls devoured it eagerly.","SwordMaster. As expected, this person is extraordinary as well.","But it did not matter.","Yu Sowol shifted her gaze.","Where she looked, the message window containing the conversation she had just exchanged with Grylls was still open.","Unlike trades, one-on-one conversations allowed them to communicate in real time.","The entire conversation history remained as well, meaning she could review it whenever she pleased.","For fruit to grow, the roots must first be strong.","What Yu Sowol wanted was simple.","For Grylls to fully understand every insight of the Heavenly Demon Divine Art and eventually bear fruit.","She planned to use SwordMaster’s advice to strengthen his weak foundations.","In the end, people are always more interested in sweet fruit than in the roots beneath it.","Even if Grylls received SwordMaster’s advice, the foundation itself remained the Heavenly Demon Divine Art.","That had not changed.","Eventually, he would realize the greatness of the Heavenly Demon Divine Art, and his respect for her would naturally grow.","SwordMaster was merely an assistant.","The one who would ultimately pass everything on to him was the Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol.","It is only proper that I do this for my benefactor.","Now it was time to fulfill her duties as a sub-mod.","Yu Sowol turned her attention back to the board.","But even then, she did not yet realize—","└ Wild Grylls) Oh? It worked? My sword is glowing!","└ SwordMaster) Holy shit. Seriously? How did you do that?","└ Wild Grylls) Why are you asking me that? ;;","└ SwordMaster) I’m more amazed that you actually do everything I tell you just from hearing it ;;","When the roots changed, the branches growing from them were bound to change little by little as well.","Especially because SwordMaster’s true specialty was not breathing techniques—","but swordsmanship itself.","└ SwordMaster) With a little more practice, you might be able to stop carrying a shield and just use a sword. But seriously, how did you do that?","└ Wild Grylls) I told you, I don’t know either ;;","Very slowly, it was beginning to seep into him."]},{"title":"Chapter 38","paragraphs":["Fireball (1)","Would you believe me if I said a strange haze started rising from a sword?","It was the sort of phenomenon you would expect to see in fantasy or martial arts fiction, so even I had a hard time believing it.","According to SwordMaster, once you got the feel for it, it was actually very easy.","But apparently, I was the first person she’d ever seen who managed to release energy immediately after hearing a few tips.","SwordMaster herself said it had taken her around an hour just to get the hang of it.","Of course, maybe that was because her advice was packed with all the know-how she had accumulated over the years.","Title: Is this really aura?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a sword with a shimmering haze rising from it)","I did what SwordMaster told me to do. Is this really aura?","Asking because it worked way too easily.","└ SwordMaster) That really is aura ;; I thought maybe, but you actually did it.","└ Wild Grylls) That’s a good thing, right?","└ Stop humblebragging. It’s pissing me off.","└ Some people take months and this guy does it in one day lmao.","└ Months, my ass. It took me three years, damn it lol.","└ How the hell did SwordMaster teach him? Tell me too.","└ Wild Grylls) She just told me to reproduce the sensation I feel when circulating mana, then imagine letting that mana flow into the sword. So I did exactly that.","└ Ha ;; I can’t decide what’s more ridiculous, someone explaining it like that or someone actually succeeding from that explanation.","└ Fuck, if you could emit aura from an explanation like that, every random idiot would be using it lmaooo.","└ Starlight Princess) Wow. That’s amazing. If you compared it to a mage, what Circle would that be?","└ For a mage, it’d be like starting at the 3rd Circle immediately.","└ Starlight Princess) I see. So it really is impressive, right?","└ What Circle did you start at, then?","└ Starlight Princess) The 5th Circle. I could have started higher under normal circumstances, but my illness prevented me from doing so.","└ This one’s flexing too lmaooo.","└ That’s basically like saying you started with an Aura Blade lol.","└ It’s not an Aura Blade. It’s Sword Force.","└ Same damn thing, asshole. Do you really have to nitpick?","└ Pride.","└ Wild Grylls) Anyway, if I think of compressing this stuff, that makes it an Aura Blade, right? Lol, I’ll practice.","└ SwordMaster) Practicing is good, but maintaining the sensation is more important. Sometimes people forget it.","└ Wild Grylls) You can forget it?","└ SwordMaster) It works on the same principle as consciously thinking about your breathing.","The comment section exploded the moment I showed them the aura.","Maybe the Heavenly Demon was busy carrying out her duties as a sub-mod, because she did not leave a comment.","Well, now that she could have one-on-one conversations, I figured she would just message me directly if she had anything to say.","Is this really that impressive?","I stared closely at the sword with the shimmering haze rising from it.","I could definitely feel mana leaving my body.","But since it replenished every time I breathed, it did not feel particularly significant.","SwordMaster told me to compress it as tightly as possible, right?","She had advised me to keep practicing until the haze took on a sharp, defined form.","From that point onward, she said it entered the realm of talent, so there was only so much she could do for me.","Even so, SwordMaster said she would help me as much as she could.","Feels like I’m only ever receiving things from her...","I wanted to give SwordMaster something in return for all the useful tips she kept teaching me.","But she was the kind of person who had even refused rare medicinal herbs because she did not want to become healthier.","Then what could I give her that she would willingly accept?","Would she take something material, as long as it was not an herb?","This is difficult.","SwordMaster was especially troublesome compared to the Heavenly Demon.","I did not like continuing to receive things without giving anything back.","She claimed that all she wanted was for me to marry her, but that was obviously a joke.","Besides, I did not even know whether I would ever be able to leave this place.","For now, should I test this out?","Instead of the Heavenly Demon’s sword, I brought out an ordinary logging axe.","Wonmo was taking a nap, while Tree Sloth was riding on my back.","There was no better way to test the performance of aura—or sword energy—than chopping wood.","How many swings did this usually take?","I recalled the sensation of channeling mana into the sword.","First, I had to become aware of the mana stored in my dantian.","SwordMaster had told me to think of the mana stored in my lower abdomen as a kind of reservoir.","All I had to do was draw mana from that reservoir and send it into my weapon.","She said that once the mana in the reservoir runs dry, I’d need to circulate the cultivation method to refill it...","SwordMaster said she had never once suffered from a mana shortage in her entire life.","Because mana accumulated in her body every time she breathed, it apparently functioned almost like a perpetual-motion machine.","She said that given my environment, I might eventually become similar, but I had no idea whether that would really happen.","I should keep circulating the internal energy cultivation method consistently.","I let mana flow into the axe.","A faint haze began rising from it.","In the Central Plains, this energy was called sword energy.","In other countries, it was called aura.","Apparently, with this energy, you could produce several times the power of an ordinary person.","\"Hup!\"","Then just how powerful was it?","I swung the axe with all my strength.","The target was a thick tree trunk.","It was a tree that had taken several axe swings to bring down just yesterday.","Crack!","The axe blade sank deeply into the trunk—","and kept going.","It did not slice through it like tofu, but the entire center of the tree was torn apart.","Crrraack!","With its trunk practically shattered, the enormous tree began toppling over on its own.","It leaned farther and farther until—","THUD!","—it crashed to the ground with a deafening noise.","Good thing I had been chopping from the side opposite the cave.","Otherwise, I might have destroyed the barricade the dwarf had gone through all that trouble to give me.","It doesn’t cut. It explodes.","I carefully examined the fallen tree trunk.","I knew the weapon’s destructive power would increase, but I had not expected it to be this extreme.","According to SwordMaster, the shimmering haze was simply evidence of mana leaking out.","She had specifically mentioned that the fundamental nature of the weapon itself did not change.","Considering the characteristics of an axe, I guess it makes sense.","An axe was a weapon specialized more for smashing than cutting.","So it made sense that the tree trunk had been ripped apart rather than neatly sliced through.","If I had put the same energy into a sword, I probably could have cut through it like tofu.","...Could I really?","The moment that thought occurred to me, I went back into the cave and brought out the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","To test it, I placed the sword against a tree trunk without channeling any mana into it.","Before, I had never even tried this because I was worried I might chip the blade.","But I was not trying to saw through the tree with a sword.","I only wanted to check whether the blade could cut into the trunk as a basic performance test.","Sssshk—","\"Huh?\"","My eyes widened.","The Heavenly Demon’s sword sank deep into the tree with only the slightest bit of force.","Then it slid smoothly through the trunk as though there were hardly any resistance at all.","Rumble—","I was so busy staring at the Heavenly Demon’s sword that I barely cared about the tree falling over.","I knew it was a good weapon, but I had never expected it to be this ridiculous.","What kind of absurdly broken item is this?","With a sword like this, there was barely any need to emit aura in the first place.","Of course, I had absolutely no intention of using the Heavenly Demon’s sword for logging.","If I accidentally chipped the blade, that would be a disaster.","She just gave me a sword like this without hesitation?","My respect for the Heavenly Demon shot upward.","At the same time, I started to worry.","Hadn’t she given me something far too valuable?","Part of me wanted to return it immediately, but the Heavenly Demon would probably refuse.","If I find a good sword later, I’ll return this one to her.","This sword was simply too excessive.","It was something that ought to go back to its owner someday.","I put all but one of the fallen trees up on the auction house.","Since I was already there, I checked the price of the inner core I had listed that morning.","[Inner Core: 500 taels of silver]","\"Whoa.\"","The price just kept climbing.","I stared at the current bid in admiration.","Five hundred taels of silver converted to 5,000 gold.","The owlbear corpse had sold for 250 taels, so this was already twice as much.","It seemed the price had risen this high because the Heavenly Demon herself had vouched that it was an inner core.","What if it turns out to be fake after all?","Would I have to refund the money?","I had no idea.","Still, with the Heavenly Demon backing me up, the buyer probably would not be able to make a fuss.","And even if they did, there should not be a problem as long as the Heavenly Demon testified for me.","Let’s see. What time is it...?","I opened the gallery and checked the time.","More than an hour had flown by while I practiced the cultivation method and aura.","It was currently 1:30 in the afternoon.","There was still plenty of time before sunset.","Should I try making some traps?","It seemed like a good idea.","I could improve my handiwork and get some meat at the same time.","As for how to make traps, I could find everything I needed just by searching the gallery.","Adventurers occasionally uploaded guides on making hunting traps.","Some of them had even made it into the recommended-post section, so I should be able to make one without much trouble.","The problem is the area where the small animals live...","I knew where little animals like rabbits tended to pass through.","The problem was that Muscle Mushroom was located in that direction.","It should be fine as long as I did not provoke it, but there was no guarantee.","It might still be awake and wandering around nearby.","For safety’s sake, it would be better to eliminate Muscle Mushroom first.","There was a cave there too, so I can check that out while I’m at it.","Decision made.","I would deal with Muscle Mushroom first.","Its individual attacks were powerful, but it was slow.","And since I had heard that it was weak against fire, defeating it should not be too difficult.","Wait, did they actually say it was weak against fire? They said fire was essential because of those spores or whatever.","It looked like I would have to hold a sword in one hand and a torch in the other.","I remembered the golden shield that had been crushed by a single Beng Quan punch.","If I took a direct hit from something like that, there was a good chance there would not even be enough of my bones left to collect.","So fighting from a distance would be better.","It didn’t look like arrows would work, though.","Even ants had clearly distinguishable heads, thoraxes, and abdomens.","Muscle Mushroom was different.","Aside from its arms and legs, its body was long and narrow like a branch.","It was essentially closer to a plant, which meant I would probably have to either smash it apart or burn it.","...They said magic exists too, right?","Something suddenly occurred to me.","Magic.","The iconic power that appeared in practically every fantasy story.","It was supposedly an ability only geniuses were qualified to learn.","Maybe I could learn just a little?","If I could use magic, it would be useful in all sorts of ways.","Not just for ranged attacks, but for everyday survival as well.","The moment the thought occurred to me, I immediately opened the gallery.","Title: Is magic easy to learn?","Wild Grylls","I just want to learn some simple fire or water magic. Is it difficult?","└ Heavenly Demon) Ahem. One must devote oneself to a single path in order to achieve greatness. Are you already allowing your mind to wander elsewhere?","└ SwordMaster) The sub-mod is right. Even I gave up on magic almost immediately because of how difficult it is, so don’t even try.","└ Guess he has no idea how many aspiring mages there are in the gallery lol.","└ Grylls, you’re going to get yourself in serious trouble messing with that. Don’t do it.","└ Seriously, we’re only telling you this because we’re nice.","Everyone reacted negatively.","Even the Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster.","I could not understand why they were all so against it.","└ Wild Grylls) Didn’t you say elves and demons can use magic just fine?","└ Their starting point is high enough that they can usually reach the 3rd Circle. Going beyond that is difficult.","└ Didn’t you say you were human, Grylls?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah, yeah. I was just curious.","└ Magic is difficult enough to make even demons and elves grind their teeth. In terms of theory, they’re actually worse than humans.","└ Wild Grylls) Why?","└ Do you carefully analyze the theory behind how you breathe? Humans just happen to be unusually curious. Other races usually aren’t.","└ Wild Grylls) Oh. Got it.","└ Princess Chaenggu) But our Mephisto is still better when it comes to magic! You can tell just by looking at broadcast magic!","└ Demonic-race utility magic really is impressive. Life has gotten way more comfortable thanks to them lol.","└ Praise the demon who invented air-conditioning magic!","└ What’s air-conditioning magic?","└ Air conditioning.","└ Oh lmao, yeah, that deserves praise.","└ Refrigeration magic for me lol. I get to drink cold alcohol every day now.","└ Let’sGrowTrees) Elves are inventing all kinds of magic too!","└ What kinds of magic are they inventing?","└ Let’sGrowTrees) Communication and reconnaissance magic, as well as explosive magic!","└ Whoa, shit ;; that sounds scary as hell.","└ Are those bastards seriously not preparing to start a war?","└ Let’sGrowTrees) Don’t worry. Elves love peace.","└ Wild Grylls) How is that any different from \"If you want peace, prepare for war\"? ;;","└ Let’sGrowTrees) Ooooh! That’s a wonderful saying. I’ll take it to heart.","└ Wild Grylls) What?","There seemed to be someone seriously wrong in the head, but it would probably be fine.","Anyway, magic appeared to be used in all sorts of fields.","It was quite literally magic replacing science.","No.","In this world, perhaps magic itself was science.","└ Starlight Princess) Are you trying to learn magic? I can help you.","└ Wild Grylls) Aren’t you busy exercising?","└ Starlight Princess) Other than the time I spend exercising, I’m pretty free. Forgive me for asking, but you do know arithmetic, right?","└ Wild Grylls) I graduated high school ;;","Was she looking down on me too much?","Or maybe there were simply a lot of people in this world who could not even do basic arithmetic.","Given the era, there was no reason to expect anything like universal public education.","Then again, they did have academies, so perhaps she was accounting for people from underdeveloped regions.","└ Starlight Princess) \"Graduated high school\"? I don’t know what that means, but I assume it means you can do arithmetic. Good. Then you should be able to express fire mathematically.","└ Wild Grylls) Huh? Express what mathematically?","└ Starlight Princess) Fire. You formulate it mathematically. It’s very easy. It works like this—","As Starlight Princess continued explaining, all I could do was stare with my mouth hanging open.","There were plenty of symbols.","There were just no numbers.","My knowledge of mathematics had reset itself the instant the college entrance exam ended.","And since I had been a humanities student on top of that, I understood absolutely none of it.","└ Starlight Princess) Well? Do you understand?","└ Wild Grylls) That’s the basics?","└ Starlight Princess) Yes. You learn this before even entering the academy.","└ Anyone else feel like their head is going to explode just looking at that?","└ Me first lol.","└ Ah lmao, you don’t need this crap to live normally.","Were all the mages in this world Newton or Einstein?","Then again, scientists on Earth were geniuses compared to ordinary people too.","I decided to cleanly give up on learning magic.","└ Wild Grylls) Uh... I’ll just give up. Starlight Princess, do you find math easy?","└ Starlight Princess) I love mathematics. You can express everything in the world through mathematics, can’t you? Someday, I’m going to express the Forest of Four Seasons mathematically too.","└ Wild Grylls) You don’t have calculators here, right?","└ Starlight Princess) Why would I need a calculator? I can just calculate it in my head.","└ Wild Grylls) ;;;","└ God, that’s obnoxious lmao.","└ You’d be surprised how many people like that actually exist.","└ Their entire thought process is different from ours.","Yeah.","I should give up on magic completely.","If I kept entertaining pointless hope, I was only going to hurt myself.","Still, I should thank Starlight Princess for offering to help.","Seeing how disappointed she seemed made me feel a little guilty.","In the end, I guess I’ll have to solve this physically.","Was there really no other way?","I looked around the cave.","Then one particular object caught my eye.","Something I had left untouched until now.","That’s it!","It was the alcohol the dwarf had given me as a gift."]},{"title":"Chapter 39","paragraphs":["Fireball (2)","There was a saying: if you had no teeth, you made do with your gums.","In other words, if the best option was unavailable, you came up with the next best thing.","Since my best option—magic—was gone, I needed to settle for an alternative too.","It was technically magic.","Just... magic with a little physics mixed in.","Similar to a Fireball, but slightly different in nature.","Pop!","I struggled to pull out the cork that had been wedged deep inside the bottle.","Fortunately, the dwarf had given me an opener along with the alcohol, so I was able to get it out.","\"Ugh...!\"","The instant I uncorked it, I couldn’t help but grimace.","I had no idea how to describe the sensation.","It felt like the overpowering smell of alcohol was beating my sense of smell into submission.","Like a hired thug barging in and forcibly driving every other scent out of the place.","\"Grragh!\"","Even Tree Sloth, who was clinging to my back, recoiled in horror.","The little guy barely ever made a sound, yet even he was clutching his nose.","That alone showed how vicious the smell was.","He gave me this to drink? This is basically poison.","I was seriously curious about the alcohol content.","It had to be absurdly high.","At this level, I could probably mix in just a little oil and still get what I wanted.","Should I at least taste it once?","Still, it seemed like a waste to throw it away without trying it, so I decided to take a single sip.","Even if I got drunk, it shouldn’t be a problem.","I had an internal energy cultivation method now.","I vaguely remembered hearing that circulating a cultivation method could sober you up.","I stared at the alcohol, which was still reeking like pure ethanol, then quietly brought the bottle to my lips.","Gulp.","Surprisingly, the first thing I tasted was sweetness.","There was the characteristic bitterness of alcohol too, but the sweet aroma was much stronger.","This is actually pretty good.","At this level, I could drink it like a beverage.","That was what I thought.","For exactly two seconds.","\"HUARGH! UUUUAGH!\"","Something was wrong.","I had clearly swallowed a liquid, so why did it feel like my throat was on fire?","Had I swallowed flames?","No, forget flames. Had I just swallowed hydrochloric acid?","I clutched my throat in agony.","And then I realized the truth.","That dwarf bastard had finally gone and poisoned me!","Right after that realization came the distinct sensation that my life was in danger.","I couldn’t die like this.","I started feeling around the floor for an elixir, but before long, the pain gradually began to subside.","If it hadn’t, I genuinely would have used up one of my elixirs.","That was how bad it hurt.","\"Ugh...\"","I rubbed my still-stinging throat.","Tears had formed in the corners of my eyes.","I had no idea what the hell that dwarf had given me, but it wasn’t alcohol.","It was poison in liquid form.","Otherwise, there was no reason my throat should hurt like I had suddenly developed severe acid reflux.","And I wasn’t even exaggerating.","I felt like drinking actual hydrochloric acid couldn’t possibly hurt this much.","It’s not like the dwarf is crazy enough to actually give me poison.","So they really drank this stuff as alcohol?","My respect for dwarves rose dramatically.","I sighed and stepped outside for a moment to drink some water.","After drinking from the hose, the burning pain finally eased.","I feel like this would catch fire even without oil.","There was probably no need to fill the whole thing with oil.","Muscle Mushroom was still a mushroom in the end, so it should burn fairly well.","If I filled the bottle entirely with oil and the fire spread, I’d be in trouble.","Let’s check whether this stuff ignites first.","I went back into the cave and poured a little alcohol onto the ground.","Then I picked up a random twig and touched an ignition stone to it.","The dry branch caught fire easily.","It might have been dangerous to put the ignition stone directly against the alcohol, so precautions like this were necessary.","Whoosh!","\"Oh.\"","The moment I brought the flame close, the alcohol flared up.","Apparently, with an alcohol content that high, it ignited extremely well too.","In that case, there shouldn’t be any problem throwing the bottle as-is.","Come to think of it, the bottle’s glass too. Perfect.","Now that I’d confirmed it worked, all that remained was making the actual weapon.","Making a Molotov cocktail was simple, yet surprisingly tricky.","If I screwed up, I could end up setting myself on fire.","Its destructive power wasn’t something to underestimate either.","I had heard they were useful enough to be used against tanks in wartime.","First, I need oil.","I planned to mix oil and alcohol in suitable proportions.","Like I said before, filling the whole bottle with nothing but oil could cause all sorts of problems.","At the very least, I needed to be able to put the fire out relatively easily.","And I’ll add sand too.","Sticky oil and sand.","Just hearing the combination made it sound perfect.","I bought vegetable oil from the auction house.","Apparently, people sold that there.","As for sand, I just gathered some from around the area, dried it, and poured it in.","The last and most important part was the wick.","That was the part I wasn’t completely sure about.","If it burns too fast, I’m the one in danger.","It needed to burn slowly enough while still catching fire easily.","Considering all of that, cloth seemed like the best choice.","Still, I needed to test it.","I bought wastepaper, old newspapers, cloth, and various other flammable materials from the auction house.","As expected, cloth is the safest.","After testing them, cloth turned out to be the most suitable.","I immediately stuffed a strip of cloth into the mouth of the bottle.","Even using a chopstick to force it in took some effort.","Finally, I turned the bottle upside down to check whether any liquid leaked out.","The cloth was thick, so there didn’t seem to be any problem.","Title: Learned Fireball.","(Photo of a hastily made Molotov cocktail)","From now on, call me a fire mage.","└ Passing Dwarf) ??? Isn’t that the alcohol I gave you?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah, yeah. That shit’s insanely strong lmao.","└ Passing Dwarf) Don’t tell me you threw it away without even drinking it.","└ Wild Grylls) Nah, I took one sip. Thought I was gonna die lol.","└ Passing Dwarf) Assassination successful.","└ Wild Grylls) Are you insane? lmao. You call that alcohol? I’d rather drink rubbing alcohol.","└ Passing Dwarf) It’s still pretty expensive stuff lol.","└ Why’d you make a Molotov cocktail? What are you planning to do with it?","└ Wild Grylls) Gonna kill that mushroom man. If its whole body catches fire, won’t the spores burn too?","└ That’s certainly the straightforward method. Didn’t expect you to make a Molotov cocktail though ;;","└ Wild Grylls) How do people normally kill them? With mages?","└ Just throw a bottle of oil and then toss a torch. That’s safer.","└ Grylls is alone, though, so this probably works better for him.","└ Mage (Physical) lmaoooo.","└ Starlight Princess) Fireball is really easy... It’s not difficult at all.","└ Wild Grylls) Teacher?","└ Starlight Princess) It’s nothing. I’m just a little disappointed. It’s incredibly satisfying to understand the principles of magic one by one.","└ Is this magic (mathematics)?","└ Magic is basically advanced mathematics to begin with.","└ What did you mix into it? Did you add oil?","└ Wild Grylls) About half oil. The rest is alcohol and sand. I’d be screwed if the fire spread somewhere else.","└ You’re not seriously planning to put it out with water after burning everything, right?","└ Wild Grylls) I’ll smother it with sand. I’m not that stupid.","└ You know your stuff, huh? I was about to report you for arson lol.","└ Wild Grylls) Go ahead and report me. That’d be great for me lmao.","└ Allfather) You should be careful once the mushroom man catches fire. It will explode the moment it releases its spores.","└ Wild Grylls) I’ll be careful. Are its spores especially weak to fire?","└ Allfather) They are weak to it, but it’s also instinct. Spreading offspring when one’s life is in danger is an instinct shared by living creatures.","└ Wild Grylls) Thanks for the advice. I’m heading out to kill it now.","└ Do you really have to kill it?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah. Rabbits pass through that area, so I need it gone if I want to set traps there.","└ Then I guess you don’t have much choice.","└ PraiseTheSun) Are you going to use the golden shield I gave you?","└ Wild Grylls) I’m taking it with me for now. It can block at least one hit.","└ PraiseTheSun) I’ll give you a better shield later. Just wait.","└ Wild Grylls) I’m fine, though.","└ PraiseTheSun) Well, I’m not.","The preparations were complete.","All that remained was to get properly equipped.","I didn’t need the crossbow, so I packed everything else.","The Molotov cocktail was a little cumbersome, though. It looked like I needed to buy a small bag.","I’ll just grab something suitable.","I bought a small pouch from the auction house, one that could be hung from my waist.","I stored the Molotov cocktail and an elixir inside it. Just in case, I also packed the bottle containing extra oil.","I thought that was everything, but then I remembered one more thing I needed.","Ah. I need a shovel too.","A shovel for smothering the fire.","That was necessary.","Sword and shield in my hands, shovel strapped to my back.","Now it was time to go hunt Muscle Mushroom.","\"Guard the house.\"","\"...\"","I entrusted the cave to Tree Sloth, who had already climbed down from my back, and started walking.","Wonmo was still peacefully taking a nap even as I left.","He was cute, so I’d let it slide.","Everything was ready.","I set off with a slight sense of tension.","I needed to eliminate Muscle Mushroom before I could set traps and hunt the smaller animals in the area.","And while I was at it, I could also inspect the inside of the cave the mushroom had been blocking.","I wonder what’s inside.","Honestly, I was curious about the cave just as much as I was interested in setting traps.","There had to be a reason Muscle Mushroom was guarding it.","It’s not some kind of dungeon, right? And the mushroom is literally the gatekeeper?","If that were the case, going inside would be no different from poking a hornet’s nest.","There was a reason people said curiosity killed the cat.","Half worried and half excited, I headed toward the place where Muscle Mushroom was located.","Rustle—","Something suddenly sprang out of the bushes while I was walking.","Long ears and an adorable, tiny appearance.","\"Squeak?\"","A rabbit.","A rabbit had suddenly appeared.","The moment it saw me, it raised its body high, and its long ears shot upright as well.","Anyone could tell it was on guard.","Even so, the way its mouth kept twitching was ridiculously cute.","\"Hey, hey. Go on. Shoo. Shoo.\"","I had no intention of hunting it right now, so I lightly nudged it with my sword.","Maybe even that felt threatening to the rabbit.","CLANG!","The rabbit suddenly kicked the sword with all its strength.","Not the edge, but the flat of the blade.","Judging by the clear metallic sound, the kick carried considerable force.","It was strong enough to throw me off balance and make me stagger.","\"What the hell...?\"","I stared in disbelief as the rabbit fled into the bushes.","I had almost fallen over from a single kick.","Apparently, even rabbits were different when they lived in the Forest of Four Seasons.","If that kick hit me directly, I’d probably end up with a cracked bone at minimum.","What kind of ridiculous forest is this?","Now even the rabbits were dangerous.","This was absurd.","If I wanted to set traps, I would probably need to use something with serious killing power.","Otherwise, those rabbits might just destroy every trap I set.","My head was already starting to hurt, but hunting the mushroom came first.","\"...Found it.\"","Following the familiar path, I arrived at Muscle Mushroom’s location.","It was still stationed in front of the cave like a gatekeeper.","As long as I didn’t approach too closely, it probably wouldn’t wake up.","I carefully pulled the Molotov cocktail out of my bag.","Crackle!","I lit the wick with the ignition stone, and flames immediately began licking upward.","I stared at Muscle Mushroom.","It still hadn’t moved an inch.","Apparently, it really did only wake up when something came close.","\"Hraaah!\"","With a forceful shout, I hurled the Molotov cocktail as hard as I could.","It flew through the air while spinning, leaving a ring of flame behind it.","Muscle Mushroom remained rooted to the ground right up until the bottle reached it.","Crash!","The Molotov smashed against the mushroom’s body and shattered.","WHOOOSH!","A huge blaze engulfed the entire mushroom.","The easily ignited oil and alcohol fed the flames, while the sand clung thickly to its body.","\"Kuuuuuu!\"","Sensing danger, Muscle Mushroom began pulling its arms and legs out of the ground.","I didn’t miss the opening.","I charged forward exactly as planned.","The flames were hot, but I only needed to get close once.","Slash!","Before one of its legs could completely pull free, I severed it with my sword.","No matter how muscular it was, losing a leg was enough to make it fall.","BOOM!","Muscle Mushroom crashed to the ground.","The flames intensified.","Pop-pop-pop!","\"Ugh!\"","Then a series of small explosions suddenly erupted.","Fortunately, I had already backed away.","Otherwise, I might have been caught in them.","They were only about as powerful as firecrackers, but burns were still serious injuries.","It released its spores.","Allfather’s advice had been right.","Apparently, it had tried to scatter spores to reproduce, only for them to explode in the flames.","The creature thrashed around for a while.","Only after its entire body was engulfed in fire did it gradually grow still.","Perhaps because it was a mushroom, the smell of it burning wasn’t particularly unpleasant.","If anything, it had a strangely appetizing aroma.","That doesn’t mean I’m going to eat it.","Thanks to the strategy I had prepared in advance, I defeated it without much trouble.","Still, I planned to wait a little longer to make sure it was truly dead.","Crackle. Crackle.","After some time, Muscle Mushroom had been burned completely black.","The flames gradually began to die down as well.","Deciding that was enough, I pulled the shovel off my back.","Then I covered the remains with sand and completely extinguished the fire.","Animals might come because of the smell.","The aroma was pleasant enough that it might attract beasts.","I thought about what to do before deciding to move the mushroom corpse.","There might still be embers, so I’ll push it somewhere with less grass.","I shoved it along with the shovel until it was tucked away in a corner.","Even if an animal came, it would probably be more interested in the mushroom than the cave.","With the cleanup finished, I finally looked into the cave Muscle Mushroom had been guarding.","Because of the angle of the sunlight, the interior was extremely dark.","I could see reasonably well even in darkness.","But if I wanted to investigate properly, I would probably need a torch.","Good thing I brought some cloth.","I picked up a large branch from the ground.","After wrapping it tightly with cloth, I lit it using the ignition stone.","Whoosh!","The moment the torch flared to life, the inside of the cave became much brighter.","Overall, the interior resembled the cave where I lived.","It was spacious in every direction, giving it a surprisingly comfortable atmosphere.","\"Not bad...\"","I stopped halfway through looking around.","Thanks to the torchlight, I could now see what was at the far end of the cave.","It wasn’t some dangerous beast.","It had just caught me off guard because it stood out so much.","Sparkle. Sparkle.","\"...A mushroom?\"","A golden mushroom was shining brilliantly.","Is it poisonous?","It looked like the kind of thing no sane person would ever want to eat."]},{"title":"Chapter 40","paragraphs":["Scammer (1)","I stared at the golden mushroom sparkling in front of me.","Even after I extinguished the torch, the mushroom continued emitting its own golden light.","Apparently, this was what Muscle Mushroom had been guarding.","It looks poisonous just from looking at it.","As a rule of thumb, it was safer to assume most mushrooms were poisonous.","And brightly colored plants and animals were poisonous nine times out of ten.","So there was a very high chance this golden mushroom contained poison.","It is pretty fascinating, though.","I slowly approached the golden mushroom.","Only after getting closer did I realize it was much larger than I had expected.","It was only slightly smaller than the fish I had caught before.","For a mushroom, it was enormous.","This seriously looks like something that mustached character would eat.","A certain plumber in overalls suddenly came to mind.","Would he grow bigger or stronger if he ate this mushroom?","Maybe he could just run straight into monsters and send them flying.","Even while entertaining those pointless thoughts, I didn’t lower my guard.","For all I knew, this thing might suddenly start moving like Muscle Mushroom had.","Fortunately, the golden mushroom did not spring to its feet.","It merely continued sparkling.","What the hell is this thing?","Even as I examined the mushroom, I kept watch behind me.","For safety’s sake, it would probably be best to pick it and return to the shelter.","I should put on gloves, just in case.","I put on the gloves I had stored in my pouch.","The mushroom was large enough that I would need both hands to carry it, but that wasn’t a problem.","I could hang the sword at my waist and strap the shovel and shield to my back.","Come to think of it, I need a scabbard.","Normally, swords came with scabbards, but the Heavenly Demon’s sword did not.","Either it had never had one to begin with, or she had simply forgotten to include it when she gave me the sword.","I was planning to trade fasting pills with her soon anyway, so I could ask through the one-on-one chat.","Tug!","\"Hm?\"","My eyes widened.","It seemed firmly embedded and wouldn’t come out easily.","No, wait.","As far as I knew, mushrooms didn’t have roots.","So it was simply stuck.","\"GRAAAAH!\"","Pop!","Only after putting almost all my strength into it did I finally manage to pull it free.","The recoil nearly made me fall backward, but I barely managed to regain my balance.","Then I looked at the spot where it had been growing and noticed a round hole in the ground.","Was it growing here for a really long time?","Apparently, it had stayed there long enough to bore a hole into solid stone.","I carefully carried the golden mushroom outside with both hands.","The moment I stepped out, a rich, savory aroma tickled my nose.","It was coming from the charred remains of Muscle Mushroom.","\"Let’s get out of here.\"","I hurried away before some beast was attracted by the smell.","Part of me wanted to poke around inside the cave with the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","But any further curiosity might genuinely put my life in danger.","It was better to restrain myself.","Throb!","As I hurried along, a sudden headache struck me.","I frowned at the unexpected pain, but it wasn’t something I could easily ignore.","\"What is this?\"","Even while grimacing, I kept moving.","The headache disappeared before long, but the uneasy feeling remained.","Maybe the golden mushroom was the cause.","I should probably get back to the shelter as quickly as possible.","At least nothing attacked me on the way back.","After arriving at the shelter, I examined the golden mushroom again.","It really was huge.","And I was curious about what exactly it was.","I took a photo of the mushroom and posted it on the gallery.","Title: Anyone know this mushroom?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the golden mushroom compared to a hand)","Found this in the cave Muscle Mushroom was blocking.","It shines this beautiful golden color. It’s poisonous, right? It’s also freaking huge.","└ Starlight Princess) What a pretty mushroom. But you really shouldn’t eat mushrooms.","└ Wild Grylls) I only brought it back because it looked interesting. I have absolutely no intention of eating it.","└ Eat that and I’ll give you 100 billion euros lol.","└ I’ll give you 100,000 gold lmao.","└ Starlight Princess) You people are terrible.","└ PraiseTheSun) Look at that brilliant glow. You found it in a cave?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah. It was really hard to pull out too.","└ PraiseTheSun) That thing looks like it’s literally advertising, \"I’m poisonous.\"","└ Wild Grylls) That’s why I’m thinking about keeping it as decoration.","└ PraiseTheSun) Wouldn’t be bad as an ornament.","But everyone only commented on how pretty it was.","Apparently, none of them knew what the mushroom actually was.","That left only one person.","Allfather.","└ Allfather) Hoho. You’ve found another unusual thing this time.","└ Wild Grylls) Do you know what this mushroom is?","└ Allfather) Of course I do. Throw it away immediately.","└ Wild Grylls) Huh?","A comment telling me to get rid of it immediately appeared.","Naturally, I couldn’t help but wonder why.","Then Allfather’s following comment hit me with quite a shock.","Everyone else had simply thought the golden mushroom looked fascinating.","└ Allfather) Did you experience any headaches or dizziness while bringing it back?","└ Wild Grylls) I did get a slight headache, but it disappeared right away.","└ Allfather) It seems the medicine I gave you before was effective. Simply being near it should normally cause symptoms.","└ Wild Grylls) What kind of mushroom is this?","└ Allfather) Its name is quite ordinary. It’s called the Golden Mushroom. It’s one of the rarest mushrooms in existence and is sometimes called the King of Mushrooms.","As expected of the Forest of Four Seasons.","It truly was a place inhabited by all sorts of bizarre plants and animals.","This thing was even called the King of Mushrooms.","I became curious about exactly what made it a \"king.\"","└ Wild Grylls) If it’s the king, doesn’t that mean it’s good?","└ Allfather) With mushrooms, that title carries both positive and negative meanings. Which would you like to hear first?","└ Wild Grylls) Tell me the negative part first.","└ Allfather) A single bite will cause all your internal organs to melt. Your bones and muscles as well.","└ Wild Grylls) ;;;","That sounded horrifying just from reading it.","Not only your bones and muscles, but even your organs would melt?","Even drinking a bucket of hydrochloric acid probably wouldn’t do that much damage.","That meant the mushroom contained an unimaginably potent poison.","Naturally, I wanted to stay far away from it.","└ Wild Grylls) What’s the positive part?","└ Allfather) If you’re lucky, those melted organs, bones, and muscles can be restored. And not merely restored—your entire body would advance several stages beyond what it was before.","└ Isn’t that basically Body Reformation?","└ From the sound of it, yeah.","└ Allfather) It isn’t merely Body Reformation. According to legend, one can obtain the body of a god.","└ Wild Grylls) Whoa.","So there was a reason it was called the King of Mushrooms.","High risk, high reward.","Which meant I definitely wasn’t eating it.","There was absolutely no reason for me to take that gamble.","Just imagining my entire body melting was horrifying enough.","└ Allfather) It would likely be dangerous even for someone with complete immunity to poison. I recommend throwing it away.","└ Wild Grylls) So even poison immunity doesn’t matter?","└ Allfather) According to legend, the odds are fifty-fifty. It makes no distinction between people.","└ Wild Grylls) Guess I should throw it away, then. Unless you want it for research?","└ Why don’t you give it to us?","└ I’ll eat it and tell you what happens.","└ Do you seriously not value your life?","└ My life’s already ruined, so I might as well try eating that thing lol.","└ Why is your life ruined?","└ I went all-in on Kaspel Mine stock and got wiped out.","└ Why?","└ The mine collapsed.","└ Ah... damn. Hang in there.","└ Heavenly Demon) It is certainly intriguing, but it seems far too dangerous. This lady is not particularly interested either.","└ SwordMaster) Scared?","└ Heavenly Demon) Hm. I suddenly feel like bringing down the banhammer.","└ SwordMaster) Shit ;;","└ Lmaoooo, she’s already getting drunk on power.","└ Isn’t she going to develop bad habits like this?","└ The head mod will deal with it somehow.","└ Passing Dwarf) Can’t you make alcohol out of that?","└ Wild Grylls) Probably not with mushrooms. There was a guy who died after drinking water he’d boiled mushrooms in.","└ Passing Dwarf) Who was that? What a fucking idiot.","└ Wild Grylls) My father, asshole.","└ Passing Dwarf) Ah. I’m seriously sorry ;;","└ Wild Grylls) I’m kidding lol. My dad died in an accident.","└ Passing Dwarf) You bastard.","└ Passing Dwarf) No, wait ;; sorry. I’m just sorry ;;","└ He sobered up the second he cursed at him lmaoooo.","└ That panic lmaooo.","└ PraiseTheSun) Can’t you at least keep it as decoration?","└ Wild Grylls) Apparently just being near it causes headaches and dizziness.","└ PraiseTheSun) Then put it behind glass. I really like the golden color.","└ Allfather) Forgive me for saying so, but I believe researching it would be far more valuable. If you give it to me, I’ll compensate you well enough that you won’t feel disappointed.","└ PraiseTheSun) I can make sure you’re not disappointed either. How much money do you need?","└ Wild Grylls) I don’t really need money, though...","At the moment, money was the one thing I had in abundance.","The owlbear corpse alone had left me quite well-off.","The real problem was that even with plenty of money, I still couldn’t buy most of the things I actually needed.","PraiseTheSun seemed to realize that too and immediately left another comment.","└ PraiseTheSun) Now that I think about it, you’re right. Is there anything you want?","└ Wild Grylls) I want to get out of here.","└ PraiseTheSun) Uh... sorry. Don’t think I can help with that. Just give the mushroom to that mage.","└ Allfather) I don’t seem to have anything particularly suitable to give you either. Is there anything you need?","There they go fighting again.","Why are these people always so eager to tear into each other?","But as everyone knew, the Heavenly Demon was currently a sub-mod.","And sub-mods had the authority to ban people too.","I couldn’t put the Golden Mushroom up on the auction house either.","I didn’t want to hear the next day that someone had eaten it and died.","But selling it for money also felt awkward.","The risk was simply too high.","It was, quite literally, more trouble than it was worth.","After thinking for a while, I left another comment.","└ Wild Grylls) If anything, maybe armor? I think that’d be useful.","└ SwordMaster) That’s a good idea. Since you’re in a forest, leather armor would probably be better than metal armor.","└ Heavenly Demon) Rather than that, why not learn protective qi?","└ Wild Grylls) How do I use that?","└ SwordMaster) Grylls still can’t even use an Aura Blade. It’ll be a long time before he can use an Aura Shield.","└ Heavenly Demon) It is not an Aura Blade, but Sword Force. And it is not an Aura Shield, but protective qi.","└ SwordMaster) Same thing. Do you really have to nitpick every time?","└ Heavenly Demon) What did you say? To this lady, that sounded very much like you were asking for the banhammer.","└ SwordMaster) Ha, shit ;; That’s seriously too much. Head mod, are you watching this?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) Sub-mod! Please restrain yourself a little!","└ Heavenly Demon) Hm. Very well. This lady shall overlook it out of her boundless generosity.","└ SwordMaster) ;;","└ Princess Chaenggu) Huh? Why do you need armor? I already gave you a uniform!","└ Wild Grylls) This thing actually provides protection?","└ Princess Chaenggu) That’s hurtful! The uniforms developed by Mephisto perform even better than leather armor!","└ Wild Grylls) Seriously?","└ That’s actually true. Sometimes people even wear the uniform into dungeons lol.","└ It’s expensive, but it’s more convenient and performs better than leather armor.","└ Wild Grylls) Why is it made like that?","└ Because there were way too many people stabbing each other.","└ It’s for protecting the players. Sports are basically miniature battlefields here.","└ You’d probably be fine even after getting hit by a magic arrow lmao.","└ Wild Grylls) ;;","Apparently, no matter how advanced the culture was, the savagery of the era still showed through.","Just in case, I looked for another uniform.","I couldn’t exactly test it with the Heavenly Demon’s sword, so I used an ordinary dagger.","Scrape! Scrape!","\"Oh.\"","Even after dragging the dagger firmly across the uniform several times, it remained intact.","Curious, I stretched the uniform taut and stabbed at it with the dagger.","Still nothing.","This was perfect for me.","Beasts are dangerous in the forest, but minor injuries are even more dangerous.","Even a tiny cut could cause serious trouble if poison or germs got inside.","That said, the uniform was still far too thin despite its performance.","If I wore leather armor over it, the protection would probably be even better.","└ Wild Grylls) The uniform really is good. Still, I think I should have leather armor too, just in case. This is too thin.","└ Princess Chaenggu) Then how about wearing several uniforms on top of each other?","└ Wild Grylls) Are you a genius?","└ Princess Chaenggu) Hehe. I’m pretty smart.","└ Sure. Still an idiot who cheers for Chaeyu though lol.","└ Just wear the uniforms lol. Whatever the hell you put on, you’ll probably die in one hit anyway.","└ One hit and you’re off to join Aragon~","In the end, even the extra armor was replaced with more uniforms.","Afterward, I tried offering the mushroom to Princess Chaenggu, but she immediately refused.","She had no interest in buying it as decoration either and simply said she’d give me a few more uniforms.","I’m receiving way too much from this person.","She said supporting her team was enough, but I still felt guilty.","If I found something good later, I was definitely giving it to her.","Anyway, I decided to postpone figuring out what to do with the Golden Mushroom.","It was such a high-risk item that its position was awkward.","Wonmo might eat it too...","I needed to store it somewhere as inconspicuous as possible.","Granted, something golden would stand out no matter where I put it, but I had somewhere in mind.","The box that had come with the items the dwarf gave me last time.","I stored the mushroom inside it.","Then, so Wonmo’s sharp sense of smell wouldn’t pick it up, I placed the box outside the cave.","The elixirs were stored in a different box, so there wasn’t much of a problem.","If I ran low on them, I could just buy more from the auction house.","Good. That’s settled.","With the Golden Mushroom dealt with, I raised my head.","The sun had already begun to sink, if only slightly.","It looked like I should start preparing for the night.","There might be spores on my clothes, so I should wash immediately.","And just like that, another day came to an end.","***","Deep in the night, when everyone was asleep, only the sounds of insects filled the forest.","Inside the cave, the faint crackling of the campfire could be heard.","Beyond that were the quiet breathing of a person, the breathing of beasts, and other gentle sounds.","Everyone was asleep in their own way.","It was an extremely peaceful scene.","Clatter! Clatter!","A rough noise suddenly broke through the silence.","It wasn’t coming from inside the cave.","It came from the box outside.","The box continued rattling several times before eventually toppling onto its side.","Roll—","Its contents spilled out.","Among them was the mushroom that glowed golden even beneath the darkness of night.","Rustle—","Amazingly, the Golden Mushroom, which had fallen onto its side, pushed itself upright.","Tiny arms and legs had sprouted from its body.","They were infinitely more pitiful and adorable than the limbs of Muscle Mushroom.","But the fact that it had limbs meant one thing.","It could move.","Pitter-patter-pitter-patter—","The Golden Mushroom moved its short little legs and headed into the dark forest.","Quietly.","Secretly.","So that no one would ever find it.","Until the Golden Mushroom completely disappeared, nothing but peaceful breathing could be heard from the cave.","Time passed.","Morning came.","\"What the hell? Where’d the mushroom go?\"","Only then did Grylls realize the mushroom had disappeared.","He had already sensed something was wrong when he saw the box outside lying on its side.","When he immediately checked inside—","the Golden Mushroom he had stored there was gone.","\"N-No way...!\"","Grylls’s eyes widened.","He thought he knew why the mushroom had disappeared.","He stopped rummaging through the box and hurried back into the cave.","\"Wonmo! Open your mouth!\"","\"Kkyuu...?\"","\"What did you eat yesterday? You didn’t eat the mushroom, did you?!\"","Grylls forcibly opened poor Wonmo’s beak for no reason.","Fortunately, Wonmo hadn’t eaten the mushroom.","He had simply slept peacefully through the night.","After thoroughly checking him over, Grylls sighed in relief.","He didn’t bother inspecting Tree Sloth separately.","That creature had absurdly sharp instincts and hadn’t gone anywhere near the mushroom in the first place.","Relieved, Grylls was left with a new question.","\"No, seriously. It’s not like the thing had legs. Where the hell did it go?\"","It actually had grown legs.","Grylls simply had no idea.","Such was the mysterious Forest of Four Seasons."]},{"title":"Chapter 41","paragraphs":["Scammer (2)","It was enough to make a ghost wail in disbelief.","I stared at the empty box.","No matter how many times I searched through it, the golden mushroom was nowhere to be found.","Wonmo hadn’t secretly eaten it either.","Unless it had somehow grown arms and legs, it had practically vanished on its own.","I couldn’t make sense of it at all.","’Did some thieving bastard like the Tree Sloth steal it?’","I stared at the Tree Sloth.","It had one of the fasting pills I had given it hooked on its claw and was nibbling away at it.","I wasn’t saying that thing had eaten the golden mushroom.","If something had eaten it, it was probably some other animal.","The Tree Sloth had tried stealing fish before.","It had failed, though.","Considering that, there were probably beasts out there that specifically targeted plants and animals rich in nutrients.","’Even so, wouldn’t the golden mushroom be way too risky?’","Even wild animals generally avoided mushrooms.","And the golden mushroom practically screamed:","I’m poisonous! Eat me and you’ll die!","Bright colors usually meant deadly poison.","Animals knew that much too.","Even if something had eaten it, there should have been some traces left behind.","The mystery refused to clear up.","’Strange.’","Then again, maybe this was for the best.","I had already been wondering what I was supposed to do with it.","Still, since there were people who wanted the golden mushroom, I made a post on the Gallery.","Title: Mushroom Disappeared","Wild Grylls","(Photo of an empty box)","I put the mushroom I picked up yesterday in this box, but when I woke up today, it was gone ;;","I thought maybe Wonmo ate it, but apparently not.","This is seriously weird.","└ Heavenly Demon: To think a mushroom escaped. Truly astonishing. Did it perhaps grow feet?","└ Wild Grylls: I’m not sure either. I looked around, but I can’t even find footprints.","└ Heavenly Demon: Surely a mushroom cannot perform Void-Stepping.","└ Wild Grylls: What’s Void-Stepping now?","└ Heavenly Demon: It is a technique that allows one to walk or run through empty air. The pinnacle of lightness techniques.","└ Wild Grylls: Can you do that too, Heavenly Demon?","└ Heavenly Demon: This Lady has surpassed mere Void-Stepping and reached the realm of Treading the Empty Sky. I can fly freely through the heavens.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh ;;","└ SwordMaster: Aren’t you exaggerating a little too much? If you’re really at that level, wouldn’t that be Grand Master territory?","└ Heavenly Demon: What does that mean? Explain it in terms this Lady can understand.","└ Wouldn’t that be equivalent to the Profound Realm in the Central Plains?","└ Probably around there. Has anyone in the Central Plains even reached the Profound Realm?","└ You’d probably have to dig through historical records to find one.","└ Even someone in the Transformation Realm could destroy an entire city, so the Profound Realm is just lol.","└ Heavenly Demon: I understand. This Lady has reached that so-called Profound Realm.","└ SwordMaster: Yes, yes~ I’m sure you have.","└ Allfather: Perhaps the mushroom really did have legs.","└ Wild Grylls: Seriously?","└ Allfather: Considering muscular mushrooms exist, arms and legs would practically be standard equipment for a golden mushroom.","└ Wild Grylls: But it was completely still when I caught it?","└ Allfather: It would be a mistake to judge the laws of nature by your common sense, Mr. Grylls. Think of the Tree Sloth.","└ Wild Grylls: Ah.","After hearing the wisdom of the sage Allfather, I realized something.","Maybe it really did have legs.","This world was fantasy.","And the Forest of Four Seasons was a place where even the common sense of people from this world didn’t apply.","And I was stuck suffering there.","Putting it that way made me a little sad.","Anyway, no matter what happened, I couldn’t afford to judge things by common sense.","I didn’t even need to look far.","There was a sloth around here that could snatch arrows out of the air.","└ Wild Grylls: Guess I should just consider it lost.","└ Allfather: A shame. I wanted to study it.","It was unfortunate, but there was nothing I could do.","It had happened because of carelessness that wasn’t exactly carelessness.","I should probably just be thankful that nobody had raided me in the middle of the night.","I closed the Gallery and approached the hose to wash my face.","Trickle, trickle—","The stream of water coming through the hose was weak.","The moment I saw it, I realized what had happened.","Another fish had been caught.","Apparently, one got stuck at least once every day.","This was great.","’Once I get a fish trap from the dwarf too, I won’t have to worry about food anymore.’","It looked like I could stop worrying about food for the time being.","I was planning to set more traps soon too, so things would only become more plentiful.","If I learned even a half-decent method of hunting, starving to death probably wouldn’t be an issue.","I’d die from poison, disease, or getting eaten by a beast instead.","Or maybe I’d step into some bizarre place and die a pointless death.","There were plenty of ways to die.","’...Right. Better than starving, I guess?’","I suddenly felt depressed, but quickly shook it off.","The important thing was the fish.","I gathered the necessary gear and headed toward the river.","I didn’t forget to feed Wonmo before leaving.","Splash! Splash!","When I eventually reached the river, just as I expected, a fish was trapped in the narrow passage.","It was huge, large enough to completely block the hose’s intake.","Until now, the fish I had caught had all been red.","This one was golden.","’...Does this one have poison too?’","The only poisonous fish I knew of was the pufferfish.","And as far as I knew, even those lived in the ocean.","’It doesn’t have spines either.’","More importantly, there were no spines.","Its body was completely smooth.","It was golden, but it wasn’t covered in flashy multicolored patterns.","After thinking about it for a moment, I decided to take it back as it was.","If I stayed here too long and the golden frog showed up, things would get troublesome.","\"Heave-ho.\"","This one was big enough that I had to wrap both arms around it too.","Were all the fish living in the Forest of Four Seasons this huge?","From my perspective, that was nothing but a blessing.","It meant I could eat my fill.","’I should bring a big container with me from now on.’","I made plans while wrestling with the thrashing golden fish.","For convenience, I really needed at least a container or a net.","It wasn’t because I lacked strength.","The fish was simply so large that I needed both hands to carry it.","’Or I could bring the Tree Sloth.’","The Tree Sloth was surprisingly useful.","It was practically perfect as a bodyguard.","I returned to the cave and started preparing my meal.","I was getting used to cleaning fish by now, so it didn’t take long.","’Another one?’","Out of curiosity, I searched through the organs.","Sure enough, there was another inner core.","This time, instead of red, the inner core was closer to golden in color.","Did every fish living in the Forest of Four Seasons carry an inner core?","This wasn’t just once or twice anymore.","It was already the third time.","I was seriously starting to suspect something.","’Doesn’t this mean I can become stronger just by eating fish? Then why is the survival rate here supposedly so atrocious?’","While the fish grilled to a golden brown, I stared at the inner core.","The Heavenly Demon had said they were more like inferior versions of elixirs, but an inner core was still an inner core.","The fact that eating one could make me stronger in a short amount of time hadn’t changed.","’Maybe it’s because you still can’t escape, regardless of how strong you become?’","That seemed highly likely.","What good was getting stronger if you couldn’t get out?","’And I’m an unusual case too.’","More importantly, I was an unusual case.","I could still use the Gallery perfectly fine despite being trapped in the Forest of Four Seasons.","Unlike everyone else, I could at least ask for advice.","Other people had nothing like that.","They were basically smashing their heads against a wall with no information whatsoever.","Even I would have been torn to pieces by the Mad Dog if I hadn’t had the Gallery.","’I should flip the fish.’","At this rate, it was going to burn.","I flipped the fish cooking on the broad stone slab.","I could decide what to do with the inner core later.","There was no rush.","If nothing else worked, I could always put it up on the auction house.","The Heavenly Demon had advised me not to eat one until I reached at least the Peak Realm.","’I don’t even know exactly how strong the Peak Realm is.’","More importantly, my fundamentals were still lacking.","Right now, strengthening my foundation was more important.","Eating the inner core probably wouldn’t hurt me permanently, but I could end up bedridden and feverish for several days.","For someone whose survival was the top priority, a high fever was extremely dangerous.","I had felt how serious it was the last time I suffered from one.","’Come to think of it, the auction should be ending soon.’","The thought occurred to me while I tore into the deliciously grilled fish.","I had listed it around lunchtime yesterday, so the auction should finish in a few hours.","[Inner Core: 750 silver taels]","The price had risen considerably.","Judging by how much the frequency of new bids had slowed, there was a good chance it would stay around that amount.","’Trust really is important, huh?’","The auction house had a review system.","There was no numerical rating, but by reading reviews, you could more or less judge how trustworthy someone was.","Without something like that, the auction house would have become a paradise for scammers.","And considering the brutal transaction fees, scamming people wasn’t exactly a smart idea anyway.","’For me, trust is everything.’","Once trust was lost, it was difficult to recover.","For someone like me who obtained most things through the Gallery, losing credibility would be devastating.","And this wasn’t some tiny amount of money either.","It was an enormous sum.","I couldn’t afford to treat it like a joke.","’Even if what I gave the Heavenly Demon really was an inner core, if the one on the auction house isn’t...’","There was a high probability that it really was an inner core.","Still, I couldn’t completely rule out the possibility that someone was lying.","You might say I distrusted people too much, but at the very least, I didn’t trust anonymous users.","When I first fell into the Forest of Four Seasons, there had even been bastards telling me to die and become fertilizer.","That said everything.","A person’s true malice emerged when they could hide behind anonymity.","’Let’s see how the auction turns out first.’","For now, what mattered was eating this delicious fish.","I gave Wonmo a few chunks of meat and finished off the rest.","It tasted far better than the red fish.","I wasn’t exaggerating when I said it tasted almost like pork.","\"Now that was filling.\"","After finishing off such a huge catch, I entered the cave and began circulating my cultivation technique.","It was the method I practiced based on the fundamentals the Heavenly Demon had taught me and SwordMaster’s advice.","Was it because I had just eaten the golden fish?","I could feel an energy like raging waves coursing through my body.","’Rather than waves... what should I call it? A storm?’","The cultivation technique the Heavenly Demon had taught me was called the Heavenly Demon Divine Art.","So maybe it was more appropriate to describe the sensation as a storm rather than waves.","Eventually, I brought that storm-like energy completely under control and raised my hand.","A faint blue energy shimmered above it like heat haze.","’It amazes me every time I see it.’","I had definitely been an ordinary person.","A completely average man with nothing particularly remarkable about him.","And yet I had somehow fallen into this bizarre forest, and now I could even manipulate mana.","I constantly reminded myself that this place was reality, but sometimes I still wondered.","Was I actually dreaming?","The haze rising from my hand was fantasy itself.","That only made the feeling stronger.","’Considering what it felt like when the Mad Dog bit me, this is definitely real.’","I extinguished the haze and stepped outside the cave.","I planned to spend the morning making traps and exploring.","As for where I would explore—","The muscular mushrooms I had burned yesterday with fire magic (physical), and the cave they had come from.","Continuing with the same glossary and style, including Wild Grylls, Heavenly Demon, SwordMaster, Allfather, Forest of Four Seasons, Tree Sloth, Wonmo, inner core, Gallery , and the established martial-arts terminology.","If the golden mushroom really had grown two legs and run away, there was a chance it had gone back to the cave.","Title: Want to Make a Trap, Any Advice?","Wild Grylls","I found a place where rabbits show up yesterday. Anyone know how to make a decent trap?","They’re not ordinary rabbits, though. Their back kicks are insanely strong, so take that into consideration.","└ Why not just buy a bear trap and set it up?","└ If you use a bear trap, a rabbit will just get split in half ;;","└ Just dig a decent-sized pit and stick spears in it.","└ That’s dangerous. Better to aim for capturing them alive rather than using something lethal.","As expected of the Gallery.","They generously shared all kinds of useful tips.","└ Why don’t you use yourself as bait? You might catch a big one that way lol.","└ Sounds fun lol.","└ If you fail, you die. If you succeed, you feast. Isn’t that perfect?!","As expected of the Gallery.","Idiots and morons appeared occasionally—","No, frequently.","I ignored all the nonsense and started designing a trap.","The best option seemed to be a pitfall.","Dig a hole and cover it with a board.","Once enough weight was placed on top of it, the board would give way and whatever stepped on it would fall into the pit.","’Considering how powerful those rabbits’ back kicks are, they’d jump right out of a shallow pit.’","Digging the pit deep enough was important, but the board covering it mattered just as much.","I didn’t want the board to simply collapse and fall into the pit.","I wanted a trap that worked through weight.","’Step on the board, the board opens, you fall into the pit, and then the board closes again.’","This seemed like the best method.","I decided on that design.","Of course, choosing a design and actually building it were two different things.","I squeezed my brain as hard as I could while planning the mechanism.","’The board has to open and close depending on the weight. I need to account for the rabbit’s weight too.’","Securing the board in place was essential.","I bought some large iron nails from the auction house.","I planned to use them to anchor one side of the board.","’And I’ll need a counterweight to pull the board back up.’","I set up two sturdy branches and placed another branch horizontally between them.","The easiest way to picture it was like a rotisserie barbecue.","The kind where you put meat on a spit and rotate it while roasting.","This wasn’t a barbecue, though.","It was a trap.","So instead of meat, I fitted a metal cylinder onto it.","Finally, I tied a rock to a cord to serve as the counterweight.","Clunk!","I pressed down firmly on the board with one finger.","It lowered.","The instant I removed my finger, the counterweight pulled the board back up.","Perfect.","The trap was complete.","Now all I had to do was move this design over there.","’Though I’ll need to make it bigger.’","For that, aside from the nails and hammer, I would have to make several trips back and forth.","I told the Tree Sloth to guard the house properly and finished preparing.","A weapon to protect myself.","A shovel for digging.","An elixir in case something went wrong.","And various other necessities.","Once everything was ready, I headed toward the area where the rabbits appeared.","’After moving the trap, I should check whether the mushroom is there first.’","Unfortunately, the golden mushroom wasn’t inside the cave.","The muscular mushrooms that had been burned completely black were still there too.","Apparently, despite their appetizing smell, they still looked too suspicious to eat.","Now that I had checked for the mushroom, only the trap remained.","Digging the pit wasn’t particularly difficult either.","A while later, after finishing the entire trap setup, an indescribable sense of accomplishment washed over me.","Soon, I would finally be able to eat meat instead of fish.","’As for butchering it... well, I’ll have to do that myself.’","To prevent the animals from becoming suspicious, I scattered some dirt over the board and even placed grass on top.","Now all that remained was patience.","I gathered all my equipment and returned to the cave.","’It’s already eleven.’","Time had flown while I was busy doing this and that.","I wondered what I should do until the inner core auction ended, then rummaged through my pocket.","The golden inner core came out.","I briefly considered putting this one on the auction house too.","’Let’s see how the first auction turns out before listing this one. Before that...’","Grrrrrgle—","My stomach hurt like hell.","It happened every time I ate fish.","Previously, my stomach had started hurting almost immediately after eating, but this time it had taken a while.","I really needed to build a toilet soon.","Digging a hole every single time was becoming exhausting.","After thoroughly emptying my bowels, I logged into the Gallery.","I wanted to check the current bid on the inner core.","[Inner Core: 750 silver taels]","The bid hadn’t changed.","It had been frozen at that amount for six hours.","I had a feeling the auction would probably end like this.","So I modified the remaining auction time.","[Would you like to change the auction end time to 30 minutes from now?]","[Once the deadline has been modified, it cannot be changed again.]","I accepted without hesitation.","Thirty minutes was still plenty of time.","And what was I going to do during those thirty minutes?","Practice my cultivation technique.","Not recklessly, either.","I planned to firmly establish my fundamentals, just as the Heavenly Demon had taught me.","If I somehow patched all the holes in my foundation, it would probably become easier to obtain something like an Aura Blade or Sword Gang or whatever it was called.","’This is hard. Really hard.’","Fundamentals weren’t something you simply memorized.","You had to understand them.","That was the hardest part for me, since I wasn’t originally from this world.","Even though I had grown stronger until now through what could almost be called shortcuts, the basics were still a problem.","’Just thirty minutes of practice.’","It took more than an hour.","Once I became immersed in it, I completely lost track of time.","And unless I logged into the Gallery, my sense of time became especially vague.","So I opened the Gallery to see how much the inner core had sold for.","[Why Grylls Is a Scammer]","[Grylls, Explain Yourself!]","[Grylls, Explain Yourself!]","[This bastard is just a scammer lol]","[Isn’t the whole \"I’m in the Forest of Four Seasons\" thing a lie too?]","[Honestly, I think he should be banned.]","[Upvote if Grylls is dead lol]","\"What the hell?\"","What had happened for the Gallery to become this much of a dumpster fire?","And most of the posts were about me.","I couldn’t understand it at all.","The easiest thing to do was check the trending posts.","Something must have been posted there to cause all this.","[Wild Grylls Is a Scammer. Don’t Trust This Bastard.]","It was the trending post with the highest number of upvotes.","Naturally, it was about me.","There was no way I could just ignore a title like that.","I opened it immediately.","Title: Wild Grylls Is a Scammer. Don’t Trust This Bastard.","(Photo of an inner core resting on someone’s palm)","This is supposed to be an inner core? LMAOOOO what kind of bullshit is this?","It’s just a normal marble.","I’m actually legendary for paying 750 silver taels for this shit.","You can’t trust this Grylls bastard.","Take responsibility, you son of a bitch.","Give me my money back.","└ Didn’t Heavenly Demon say it was real?","└ And you believed that? LMAO.","└ It was kind of weird that an inner core came out every time he caught a fish though~","└ I’m never buying anything from Grylls again lol.","└ You never bought anything from him in the first place.","└ Exactly lol.","└ Is this bastard some kind of scammer?","└ Are we sure this guy is actually the buyer?","└ Yeah. The number beside his name matches the winning bidder.","└ Holy shit lol. How much did he lose? LMAO.","└ At that price, he probably blew his entire fortune lol.","└ Damn. Poor bastard lol.","└ Shouldn’t Grylls refund him?","└ What about the transaction fee?","└ Why should that matter? If you scammed someone, you should return all the money, dumbass.","└ Doesn’t the Moderator ban people for scamming?","└ Yeah. Permanent ban at minimum.","Just what exactly are you trying to do?","’Is he going to ban me?’","***","I had suspected it.","And sure enough, things unfolded exactly as I feared.","Apparently, I had trusted people too much.","Fortunately, this was at least one of the possibilities I had already anticipated.","I was just about to leave a comment when—","[Heavenly Demon: You need not worry, sir. This Lady shall resolve the matter.]","[Wild Grylls: What?]","[Heavenly Demon: That ungrateful wretch requires divine punishment. Wait there.]","A private message from the Heavenly Demon arrived.","The strategist and brains of the Demonic Cult.","The Demon Brain was currently extremely confused.","Being summoned by the Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol, wasn’t particularly confusing.","When Heaven called, one naturally answered.","But even the Demon Brain, famed throughout the world for his intellect, couldn’t help being flustered by the order Heaven itself had just given him.","\"H-Heavenly One. May I... ask you to repeat what you just said?\"","\"How strange for you to ask twice. Very well. In this Lady’s boundless generosity, I shall command you once more.\"","Yu Sowol, seated upon her jade throne, spoke in a deliberately irritated tone.","\"Log into the Gallery.\"","\"...\"","\"You ate the inner core this Lady gave you and advanced in your realm. All you need do is make a post proving it.\"","In other words, she wanted him to log into the Gallery and upload what people commonly called a verification post .","On the surface, it sounded extremely simple.","But who was the Demon Brain?","Wasn’t he a hardcore Gallery addict who spent most of his time there insulting his superior—the Heavenly Demon?","’I’m fucked.’","The Demon Brain.","The Clever Demonic Cultist.","Wi Seorak.","’I’m seriously fucked.’","He had found himself in a life-or-death crisis."]},{"title":"Chapter 42","paragraphs":["Scammer (3)","The Demon Brain, Wi Seorak, had survived countless crises throughout his life.","The greatest among them had been the oppression of those in power.","With his extraordinary intellect, Wi Seorak was a threat to them.","A mere commoner like Wi Seorak being vastly superior to the proud scions of prestigious families?","That was something they could never tolerate.","So whenever they found an opportunity, they kicked away the ladder beneath him.","But Wi Seorak had clawed his way upward through sheer spite and grit.","He had never needed a ladder in the first place.","By this point, one might have expected them to acknowledge him.","Unfortunately, Wi Seorak had terrible luck with people.","All that came back to him was even more vicious oppression.","And through that process, bitterness took root inside him.","Carrying that bitterness with him, he entered the Demonic Cult and used his exceptional mind to rise all the way to the position of Demon Brain.","\"Why are you acting like that? Do you perhaps use the Gallery as well?\"","\"That is...\"","And today, Wi Seorak found himself facing yet another crisis of a lifetime.","It was an order from the Heavenly Demon, the one who stood above all men and beneath only the heavens.","Wi Seorak’s mind spun furiously as he processed the Heavenly Demon’s command.","And after all that frantic calculation, he arrived at a single conclusion.","’I’m fucked.’","He was seriously screwed.","For an utterly ridiculous reason, he had come face-to-face with the greatest crisis of his life.","Since Wi Seorak himself was an avid Gallery user, he understood the current situation perfectly well.","The inner core listed on the auction house had supposedly been fake.","And the incident involved Wild Grylls, the man who had recently caused one uproar after another.","’Wild Grylls. She must have stepped in to help him.’","Yu Sowol had obviously summoned him because she wanted to help Wild Grylls.","That much, Wi Seorak could have predicted.","But ordering him to log into the Gallery was completely outside his expectations.","Wi Seorak rapidly worked his mind and opened his mouth.","If even a single second of silence passed, Yu Sowol might grow suspicious.","\"Heavenly One, by the Gallery... do you mean the Continental Integrated Gallery?\"","\"That is correct.\"","\"As this is Heaven’s command, I shall obey. However, with my foolish mind, I find it difficult to grasp the situation. Please enlighten me as to your reason.\"","Even as he stalled for time, Wi Seorak’s brain never stopped turning.","If he obeyed the order, logged into the Gallery, and uploaded a verification post...","All the posts he had written insulting Yu Sowol would be exposed.","What made matters worse was that he hadn’t been using a semi-anonymous nickname.","He had been using a fully registered account.","’Damn it. I only made a registered account because I needed one, and now it’s come back to bite me like this...’","Why had Wi Seorak used a registered account?","For trading and the auction house.","The Demonic Cult was located in a fairly remote region.","As a result, maintaining a stable supply chain was critically important.","In the old days, the place had been practically abandoned, and quite a few people had gone hungry.","Things had improved considerably only after Wi Seorak restructured everything and Yu Sowol began venturing into the martial world.","’I need to resolve this without getting caught.’","At the time, he had created the account out of necessity and hadn’t thought much of it.","But who could have predicted that Yu Sowol would one day bluntly tell him, \"Reveal your username\"?","It had been Wi Seorak’s mistake not to anticipate just how different her way of thinking was from everyone else’s.","’Will Heaven respect my privacy?’","The Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol, had a domineering and overbearing personality.","She was the type who did whatever she wanted without caring what others thought.","And because she possessed the overwhelming strength to back up that attitude, the demonic practitioners revered her.","’She has to. Otherwise, I’m dead.’","On the other hand, the Heavenly Demon on the Gallery was subtly different.","Her characteristic arrogance and self-centered nature were still there, but she had a certain humanity to her.","One only had to look at how endlessly accommodating she was toward Grylls to see that.","Wi Seorak desperately prayed that some of that consideration would extend to him as well.","Otherwise, he was going to die.","Socially.","And physically.","\"A reason... Must this Lady explain even that much to you?\"","\"...\"","\"Or is there some truth you desperately need to keep hidden from me on the Gallery?\"","\"I do not use the Gallery, Heavenly One.\"","\"You lie without so much as wetting your lips.\"","Fuck.","Wi Seorak cursed internally.","He had spoken while doing his best to keep his voice from trembling, but she had seen through him anyway.","Still, he had no choice but to lie.","Only by doing so could he hope for Yu Sowol’s \"understanding.\"","If Yu Sowol had been a completely unrestrained tyrant, his head would have been flying through the air already.","Fortunately, she was not a tyrant.","At the very least, she knew how to respect those beneath her.","Otherwise, she would have ordered them long ago to force their way into the Forest of Four Seasons.","Of course, asking for understanding after lying to her was already unreasonable.","But if he wanted to grasp even the tiniest possibility of survival, he had no other choice.","The moment he logged into the Gallery, his physical death was practically guaranteed.","This was a gamble with his life as the stake.","\"I shall believe your lie. However, from now on, it would be wise to speak the truth.\"","\"I shall keep that in mind.\"","\"Good. You asked for the reason earlier, did you not? I shall tell you everything.\"","Thank goodness.","Seriously, thank goodness.","Wi Seorak inwardly breathed a sigh of relief.","His life-or-death gamble had ended successfully.","That did not mean the crisis itself was over, however.","\"This Lady’s benefactor is currently being falsely accused. Lend me the wisdom needed to resolve the situation.\"","\"All of this humble one’s wisdom belongs to Heaven. Simply give the command.\"","\"The situation is as follows...\"","Yu Sowol’s explanation was concise yet packed with all the important details.","Of course, Wi Seorak had already pieced together the entire situation, so he was mostly pretending to listen.","Countless hypotheses had already formed in his mind.","Testing and eliminating them one by one would not be difficult.","\"Do you understand?\"","\"I understand. To think there is someone who not only doubts Heaven’s discernment but even dares to spread falsehoods. Such a person deserves divine punishment.\"","Yu Sowol narrowed her eyes at Wi Seorak.","Her gaze seemed to say:","You, of all people, have the right to say that after lying to me just now?","Wi Seorak, who had his waist bowed, couldn’t see her expression.","But he could read the atmosphere well enough.","His conscience wasn’t merely pricking him.","It felt as though someone were repeatedly stabbing it with a dagger.","He did his best to ignore it.","If a single lie was enough to save his life, then it was an absurdly cheap price.","\"May I offer my opinion?\"","\"Speak.\"","\"First, we cannot rule out the possibility that the inner core purchased at auction truly has no effect whatsoever and is merely an ordinary bead. The one given to this humble servant was certainly genuine, but there is no absolute guarantee that the other one was an inner core as well.\"","\"Hmm.\"","Yu Sowol nodded.","In truth, that point had been bothering her too.","It was also why she had let Wi Seorak’s lie slide.","This was not a problem that could be solved through simple assumptions alone.","Yu Sowol had originally planned to first confirm whether Wi Seorak knew about the Gallery, then borrow his wisdom.","It was only because of her characteristically overbearing way of speaking that she had ordered him to reveal his username first, though Yu Sowol herself failed to realize that.","’Looks like he has something to hide.’","In any case, Yu Sowol understood him.","The Gallery was the perfect piece of culture for venting desire and stress.","He had probably done plenty of things there that he would be ashamed to show others.","Every Gallery user was like that.","It was perfectly understandable.","\"Then is there no solution?\"","\"The other side has latched onto uncertainty, so we should make clever use of that same uncertainty. It is ultimately a matter of credibility.\"","\"I would say my benefactor has greater credibility.\"","\"This is not something to take lightly. Gallery users are like jackals. Once they find prey, they tear into it without caring about what came before or after.\"","\"Jackals...\"","Yu Sowol nodded at the comparison.","Whenever something entertaining happened, Gallery users swarmed toward it like madmen.","Whether it was actually true or false didn’t matter.","They simply bit and tore at it because it was entertaining.","Conversely, if they could secure enough credibility, that entire pack of jackals could be turned into allies.","\"The one who framed your benefactor likely has only one objective. To force him into an amicable settlement.\"","\"An amicable settlement?\"","\"If he were suspended from the Gallery, his life itself could be placed in danger. That is what the culprit is exploiting.\"","\"So he is playing games with another person’s life.\"","Yu Sowol looked openly displeased.","If she had her way, she would track down the bastard’s location and beat him into the ground.","But location tracking was a privilege available only to the Moderator.","She doubted the Moderator would grant her that authority.","Especially not in a situation like this.","\"Is there a way to resolve it?\"","\"There is a simple and easy method.\"","\"And what would that be?\"","\"Heaven should make an appearance in the Gallery.\"","The phrase make an appearance in the Gallery sounded ridiculous, but his point was simple.","She should verify her identity on the Gallery.","In other words, she should prove that she really was the Heavenly Demon .","The registered user who had spent all this time posting nonsense—and who had now become a Sub-Moderator—should prove that she was actually the Heavenly Demon in real life.","\"You refused this Lady’s command, yet you dare recommend that this Lady do the same thing. What a contradiction.\"","\"My apologies, Heavenly One.\"","\"Speak your true feelings without a single lie. Do you have no intention of verifying your own identity?\"","\"I would rather hang myself.\"","\"Hmm.\"","So he hated the idea that much.","Yu Sowol nodded.","She had no desire to lose a talent as capable as Wi Seorak for such an absurd reason.","\"Besides, even if I verified my identity, it would likely mean little. They could simply claim that we coordinated our stories in advance.\"","\"I see.\"","\"As for Heaven, perhaps—\"","\"Denied.\"","The answer came from Yu Sowol without the slightest hesitation.","A flat refusal.","Wi Seorak found her reaction puzzling, but he did not dare ask why.","’Is she embarrassed?’","That possibility seemed quite plausible.","After all, he knew all about the Gallery activities of the Sub-Moderator known as Heavenly Demon.","Perhaps that was also why she had been so lenient about his lie.","Empathy was the beginning of understanding.","’Maybe if she reveals her identity, there would be no point in using the Gallery anymore?’","But Wi Seorak’s guess was completely wrong.","Was Yu Sowol refusing to reveal her identity because she was embarrassed?","Absolutely not.","’How could I possibly give up a place where I can act purely on instinct without any formality or dignity whatsoever?’","If anything, Yu Sowol was completely unashamed.","Her manner of speaking and behavior barely changed between reality and the Gallery.","What she treasured was the joy of existing as a single human being , free from the mold of the Heavenly Demon .","Yu Sowol liked that life immensely.","That was precisely why she was reluctant to reveal her identity.","If she had to live as the Heavenly Demon even inside the Gallery, it would become monotonous to the point of boredom.","’There would also be those who approach me only because of this Lady’s prestige.’","Kindness directed not toward a human being , but toward the Heavenly Demon .","That would be no different from reality.","If that happened, she would quit the Gallery immediately.","Therefore, Yu Sowol could never give up her anonymity.","Anonymity was normally used as a shield.","For her, however, it was a means of revealing her true self.","’Though my benefactor doesn’t seem to care who this Lady is anyway.’","That was also one of the reasons she liked Grylls.","His consideration and respect were filled with pure goodwill.","And courtesy.","It was a warmth Yu Sowol had never experienced throughout her entire life.","That was why she wanted to help him.","\"If there is no other choice, this Lady can stake her name upon it. However, I question whether the matter is truly worth that much.\"","\"Your words are most wise.\"","So even the Heavenly Demon was human after all.","She knew how to feel embarrassment.","While Wi Seorak continued along with his not-quite-correct misunderstanding, Yu Sowol opened her elegant lips.","\"Is there another method?\"","\"There is. We simply need to redirect the pack of jackals toward the one who lied. And since your benefactor has already built up credibility, it should be relatively easy.\"","\"Then explain—wait a moment.\"","With those words, Yu Sowol stared into empty space.","Wi Seorak glanced at her behavior and immediately entered the Gallery himself.","Something had definitely happened there.","She wouldn’t have reacted like that otherwise.","’Nothing special happened, though?’","The Gallery looked no different.","It was still filled with posts insulting Grylls.","There were occasionally people defending him, but they were only a small minority.","The posts had practically become spam at this point, enough that even the Moderator had issued a warning.","\"Demon Brain.\"","\"Yes, Heavenly One.\"","\"This Lady’s benefactor says he has obtained another inner core.\"","\"What?\"","Wi Seorak’s head snapped upward.","His widened eyes clearly revealed how startled he was.","But who was Wi Seorak?","He quickly regained his composure and set his mind racing.","A moment later, having reached a conclusion, he offered Yu Sowol a suggestion.","\"Heavenly One. I have thought of a good plan.\"","\"Speak.\"","\"Is there perhaps someone on the Gallery who possesses credibility and skill, while also having no major flaws in their personality?\"","\"Hmm...\"","At that question, Yu Sowol tapped a finger against her cheek before suddenly frowning.","She looked displeased just imagining the person.","Given her appearance, even that expression was beautiful.","\"There is. Why do you ask?\"","\"Because we will need that person’s help. Though I cannot say whether they will actually agree to assist us.\"","\"They will.\"","Yu Sowol answered with certainty.","\"This Lady guarantees it.\"","\"Understood. Then...\"","Wi Seorak bowed even more deeply before making his proposal.","\"Please persuade your benefactor to give the newly discovered inner core to that person as an assistant.\""]},{"title":"Chapter 43","paragraphs":["Scammer (4)","The Gallery could be used by anyone regardless of age, gender, or social status.","Along with anonymity, that was often both its greatest strength and its greatest weakness.","In particular, it was fairly common for scammers to use the Gallery to pull all sorts of cons.","Title: Ah, fuck. I got scammed.","There was some good wild ginseng on the auction house, so I bought it, but it turned out to be ordinary ginseng. Fuck.","└ LMAOOOO, you too? Me too!","└ Ginseng and wild ginseng do look pretty similar lol.","└ This fucking bastard deleted his account immediately.","One-on-one trades were only available to registered users, but the auction house could be used by everyone.","Naturally, that meant there were plenty of criminals—in other words, shameless scammers who had no problem ripping other people off.","Whenever a large amount of money was involved, most people immediately suspected a scam.","After all, most scammers were looking for one big score.","There was no helping the suspicion.","└ Why do scammers even bother scamming? You can’t withdraw Gallery money into the real world anyway.","└ You use that money to buy other stuff. The Gallery has almost everything.","└ Being able to ignore distribution networks is a huge advantage too. You can easily get things from other countries.","└ Don’t they get banned?","└ They do, but it depends on the moderators. Some of them go, \"You want me to ban someone over something that minor? lol,\" and let it slide.","└ At least the current Moderator is better. Scammers get permanently banned on the spot.","└ Couldn’t innocent people get caught up in that?","└ Then the parties involved have to settle it among themselves.","Thanks to that, the number of scams had decreased considerably.","But they had not disappeared entirely.","Title: This fucking registered user is a scammer. Don’t trust him.","(Photo of a bizarre plant)","I planted this using a seed I won for 1,000 gold.","I thought it was some rare plant, but it wasn’t. Fuck.","└ Ugh ;; what the hell is that? A Nepenthes? Why does the flower have teeth? LMAO.","└ Nepenthes don’t have teeth. What the hell even is that thing?","└ Allfather: That is a plant-type monster called a Deathmeros, which only grows in Mephisto. How did you manage to raise one?","└ Fuck, it was a monster lol.","└ Is the OP still alive?","Fortunately, while Don’t Abandon the Hero held moderator authority, scammers were brought down hard.","Even small-scale scams were not forgiven.","Permanent bans were handed out without exception.","That did not mean people were banned blindly, however.","If the parties involved reached an amicable settlement, forgiveness was possible.","What mattered was whether the offender showed genuine remorse.","After determining the truth, that was the next most important issue.","But those who wanted to scam people still did so, and their methods and scale only grew more vicious.","Registered users never scam?","That was complete bullshit.","There were plenty of people in the world willing to build up a registered account just for one huge payout.","Moreover, the winning bid from an auction was deposited immediately.","That was tied directly to the Gallery system itself, so even the Moderator could not interfere with it.","Because of that, people had no choice but to exercise extreme caution with auctions, especially when bidding.","Most users preferred placing small bids whenever possible and generally avoided large amounts.","Unless the seller was a highly reputable registered user, people rarely spent large sums.","Title: What if the Moderator scams people?","└ It doesn’t happen often, but wasn’t there a scammer Moderator about a hundred years ago?","└ A hundred years ago? lol. Must’ve been a demon or an elf.","└ If I remember correctly, it was an elf. Went around claiming stuff was leaves from the World Tree lol.","└ So what happened? It’s hard to remove a Moderator, isn’t it?","└ People just stopped buying anything the Moderator listed. Then at some point the Moderator changed. Probably died after scamming people in real life too.","└ LMAOOO, deserved.","In that way, fraud was a crime the Gallery could never completely eradicate no matter how much people wanted to.","As a result, Gallery users reacted with extreme disgust whenever they saw the word scam .","Rumors that someone had scammed people—","Especially a registered user?","They would condemn them immediately without caring whether the accusation was true.","Even if the person had been falsely accused through manipulation and fabricated claims.","That was simply how the Gallery worked.","\"Heh heh. Idiots.\"","A middle-aged man muttered to himself.","He had the distinctive appearance and clothing of someone from the Central Plains.","His mustache resembled a rat’s whiskers.","Combined with his narrow, slit-like eyes, it gave him a rather treacherous appearance.","\"They’re really so easy to manipulate.\"","The Gallery floated before his eyes.","The entire list was filled with hostility and condemnation directed at Grylls.","A single small post written by this man had created an enormous ripple.","\"He won’t be able to hold out much longer without agreeing to a settlement.\"","The man was a merchant.","Just one of the countless small and mid-sized merchants scattered across the Central Plains.","But after winning the item Grylls had listed this time, he had stumbled upon a tremendous opportunity.","Rattle.","The merchant looked away from the Gallery and opened a desk drawer.","Inside were various documents and a small ring box.","Click—","He carefully opened the case.","A faint mist carrying a trace of cold air drifted outward.","Inside rested a bead that shone brilliantly with a crimson glow.","It was the item the man had won through the Gallery auction house.","An inner core.","’I never thought it would actually be a real inner core.’","He had confirmed it through several rounds of appraisal.","There was no doubt.","This was an inner core.","It might not be one of those legendary inner cores spoken of in ancient tales, but it was still at least equivalent to a high-grade elixir.","In monetary terms, it could fetch no less than 1,000 silver taels.","’Heh. As long as I don’t reveal that, there’s no way they can know.’","But the merchant was greedy.","Extremely greedy.","He wasn’t satisfied with merely making a profit.","He wanted to manipulate the situation so that he could recover the money he had spent as well.","Even if Heavenly Demon vouched for Grylls, she was regarded as an eccentric even within the Gallery.","Unless she proved that she was the real Heavenly Demon , her testimony held little weight.","’Agitation and fabrication are easy. Clearing your name is hard.’","The merchant knew the Gallery quite well.","That was why he understood its hypocrisy.","People readily believed agitation and fabricated claims, but explanations were much harder to accept.","And even if Grylls tried to explain himself, with the Gallery already this inflamed, his defense would struggle to gain attention.","’If the Moderator tells him to settle, he’ll have no choice but to accept.’","For Grylls in particular, the Gallery was practically his lifeline.","Without it, his chances of surviving in the Forest of Four Seasons would plummet.","Rather than risk making a poor defense and getting permanently banned, he would be better off accepting a settlement.","Looking at it objectively, the merchant was effectively weighing another person’s life against money.","But he did not care.","’I don’t even know what the bastard looks like.’","His ugly true nature was hidden behind anonymity.","He felt no guilt whatsoever.","Perhaps things would have been different if he knew Grylls personally.","But in the Gallery, kindness was nothing more than a weakness.","Of course, there was always the possibility that Grylls could explain himself successfully and turn public opinion around.","Even then, the merchant didn’t care.","’Worst case, I just get permanently banned.’","Was the Gallery really more important than his real life?","To the merchant, money was what mattered most.","It would be a shame to lose access to the Gallery as entertainment, but that was fine.","He could simply use money to entertain himself instead.","The merchant waited happily.","No matter what kind of explanation Grylls offered, he was ready to respond.","[The thing Mr. Grylls gave me really is an inner core.]","\"Hmm?\"","He had been refreshing the Gallery endlessly when a particular title caught his eye.","It wasn’t a post from some ordinary anonymous user.","It had been written by one of the most famous registered users on the Gallery.","SwordMaster.","It wasn’t a post he could casually ignore, so he opened it immediately.","Title: The Thing Mr. Grylls Gave Me Really Is an Inner Core","SwordMaster","(Photo of a golden bead resting on a palm)","Mr. Grylls found another inner core and gave it to me.","This really is an inner core.","└ Wait ;; he found another inner core already?","└ Why are inner cores popping out like everyday meals? lol. That actually makes me trust him less lol.","└ Maybe it’s possible because it’s the Forest of Four Seasons?","└ Heavenly Demon is one thing, but SwordMaster verifying it is different.","└ This one’s golden. Did he catch a golden fish this time?","\"What?\"","There had been another inner core?","The merchant’s eyes widened.","This was completely unexpected.","He hurriedly typed a comment.","└ Ever consider that they coordinated their stories? Why would another inner core suddenly show up out of nowhere? lol.","└ Why would they coordinate? Like with a kiss? Smooch?","└ Oh my. How lewd.","└ There’s no reason for them to coordinate lol. And why would SwordMaster have any reason to lie?","└ Exactly lol. She’s the person who raised the average strength of swordsmen across the continent lol.","└ Heavenly Demon said one-on-one messages are possible, right? She probably threatened her through that.","└ And what would threatening her accomplish? She’d just get kicked out by the Moderator.","└ Why is this bastard’s imagination so pathetic? lol.","└ Looking at the address beside his name, isn’t this the bastard who posted that Grylls was a scammer?","└ Getting nervous? LMAO.","He had jumped in out of panic and only made things worse for himself.","The merchant frowned.","The appearance of a second inner core had been completely outside his calculations.","He felt somewhat anxious, but quickly calmed himself.","Thinking about it again, there was no reason to panic.","’I can just keep insisting that the one I received wasn’t real.’","It seemed the other side intended to fight manipulation with manipulation.","The only difference was that their version happened to contain the truth.","Even if the inner core SwordMaster had received was genuine, that didn’t prove the merchant’s inner core was genuine.","As long as he stubbornly denied everything until the end, the advantage would eventually return to him.","He simply had to exploit the uncertainty all the way through.","[I’ll Explain Everything.]","’There it is.’","Public opinion had just begun splitting roughly down the middle when Grylls finally made a post.","The merchant opened it without delay.","Title: Here’s My Explanation","Wild Grylls","Explanation, my ass.","If you’ve got a problem, reveal your address.","Reveal your address and let someone else check whether it’s an inner core or not. Simple, right?","If it’s an inner core, you’re fucking dead.","If it isn’t, I’ll return all your money.","What kind of half-assed propaganda are you trying to pull, you son of a bitch?","You parasite-looking bastard, sitting there running a scam yourself. Fuck.","SwordMaster already verified one too.","If you still have a problem, make a registered account first, you broke bastard.","└ Holy shit LMAOOOO. That felt good lol.","└ Upvote if this actually made you trust him more lol.","└ Starting with me LMAOOOO.","└ That’s the kind of rage you can only have when you know you’re innocent lololol.","└ Holy shit, I like this guy even more now lol.","└ Every single thing he said is right. Reveal the address and verify it lol.","└ I’m broke and somehow caught a stray bullet...","It wasn’t an explanation post at all.","It was just a wall of profanity.","In any normal place, that would have backfired horribly.","But this was the Gallery.","If anything, a post like this was perfect for gaining favor and credibility.","\"W-What the hell is wrong with this bastard?\"","As far as the merchant knew, Grylls hadn’t even been using the Gallery for very long.","But judging by the way he wrote, he looked like someone who had been active there for years.","After a moment of confusion, the merchant left a comment on the post.","He couldn’t retreat now.","└ I’m the one who received the inner core. Why the hell should I reveal my address? This is ridiculous lol.","└ Oh, the man himself is here.","└ Pathetic lol.","└ Seeing him act like this makes me think he really did scam him.","└ Wild Grylls: If you’re going to play games with someone else’s life, then you should put your own life on the line too, right? The Gallery is literally my lifeline.","└ Not my problem. And I’m telling you, this isn’t an inner core.","└ Wild Grylls: Say that after making a registered account first. Or just reveal your address lol.","└ You reveal yours first.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m in the Forest of Four Seasons, dumbass. Come here if you can.","He was trapped.","Completely trapped.","The merchant’s eyes darted up, down, left, and right before he backed out of the post.","[Anonymous Buyer Who Received the Inner Core, Reveal Your Address.]","[Can’t We Just Go Check It Ourselves?]","[Upvote if Grylls is Based as Hell lol.]","[Upvote if You Want All Scammers to Die lol.]","The moment he returned to the main page, he saw that public opinion had completely reversed.","Most posts were now demanding that the buyer reveal his address if he had nothing to hide.","’Are you insane? Why the hell would I reveal my address and get myself killed?’","Absolutely not.","The moment his location became public, his real-life life would be in danger.","The merchant deleted the post in which he had accused Grylls and logged out of the Gallery.","It seemed he would have to wait until things calmed down.","’What a shame. I could’ve made even more money.’","It was disappointing, but causing any more trouble now would probably make it impossible to reverse public opinion.","It would be better to simply sell the inner core instead.","About ten minutes later, the merchant cautiously logged back into the Gallery.","He had told himself that the Gallery was nothing important.","But in the end, he was just another hardcore Gallery addict.","A piece of culture like a drug—something he wanted to quit but couldn’t.","’Maybe things have calmed down a little?’","With that thought, he entered the Gallery and saw—","[Just Wait Right There. I’m in the Next Town Over LMAO.]","[Heading Over to Taste That Inner Core!]","[So Jealous of the People in the Central Plains.]","[Turns Out That Scammer Bastard Was a Merchant.]","The posts made him feel deeply uneasy.","The merchant immediately sensed something was wrong and opened the trending page.","A merchant who lacked sharp instincts was bound to be weeded out.","And the instant he entered the trending section, one post uploaded by the Moderator caught his eye.","Title: Here’s the Address!","Don’t Abandon the Hero","Mr. Grylls revealed his address, but one person refused to reveal theirs!","So I’ll kindly tell everyone the address myself!","It’s around XXX, Henan Province, Central Plains!","Mr. Grylls also said he’d return the money if it turns out not to be an inner core, so I hope you two can reach an amicable settlement!","\"Uh...\"","Only one thought entered the merchant’s mind when he saw the post.","’I’m fucked.’","He was seriously fucked.","He had never expected the Moderator to reveal his address.","Crash! Bang!","A loud commotion erupted outside.","The merchant’s head snapped upward.","A moment later, his secretary burst through the door in a panic.","\"W-What is all that noise?!\"","\"I-I don’t know either! For now, we need to evacuate—!\"","\"I heard there’s an inner core here!\"","\"We’ll just check it and give it back!\"","The voices drew closer and closer.","The merchant’s face turned deathly pale.","At this point, the Gallery no longer mattered at all.","’You’ve got to be fucking kidding me...!’","It looked like from now on, he would have no choice but to focus entirely on real life."]},{"title":"Chapter 44","paragraphs":["Scammer (5)","\"What a ridiculous bastard.\"","The inner core scam incident had flared up as quickly as gasoline catching fire, then died down just as fast.","With help from Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster, followed by the Moderator delivering the finishing blow, everything ended without too much trouble.","Things might have gotten a bit complicated without their help, but fortunately, most of the registered users had been on my side.","’So even in another world, the Gallery is still the Gallery.’","For the record, posting that \"explanation\" was entirely my own decision.","Instead of calmly explaining myself, I declared war while throwing in plenty of profanity.","No matter how carefully I explained things, the people who wanted to tear into me would do it anyway, so I chose that approach instead.","In the end, I gained favor with the Gallery users and won the battle of public opinion, so there was nothing bad about it.","Though calling it a battle of public opinion felt like an exaggeration, since the fire burned out so quickly.","It was just another ordinary day on the Gallery.","’Heavenly Demon seemed a little flustered, but it ended well.’","Looking at the Gallery now, most people were making a fuss about hunting down the scammer.","The Moderator had even revealed his address, so that bastard’s real life was probably about to become miserable.","Of all things, I never expected the Moderator to actually expose his address.","My guess was that Heavenly Demon had persuaded the Moderator.","From my perspective, this whole issue had practically put my life on the line, while the other side had risked nothing.","She probably thought that was unfair.","’I should send her a thank-you message first.’","No matter what, thanking her was necessary.","I sent her a private message.","[Wild Grylls: Is the address the Moderator gave far from you?]","[Heavenly Demon: Quite far. But this Lady can arrive there quickly.]","That made sense.","I wasn’t being sarcastic either.","I genuinely believed her.","At the very least, she was probably around SwordMaster’s level, if not stronger.","After thanking Heavenly Demon for various things, I asked her something I had been wondering about.","[Wild Grylls: Thanks to you, everything ended pretty smoothly. Seriously, thank you.]","[Heavenly Demon: It was nothing. If this Lady had her way, I would personally go there and rip out his tongue.]","[Wild Grylls: Whoa ;; that’s brutal. Heavenly Demon, you’re from the Central Plains, right?]","[Heavenly Demon: That is correct.]","[Wild Grylls: Heavenly Demon, even if you’re a Sub-Moderator, once you use a one-on-one trade, you still can’t trade again for twenty-four hours, right?]","[Heavenly Demon: Correct. Do you perhaps wish to trade frequently with this Lady?]","The way she said wish made it sound like I was desperately hoping for it.","Not that it bothered me.","That was just how she talked, so I let it slide.","[Wild Grylls: Yeah. From now on, I think it’ll be better to get important items verified before selling them. Someone could just take the item and shut their mouth like that bastard did.]","[Heavenly Demon: I understand. Permission granted. This Lady shall persuade the Moderator regarding the trade cooldown.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. Seriously, thank you. I feel like I’m always receiving help from you.]","[Heavenly Demon: Could it possibly outweigh what you did by saving this Lady’s life? If you ever need help, tell me at any time.]","[Wild Grylls: I appreciate the thought, but I’ll pass. I need to develop the strength to stand on my own too.]","As I had mentioned many times before, relying too heavily on others was never good.","The only thing I intended to use Heavenly Demon’s help for was verifying important items.","For most other things, Allfather usually identified them whenever I made a post.","So this was more like insurance.","[Wild Grylls: Then I’ll get going. I’ll message you again sometime.]","[Heavenly Demon: This Lady shall always await your messages. Ah, and the fasting pills can be prepared within a week.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you.]","[Heavenly Demon: Good. If you ever require strength, contact me without hesitation. This Lady shall help you at any time.]","Was it just my imagination, or could I sense both satisfaction and disappointment in her words?","She seemed like a lonely person, so maybe I should talk to her more often.","Before that, though, I needed to deal with lunch.","Just in case, I turned on the hose.","Unfortunately, water poured out freely without any obstruction.","Which meant no fish was stuck inside.","’Guess I’ll have to settle for a fasting pill.’","It was disappointing, but there was nothing I could do.","Fishing directly in the river was out of the question.","Unless I wiped out every golden frog in the area, fishing there would be suicidal.","I chewed on the bitter fasting pill while thinking about what I should do after lunch.","’The trap... I’ll check it tomorrow. It’s way too soon.’","It was better not to expect too much from the trap.","That left only one thing.","Making a post on the Gallery.","After what had happened today, I wanted to let everyone know how I planned to handle things from now on.","Title: This Is Grylls","Wild Grylls","Hello, everyone.","I’m Wild Grylls, the guy who fell into the Forest of Four Seasons.","Because of some parasite today, I’m planning to have important items verified before listing them from now on.","Especially expensive items. I probably won’t put those on the auction house anymore.","Whenever possible, I’ll prioritize selling them to registered users, and only use the auction house when I don’t have another choice.","The Gallery is honestly terrifying.","For one person, this is literally a matter of life and death, while someone else can ruin that person with a single click.","I rambled on a bit.","Anyway, I’m going to do everything I can to escape this forest.","And if I want to do that, I’ll need the Gallery.","So please cheer me on.","Ah!","And SwordMaster, thank you so much for helping me.","Just keep the inner core.","Three-line summary:","I’ll prioritize trading with registered users from now on.The Gallery is scary, but I’ll keep using it so I can escape.Thank you, SwordMaster.","└ Forget everything else, the three-line summary is the best part lol.","└ Exactly. Just read the bottom lol.","└ Hang in there, Grylls. Just think of it as stepping in shit.","└ Weren’t you one of the guys trashing Grylls earlier?","└ Starlight Princess: I’m glad everything worked out. I was really disappointed because it seemed like there were nothing but awful people here. Mr. Grylls even helps complete strangers.","└ We’ve decided to call people like that suckers.","└ Isn’t that just being kind rather than being a sucker?","└ And didn’t he trade with Starlight Princess before anyway? He’s a good guy as long as you’re actually trading with him.","└ SwordMaster: Wait ;; you’re dumping this on me immediately? I don’t need this.","└ Wild Grylls: You’re going to send it back? Why not just sell it?","└ SwordMaster: I already have plenty of money. Besides, eating an inner core wouldn’t do much for me anyway ;;","└ Wild Grylls: Dun care. Just take ittt.","└ SwordMaster: ;_;","└ What even is this LMAO.","└ It’s not pickpocketing, it’s reverse-pickpocketing lol.","└ He really just said \"dun care\" LMAO.","As expected, SwordMaster looked seriously flustered.","I had no idea why she didn’t want to become healthier.","Starlight Princess had been desperate to improve her health.","The world really was unfair.","’Come to think of it, she used a military expression too. Is she a soldier?’","That would explain why she knew so much about swordsmanship and kept posting sword-training tips.","It made sense.","Since I was already thinking about swordsmanship, this seemed like a good opportunity to thoroughly reread her posts.","I trained diligently while studying SwordMaster’s beginner swordsmanship guide.","’I’m sticking with the sword-and-shield warrior build.’","The owlbear incident and the muscular mushroom incident had both taught me the same thing.","Carrying a shield along with a sword was far safer than relying on a sword alone.","People on the Gallery mocked me by saying I’d die in one hit anyway.","But the whole point of a shield was to block that one hit.","The fist-shaped dent clearly visible on the golden shield was proof enough.","If I had taken that attack directly with my body, my internal organs would have ruptured.","’I can’t really do anything about the proficiency issue, though.’","My swordsmanship itself was destined to hit a wall sooner or later.","The difference between wielding a weapon with one hand and two hands was as vast as heaven and earth.","In my case, I had no choice but to sacrifice technique in exchange for stability.","That was the only way to raise my survival rate significantly.","It wasn’t really a choice.","It was a necessity.","’Isn’t there anyone who’s good with a shield?’","SwordMaster focused almost entirely on swordsmanship, so there was barely any theory related to shields.","At most, it was something like, Block, then hit back.","There wasn’t much that could be done about that.","Well, I was still a complete beginner anyway, so there was no need to rush.","’Let’s see. Time the block properly, then slash immediately?’","I studied SwordMaster’s posts and trained until just before dinner.","Of course, I didn’t expect my skills to improve dramatically after only a few days.","Besides, it had only been a few days since I first picked up a sword and shield.","Getting used to them came first.","\"Hoo...\"","I slowly steadied my breathing.","Beads of sweat formed and rolled down my cheeks.","Even though I was practicing while reading the posts, I still felt uneasy.","It wasn’t that I doubted SwordMaster.","Her posts were said to have raised the average combat strength of the entire continent.","I simply had no idea whether I was doing things correctly.","With nobody beside me to watch and correct me, I couldn’t help feeling a little anxious.","’I heard martial arts are difficult without a teacher.’","Martial arts were techniques humanity had developed for combat.","They were the result of studying how to beat the hell out of an opponent as efficiently as possible.","There was an obvious difference between a punch thrown by an ordinary person and one thrown by a trained fighter.","Some random street brawler beating a professional martial artist?","That was complete bullshit.","That was how enormous the difference was between having martial training and having none.","And progressing properly without a teacher was almost impossible.","So naturally, I couldn’t help wondering whether I was simply swinging my weapons around however I pleased.","’For now, all I can do is study SwordMaster’s posts carefully and complete the goals she laid out.’","SwordMaster’s posts didn’t just contain advice.","They also provided specific goals.","The idea was that once you accomplished one goal, you were ready to move on to the next stage.","Drawing a perfectly straight line with the sword.","Slashing several times without taking a breath.","Thrusting through the inside of a long, hollow cylinder.","There were also some strange goals mixed in that somehow still seemed useful.","’So I should accomplish each goal two or three times over?’","Without a teacher, this was probably the best I could do.","I would simply have to make up for it through effort.","I continued practicing sword-and-shield techniques until evening.","I even visualized scenarios so I could subdue opponents more efficiently.","\"Huaa!\"","I had no idea how long I kept at it.","By the time I stopped, my entire body was drenched in sweat.","This should be enough for today.","I set down the sword and shield and entered the cave.","I planned to rest for a while in the cool interior before eating dinner.","’Come to think of it, I wonder what happened to that scammer. Someone said they lived in the next town over.’","Curious, I immediately logged into the Gallery.","There was nothing quite like the Gallery when it came to relaxing.","As always, the Gallery was a gathering place for idiots.","I figured I should check the trending posts.","The moment I entered, one post with an unusually high number of upvotes caught my eye.","It was related to me.","Naturally, I opened it.","└ Damn, I’m jealous. You guys didn’t kill each other or anything?","└ Nah. The authorities might’ve shown up, so we just settled it with rock-paper-scissors.","└ Rock-paper-scissors LMAOOOO.","└ Don’t underestimate rock-paper-scissors. Visual reaction speed is seriously important in that game lol.","└ You didn’t ask the merchant what he thought?","└ Why the hell would we care about a scammer’s opinion?","└ Guess we should buy everything Grylls lists on the auction house from now on.","└ Fuck. He used to list stuff without going through registered users first. This suddenly sucks.","└ What’s the scammer doing now? He must be furious.","└ What’s he gonna do about it? He ran away immediately LMAO.","└ Serves him right lol.","Title: Yep, This Really Is an Inner Core LMAO","That scammer bastard lived in the town right next to mine, so I stormed over there and ate the inner core.","Some other guys showed up too, but somehow I ended up being the one who ate it and verified it.","I was only at the Second-Rate Realm before, but I immediately broke through to the Peak Realm.","Grylls wasn’t the scammer.","That merchant bastard was.","Stop slandering Grylls from now on.","Looks like things had somehow been resolved.","I probably wouldn’t be mistaken for a scammer again after this.","Even so, I wasn’t going to start listing expensive things on the auction house again right away.","Like I said earlier, I planned to give registered users priority from now on.","I browsed around the Gallery for a while.","By then, my sweat had dried, so I got up.","The sun was starting to set.","It was about time to check the trap.","’It’d be nice if something got caught.’","Not even a full day had passed.","Maybe I was being greedy.","But greed was exactly what could make my dinner more plentiful.","After preparing some basic gear, I headed toward the place where I had set the trap.","I didn’t forget to ask the Tree Sloth to guard the house before leaving.","\"Oh?\"","The moment I reached the trap, I immediately noticed something different.","All the grass I had placed on top of the board was gone.","On top of that, I could faintly sense something moving beneath it.","’Caught something!’","Looks like I’d finally get to eat something greasy again.","Filled with anticipation, I slowly lifted the board.","\"Ta-da~ ta-da-da~ boom-cha-cha~ boom-cha...\"","Clunk—","\"Boom-cha...\"","Inside the trap was a rabbit.","Or rather—","No.","There wasn’t.","Instead, there was something else.","It was large enough to fill the entire pit, with striking pitch-black fur.","And it wasn’t even an ordinary animal.","This thing had eight legs .","Worse still, smaller versions of it were clinging all around its body.","They looked like babies.","Clunk—","I carefully lowered the board again.","Apparently, instead of digging a trap, I had dug myself a spider nest.","’...Should I roast that thing and eat it anyway?’","I immediately gave up on the idea.","If it bit me, I might die."]},{"title":"Chapter 45","paragraphs":["Scammer (6)","Title: Ditched the Spider Trap","Wild Grylls","I just went to check the pit trap, and there was a spider living inside it instead of a rabbit.","It was even covered in pitch-black hair. It was fucking hideous. Just looking at it scared me so much that I left it alone.","From now on, I think I should use snares instead of pit traps.","Heavenly Demon: Keep your spirits up. If things prove difficult, this lady shall send you some meat.","↳ Wild Grylls: It’s okay. I can still hold out for now.","↳ How big was the spider?","↳ Wild Grylls: I think it was at least a meter long? I almost fainted the moment I saw it ;;","↳ Ugh;; What kind of spider is that freaking huge?","↳ Wild Grylls: I was too scared to even take a picture. I think it’d be better to just ignore it lol.","↳ Why not roast that thing and eat it?","↳ Wild Grylls: It’s not like I didn’t think about it, but even if it has babies... I can’t just kill their mother.","↳ Lmaoooo, look at this fucking saint lmaoooo.","↳ Says the guy who killed Wonmo’s mom?","↳ Wild Grylls: Wonmo’s mom was trying to kill me, though ;;","↳ Lmaoooo, fair point.","↳ What would Wonmo think? The person raising him is actually the murderer who killed his mom... and his mom was someone who tried to kill that very person...","↳ Anyone got a novel like that to recommend? Sounds like it’d be fun.","↳ There’s a whole story premise right there lol. I’m off to write it.","↳ Allfather: What did it look like overall?","↳ Wild Grylls: I ran away the moment I saw it, so I’m not really sure either. It was just a spider covered in pitch-black hair.","↳ Allfather: Hmm. That alone makes it difficult to identify. It sounds like some kind of tarantula, so I recommend that you don’t try to catch it.","↳ Wild Grylls: I was already thinking of just burning it with fire.","Since it lived inside a pit, some oil and fire would probably burn it to death in no time.","But I had no intention of going through that much trouble for no reason. I wasn’t even planning on looking at it again.","Just imagine lifting the cover and seeing a whole swarm of grotesque spiders underneath. It wouldn’t be strange to come away traumatized.","’Where the hell did that spider even come from?’","Only a few hours had passed, yet it had already turned the pit trap into its habitat.","It was one of those mysteries of nature that somehow made sense and yet didn’t at the same time.","In the end, I had no choice but to make do with a fasting pill for dinner again.","I could only hope that a fish would be caught by tomorrow morning.","’Would it be better to smoke it instead?’","That wasn’t a bad idea. If I smoked the fish, bugs probably wouldn’t swarm around it as much.","What worried me were wild animals, but honestly, if any were going to come, they probably would have shown up already.","Considering no dangerous beasts had appeared so far, there had to be some reason for it.","’At least finding owlbear droppings gives me some hope...’","Wonmo’s mother, the owlbear, might have come here to scout the area just like I had.","After all, the owlbear had thoroughly chewed up, torn apart, tasted, and enjoyed the Mad Dog’s corpse.","Since the enemy that had once divided up the territory was gone, she might simply have come to check out its former base.","’I guess I have no choice but to keep exploring.’","The Forest of Four Seasons was a place where nothing that happened could be considered strange.","So preparing for every possible contingency wasn’t optional. It was essential.","As the sky gradually darkened, I picked up a few pieces of firewood and headed back inside the cave.","When I entered, Wonmo had woken up and was sitting there blankly.","\"You awake? Want some food?\"","\"Kkyuu!\"","What a cute little guy.","I bought a huge chunk of meat from the auction house.","I wouldn’t have to worry about money for a while. I’d made an enormous amount from selling the inner core.","The funny part was that the scammer hadn’t even gotten to eat the inner core.","Served him right.","’Allfather will need the frog tomorrow, right?’","My plan for tomorrow was simple.","I’d explore in the morning and return before lunchtime.","Then I’d hunt a Golden Poison Frog and trade it with Allfather, and if possible, get a fish trap from the dwarf.","If I could get a fish trap from the dwarf, I wouldn’t have to worry about food anymore.","And since it would be made by a dwarf, there was no reason to doubt its durability.","’The question is whether I should follow the river upstream or downstream...’","There was one of the easiest ways to escape when stranded.","Follow a river downstream.","Since ancient times, civilizations had often begun near rivers.","Even if there wasn’t a country nearby, there should at least be a small village somewhere.","’The problem is that space is all over the place here, so the river might suddenly get cut off halfway.’","Space being all over the place.","It might sound like a strange way to put it, but I wasn’t wrong.","The land on the other side of the river was literally changing in real time, going from snowy mountains to desert and back again.","Last time, it had even changed into an area completely shrouded in fog. I’d been utterly dumbfounded when I saw it.","So if the river ever seemed to come to an unnatural end, I planned to turn back without hesitation.","’Nothing is ever easy.’","I sighed.","That was also why I’d made adaptation my top priority instead of escape.","With space constantly changing, escaping was difficult even if I wanted to.","’At least it’s reassuring that my map is gradually getting bigger.’","I turned my head toward the wall.","A map had been drawn on a large sheet of paper.","With this cave at its center, various points of interest were marked in every direction.","The river where Golden Poison Frogs appeared. The colony of mature Mandrakes. The Golden Mushroom Cave I had recently discovered, and so on.","Since even compasses didn’t work in this place, it wasn’t perfectly reliable, but it was still a huge help.","’Tomorrow, I’ll follow the river downstream.’","As long as I followed the river, I wouldn’t get lost.","Once the sun had completely set, I lit a campfire.","Warmth slowly began spreading through the cave that had been growing increasingly chilly.","\"Nom, nom.\"","Wonmo happily munched away when I gave him the meat.","I stroked his head.","He flinched at first, but soon settled down and continued eating peacefully. It seemed like he had become completely accustomed to my touch.","’It’d be nice if he could just grow out of the cub stage.’","It took several years for an owlbear to reach adulthood. That was what the gallery had told me.","But it didn’t have to be fully grown before it could hunt independently.","If I remembered correctly, I’d heard that it would grow considerably bigger within about a year.","I watched Wonmo happily devouring the neatly butchered raw meat for a while before turning my head.","The Sloth was staring blankly at me with its usual dumb-looking face.","\"You’re fully grown, right?\"","\"...\"","\"Yeah. Thought so.\"","Can’t you tell just by looking?","That was what its expression seemed to be saying.","Of course, that was nothing more than my own guess.","Afterward, I had a simple meal of fasting pills and stepped outside for a moment.","It was better to wash up before going to sleep.","For hygiene.","’Why does this Sloth hate being washed so much?’","Thankfully, I hadn’t shown any symptoms of anything yet, but you never knew.","Until I managed to wash the little bastard, I had no choice but to keep myself as clean as possible.","After quickly washing up, I went back inside the cave.","’Oh. Right. The scabbard.’","The moment I saw the Heavenly Demon’s sword propped up against one side of the cave, I remembered.","I was going to be traveling around a lot from now on, so I couldn’t exactly carry it around like this.","I logged into the gallery and opened a private chat with the Heavenly Demon.","She replied in less than a second.","It caught me a little off guard.","[Wild Grylls: By the way, does the sword you gave me before not have a scabbard?]","[Heavenly Demon: It did. However, the blade was so exceedingly sharp that the scabbard ended up in tatters.]","[Wild Grylls: Hmm. That makes sense.]","In truth, a scabbard might not mean all that much.","The Heavenly Demon’s sword already had a record of cleanly slicing a Mad Dog in half, after all.","But if I just carried it around bare, it would inevitably become inconvenient whenever I was moving.","[Wild Grylls: Heavenly Demon, are you there?]","[Heavenly Demon: Speak.]","[Heavenly Demon: If you desire a scabbard, this lady shall command one of my close aides to prepare it.]","[Wild Grylls: No, that won’t be necessary. Do you happen to know Passing Dwarf?]","[Heavenly Demon: Do you mean that drunken dwarf? I have never spoken with him directly, but I know of him.]","[Wild Grylls: I was thinking of asking him. He seems to be an exceptionally skilled blacksmith.]","[Heavenly Demon: It is not a bad idea, but can you not simply carry the sword as it is?]","[Wild Grylls: I could, but I think I’ll still need a scabbard.]","I was talking about situations where I needed to investigate something or use my hands.","That happened fairly often.","Having one would be better than not having one. That was the conclusion I had reached from living here.","[Heavenly Demon: Your way of life differs from this lady’s, so I shall respect your judgment. But I can assure you that it will not be easy.]","[Wild Grylls: You said it was made from something called Ten-Thousand-Year Cold Iron, right? Is it a particularly good metal?]","[Heavenly Demon: That too, but it was also forged by an outstanding blacksmith.]","[Wild Grylls: Ah.]","So it was a masterpiece among masterpieces.","And the Heavenly Demon had given it to me.","No matter how many times I said I would return it, she adamantly refused.","[Heavenly Demon: If you are thinking of returning it, I forbid it. This lady has already reached a point where she no longer clings to weapons.]","[Wild Grylls: Is there anything you want?]","[Heavenly Demon: If you happen to find another inner core, could you give it to me? It is not for this lady, but for one of my close aides.]","[Wild Grylls: Ah. Of course. Understood. Could you pass along my thanks to them in return?]","[Heavenly Demon: Of course.]","That was where my conversation with the Heavenly Demon ended.","Now only one thing remained.","Asking Passing Dwarf to make me a scabbard.","The problem was, I had no idea whether he would accept.","He was making the fish trap under the pretext that I would provide him with drinking snacks, but a scabbard was another matter entirely.","Unless I found some high-quality mineral, there was a good chance he would refuse.","’In the end, I need something valuable.’","It looked like I would have to expand my exploration range from now on.","The best places to target would be areas where space became chaotically entangled, like on the other side of the river.","’Though finding places like that won’t be easy.’","I would just have to put in the effort.","If I wanted to escape, reckless challenges were sometimes necessary.","I took a picture of the campfire and posted it on the gallery.","Title: Day 4 Complete!","(Photo of the campfire)","Good night, everyone! See you tomorrow!","↳ Heavenly Demon: You have done well.","↳ SwordMaster: Good work today.","↳ Starlight Princess: See you again tomorrow!","↳ Praise the Sun: You had to suffer because of some pathetic bastard.","↳ Princess Cheonggu: Bye-bye! Don’t die! I’ll send you some pants tomorrow!","Receiving encouragement from the fixed users and bullshit from the anonymous users at the same time, I closed the gallery.","Now I planned to practice the internal energy cultivation method for a while before going to sleep.","’It really does feel like my fatigue disappears every time I circulate the cultivation method.’","I was basically forcing myself to sleep, but there was nothing else I could do.","Going outside in the middle of the pitch-black night was practically suicide.","Even if I could technically see ahead, the forest at night was completely different from the forest during the day.","’Then...’","A good idea suddenly occurred to me.","My fatigue disappeared whenever I practiced the internal energy cultivation method?","Then I could simply keep practicing until I became tired again.","I had nothing else to do anyway, so this was probably the best option for me.","’If I keep at it, I’ll get sleepy eventually, right?’","With that simple thought in mind, I began circulating the cultivation method.","The mana inside my body gradually began to circulate, accelerating with each breath as though it were being pumped through me.","’Start slowly from the basics...’","Time was the one thing I had plenty of.","Using that time, I carefully refined the foundation the Heavenly Demon had taught me.","Little by little, I sank into stillness.","By the time Grylls had become completely absorbed in his internal energy cultivation, the gallery was still as active as ever.","The disappearance of a single fixed user was nowhere near enough to bring the gallery to a halt.","However, most of the gallery’s discussion revolved around Grylls.","Title: From now on, I’m buying anything Grylls puts up for auction.","Nothing that bastard sells ever turns out to be bad lol.","At this rate, maybe mithril or something will pop up next instead of an inner core? lol","↳ Mithril, my ass lol. It’s not like mithril is some random rock lying by the roadside.","↳ Then is an inner core just some random marble?","↳ It’s not like it has that huge of an effect.","↳ It’s still an inner core. A second-rate warrior jumped straight to the peak realm after taking one, didn’t he?","↳ I’m telling you, there’s basically no downside to buying one.","↳ The fact that there’s already an entire colony of mature Mandrakes there is broken as hell lol.","↳ Damn it, if it weren’t for that fucking scammer, we could’ve gotten things cheaper.","↳ Seriously, it’s basically because of that bastard that everything has to pass through the fixed users now. Thinking about it is pissing me off again.","Title: Gallery bro is fucked in real time.","My boss told me to somehow build a connection with Grylls.","When I said I didn’t want to, he told me to leave the merchant company if I didn’t like it.","Can’t I do something about this legally? It’s closely connected to my private life ;;","↳ Smart Mind: Do you normally talk shit about your boss?","↳ You don’t?","↳ Smart Mind: I do too. My boss recently told me to reveal my gallery username and I almost got fucked lol.","↳ How’d you get out of it?","↳ Smart Mind: I just bullshitted my way through it. You should ask your boss to reveal his gallery username too. He’ll probably back off then.","↳ Lmao, useful tip.","↳ At this point, I think I’ll believe Grylls no matter what he discovers. What’ll it be next?","↳ I already told you. It’ll definitely be some kind of mineral. I believe it lol.","Title: Honestly, He’s Hard to Trade With","What does Grylls actually need?","Stuff directly related to survival.","He doesn’t really need money.","At this point, it’s basically barter, so isn’t trading with him ridiculously difficult?","Unless you’re willing to hand over some legendary weapon or something.","↳ The fact that threats don’t work on him anymore is huge too. Making even a single trade has gotten ridiculously difficult ;;","↳ Inner cores and elixirs are useless too if he can just eat the ones he finds there lol.","↳ Doesn’t he already have basically all the weapons he needs? What else could he possibly want?","↳ Porn?","↳ Oh.","↳ Ohohoho lol.","↳ That’s what you need, dumbass lmao.","↳ No, seriously, he might actually need it. I’m not even joking.","The gallery burned with what was less an argument and more a prolonged debate for quite some time.","Unlike before, everyone was taking a much more active stance."]},{"title":"Chapter 46","paragraphs":["Lakeside (1)","The internal energy cultivation method really did seem to have a fatigue-recovery effect.","Even if I replaced sleep with cultivation, I would still be full of energy the next day.","Well, it still wasn’t perfect, so mental fatigue was harder to get rid of.","Physical fatigue was manageable enough, but mental fatigue could only really be resolved through sleep.","[XXX has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","[@@@ has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","[I’ll Become a Duke has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","\"What is all this now?\"","The moment I logged into the gallery, countless trade request windows floated before my eyes.","Had something happened again while I was away?","Just in case, I searched my own name, but nothing particularly noteworthy came up.","The only thing was that my credibility had skyrocketed because of yesterday’s incident.","It seemed the fixed users who had previously hesitated because of trust issues were now sending me trade requests because of that.","’Seriously, these people... I keep telling them I’m as fragile as a sunfish.’","Or were they trying to suck me dry to the marrow before I actually ended up dead?","From what I had heard, even a single mature Mandrake was worth an enormous amount.","Apparently, they figured that even if I didn’t have another inner core, one mature Mandrake alone would be enough to make a trade worthwhile.","’At least offer something that would tempt me.’","I searched the names of the fixed users who had sent me trade requests.","Some of their accounts had only been created recently, while others had surprisingly long histories of activity.","Especially this I’ll Become a Duke person.","If I remembered correctly, they had sent me a trade request before too.","I had to admire the persistence, but right now, it was mostly just annoying.","’And they didn’t even make a post.’","I had already said this last time.","If someone offered something I needed, I would be the one to initiate the trade.","Apparently, they had already forgotten.","With no other choice, I made another post.","Title: Let Me Say This Again","Wild Grylls","I woke up to countless handshake requests... no, trade requests.","Like I said before, I have no intention of trading unless you offer something that will actually help me.","If you want to trade, post what you’re offering first.","I’ll look at it and decide.","↳ Heavenly Demon: You are awake. Is there anywhere that feels uncomfortable?","↳ Wild Grylls: I feel way more refreshed when I sleep while practicing the internal energy cultivation method.","↳ Heavenly Demon: Naturally. That is the effect of circulating and regulating your qi. Your foundation is still lacking, but once you reach full mastery, you will remain perfectly well even without sleep.","↳ Wild Grylls: Wow.","↳ Starlight Princess: You’re awake! Is today Day 5?","↳ Wild Grylls: Yeah. If I had my way, I’d escape as soon as possible.","↳ Starlight Princess: There’s a saying that the more urgent you are, the more you should take the long way around. I made another elixir today, so I’ll send you a trade request in a little while!","↳ Wild Grylls: Huh? Didn’t you already give me all the elixirs?","↳ Starlight Princess: This one is for animals. Please use it on Wonmo and the Sloth. One picture of Wonmo is more than enough payment, so please accept it!","↳ Wild Grylls: Thank you. You’ve been feeling healthy, right?","↳ Starlight Princess: Like I told you before, I feel like I’ve been reborn. My parents are still worried, though.","↳ Wild Grylls: Parents are always like that. Just in case, take your rehabilitation slowly.","↳ Starlight Princess: Thank you. I’ll keep cheering you on from now on. You can do it!","↳ Wild Grylls: Thank you, haha.","↳ Passing Dwarf: Hey. I finished the fish trap. Hurry up and present this great one with some drinking snacks.","↳ Wild Grylls: Before the snacks, there’s something I want to ask you for.","↳ Passing Dwarf: What is it? I’m not doing it for free.","↳ Wild Grylls: I do have a conscience. I need a scabbard, and I need one that’s seriously durable.","↳ Passing Dwarf: A scabbard? Just buy any old one.","↳ Wild Grylls: The sword the Heavenly Demon gave me is too good. It cuts through wood like tofu.","↳ Passing Dwarf: Ah. There are swords like that sometimes. I’ll send you one to use temporarily along with the fish trap. If you want a proper one, bring me something good in exchange.","↳ Wild Grylls: I’ll trade with Starlight Princess first, then I’ll take yours.","↳ Princess Cheonggu: Hellooo! The pants I mentioned yesterday are ready!","↳ Wild Grylls: Thank you so much. When’s your next match?","↳ Princess Cheonggu: Pretty soon! It’s Boxing Day, so we have one about every three days!","↳ Wild Grylls: I hope you win. Go, Cheonggu!","↳ Princess Cheonggu: Thank youuu!","It really did pay to live kindly.","There were people leaving comments for me first thing in the morning.","Of course, I wasn’t entirely without worries.","If the head moderator saw this, they might think it counted as excessive fraternizing.","The rules specifically said that too much personal bonding was prohibited.","That made things awkward.","’They must know the Heavenly Demon gives me special treatment too.’","Apparently, this much was tolerated.","Or maybe it was because my circumstances were unusual.","[Starlight Princess has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","After announcing the start of my day like that, Starlight Princess was the first to send a trade request.","Before accepting, I looked over at Wonmo.","He was still sprawled out asleep.","The funny part was that he had stretched his entire body out flat like a person.","Apparently, when an animal slept like that, it meant it felt safe in its surroundings.","That gave me a strange feeling.","[Starlight Princess has registered trade items.]","[Starlight Princess: I put in one animal-use elixir and another gift too!]","[Wild Grylls: Huh? Another gift?]","[Starlight Princess: I think you’ll like it. So, where’s the picture?]","[Wild Grylls: (Photo of Wonmo sleeping sprawled out flat) Is this enough?]","[Starlight Princess: He’s so cute! How can he even sleep like that?]","[Wild Grylls: I thought it was amazing too.]","[Starlight Princess: I hope you continue to stay safe! You can do it!]","That was the end of my conversation with Starlight Princess.","I checked the items she had given me.","She had called it an animal-use elixir, but judging by the way it glowed golden, it looked like an ordinary elixir no matter how I looked at it.","I wasn’t even sure whether animal-specific elixirs existed in the first place.","I decided to just think of it as a gift.","And then there was the other item.","The thing she had confidently claimed I would like was actually a little surprising.","’Cake?’","A slice of cake sat on top of a glass plate decorated with an elegant design.","Soft-looking sponge cake covered in whipped cream, with a small strawberry perched on top.","She had even thoughtfully included a fork to make it easier to eat.","I swallowed and picked it up.","\"Damn...\"","The moment I put a small bite of cake into my mouth, an exclamation escaped me.","The sweetness spread throughout my entire mouth.","The distinctive sugary taste stimulated my tongue.","I sprinkled salt on fish whenever I ate it, so I hadn’t forgotten what saltiness tasted like.","But it had been a long time since I’d tasted something so sweet it practically made my tongue tingle.","’She really knows what people like.’","I set the cake aside for a moment and logged back into the gallery.","There were still fixed users I needed to trade with.","The next person to send me a request after Starlight Princess was Passing Dwarf.","He seemed like the kind of person who would handle exactly what needed to be done and move on.","[Passing Dwarf has registered trade items.]","[Passing Dwarf: Put in the fish trap and a temporary scabbard. You know how to install the trap, right?]","[Wild Grylls: Yeah. I’m thinking of widening the spot where I inserted the hose.]","[Passing Dwarf: That should work. Deal with the scabbard however you want, but make sure you give me snacks for my drinks. Got it?]","[Wild Grylls: Do you like sashimi?]","[Passing Dwarf: My mouth’s already watering.]","[Wild Grylls: But I’m not very good at slicing sashimi lol.]","[Passing Dwarf: You fucking bastard.]","[Wild Grylls: Anyway, I’ll do my best. Thanks for the stuff.]","Once the trade was complete, I checked the items I had received from the dwarf.","’Why the hell is this fish trap so huge?’","The fish trap was enormous.","It was almost as big as my entire body.","I was a little taken aback, but that might actually be better.","Considering the size of the fish I had caught so far, it was probably about right.","’Installing this is going to take a while. I’ll do it after I’m done exploring.’","I decided to postpone setting up the fish trap.","It felt like I would waste the whole morning just installing it.","The next thing to check was the scabbard.","The temporary scabbard the dwarf had mentioned was inside the fish trap.","’It looks like an ordinary scabbard.’","It was a plain black scabbard, roughly the same size as the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","I picked up the Heavenly Demon’s sword from where it rested against the wall and slid it inside.","Shhk—click!","The sword went in smoothly without catching anywhere.","He had said it was only temporary, but I was more than satisfied.","It even came with a belt, so it looked useful in all sorts of situations.","’That dwarf is surprisingly nice, too.’","I chuckled and contacted the next person I had to trade with.","Next up was Princess Cheonggu.","[Wild Grylls: Go, Cheonggu! Don’t get too discouraged even if the slump lasts a while! No one stays on top forever!]","[Princess Cheonggu: Thank youuu! I’ll give you another special uniform too!]","[Wild Grylls: Whose is it this time?]","[Princess Cheonggu: It belonged to a legendary midfielder named Sun! He’s unusual because he’s from the Central Plains!]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you! Can’t I watch Cheonggu’s matches through the gallery?]","[Princess Cheonggu: You have to pay for broadcast magic, so only the highlights will get uploaded!]","[Wild Grylls: That’s too bad. I wanted to watch one of your matches.]","[Princess Cheonggu: I’d love to let you watch too, but broadcasts probably won’t work in the Forest of Four Seasons. But why do you want to watch?]","[Wild Grylls: I feel like I’m always the one receiving things. I wanted to show you that I’m genuinely cheering for you.]","[Princess Cheonggu: Kyaaah...! What a wonderful attitude! Such an admirable mindset! I really hope you escape soon!]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. If I find anything good, I’ll send it to you right away.]","What kind of item would Princess Cheonggu like?","That was something worth thinking about.","For now, I checked what she had sent me.","Just as she had said, there were long pants and a uniform shirt.","The pants were made of the same highly elastic material as the uniform.","And she had sent not one pair, but two.","I smiled in satisfaction and put them on.","They definitely felt different right away.","’I could probably live in just these.’","It reminded me of the days when I used to lounge around at home wearing nothing but tracksuits.","I tossed the pants I had been wearing until now into a corner of the cave.","From now on, those would be my emergency pair.","’Now that all the trades are done, time for the cake... Huh?’","My excitement at the thought of enjoying the cake lasted only a moment.","I had definitely eaten only one bite.","So why was the plate completely empty?","I blinked at the incomprehensible sight and looked around.","Wonmo was still sleeping soundly on the mat.","That only left the Sloth...","\"...\"","\"...Hey.\"","At my voice, the Sloth tilted its head.","The sheer shamelessness of its behavior made anger rise inside me.","\"Maybe wipe the cream off your mouth first?\"","\"...\"","Only then did the bastard start feeling around its mouth.","There wasn’t just a tiny speck of whipped cream there.","A huge glob was smeared all over it.","The Sloth looked at the cream now stuck to its claw, then very slowly brought it to its mouth.","\"...\"","\"Munch, munch.\"","Was there anything in the world more infuriating than this bastard?","The worst part was that I had no way to beat it in a fight.","In the end, there was only one thing I could do.","\"You little bastard!!!\"","Roar at it at the top of my lungs.","It seemed to work surprisingly well, because the Sloth covered its ears.","\"Kkyuak?!\"","Ah.","Right.","Wonmo was here too.","When Wonmo jolted awake in fright, I immediately felt terrible.","’This is all the Sloth’s fault.’","Thinking that to myself, I gently soothed Wonmo.","Fortunately, Wonmo just looked bewildered and didn’t seem to understand what had happened.","\"Wonmo. Want breakfast?\"","\"Kkyuu!\"","Even if he had understood, the whole incident probably would have ended the moment I offered him breakfast anyway.","I gave Wonmo some meat and stepped outside.","When I opened the hose, water came pouring out beautifully.","Unfortunately, it didn’t look like any fish had been caught.","’Guess I should get ready.’","I had another fasting pill for breakfast.","Maybe because I had tasted something sweet just moments ago, the bitterness seemed especially strong today.","’Should I ask her for another one?’","That felt far too shameless, so I gave up on the idea.","The day had only just started, yet I already felt drained.","’Please let me find somewhere with plenty of food.’","That was my small wish.","I sighed and finished preparing.","The Sloth might be annoying as hell, but it was the only one capable of protecting Wonmo while I was gone.","I decided to think of the cake as payment for all the time it had spent guarding the cave.","That made me feel a little better.","\"Hey, Sloth.\"","When I called out, it tilted its head.","\"I’m heading out. Guard the house properly while I’m gone, got it? You’ve got to earn the price of that cake.\"","\"...\"","Flap. Flap.","The Sloth lazily waved its arms as if to say it understood.","I chuckled at the response and finished the rest of my preparations.","At my waist were the scabbard containing the Heavenly Demon’s sword and a small bag.","In my left hand, I carried the Golden Shield in case I was suddenly attacked.","I kept my right hand free so I could maintain my balance if something unexpected happened.","’And I should circulate the cultivation method before leaving.’","Once I had properly circulated the internal energy cultivation method, all that remained was to depart.","With a tense heart, I started walking toward the river.","Once I reached it, I planned to follow the flow downstream.","’Hopefully I can find some clue that’ll help me escape.’","Whether the world understood my hopes or not...","Or perhaps some god of this world was deliberately screwing with me.","\"Ah, fuck.\"","After following the river downstream, I couldn’t help swearing at the environment spread out before me.","It wasn’t like the other side of the river, where space itself changed in real time.","This place was clearly connected to the river.","The problem was simply that the environment itself was ridiculous enough to make me curse.","\"Is this the ocean or a lake?\"","An immense lake stretched out before my eyes."]},{"title":"Chapter 47","paragraphs":["Lakeside (2)","I didn’t run into any dangerous animals while following the river downstream.","Normally, all kinds of animals would come to a river, but whether it was because the current was too strong or because of the Golden Poison Frogs, I didn’t see any.","That didn’t mean I encountered no animals at all, though.","Every now and then, I came across smaller creatures.","Title: This Is a Lizard, Right?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a fucking huge lizard)","What species even is this? The size is ridiculous.","Of course, it only counted as a small animal by Forest of Four Seasons standards.","The lizard bolted the moment it saw me.","I was glad it avoided a fight, but I was still curious, so I asked the gallery.","↳ Heavenly Demon: What an enormous lizard. Why not catch it and eat it?","↳ Wild Grylls: Not a bad idea, but it ran away.","↳ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. It must have instinctively sensed your strength and fled.","↳ Wild Grylls: I don’t think that’s it lol ;;","↳ Allfather: Judging by its appearance, it is an iguana. It seems to have grown much larger because it lives in the Forest of Four Seasons.","↳ Wild Grylls: Is it a herbivore?","↳ Allfather: Yes. It is herbivorous, so you do not need to be wary of it. Still, given its size, you should remain careful.","↳ Wild Grylls: What does it taste like?","↳ Allfather: Probably like ordinary meat.","Damn.","I should’ve caught it instead of taking a picture.","But no matter how quickly you regret something, regret always comes too late.","I put my disappointment behind me and continued walking.","Trickle, trickle—","As I followed the river downstream, the current gradually slowed.","The river also grew considerably wider, so this was probably somewhere near the lower reaches.","There were no sudden distortions in space or drastic changes in the surrounding environment along the way.","Bzzzzzzzz—","The real problem was the gigantic mosquitoes flying around.","At first, I wondered if my sense of perspective was off.","But when one threatened me with its sharp proboscis, I finally realized it was a monster.","Clang!","I barely managed to block it with my shield in my panic.","The Golden Shield had been dented by the Muscle Mushroom, but it was still plenty useful.","The instant I blocked the attack, I drew the sword hanging from the left side of my waist.","Slash!","Then I swung it at the mosquito, which was about the size of my head.","Given how huge it was, the mosquito was cleanly sliced in two.","Watching its severed body twitch on the ground left me dumbfounded.","’Did I fall into some dark fantasy world?’","I shook my head.","It was probably better for my sanity to believe that this forest itself was just abnormal.","But there was one thing that worried me.","If mosquitoes were this huge...","What about bees?","How large would bees be when they formed enormous colonies?","Just imagining a swarm of bees the size of my head attacking me was horrifying.","’Thank god there isn’t a beehive near the cave.’","Thinking that, I walked past the mosquito corpse.","A few steps later, I suddenly heard a rustling sound from behind me.","Rustle! Rustle!","Since I had no choice but to react sensitively even to the smallest noise, I spun around in alarm.","I didn’t forget to raise my shield as I turned.","Scurry!","The iguana I had seen earlier was running away with the mosquito corpse in its mouth.","I stared blankly at the creature disappearing at high speed.","This place was impossible to get used to.","’There are probably things even weirder than that.’","Just how many more bizarre creatures would I end up seeing?","I could hardly wait.","I continued silently downstream.","This time, I kept my sword drawn so I could counterattack immediately.","I had no idea how long I continued following the river.","It felt like I had been walking for around an hour, but nothing particularly noteworthy appeared.","Splash!","The only thing that stood out was the fish.","Every now and then, an enormous fish would leap out of the water.","Maybe it was just my imagination, but they looked much bigger than the ones I had caught before.","Since this was downstream rather than the fast-flowing upper reaches, there were probably far more fish living here.","’It wouldn’t be bad to install the fish trap here—’","SPLASH!","I had just started thinking that when something burst out of the lower reaches of the river.","It was a little too small to call a whale, but far too large to call an ordinary fish.","Its entire body was pitch black, and just looking at it gave off an intimidating pressure.","SPLASH!","Its enormous body plunged back into the river, sending a column of water spraying into the air.","I could only stare at the scene in a daze.","’Do whales even live in rivers?’","The urge to turn around and go straight back to the cave rapidly grew.","I could probably deal with most beasts at this point, but there was absolutely no way I could take that thing down.","Still, I wanted to at least see where the river ended.","I couldn’t give up yet.","So I continued downstream in tense silence.","And when I finally reached the end—","\"Ah, fuck.\"","The words came from the very bottom of my heart.","It was less a curse and more an exhausted sigh caused by sheer disbelief.","\"Is this the ocean or a lake?\"","A vast lake stretched out at the end of the river.","Though calling it a lake felt a little strange.","Despite its incredible size, the water was extremely shallow.","The water was so clear that I could see the bottom perfectly.","’It’s practically stamping \"You’re not getting out\" right on my forehead.’","I could feel my spirit slowly breaking.","I sighed and made a post on the gallery.","I was feeling gloomy, so I wanted to post something and see how people reacted.","Title: Found a Pretty Lake","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a vast lake)","I followed the river downstream and found a lake.","Pretty, right?","How the hell am I supposed to escape now? Hahahaha.","↳ Heavenly Demon: What beautiful scenery. It makes this lady wish to take out a small boat and recite a poem.","↳ Wild Grylls: Teacher?","↳ Heavenly Demon: Is there some problem?","↳ SwordMaster: Read the room. Do you think Grylls has the luxury of taking a boat out there?","↳ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. That is true. This lady apologizes. I must have been momentarily captivated by the beautiful scenery.","↳ Wild Grylls: No, it’s fine. I guess that can happen...","↳ It really is pretty though lol.","↳ I’m gonna paint this.","↳ There are a lot of rocks in the lake.","↳ Looks really shallow too.","↳ Hey, what’s that faint thing way over there? Looks fucking huge.","↳ Isn’t it just a rock?","↳ Grylls, it’s hot out. Take a refreshing dive lol.","↳ Wild Grylls: It’s too shallow. If I dive in, I’ll crack my head open ;;","↳ It’s a lake but it’s shallow? Is it even a lake?","↳ Wild Grylls: I don’t know either. It’s way too wide to call a pond, but too shallow to feel like a proper lake.","↳ Normally something like that would be a wetland.","↳ Wild Grylls: There are too many pebbles for it to be a swamp.","↳ Passing Dwarf: Are your shoes any good? If you’re going to cross that place, you’ll definitely need boots.","↳ Wild Grylls: That’s what I’m worried about. I’d ask you, but I feel like I’ve already asked you for too much, so I’m thinking of asking someone else.","↳ Passing Dwarf: Yeah. I’m not that confident when it comes to shoes either. I don’t know about my own kind, but there are plenty of humans better at making them than me.","↳ Wild Grylls: Guess I’ll need to get myself a pair of proper shoes later.","Come to think of it, while I’d been focused on getting clothes, I had completely neglected getting proper shoes.","For someone like me who had to walk long distances, footwear was extremely important.","I wanted to ask the dwarf, but like I’d said myself, I felt like I was relying on him too much, so I decided against it.","The dwarf had also advised me that when it came to shoes, I was better off asking someone else.","’I thought I’d never wear combat boots again unless I was called up for reserve training.’","And now here I was, looking for combat boots.","Life really was unpredictable.","Still, more important than combat boots themselves right now was waterproofing.","If I wore soaked shoes for too long, I could get sick, and my feet would swell up from being waterlogged.","’There’s no rubber in the auction house... Should I just put up with it for today?’","I debated whether to endure it for just one day or turn back right now.","Going back would have been perfectly reasonable, but something about it felt unsatisfying.","I hadn’t even reached a true dead end yet.","I couldn’t give up that quickly.","’Yeah. If necessary, I can always build a boat. Let’s investigate a little more.’","If the water got even slightly deeper, I planned to turn back immediately.","I nodded to myself and moved around only where the water was as shallow as possible.","It felt like I was circling around the edge of the lake, but even this was yielding results.","’If I keep going like this, I might actually get around the lake.’","It seemed possible to reach the opposite side without needing a boat at all.","Of course, there were puddles here and there, so there was no avoiding getting my shoes wet.","I continued forward while carefully watching my surroundings.","\"Gururuk.\"","\"Guruk. Guruk.\"","\"Hm?\"","I heard a strange sound.","It came from directly ahead.","When I looked, I saw several large rocks clustered together.","It didn’t take me long to realize they weren’t rocks at all.","’Crabs? Why are there crabs here?’","They were crabs.","Crabs walking sideways.","And they were far bigger than lobsters.","Each one was roughly the size of my upper body.","The crabs twitched their stalk-like eyes and moved their claws around.","I cautiously approached.","Even when I got closer, they showed no sign of wariness and remained busy working their claws.","’Fish?’","It was fish.","The crabs were eating fish carcasses.","I vaguely remembered hearing that crabs sometimes acted as scavengers.","But that still didn’t explain why there were fish corpses here in the first place.","’The water’s so shallow that swimming should be difficult. Were they just unlucky?’","First, I should take a picture and figure out what species they were.","I photographed the crabs enjoying their meal and uploaded it to the gallery.","Title: Anyone Know What Species This Is?","(Photo of crabs happily eating)","I was walking around the lakeside and found these crabs eating.","They’re about the size of my torso.","Anyone know what species they are?","↳ Do crabs even live in lakes?","↳ Yeah. Those things are adaptation experts. As long as there’s water, they’ll live anywhere.","↳ I heard crab tastes amazing.","↳ They look ordinary enough. You could probably roast them and eat them.","↳ Allfather: They are edible Gophers Crabs. Normally, they are only about the size of a fist.","↳ Wild Grylls: No parasites or anything inside them?","↳ Allfather: There is nothing that cannot be killed by fire.","So as long as I didn’t eat them raw, I’d be fine.","Excellent.","I could take one of these things back with me on the way home.","’Their shells shouldn’t be too hard, right?’","Just in case, I stabbed one with the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","Crunch!","With a satisfying sound, the blade pierced straight through its shell.","The crab, now skewered through the back, flailed its claws and legs.","The other crabs didn’t care whether one of their own was dying.","They remained completely focused on eating the fish.","’As expected of the Heavenly Demon’s sword. I should never doubt it.’","I flicked the sword and shook the crab off.","The crab landed upside down and trembled for a while.","I felt a little sorry for it.","For about a moment.","\"Gururuk.\"","\"Guruk. Guruk.\"","More crabs slowly started approaching from elsewhere.","They were heading toward the crab whose shell I had pierced.","Curious about what they were doing, I stood still and watched.","Soon, the crabs surrounded their wounded companion and raised their enormous claws.","Crunch! Crunch!","They slammed their claws down onto the overturned crab.","Its shell shattered further with every strike.","Eventually, the crab even stopped trembling.","It was dead.","And the dead crab became a meal for its own kind.","\"...\"","Nature really was brutal.","I shook my head and kept moving.","Countless crabs inhabited the lakeside.","Almost all of them looked exactly the same.","Normally, a lake would support all sorts of life, so I couldn’t help finding this a little strange.","’How did these crabs take over the entire lakeside?’","Their claws were powerful, sure, but ultimately, these things were weak creatures.","While pondering that question, I suddenly came face-to-face with a large boulder.","It was much bigger than I was.","A random boulder jutting up here felt a little strange, but I could simply go around it.","\"Guruk.\"","\"Hm?\"","Except the boulder made a strange noise.","The exact same sound the crabs had been making earlier.","Confused, I stared at the boulder.","Rumble—","With a faint vibration, several legs suddenly protruded from underneath it.","Then two gigantic claws emerged from either side.","The boulder had already been huge.","Now it looked even bigger than before.","So large that I had to tilt my head all the way back just to look at it.","\"Guruk. Gururuk.\"","Its stalk-like eyes stared directly at me.","I couldn’t help slowly backing away.","The boulder—","No.","The gigantic crab stared at me for a while before rapidly scuttling its legs.","Thankfully, it wasn’t coming toward me.","Instead, it turned its whole body around.","It seemed to have lost interest.","’...Wait a second.’","Don’t crabs move sideways?","The moment that thought crossed my mind—","Whoosh!","A gigantic claw came crashing down toward my head.","As I said before, crabs were creatures that acted as scavengers.","BOOM!","\"Ugh!\"","In other words—","They were omnivores."]},{"title":"Chapter 48","paragraphs":["Lakeside (3)","The giant crab brought its claw crashing down.","I narrowly dodged the attack.","Its movements were large and surprisingly sluggish, so avoiding it wasn’t particularly difficult.","But the vibration that shook the ground when the claw struck...","That was no joke.","’F-First, the mana.’","I steadied my startled heart and circulated my mana.","A refreshing stimulation spread through my muscles.","Since I practiced whenever I had spare time, I was able to respond quickly.","\"Gururuk.\"","In the meantime, the giant crab raised its claw again.","For something that huge, it was surprisingly agile.","The moment I saw it, I moved both legs.","Trying to block that thing head-on was a bad idea.","Thud!","\"Ugh?!\"","But the unfamiliar terrain caused me to make a mistake.","Something caught my foot as I stepped backward.","For a moment, the world seemed to spin, and then the sky filled my vision.","Even as my body tipped backward, I reacted instinctively.","\"Urgh...!\"","A considerable impact traveled through my back.","Still, it was bearable.","Just before falling, I curled my body to minimize the impact.","It was the breakfall technique SwordMaster had explained in his post.","Rumble—","Even while I staggered and fell, the giant crab didn’t stop.","Maybe because it had so many legs, it closed the distance quickly despite its enormous body.","Slip—","I tried to force myself back up, but my footing slipped slightly.","In that brief moment, the giant crab slowly raised its claw, casting a shadow over my head.","Getting up in time would be difficult.","Acting on instinct, I raised my shield.","Praying that it would protect me, I drew out as much mana as possible from within my body.","BANG!","A sound like metal colliding with metal rang out.","Then came the impact transmitted through the shield.","My arm went numb, but I could endure it.","It was weaker than the Muscle Mushroom.","Before another blow could come, I hurriedly rolled away.","BOOM!","While I was rolling, the giant crab slammed its claw down again.","Feeling the vibration travel through my entire body, I silently got back to my feet.","The giant crab adjusted its direction by moving its countless legs and approached me again.","’Forget about blocking and counterattacking.’","If I kept blocking with the shield, my arm would give out first.","I had to exploit an opening somehow, but finding one wasn’t easy.","’Its attacks are simple, but the problem is that they’re fast.’","I kept moving my legs while thinking.","That was another tip SwordMaster had taught me.","Think while moving.","That way, you wouldn’t give your opponent an opening and could steer the situation in your favor.","BOOM!","And SwordMaster’s advice worked.","The giant crab missed.","Its claw smashed into the spot where I had been standing just moments earlier.","Now.","This was my chance.","I poured mana into the sword and swung with all my strength.","The blade shimmered like a heat haze before slicing straight through the claw.","Slash!","The pincer portion of the claw fell cleanly to the ground.","It wasn’t a particularly major hit.","I had only cut off the pincer itself, not the entire claw.","With something this huge, that couldn’t be helped.","It wasn’t like I could slice the whole thing apart with a single sword strike like someone else could.","’Just cut it apart piece by piece.’","But this was enough.","If I kept dismantling it little by little, I could kill it.","Whoosh!","The giant crab swung the claw that had lost its pincer.","The limb itself was still basically a gigantic blunt weapon, so it remained more than threatening enough.","I kept my legs moving while searching for a weakness.","’Wait a second. This thing...’","As I watched, I noticed one weakness.","A very serious one.","Crabs, by nature, could only walk sideways.","Even after growing enormous, that trait hadn’t changed.","In other words, its effective attack range was extremely limited.","No matter how wildly it swung its claws, there was still a clear limit.","’And especially... it turns incredibly slowly.’","While the giant crab flailed its claws, I quickly moved around and took its rear.","It tried desperately to turn around, but it was far too slow.","It couldn’t hit me with its claws either.","Such was the unfortunate fate of a creature designed only to move sideways.","Slash!","While it struggled to turn, I cut through its legs instead of attacking its claws.","Two legs were severed in a single strike.","It was the combined result of the Heavenly Demon’s sword and aura.","Thud!","Having lost two legs at once, the giant crab lost its balance.","One side of its body tilted awkwardly, making it difficult for the creature to stabilize itself.","My goal was to completely destroy its mobility.","Since the bastard turned as slowly as a turtle, I exploited that weakness thoroughly.","Slash! Slash!","Instead of standing in front of it, I continually stayed behind it and cut off its legs.","Once I severed two legs from each side, it completely lost even its ability to turn.","After that, cutting off the remaining legs was easy.","Slash!","Finally, I completely severed its prized claws as well.","The creature collapsed onto the ground with nothing but its torso remaining.","Maybe because it was a crustacean, its body was still twitching even after all of its limbs had been cut off.","Crunch!","I climbed onto the giant crab’s shell and drove my sword down.","I stabbed between its eyes, directly into the center of the upper shell.","Krrrrrk!","Then, as though pulling a lever, I dragged the sword downward.","The Heavenly Demon’s sword could split even solid wood like tofu, so the blade slid through surprisingly easily.","Eventually, the sword reached the very bottom of the shell.","I gripped it tightly and pulled with all my strength.","Slash!","Since all of its legs were already gone, the body didn’t split dramatically in half.","But I was satisfied simply seeing it stop moving entirely.","I lightly shook the bits of innards from the blade.","\"Haaah!\"","I exhaled heavily.","My heart was pounding violently from the adrenaline surging through me.","If I hadn’t figured out its weakness, that fight would have been much harder.","No.","Forget \"harder.\"","One wrong move and I could have lost my life.","Strangely enough, it was exhilarating.","\"Gururuk.\"","\"Guruk.\"","Before I knew it, the smaller crabs had gathered around and begun picking apart the giant crab’s corpse.","Even the giant ones seemed to faithfully fulfill their role as scavengers.","I watched them for a moment, then made a post on the gallery.","Title: Hunted a Giant Crab","(Photo of an enormous giant crab corpse)","A giant crab way bigger than a person jumped me at the lakeside ;; It used its claws like blunt weapons.","Luckily, it turned ridiculously slowly, so it wasn’t too hard to kill.","What the hell kind of creature is this ;;","I only posted the message and didn’t bother checking the comments.","Getting back to the cave was more urgent.","Not only had I fallen on my ass, I had rolled all over the ground.","If I left myself like this, the smell would be bad enough, but I could also get sick.","’Next time I come here, I need to bring proper shoes.’","This incident had made me realize just how important footwear was.","Especially when I slipped earlier.","For a second, I genuinely felt like my life flashed before my eyes.","I caught my breath again and started walking back.","’The fish corpse is... over there.’","I hadn’t forgotten the route back.","There were fish carcasses and partially eaten crab corpses along the way, after all.","Just thinking about walking back through all this filth made me feel sick, but I had no choice but to endure it.","\"Gururuk. Guruk.\"","\"...\"","When I spotted a crab along the way, I gently picked it up.","Then I bought a backpack from the auction house.","Not one of those small bags worn at the waist, but a proper backpack worn on the back.","’I can’t resist.’","The moment I got back to the cave, I was eating this.","I needed to give some to Wonmo and the Sloth too, so I stuffed two more crabs inside.","I considered taking one for the dwarf as well, but unfortunately, I wouldn’t be able to trade with him until tomorrow.","Crab was perfect as a drinking snack, so I planned to come back tomorrow anyway.","’Allfather said they’re edible, so they should taste good, right?’","I wasn’t particularly worried about parasites.","They probably wouldn’t kill each other and spoil inside the bag either.","So far, I had only seen them eat members of their own species after they were already dead.","Rrrrrumble.","Just as I was happily imagining the meal ahead, the ground began to shake.","Nothing good had ever happened to me when the earth started trembling.","The instant that thought crossed my mind, I hurriedly looked around.","Splash! Splash!","One giant crab after another began emerging from deeper inside the lake.","Each was about the same size as the one I had just fought, or slightly larger.","There were at least five of them.","I stared at the sight in disbelief.","I had barely managed to kill one, and now five had appeared.","If I had stayed there any longer, I would have been in serious danger.","’Is this really a lake? Not an ocean?’","There was no salty sea smell, so it definitely seemed to be a lake.","I moved carefully, worried that the giant crabs might notice me.","Thankfully, not one of them so much as glanced in my direction before I reached the mouth of the river.","They were too busy picking up and eating the corpse of their own kind with their claws.","’They really are slaves to their instincts.’","Judging by their behavior, corpses seemed to be their first priority.","\"Scavenger\" really was the perfect word for them.","I slowly backed away, then turned around.","It was about time I headed back to the cave.","RUMBLEEEEE!","That was when I felt a tremor on an entirely different level from before.","It was far stronger than the shaking caused by the giant crabs.","For a moment, I wondered if this was an actual earthquake.","Then a tremendous noise came from the lake, impossible to ignore.","ROOOOAR!","Water surged high into the air before crashing back down.","At the sound, I turned toward the lake.","The moment I looked back, I froze.","I had thought the giant crabs were already absurdly huge.","Apparently, something even worse lived in this lake.","’...Fuck. What the hell is that?’","If the giant crabs were the size of large trucks, the crab I was looking at now was the size of a building.","In terms of height alone, it was comparable to a small apartment building.","It was so absurdly huge that perspective itself felt meaningless.","Could I even call that thing a crab?","It was basically a walking building.","Title: Find What’s Wrong With This Video","Wild Grylls","(Video of a building-sized crab with giant crabs beside it)","What’s wrong with this picture?","Take a guess!","↳ Heavenly Demon: Hmm? Why does the sky look so small?","↳ Wild Grylls: Right? I wonder why it looks so small.","↳ SwordMaster: I’ve never seen a crab that huge in my life. Does something like that actually exist?","↳ Wild Grylls: Good eye. I’m looking at it myself and still can’t believe it.","↳ Heavenly Demon: Looking again, it truly is enormous. It has piqued this lady’s interest.","↳ Wild Grylls: Want to come over? We can catch it and steam it.","↳ Heavenly Demon: My close aides are desperately stopping me, so I cannot go. My apologies.","↳ Allfather: Oh ;; Ooooh;; Fuck, what is that?","↳ Wild Grylls: Lmaoooo, I don’t know either. First time seeing one too, Allfather?","↳ Allfather: The species is definitely a Gophers Crab... but I do not know whether that should be considered an entirely new species at this point. What on earth is that?","↳ Wild Grylls: I’m amazed too.","↳ Passing Dwarf: Looks like a mountain is walking around ;; Hey, can I ask you for something?","↳ Wild Grylls: You want a crab as drinking snacks? Trade cooldown means I can give you one tomorrow.","↳ Passing Dwarf: Yeah. And while you’re at it, give me that huge one.","↳ Wild Grylls: You fucking lunatic lmao.","↳ Whoa ;; I don’t even know what to say. Isn’t that thing basically a spirit beast at this point?","↳ Yeah, I bet there’s an inner core inside that shell.","↳ If it’s that huge, you could definitely call it a spirit beast lol.","↳ You planning to hunt it?","↳ Wild Grylls: You do it ;; There’s absolutely no way I can kill that thing. I already struggled just taking down one giant crab.","↳ Nothing in this world is impossible. You just have to try.","↳ If you kill that thing, the gallery’s gonna explode lmao.","↳ Wild Grylls: I’ll try if someone comes and helps me lol.","↳ (No replies)","↳ Wild Grylls: Answer me, you bastards.","I kept walking while looking at the gallery.","I wanted to get back as quickly as possible.","The dampness made my entire body feel heavier.","’Why is the back of my neck so itchy, though?’","Maybe because the tension had finally eased, my senses had become more sensitive.","And because of that, I could clearly feel every itchy spot.","Unable to stand it, I reached behind my neck with my right hand and scratched.","Squish.","Then I felt something soft.","The instant I felt it, I froze.","My instincts were screaming at me.","Whatever this squishy thing was, it was absolutely nothing good.","Worse yet, even when I flicked it with my fingers, it refused to come off.","I swallowed hard and grabbed it.","Then I pulled with force, tearing it off.","It stretched like jelly.","Pop!","Something detached from the back of my neck with a strange sound and a sharp sting.","It was big enough that I had to grip it in my hand.","And it was slippery.","Very slowly, I brought my right hand around in front of my face.","I needed to see what I was holding.","Wriggle. Wriggle.","Something red and slime-like squirmed in my hand—","No.","It was a grotesque brown leech.","An obviously disgusting one.","And it was enormous.","\"KYAAAAAAAAAAAH!!!\"","I wanted to get out of here as fast as possible."]},{"title":"Chapter 49","paragraphs":["Shoes (1)","The leech incident caused quite a commotion, so I hurriedly made a post on the Gallery.","I asked what I was supposed to do after getting bitten by a leech. I explained that I’d accidentally grabbed the one on the back of my neck and ripped it off.","The ever-so-kind veteran adventurers promptly told me what to do.","_What the fuck? Why would you remove a leech like that? Are you fucking desperate to get an infection?","└ Wild Grylls) I didn’t know anything about leeches...","_Whatever. If you have a potion, apply it to the bite. You might’ve gotten infected with a parasite, so take a deworming medicine too.","└ Wild Grylls) It’s not a potion, it’s an elixir. Is that okay? Does an elixir disinfect wounds too? I know it regenerates them.","_Just fucking put it on ;; Why are you asking such a weird question ;;","└ An elixir is literally a higher-tier item than a potion kekeke","└ Feels like watching a rich newbie kekeke","└ The fact that he ripped a leech off with his bare hand proves he’s got guts, at least.","_The teeth might still be stuck in there, so remove those before applying it.","Only after receiving their affectionate(?) advice was I able to treat the wound properly.","Normally, I would’ve needed to take deworming medicine too, but apparently the elixir alone was enough.","Next time I came here, I’d probably have to wrap something around my neck.","’Why the hell am I going through all this?’","I sighed. Still, it was some consolation that the trip hadn’t been completely fruitless.","Once I got back to the cave, I’d have to dry my damp clothes and shoes, make something to eat, and take care of a bunch of other things.","I’d wanted to install the fish trap too if possible, but with my shoes soaked through, that seemed unlikely.","’I absolutely need to get some shoes.’","The shoes I was currently wearing were sneakers. The same sneakers I’d been wearing before I fell into this place.","You might wonder why I’d been wearing shoes when I’d been at home before ending up here.","I didn’t really know either. The last thing I remembered was drinking.","’I don’t know if I should call that lucky or not.’","Still, at least I had sneakers.","I trudged along with the unpleasant dampness clinging to my feet.","The farther back I went, the narrower the river became and the stronger the current grew.","It wasn’t until I reached the section of the river where I’d installed the hose that it finally sank in that I was almost back.","’I really did go pretty far this time.’","I accessed the Gallery to check the time.","It was currently 12:20 p.m. It hadn’t taken as long as I’d expected.","I’d spent more time walking along the river than actually exploring the lakeshore.","’Wonmo’s probably going to be demanding food.’","Or maybe he’d gotten anxious because I’d disappeared.","The thought made me quicken my pace slightly.","Eventually, I arrived at the cave that had now begun to feel strangely familiar, and there I saw it with my own two eyes.","\"Kuu...\"","\"...\"","Wonmo was sprawled out asleep with his belly completely exposed.","He was even scratching his own stomach with his claws.","Apparently, he couldn’t care less whether I disappeared or not. He was perfectly content taking a nap.","\"...What, punk? What are you looking at?\"","The tree sloth was just sitting there stupidly too.","A sigh escaped me as I realized I’d worried for nothing.","Anyway, I still had to clean everything up.","I took off the backpack containing the crabs.","When I looked inside, the crabs were barely moving, just twitching their legs every now and then.","’First, let’s get a fire going.’","I had a mountain of things to do.","I stripped off the clothes that had partially dried.","Laundry could wait. Washing the grime off my body came first.","I also made sure to inspect myself thoroughly in case there were any other leeches hiding somewhere I couldn’t see.","’So there really was only one on my neck.’","It was honestly impressive that the thing had managed to latch onto me during the brief instant when I’d fallen.","I turned on the water from the hose and thoroughly washed every part of my body.","Soap was a must.","Following the advice of Gallery users—or, more specifically, the adventurers—I used unscented soap.","\"Phew.\"","After giving myself a quick wash, I used a towel to remove as much moisture as possible.","Then I approached the campfire I’d prepared beforehand and thoroughly dried myself by the heat.","’First, I should buy some shoes I can use temporarily.’","My sneakers were completely soaked, so I needed something to wear until they dried.","I entered the Auction House and bought a decent pair of leather shoes.","I didn’t bother worrying about the size. I was basically going to use them as slippers, so as long as they roughly fit, they’d be fine.","\"I’ll leave the laundry here, and now that I’m dry, I should change into something else.\"","I still had plenty of the uniforms Princess Cheonggu had given me.","The problem was that the pants were shorts.","Long pants were essential for exploring, so I planned to wash and dry mine today.","I also had plenty of charcoal for doing laundry. The veteran adventurers had told me I absolutely had to collect it.","’Now, all that’s left is...’","Grilling the crabs.","I took the crabs out of the backpack and put them into the metal container.","Then I filled it with water to keep them as fresh as possible.","Between the fish and now the crabs, that metal container was proving incredibly useful.","All that remained was asking the Gallery how to prepare them.","Apparently, I just had to pry open the mouth(?) or something, but I wasn’t exactly sure what that meant.","Title) Anyone know how to prepare crabs?","(Photo of crabs inside a metal container)","I’m planning to grill them instead of steaming them. Anyone know how I should prepare them?","└ Passing Dwarf) Wow. Those look fucking delicious. Can’t you give me just one?","└ Wild Grylls) I told you I’ll give you one tomorrow. We can’t even trade today anyway.","_ Passing Dwarf) Ha, seriously ;; If I’d known this would happen, I wouldn’t have used up my trade.","└ Wild Grylls) Just wait one day. You seriously can’t even manage that?","└ Passing Dwarf) Yeah yeah. The hand holding my beer is literally trembling right now.","└ Wild Grylls) Dude, those are symptoms of alcoholism. Lay off the booze.","└ Telling a dwarf to stop drinking kekeke","_ Might as well tell him to quit drugs lol","└ Wait, don’t tell me you actually do drugs?","└└└ It was just an example kekeke","└ This bastard’s suspicious, isn’t he?","└ Preparing crabs is actually pretty easy. There’s a part around the mouth that’s slightly open, right? Stick a knife in there and twist it to drain the blood and water.","_ If you’re grilling it instead of steaming it, don’t put it back in the water afterward. Just grill it as is.","└ Don’t worry about the body burning all the way through.","└ It’s best to drain as much moisture as possible. Otherwise, you might end up boiling it instead of grilling it.","So I had to twist open the mouth first.","I nodded and pulled out my dagger.","Then I took one of the crabs from the metal container and turned it around, examining it from different angles.","Just as the Gallery had explained, its mouth had a structure that opened toward both sides.","’If I stick the dagger in here and twist it sideways...’","Riiip!","With a satisfyingly sharp sound, the crab’s mouth was forcibly pried open.","The moment its mouth opened, I flipped it upside down.","Clear blood mixed with water dripped steadily from its mouth.","\"Kkyuu.\"","\"Ah. You’re awake?\"","While I was preparing the crab, Wonmo woke up from his nap.","The tree sloth also began inching closer, apparently asking for food.","\"Just wait a little. I’ll give you something really delicious.\"","\"Kkyuu!\"","\"...\"","Wonmo’s eyes sparkled at the mention of something delicious.","The tree sloth didn’t show much of a reaction, but it was probably looking forward to it too.","’Now that all the blood’s drained...’","Straight onto the campfire!","The crab was so large that it more than covered the entire campfire.","I added more firewood so that not only the body but the legs would cook evenly.","At the same time, I didn’t want it completely charred, so I positioned it slightly away from the flames.","’They said to wait twenty to thirty minutes, right?’","In the meantime, I entered the Auction House and searched for shoes.","The shoes I wanted had to meet some fairly demanding requirements.","Since I’d be walking for long periods, they needed ventilation and comfort, as well as waterproofing.","Most importantly, they had to be durable. The moment I injured my feet, my chances of survival would plummet.","Like I’d told the dwarf, what I basically wanted was something close to combat boots, with \"durability\" as the foundation.","’Thinking about combat boots reminds me of the military.’","Back when I’d just become a recruit, I thought I was going to die during my first march.","Actually, the march itself wasn’t the worst part. The real mess came afterward.","Everyone else had blisters or patches of skin rubbed raw, but I was perfectly fine.","To me, combat boots were just slightly heavy shoes. I’d never found them particularly uncomfortable.","’No matter how much I search, there’s nothing.’","Even the expensive shoes didn’t meet the conditions I wanted.","Besides, most of those expensive ones were related to sports. Soccer cleats, basketball shoes, things like that.","In the end, it seemed I’d have no choice but to make a post.","Before doing that, I bought a measuring tape from the Auction House.","Since I wasn’t familiar with the units of measurement here, I planned to put the tape next to my foot for reference.","Title) Commissioning a Pair of Shoes","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a measuring tape placed beside my foot)","(Photo of a measuring tape placed over my foot)","Just like the title says, I’m looking for shoes suitable for exploration. However, the requirements are pretty demanding.","(Most important) They must be durable. An injury to my feet would be disastrous, so this is the highest priority. Waterproofing. I’ll often be in situations where my shoes could get wet. Ventilation and comfort. Honestly, comfort matters more than ventilation. I may have to travel through high-altitude areas. Slip resistance. I nearly died after slipping while trying to stand up. Preferably made of leather. Same reason as number three.","If someone can make shoes that roughly meet the conditions above, I’ll give them a mature Mandrake as payment.","I’d also appreciate it if you could upload videos and photos demonstrating their performance. I hope plenty of people see this.","_ Heavenly Demon) May this lady participate as well?","└ Wild Grylls) Huh? Why would you, Heavenly Demon?","└ Heavenly Demon) This lady is bored.","└ Wild Grylls) Teacher;;;","└ SwordMaster) If you’re bored, want to have a debate on swordsmanship with me? I’ll wipe the floor with you.","_ Heavenly Demon) Foolish one. Very well. This lady shall message you.","└ Passing Dwarf) Can I have someone else make these for me? I know a guy who’s damn good at making armor.","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah, do whatever you want. But do you even need a mature Mandrake? Planning to make more booze with it?","└ Passing Dwarf) That’s part of it, but my friend keeps pestering me for a drink. Wouldn’t it be easier to just give him one?","└ Wild Grylls) Do whatever you want. I’m fine as long as I get the shoes.","└ Passing Dwarf) Okay. By when do you need them?","└ Wild Grylls) The sooner, the better. I think I’ll need at least two pairs for now?","└ Passing Dwarf) Okay, got it.","└ I’llBeADuke) Are you truly offering a mature Mandrake as the prize?","└ Wild Grylls) I don’t really have anything else to offer. Or would you rather have some of the crab I’m grilling right now?","└ I’llBeADuke) No. I will procure them for you as quickly as possible.","└ Wild Grylls) Thank you.","_ I’llBeADuke) If I acquire shoes that outperform the winning pair, would you be willing to accept them as well?","└ Wild Grylls) Honestly, this is basically a trade anyway, so as long as I like them, I don’t mind.","└ I’llBeADuke) Understood.","There was something strangely refined about the way he spoke.","Even his username sounded ambitious.","You could call this an event of sorts, but in reality, it was closer to a trade. A straightforward exchange where both sides gave and received something.","It wasn’t as though I planned to stop exploring just because I didn’t have proper shoes.","There were still plenty of places left to investigate.","Still, I intended to avoid unnecessary exploration whenever possible.","After nearly dying yesterday, I needed to be careful.","Crackle! Pop!","\"Is it done... Hot, hot, hot, hot!\"","The moment I pressed it with my finger to check whether it was cooked, an incredible wave of heat hit me.","Thankfully, I pulled my hand away immediately. Otherwise, I would’ve burned myself.","I put on my gloves and lifted out the deliciously cooked crab.","It was supposedly an ordinary crab, yet it was even larger than a king crab. There had to be plenty of meat inside.","’Let’s start with a leg.’","One of the tastiest parts—the legs.","I cut through one of the crab’s legs with my knife.","Crack!","The crab leg came away with a satisfyingly crisp sound.","I cut along the side with my knife and slowly pried the shell apart, sending wisps of steam curling into the air.","\"Wow.\"","Just look at that plump meat.","My mouth watered just from looking at it.","Now, how would it taste?","I’d sprinkled some salt on it, but hadn’t added any other seasoning.","Since it was still hot enough to burn me, I blew on it several times.","\"Munch. Munch. Haa.\"","This was seriously delicious.","Even with nothing but salt, it was packed with savory flavor.","There wasn’t even a hint of fishiness, making it incredibly easy to eat.","For a moment, all the crabs I’d seen scattered around the lake flashed through my mind.","Crack!","\"Kiya!\"","Of course. You couldn’t eat crab without taking off the top shell.","I exclaimed in delight when I removed the shell and saw the innards underneath.","For a moment, I regretted grilling it instead of steaming it.","Then I immediately started eating.","’I thought the innards would taste fishy, but they don’t?’","Even the innards were delicious.","There wasn’t a single disappointing part of it. Everything tasted fantastic.","After finishing the innards, I tore off another leg.","This one was for Wonmo.","\"Wonmo. I’ll give you more later, so eat this for now.\"","\"Kkyuu!\"","\"Speedy, want some too?\"","The tree sloth gestured for me to hand some over.","I cut off a leg and gave it to him too.","The tree sloth accepted it without the slightest suspicion, only to immediately start flailing its arms.","Even its normally drowsy eyes shot wide open. It must have been seriously startled.","’Yeah. It’s pretty damn hot.’","I was wearing gloves, but the tree sloth had grabbed it barehanded.","Considering how much the bastard had messed with me until now, this much revenge was nothing.","I snickered.","Smack!","Except the bastard threw it straight back at me.","It hit me square in the face.","A collaboration between a sloth’s powerful shoulder and a scorching-hot crab leg.","Right after the pain came an intense blast of heat.","\"Aaaaaagh!\"","Just you wait, you bastard.","**","While Grylls was happily enjoying his crab feast—","\"I assume you saw the post uploaded to the Gallery as well.\"","\"You mean...\"","\"Bring the craftsman here immediately. As quickly as possible.\"","\"Yes!\"","A subtle undercurrent began to ripple through the world."]},{"title":"Chapter 50","paragraphs":["Shoes (2)","While Grylls was busy bickering with the tree sloth, the Gallery erupted into another commotion because of the post he’d uploaded.","Normally, whenever he needed something, he maintained the stance that he’d simply trade for it.","Money meant nothing to him, and even noble titles were useless in his life in the wilderness.","Pressure didn’t work on him either.","Title) What kind of item would Grylls like?","I really want to get my hands on one mature Mandrake.","└ Just draw him some porn. Honestly, I don’t think there’s anything else.","└ Stop fucking around and answer seriously.","└ I am being fucking serious. What else is there to relieve yourself with in the Forest of Four Seasons? kekeke","└ Tofu?","└ You crazy bastard kekekekeke","That was why the users—especially the named users who wanted to establish a connection with him—had been racking their brains.","What kind of item could they give Grylls that he would actually like?","And how could they use that item to trade for a mature Mandrake?","Continuous trade was difficult because of how unstable his situation was.","But a one-time trade was enough.","Even succeeding just once could bring an enormous profit.","Title) Grylls obviously has the advantage","Where the hell are you guys going to get a mature Mandrake? kekeke Right now, Grylls is literally the only one who can get one kekeke","└ If it were just a regular Mandrake, maybe, but this is a mature Mandrake kekeke","└ Ask people where they’re supposed to get one and they’ll all shut up.","└ That’s exactly why everyone’s asking him for one. Just one of those could seriously turn your whole life around.","└ Is a mature Mandrake really that good?","└ I heard you can make one top-grade elixir with a single mature Mandrake.","└ And Grylls can dig them up like they’re fucking radishes. They’re growing right near him.","A mature Mandrake was one of those medicinal herbs that couldn’t be bought even if you had the money.","Its sheer rarity alone was enough to prove its value.","Trust wasn’t an issue either.","After the inner core incident, the users’ trust in Grylls had skyrocketed.","As long as they could arrange a proper \"trade,\" they could obtain an incredibly rare item.","And if that trade also helped them establish a connection with Grylls?","Grylls benefited because he could receive all sorts of support, while the other party profited by obtaining rare goods.","It was a win-win situation.","More than anything else, Grylls possessed one particular advantage that belonged to him alone.","Rarity.","Title) Grylls’s commission is seriously demanding","The shoes Grylls wants are insanely demanding. I don’t think anyone short of a really skilled craftsman could make them.","But if you’re going to trade something like that for a mature Mandrake, wouldn’t it be better to just sell the shoes for money? kekeke","└ Gallery money can’t be converted into real-world cash. That’s why barter is actually better.","└ Ah, right. You can’t cash it out, can you?","└ Yeah. If you could, the world economy would be completely fucked kekeke","└ Maybe not completely fucked, but it’d definitely get shaken up badly. The high fees are part of why things are still under control.","└ Wouldn’t it be better to just make the shoes and sell them? Why bother exchanging them specifically for a Mandrake?","└ Exactly. Aren’t people sucking up to Grylls a little too much?","└ Try finding a mature Mandrake yourself. Then I’ll admit you’re right.","└ That’s not what I’m saying. From a craftsman’s perspective, it’d be better to sell the shoes for money. They don’t need a mature Mandrake.","└ Wouldn’t someone higher up just pay the craftsman to make them? Besides, a lot of craftsmen use the Gallery too, so this could turn into a pride contest between them.","└ Then who’s famous among shoemakers?","└ As always, dwarves are famous for it, but demons have the upper hand these days.","└ Why?","└ Because they’ve been making sports shoes lol","_ Yeah, that immediately makes sense kekekekeke","More importantly, money charged into the Gallery couldn’t be converted back into real cash.","If cashing it out had been possible, crimes such as money laundering would surely have become rampant.","Because of this structural limitation, physical goods carried even greater value.","The rarity of an item one might never see even once in a lifetime.","The advantage of barter rather than monetary payment.","And finally, trust.","Those three conditions combined to create a strange atmosphere throughout the Gallery.","It wasn’t just the named users who usually liked showing off their possessions.","Even people who wanted to establish ties with Grylls began to move.","\"I assume you’ve seen the Gallery as well.\"","\"Yes, Your Highness. Do you mean...\"","\"If this had been a matter of continuous supply, I would have ignored it. But this time, that man called Grylls personally posted a commission. And he has offered a mature Mandrake as the reward.\"","Arnold, the blond-haired, blue-eyed Crown Prince, explained the situation in a solemn voice.","At his explanation, Count Gorgon, a graying middle-aged man, broke into a radiant smile.","The man’s intentions were so obvious that Arnold chuckled inwardly, though he showed nothing on his face.","He couldn’t afford to stand by and watch this matter unfold either.","That was how important it was.","\"A long-term contract with this man Grylls would be unstable. But a one-time contract like this is extremely important. Especially since he was the one who made the request first.\"","\"Yes, Your Highness. Then I shall immediately gather the craftsmen—\"","\"Listen until I finish speaking. We mustn’t be too hasty.\"","Arnold stopped Count Gorgon from displaying excessive enthusiasm.","Count Gorgon was highly capable and otherwise perfectly satisfactory.","His only problem was that he tended to overdo things.","’That just means he’s equally ambitious.’","From the perspective of someone in power like Arnold, the most trustworthy kind of subordinate wasn’t someone utterly incorruptible.","A moderately corrupt, moderately righteous ambitious man.","That was just about perfect.","As long as you satisfied the ambition they desired, they would offer their loyalty in return.","That made them easy to trust.","’Of course, if he ever crosses the line beyond that, I’ll have his head...’","He hadn’t reached that point yet.","Count Gorgon was certainly ambitious, but he wasn’t excessively greedy.","\"If we pressure the craftsmen unnecessarily, we may only provoke resistance. Can a work produced by crushing someone under authority truly be called a proper masterpiece?\"","\"Would that not constitute disrespect toward the royal family?\"","\"Then we must make sure they never commit such an offense in the first place. We are the ones who need them, after all. And the same will be true elsewhere.\"","Anyone could use the Gallery as long as they met the necessary conditions.","There was no telling when shoes meeting Grylls’s desired quality might suddenly appear.","That was why Arnold had been thinking.","How could they break through this fierce competition?","\"Moreover, if we are too late, it may become difficult to trade with him at all. If that happens, all our effort will have been wasted.\"","\"Then shouldn’t we move even faster—\"","\"We will take a different approach. One that will force him to trade with us even if he has already obtained another pair of shoes.\"","\"Pardon?\"","Count Gorgon’s eyes widened.","He couldn’t understand what Arnold meant at all.","But Arnold wasn’t finished.","He willingly revealed the plan he’d devised.","\"Wild Grylls. What he wants is something close to an all-purpose pair of shoes. In particular, he emphasized durability above everything else.\"","\"Y-Yes. That’s correct. If he injures his feet, he could end up unable to go anywhere at all.\"","\"More than anything, what matters most to that man is trust. And in a matter like this, he will be even more cautious.\"","\"Now that you mention it, I heard rumors that he was recently scammed.\"","’I know.’","Arnold answered silently.","It wasn’t so much that Grylls had been scammed as that he’d nearly been scammed.","At the same time, it had been the incident that raised people’s trust in him.","Afterward, Grylls had become even more cautious. He’d gone so far as to declare that any item that looked expensive would only be listed on the Auction House after being verified by a named user.","Would someone like that readily agree to a trade?","Arnold was certain he wouldn’t.","Unlike the named users who had helped Grylls out of pure goodwill, trust would be crucial in this matter.","\"First, contact a craftsman. Preferably one under contract with the military. If we end up being too late, we can simply use the shoes as military boots.\"","\"Understood.\"","\"I hope for a favorable result. Once the shoes are finished, do not contact him directly. Report to me first.\"","\"I will live up to your expectations!\"","Count Gorgon strode out with a vigorous shout.","Arnold stared at the spot where he’d disappeared for a moment, then raised his head.","The Gallery window, which he’d finally started getting used to, floated before his eyes.","’Grylls will definitely check the posts of any named user he trades with. If their posting history is completely empty, he’ll obviously become suspicious.’","Arnold had spent some time analyzing Grylls’s personality.","It could be summed up like this:","He was the type who couldn’t feel satisfied unless he gave something back whenever he received something.","Kindness for kindness.","Malice for malice.","Perhaps because his personality had so few rough edges, quite a few named users had become friendly with him.","He occasionally bickered with Passing Dwarf, but they were more like bad friends who genuinely got along.","’At the very least, this man isn’t someone who deceives others. He’ll definitely hand over the mature Mandrake.’","Of course, that assumed Grylls actually received the shoes he wanted.","Someone could create a named account, hand him some bizarre pair of shoes, and then simply disappear.","It wasn’t as though there were no scammers among named users.","Human malice could be frightening.","’I’d prefer to step in personally, but...’","Arnold checked his own username again.","[AbsolutezZoneArnoldTheBest]","It was the sort of username that made him feel like coughing up blood every time he saw it.","Arnold squeezed his eyes shut.","He’d rather jump off a building than actually participate under such an embarrassing username.","Thankfully, he had the fiercely ambitious Count Gorgon available.","’We have to show him trust first if we want him to repay us with trust.’","Arnold’s plan was simple.","Instead of exchanging the items immediately during the trade, his side would send the shoes first.","Then they would receive the mature Mandrake the following day, thereby earning Grylls’s goodwill and trust.","’And to do that...’","Arnold glanced around.","The Gallery was invisible to everyone else, but he still couldn’t help feeling self-conscious.","Among all his private activities, browsing the Gallery was easily the most shameful.","After confirming that no one was around, he began writing a post.","Only moments ago, he’d thought he’d rather jump off a building than participate.","But sometimes, surviving in this world required the courage to jump.","\"...\"","Title) Grylls, please read this post.","AbsolutezZoneArnoldTheBest","There are plenty of people on the Gallery who create named accounts and still scam others.","So I recommend receiving the item from the other party first, then giving them the mature Mandrake the following day.","I believe Grylls has always conducted himself openly and honestly, so there should be nothing for you to feel guilty about.","└ Who the hell are you to tell him what to do?","└ Isn’t this bastard just trying to sabotage the competition?","└ Damn, you people live suspicious lives kekeke","_ It’s not really being suspicious. I’ve been scammed exactly like that before ;.;","└ Yeah, there are surprisingly a lot of people like that. Plenty of cases happen the other way around too.","└ Honestly, that is the standard way to do it. Makes you feel safer.","_ What if Grylls is the one who scams them?","└ Wild Grylls) If I can’t trade the next day, that means I’m already fucking dead, doesn’t it? Anyway, thanks for the advice.","Arnold smiled in satisfaction after reading Grylls’s reply.","As expected, the other party had to be the one to demonstrate trust first.","’One dwarf named user is bound to make a pair, so I should assume there’ll only be one or two mature Mandrakes left after that.’","That was the safest assumption.","Humans might have a higher potential ceiling, but it was difficult to surpass a dwarf craftsman.","Arnold sincerely hoped Count Gorgon would return with good results.","If he did, both their lives would become much easier from then on.","[Posting one fucking idiot for everyone to see.]","Arnold happened to be browsing the Gallery when a title suddenly caught his eye.","The title itself was striking enough, but the author was Grylls.","Since he was publicly exposing someone, apparently somebody had tried to scam him.","Curious about what kind of fool had managed to earn Grylls’s distrust, Arnold opened the post.","Title) Posting one fucking idiot for everyone to see.","Wild Grylls","[Wild Grylls: If you beat me at word-chain, I’ll give you two. I’ll start. Sewing machine.]","[xxx: Machine teeth.]","[Wild Grylls: Teeth your mom.]","What kind of bastard is this? I’m just exposing him.","[Wild Grylls: Have you already prepared the shoes?]","[xxx: Yes. But you’ll have to give me two mature Mandrakes.]","[Wild Grylls: ? What kind of bullshit is that?]","[xxx: There are two shoes, aren’t there? You give me one Mandrake, and I’ll give you one shoe. Keep that in mind.]","└ Is this guy mentally disabled? kekekekekeke","└ Look at Grylls setting up \"sewing machine\" just to bait him into answering \"machine teeth\" kekekekeke","└ This bastard seriously has no conscience kekekekeke","└ xxx: Delete this post. If you don’t, I’ll retaliate.","└ Wild Grylls: Retaliate how? You gonna come to the Forest of Four Seasons? I’d appreciate that. You can dig up your own mature Mandrake.","└ Kekekekeke, he really was an idiot.","└ Threatening Grylls doesn’t work, bro kekeke","└ Looking at stuff like this, his situation almost seems convenient kekeke","\"Heh. Hehehe.\"","Arnold chuckled.","The world truly was vast, and there was no shortage of idiots.","That was one of the things he’d learned from using the Gallery.","’I should browse just a little longer before getting back to work.’","Arnold slowly continued lurking through the Gallery.","And then—","\"Aaaaaaaaaagh!\"","Just like Grylls before him, he peered into an abyss that should never have been seen."]}]);
